^DIC(19,69,0)="XMAUTOPURGE^Automatic Purge of MailMan Messages^^R^11748^^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,69,1,0)="^19.06^46^46^3010425^^^^"
^DIC(19,69,1,1,0)="This option automatically purges unreferenced MailMan messages, that is,"
^DIC(19,69,1,2,0)="it deletes from file 3.9, MESSAGE, any messages which are not in"
^DIC(19,69,1,3,0)="anyone's basket.  It is strongly recommended that this option be"
^DIC(19,69,1,4,0)="scheduled to run daily, right after option XMCLEAN."
^DIC(19,69,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(19,69,1,6,0)="The following messages are considered 'referenced', and will not be"
^DIC(19,69,1,7,0)="purged:"
^DIC(19,69,1,8,0)=" - Messages in user baskets"
^DIC(19,69,1,9,0)=" - Messages in transit (arriving or being sent)"
^DIC(19,69,1,10,0)=" - Server messages"
^DIC(19,69,1,11,0)=" - Messages being edited (including aborted edits)"
^DIC(19,69,1,12,0)=" - Messages which have been latered"
^DIC(19,69,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(19,69,1,14,0)="Several fields in file 4.3, MAILMAN SITE PARAMETERS, influence the"
^DIC(19,69,1,15,0)="behavior of this option.  Here they are, but feel free to look at"
^DIC(19,69,1,16,0)="their Data Dictionary descriptions for more information on them:"
^DIC(19,69,1,17,0)=""
^DIC(19,69,1,18,0)="4.301 - NO-PURGE DAYS BUFFER - MailMan does not purge any messages"
^DIC(19,69,1,19,0)="created or received in the last few days.  You choose how many days."
^DIC(19,69,1,20,0)="The default is 2."
^DIC(19,69,1,21,0)=""
^DIC(19,69,1,22,0)="142   - NO-PURGE DAYS BUFFER (LOCAL) - MailMan does not purge local"
^DIC(19,69,1,23,0)="messages created in the last few days.  You choose how many days."
^DIC(19,69,1,24,0)="The default is 7."
^DIC(19,69,1,25,0)=""
^DIC(19,69,1,26,0)="4.304 - WEEKDAY DAYS TO PURGE - On Saturdays, MailMan goes through the"
^DIC(19,69,1,27,0)="entire MESSAGE file looking for messages to purge.  On the other days"
^DIC(19,69,1,28,0)="of the week, however, MailMan has the option of only looking at"
^DIC(19,69,1,29,0)="messages created or received recently.  You choose how many days.  The"
^DIC(19,69,1,30,0)="default is to go through the entire MESSAGE file.  It is strongly"
^DIC(19,69,1,31,0)="recommended that you set this field to something reasonable, like 30"
^DIC(19,69,1,32,0)="to 60 days.  (But only if you follow the recommendation to schedule"
^DIC(19,69,1,33,0)="this option to run daily.  Otherwise leave this field blank.)"
^DIC(19,69,1,34,0)=""
^DIC(19,69,1,35,0)="4.303 - AUTOMATIC INTEGRITY CHECK - MailMan gives you the option of"
^DIC(19,69,1,36,0)="running the MAILBOX file portion of the integrity checker (option"
^DIC(19,69,1,37,0)="XMUT-CHKFIL) before it actually purges the unreferenced messages."
^DIC(19,69,1,38,0)="The M xref on file 3.7 is used to determine whether a message is"
^DIC(19,69,1,39,0)="referenced (in someone's basket) or not.  If the M xref is messed"
^DIC(19,69,1,40,0)="up, then the purge might delete messages it shouldn't, or leave"
^DIC(19,69,1,41,0)="message it should delete.  The integrity checker ensures that the"
^DIC(19,69,1,42,0)="M xref is correct.  You choose whether to run it or not.  The default"
^DIC(19,69,1,43,0)="is to run it.  The recommendation is to run it.  However, if you find"
^DIC(19,69,1,44,0)="that it is simply taking too long, you may opt not to run it.  If"
^DIC(19,69,1,45,0)="you opt not to run it, then it is recommended that you schedule option"
^DIC(19,69,1,46,0)="XMUT-CHKFIL to run monthly, because globals can and do become corrupted."
^DIC(19,69,2)="n"
^DIC(19,69,3.96,0)="^19.396P^^0"
^DIC(19,69,20)=""
