^DIC(19,97,1,1,0)="This option produces a report of the users currently signed on to"
^DIC(19,97,1,2,0)="this CPU and this UCI.  It will show the option they are running"
^DIC(19,97,1,3,0)="and when they signed on, as well as their device and job numbers."
^DIC(19,97,25)="XUS91"
^DIC(19,97,"U")="USER STATUS REPORT"
^DIC(19,98,0)="XUTLOOPBACK^Loopback Test of Device Port^^A^1039^^^^^^^^^1^^"
^DIC(19,98,1,0)="^^3^3^2880401^^^^"
^DIC(19,98,1,1,0)="This option will allow the testing of a terminal line with the"
^DIC(19,98,1,2,0)="use of a loopback connection on the line."
^DIC(19,98,1,3,0)="A loopback connector just ties pins 2, 3 together."
^DIC(19,98,20)="D ^%ZIS Q:POP  X ^%ZOSF(""EOFF""),^%ZOSF(""TYPE-AHEAD""),""F I=65:1:90 U IO W *I R *X:1 U IO(0) W:X>32 $C(X)"" X ^%ZOSF(""EON""),^%ZIS(""C"")"
^DIC(19,98,"U")="LOOPBACK TEST OF DEVICE PORT"
^DIC(19,99,0)="XURESJOBISM^Kill off a user's job (M/11, M/11+, M/VX)^Remove only on ISM systems^R^.5^XUMGR^^^^^^^n"
^DIC(19,99,1,0)="^^2^2^2880401^^"
^DIC(19,99,1,1,0)="Sends the user to 'RESJOB' in the MGR UCI, to kill off a user job."
^DIC(19,99,1,2,0)=" (only for ISM)"
^DIC(19,99,25)="RESJOB[MGR]"
^DIC(19,99,"U")="KILL OFF A USER'S JOB (M/11, M"
^DIC(19,100,0)="XMENROLL^Enroll in (or Disenroll from) a Mail Group^^R^11748^^3247^^^^^54^^^^"
^DIC(19,100,1,0)="^^7^7^2971007^^^^"
^DIC(19,100,1,1,0)="This option enables a mailman user to enroll in & disenroll from mail"
^DIC(19,100,1,2,0)="groups for which self-enrollment is allowed."
^DIC(19,100,1,3,0)="The user chooses a mail group."
^DIC(19,100,1,4,0)="If the user is already a member of the group, then this option"
^DIC(19,100,1,5,0)="enables the user to leave the group."
^DIC(19,100,1,6,0)="If the user is not already a member of the group, then this option"
^DIC(19,100,1,7,0)="enables the user to join the group."
^DIC(19,100,20)=""
^DIC(19,100,25)="ENROLL^XMVGROUP"
^DIC(19,100,"U")="ENROLL IN (OR DISENROLL FROM) "
^DIC(19,101,0)="XUVERSION5-HELP^Kernel 5.0 for Site Managers^^A^-1^^^^^^^^^1"
^DIC(19,101,1,0)="^^2^2^2851212^"
^DIC(19,101,1,1,0)="This option will direct you to a series of help frames describing the"
^DIC(19,101,1,2,0)="features of Kernel 5.0."
^DIC(19,101,20)="S XQH=""XUVERSION5-MGR"" D EN^XQH"
^DIC(19,101,"U")="KERNEL 5.0 FOR SITE MANAGERS"
^DIC(19,102,0)="XUAUTODEACTIVATE^Automatic Deactivation of Users^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^^n^^"
^DIC(19,102,1,0)="^^17^17^3090727^"
^DIC(19,102,1,1,0)="This option will go thru the New Person file, and search for users with "
^DIC(19,102,1,2,0)="a termination date in the past who still have an access code.  It will "
^DIC(19,102,1,3,0)="delete there access code and Keys. It calls the XU USER TERMINATE "
^DIC(19,102,1,4,0)="protocol in the OPTION FILE so other applications can take any action they"
^DIC(19,102,1,5,0)="need. If the DELETE ALL MAIL ACCESS field is set then the user will be"
^DIC(19,102,1,6,0)="removed them from the mail system, this will delete their mail boxes and"
^DIC(19,102,1,7,0)="delete them from any mail groups. "
^DIC(19,102,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(19,102,1,9,0)="Patch XU*8*514 implements the Logical Access Controls section of VA "
^DIC(19,102,1,10,0)="Handbook 6500. Item 'd' states that accounts are automatically disabled"
^DIC(19,102,1,11,0)="if inactive for 30 days."
^DIC(19,102,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(19,102,1,13,0)="The routine checks for users that have an access code and a Last Signon "
^DIC(19,102,1,14,0)="Date (#202) where the Last Signon Date is more than 30 days old and sets "
^DIC(19,102,1,15,0)="the DISUSER (#7) flag for the user. If the site has set the ACADEMIC"
^DIC(19,102,1,16,0)="AFFILIATION WAIVER (#13) field to YES in the KERNEL SYSTEM PARAMETERS file"
^DIC(19,102,1,17,0)="(#8989.3) then a 90 day limit is used in place of 30 days."
^DIC(19,102,2)="n"
^DIC(19,102,25)="CHECK^XUSTERM1"
^DIC(19,102,200)="^^"
^DIC(19,102,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,102,"U")="AUTOMATIC DEACTIVATION OF USER"
^DIC(19,103,0)="XUTESTUSER^Switch Identities^^R^11748^^120^^^^^^n^^"
^DIC(19,103,1,0)="^^3^3^2880401^^"
^DIC(19,103,1,1,0)="This option will allow a user to simulate signing on as another user"
^DIC(19,103,1,2,0)="and thus test out their menus.  It will assign all keys, but will not"
^DIC(19,103,1,3,0)="allow for the execution of any options."
^DIC(19,103,25)="TESTM^XUS91"
^DIC(19,103,"U")="SWITCH IDENTITIES"
^DIC(19,104,0)="XUPRROU^List Routines^^R^.5^^^^^^y^^^"
^DIC(19,104,1,0)="^^1^1^2880708^^^^"
^DIC(19,104,1,1,0)="This option uses the %ZTPP routine to print a listing of the routines."
^DIC(19,104,25)="%ZTPP"
^DIC(19,104,99)="55487,41333"
^DIC(19,104,99.1)="54829,39174"
^DIC(19,104,"U")="LIST ROUTINES"
^DIC(19,106,0)="XURELOG^Restart Session^^A^1039^^^^^^^^^1^^"
^DIC(19,106,1,0)="^^2^2^2880401^^^^"
^DIC(19,106,1,1,0)="This option allows the user to return to the sign-on logic so that"
^DIC(19,106,1,2,0)="a session can be restarted without dropping a telecommunication line."
^DIC(19,106,20)="S:'$D(XQCH) XQCH=""REST"" G:$L(XQCH)>2 REST^XQ12 S XQUR=""REST"" G XPRMP^XQ12"
^DIC(19,106,"U")="RESTART SESSION"
^DIC(19,107,0)="XUOPTWHO^Option Access By User^^R^11748^^121^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,107,1,0)="^^3^3^2880401^^^^"
^DIC(19,107,1,1,0)="This option prompts for a menu option, then prints of a list of which"
^DIC(19,107,1,2,0)="users can access this option. The list can be printed with or without"
^DIC(19,107,1,3,0)="the menu paths to the option."
^DIC(19,107,25)="XQ55"
^DIC(19,107,"U")="OPTION ACCESS BY USER"
