^DIC(19,503,1,2,0)="to see if the inconsistencies identified indeed still exist.  If not"
^DIC(19,503,1,3,0)="the entry will be deleted from the file.  This option should be run"
^DIC(19,503,1,4,0)="periodically to insure that any data cleaned up by means other than"
^DIC(19,503,1,5,0)="those options which call up the consistency checker, i.e., fileman,"
^DIC(19,503,1,6,0)="is removed from the file."
^DIC(19,503,25)="DGRPCU"
^DIC(19,503,200)="^^"
^DIC(19,503,"U")="UPDATE INCONSISTENCY FILE"
^DIC(19,504,0)="DG CONSISTENCY PATIENT^Edit Inconsistent Data for a Patient^^R^.5^^^^^^^114"
^DIC(19,504,1,0)="^^4^4^2901022^^^^"
^DIC(19,504,1,1,0)="This option is used to edit data for patients who have been identified"
^DIC(19,504,1,2,0)="as having missing/inconsistent data.  When you select a patient name"
^DIC(19,504,1,3,0)="you will be shown the data which is inconsistent and/or missing and"
^DIC(19,504,1,4,0)="afforded the opportunity to update this data."
^DIC(19,504,20)=""
^DIC(19,504,25)="PAT^DGRPC"
^DIC(19,504,"U")="EDIT INCONSISTENT DATA FOR A P"
^DIC(19,505,0)="DG CONSISTENCY PRINT^Inconsistent Data Elements Report^^R^.5^^^^^^^114"
^DIC(19,505,1,0)="9^^5^5^2930804^^^^"
^DIC(19,505,1,1,0)="This option is used to output a listing of patients for whom inconsistent"
^DIC(19,505,1,2,0)="and/or missing data elements have been identified.  User determines the"
^DIC(19,505,1,3,0)="method of output by selecting a range of dates in which the patient was"
^DIC(19,505,1,4,0)="either admitted, registered or identified as containing inconsistent data."
^DIC(19,505,1,5,0)="Output can be sorted by either patient name or terminal digits of the SSN."
^DIC(19,505,25)="DGRPCP"
^DIC(19,505,99)="55733,50538"
^DIC(19,505,"U")="INCONSISTENT DATA ELEMENTS REP"
