^DIC(19,1093,1,3,0)="Entering the ""*"" character for any entry will substitute the word"
^DIC(19,1093,1,4,0)="""canceled"" as the result."
^DIC(19,1093,25)="LRVER"
^DIC(19,1093,"U")="ENTER/VERIFY/MODIFY DATA (MANU"
^DIC(19,1094,0)="LRRS^Interim reports by location (manual queue)^^R^11720^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1094,1,0)="^^22^22^3171120^"
^DIC(19,1094,1,1,0)="Detailed report format of all verified results for specified collection"
^DIC(19,1094,1,2,0)="dates and ordering locations sorted by location. The report prints"
^DIC(19,1094,1,3,0)="according to the ordering location, not the patient's current location."
^DIC(19,1094,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1094,1,5,0)="Each patient's verified results for orders placed under the specified"
^DIC(19,1094,1,6,0)="location(s) as well as for orders placed under other locations on the"
^DIC(19,1094,1,7,0)="specified collection date(s) will print so as to provide complete"
^DIC(19,1094,1,8,0)="laboratory information on the patient. (Patients who do not have orders"
^DIC(19,1094,1,9,0)="placed under the specified location(s) will not be printed.) The date"
^DIC(19,1094,1,10,0)="chosen for this report is the collection date.  If a test is collected on"
^DIC(19,1094,1,11,0)="one day and verified on the next day, you must select the collection date."
^DIC(19,1094,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1094,1,13,0)="The report prints site codes for tests.  You will be asked if you would"
^DIC(19,1094,1,14,0)="like to print an address page.  The address page prints on a separate page"
^DIC(19,1094,1,15,0)="at the end of the report and lists the performing lab name, address and"
^DIC(19,1094,1,16,0)="site code."
^DIC(19,1094,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1094,1,18,0)="This option is an alternative to having the Interim report tasked.  For"
^DIC(19,1094,1,19,0)="tasking, see option LRTASK DAILY INTERIM 1. If no results are available"
^DIC(19,1094,1,20,0)="for a location, the option will print out the location heading followed by"
^DIC(19,1094,1,21,0)="the next location heading. This option is not part of the cumulative "
^DIC(19,1094,1,22,0)="report and should not be charted. "
^DIC(19,1094,25)="LRRS12"
^DIC(19,1094,"U")="INTERIM REPORTS BY LOCATION (M"
^DIC(19,1095,0)="LRDIST^Graph results^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1095,1,0)="^^9^9^2870203^^^"
^DIC(19,1095,1,1,0)="This function plots data in a highly generalized fashion.  If a specimen"
^DIC(19,1095,1,2,0)="is specified, normal ranges are displayed if available.  Furthermore,"
^DIC(19,1095,1,3,0)="one may choose to plot the data centered about the normal range or"
^DIC(19,1095,1,4,0)="centered about the mean of the data being plotted.  If plot according to"
^DIC(19,1095,1,5,0)="normal ranges is selected, then any values that differ from the mean"
^DIC(19,1095,1,6,0)="of the normal ranges by more than three standard deviations are plotted"
^DIC(19,1095,1,7,0)="in the extreme left or right column of the display, as the case may be."
^DIC(19,1095,1,8,0)="In addition to being plotted in the extreme left or right column, the"
^DIC(19,1095,1,9,0)="value is distinguished by a '*' rather than a 'X'."
^DIC(19,1095,25)="LRDIST"
^DIC(19,1095,"U")="GRAPH RESULTS"
^DIC(19,1096,0)="LROS^Order/test status^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1096,1,0)="^^4^4^2870203^^^^"
^DIC(19,1096,1,1,0)="After selecting a patient, for each day prompted, the status for all tests"
^DIC(19,1096,1,2,0)="for that day are given.  The report will output for a specified patient,"
^DIC(19,1096,1,3,0)="Order #, Urgency, Status (test complete, on collection list, collected),"
^DIC(19,1096,1,4,0)="Provider, and Accession #."
^DIC(19,1096,25)="LROS"
^DIC(19,1096,99)="54031,46684"
^DIC(19,1096,"U")="ORDER/TEST STATUS"
^DIC(19,1097,0)="LR SUP SUMMARY^Summary list (supervisors')^^R^.5^LRSUPER^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1097,1,0)="^^8^8^2870204^^^^"
^DIC(19,1097,1,1,0)="All results for a given accession area (or areas) for a given date"
^DIC(19,1097,1,2,0)="and range of accession numbers.  This report can serve as an 'audit trail'"
^DIC(19,1097,1,3,0)="for a specimen.  Includes information on person placing order, "
^DIC(19,1097,1,4,0)="person performing test, verifying person, and dates and times "
^DIC(19,1097,1,5,0)="of specimen collection and test completion.  The report can"
^DIC(19,1097,1,6,0)="be sorted by accession number or by patient, and can be printed in "
^DIC(19,1097,1,7,0)="a long form, which includes the above mentioned information"
^DIC(19,1097,1,8,0)="plus the test results."
^DIC(19,1097,25)="LRLIST"
^DIC(19,1097,99)="55476,50281"
^DIC(19,1097,"U")="SUMMARY LIST (SUPERVISORS')"
^DIC(19,1099,0)="LRGVP^Group data review (verified & EM)^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1099,1,0)="^^1^1^2870602^^^^"
^DIC(19,1099,1,1,0)="Batch form of LRENTER function, for print-out only; no editing."
^DIC(19,1099,25)="LRGVP"
^DIC(19,1099,"U")="GROUP DATA REVIEW (VERIFIED & "
^DIC(19,1100,0)="LRGEN^General report for selected tests^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1100,1,0)="^^8^8^2870316^^^^"
^DIC(19,1100,1,1,0)="This function displays data in a highly generalized fashion."
^DIC(19,1100,1,2,0)="All tests requested are displayed (up to 18 fields) in a cumulative format."
^DIC(19,1100,1,3,0)="If more than 18 tests are to be displayed, an alternate format is used."
^DIC(19,1100,1,4,0)="If a test has a special format (predefined in the 'Laboratory Test' file)"
^DIC(19,1100,1,5,0)="then that test must be requested separately."
^DIC(19,1100,1,6,0)="If a specimen is specified, normal ranges are displayed if available."
^DIC(19,1100,1,7,0)="Note that if a specimen is chosen for which there is no data,"
^DIC(19,1100,1,8,0)="no data will be displayed."
^DIC(19,1100,25)="LRGEN"
^DIC(19,1100,"U")="GENERAL REPORT FOR SELECTED TE"
^DIC(19,1101,0)="LRMI^Microbiology menu^^M^.5^LRMICRO^^^^^^26^^^1"
^DIC(19,1101,1,0)="^^1^1^2930315^^^^"
^DIC(19,1101,1,1,0)="Menu for microbiology"
