^DIC(19,1214,"U")="WARD LAB MENU"
^DIC(19,1215,0)="LRACS MANUAL^Supervisor's report^^R^.5^LRSUPER^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1215,1,0)="^^7^7^2870204^^^^"
^DIC(19,1215,1,1,0)="If the Tasked routine LRTASK ACS fails to generate its output, this function"
^DIC(19,1215,1,2,0)="may be used to re-initiate the printout.  This report is based on"
^DIC(19,1215,1,3,0)="the same formats and definitions in file 64.5.  The report is printed"
^DIC(19,1215,1,4,0)="within location by patient.  If a supervisor summary is desired by"
^DIC(19,1215,1,5,0)="accession, then use the option LR SUP SUMMARY.  LRACS MANUAL requires"
^DIC(19,1215,1,6,0)="that entries be made in the DAILY SUMMARY REPORTS fields of the "
^DIC(19,1215,1,7,0)="LAB REPORTS FILE (64.5) in order to work."
^DIC(19,1215,25)="MANUAL^LRACS"
^DIC(19,1215,"U")="SUPERVISOR'S REPORT"
^DIC(19,1216,0)="LRMICROLOGIN^Accessioning, standard (Microbiology)^^A^.5^^^^^^^26^^1"
^DIC(19,1216,1,0)="^^11^11^2870721^^^^"
^DIC(19,1216,1,1,0)="This option allows you to accession manually requested tests."
^DIC(19,1216,1,2,0)="It is especially useful for accessioning unusual specimens, or"
^DIC(19,1216,1,3,0)="accessioning specimens that require a descriptive comment.  You may also"
^DIC(19,1216,1,4,0)="comment about the order.  Any test or procedure may be accessioned, though"
^DIC(19,1216,1,5,0)="different lab sections may use lists of their most frequently ordered tests"
^DIC(19,1216,1,6,0)="to speed entry.  This option can also act as a batch entry log-in of a"
^DIC(19,1216,1,7,0)="specific test if you initially select that test."
^DIC(19,1216,1,8,0)="When you are asked to select the label printer, if you enter '^', labels"
^DIC(19,1216,1,9,0)="will not be printed.  You will then be asked to select a label printer"
^DIC(19,1216,1,10,0)="with each new patient you select.  When you select a printer, that printer"
^DIC(19,1216,1,11,0)="will be used until you terminate that session."
^DIC(19,1216,20)="S X=""MICROBIOLOGY"",DIC=""^LAB(62.6,"",DIC(0)="""" D ^DIC S LRFLOG=Y D ^LRORD"
^DIC(19,1216,"U")="ACCESSIONING, STANDARD (MICROB"
^DIC(19,1217,0)="LRMIACC1^Long form accession list for microbiology^^A^.5^^^^^^^26^^1"
^DIC(19,1217,1,0)="^^7^7^2870203^^^^"
^DIC(19,1217,1,1,0)="Same as Long form accession list, except it only displays the accession"
^DIC(19,1217,1,2,0)="areas associated with microbiology.  The list produces a complete"
^DIC(19,1217,1,3,0)="listing of accessions over a specified time period.  The user can"
^DIC(19,1217,1,4,0)="opt to print only specific tests and/or only uncompleted entries."
^DIC(19,1217,1,5,0)="The status of each test for an accession is also given.  The long"
^DIC(19,1217,1,6,0)="accession list can effectively replace log books in microbiology,"
^DIC(19,1217,1,7,0)="and provide a list of uncompleted cultures for review."
^DIC(19,1217,20)="S DIC(""S"")=""I $P(^(0),U,2)=""""MI"""""" D ^LRWRKLST K DIC"
^DIC(19,1217,"U")="LONG FORM ACCESSION LIST FOR M"
^DIC(19,1218,0)="LRMIBL^Batch accessioning^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1218,1,0)="^^8^8^2870722^^^"
^DIC(19,1218,1,1,0)="You may use this option to accession any patient specimen for any"
^DIC(19,1218,1,2,0)="test/procedure ordered.  However, you are limited to ordering only"
^DIC(19,1218,1,3,0)="one test per specimen.  Use this option to accession a large number "
^DIC(19,1218,1,4,0)="of identical specimens with the same test ordered.  Once you enter the"
^DIC(19,1218,1,5,0)="site/specimen and test name, you will not be asked for that information"
^DIC(19,1218,1,6,0)="again.  It is automatically assigned to each patient until you exit "
^DIC(19,1218,1,7,0)="the option.  The date and time are assumed to be NOW.  It is a very quick, "
^DIC(19,1218,1,8,0)="simple and efficient method for accessioning specimens into the laboratory. "
^DIC(19,1218,20)=""
^DIC(19,1218,25)="LRMIBL"
^DIC(19,1218,99.1)="54224,42789"
^DIC(19,1218,"U")="BATCH ACCESSIONING"
^DIC(19,1219,0)="LRVRW^Enter/verify data (Work list)^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1219,1,0)="^^6^6^2870203^^^^"
^DIC(19,1219,1,1,0)="Data from a worklist can be reviewed/edited individually by the"
^DIC(19,1219,1,2,0)="sequence defined on the worklist.  If the LRVERIFY key is owned,"
^DIC(19,1219,1,3,0)="the data may also be verified.  Once verified, the data are not"
^DIC(19,1219,1,4,0)="available for viewing with this option.  Likewise, if test results"
^DIC(19,1219,1,5,0)="have been previously verified for a given accession, even new data"
^DIC(19,1219,1,6,0)="can neither be viewed nor verified."
^DIC(19,1219,25)="LRVRW"
^DIC(19,1219,"U")="ENTER/VERIFY DATA (WORK LIST)"
^DIC(19,1220,0)="LRVRW2^Enter/verify data (Load list)^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1220,1,0)="^^6^6^2870203^^^"
^DIC(19,1220,1,1,0)="Data from a loadlist can be reviewed/edited individually by the"
^DIC(19,1220,1,2,0)="sequence defined on the loadlist.  If the LRVERIFY key is owned, the"
^DIC(19,1220,1,3,0)="data may also be verified.  Once verified, the data are not available"
^DIC(19,1220,1,4,0)="for viewing with this option.  Likewise, if test results have been"
^DIC(19,1220,1,5,0)="previously verified for a given accession, even new data can neither"
^DIC(19,1220,1,6,0)="be viewed nor verified."
^DIC(19,1220,25)="LRVRW"
^DIC(19,1220,"U")="ENTER/VERIFY DATA (LOAD LIST)"
^DIC(19,1222,0)="LRLL NEW 1ST SEQUENCE #^Set new ""starting sequence number""^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1222,1,0)="^^4^4^2870204^^^"
^DIC(19,1222,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to reset the first sequence number in"
^DIC(19,1222,1,2,0)="the data an automated instrument transmits.  This option can only be used"
^DIC(19,1222,1,3,0)="if the instrument is set up to transmit and identify data strictly"
^DIC(19,1222,1,4,0)="by the order the data comes off the machine."
^DIC(19,1222,25)="NWSEQNM^LRLLS3"
^DIC(19,1222,"U")="SET NEW ""STARTING SEQUENCE NUM"
^DIC(19,1223,0)="LRRS BY LOC^Interim reports for 1 location (manual queue)^^R^11720^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1223,1,0)="^^18^18^3171120^"
^DIC(19,1223,1,1,0)="This option reports all verified results from one ordering location for"
^DIC(19,1223,1,2,0)="one collection date. The report prints according to the ordering location,"
^DIC(19,1223,1,3,0)="not the patient's current location. The user will request the collection"
^DIC(19,1223,1,4,0)="date and ordering location. "
^DIC(19,1223,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1223,1,6,0)="Each patient's verified results for orders placed under the specified"
^DIC(19,1223,1,7,0)="location as well as for orders placed under other locations on the"
^DIC(19,1223,1,8,0)="specified collection date will print so as to provide complete laboratory"
^DIC(19,1223,1,9,0)="information on the patient. (Patients who do not have orders placed under"
^DIC(19,1223,1,10,0)="the selected ordering locations will not be printed.) If a test is"
^DIC(19,1223,1,11,0)="collected on one day and verified on the next day, you must select the"
^DIC(19,1223,1,12,0)="collection date. "
^DIC(19,1223,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1223,1,14,0)="This option is to be used for information only and should not be charted."
^DIC(19,1223,1,15,0)="The report prints site codes for tests.  You will be asked if you would"
^DIC(19,1223,1,16,0)="like to print an address page.  The address page prints on a separate page"
^DIC(19,1223,1,17,0)="at the end of the report and lists the performing lab name, address and"
^DIC(19,1223,1,18,0)="site code."
^DIC(19,1223,15)=""
^DIC(19,1223,20)=""
^DIC(19,1223,25)="SINGLE^LRRS"
^DIC(19,1223,"U")="INTERIM REPORTS FOR 1 LOCATION"
^DIC(19,1224,0)="LRRP2^Interim report ^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,1224,1,0)="^19.06^9^9^3021031^^^^"
^DIC(19,1224,1,1,0)="This option will print or display interim reports for a selected"
^DIC(19,1224,1,2,0)="patient, within a given time period.  The printout will go in inverse"
^DIC(19,1224,1,3,0)="date order.  This report will output all tests for the time period"
^DIC(19,1224,1,4,0)="specified.  If no results are available, the option will ask for"
^DIC(19,1224,1,5,0)="another patient.  This option will only print verified results."
^DIC(19,1224,1,6,0)="The report prints site codes for tests.  You will be asked if you would"
^DIC(19,1224,1,7,0)="like to print an address page.  The address page prints on a separate page(s)"
^DIC(19,1224,1,8,0)="at the end of the report and lists the performing lab name, address and site"
^DIC(19,1224,1,9,0)="code."
^DIC(19,1224,15)=""
^DIC(19,1224,20)=""
^DIC(19,1224,25)="LRRP2"
^DIC(19,1224,99.1)="59063,46726"
^DIC(19,1224,"U")="INTERIM REPORT "
