^DIC(19,1583,"U")="UTILITY FILES MAINTENANCE MENU"
^DIC(19,1584,0)="RA MAJORAMIS^Major AMIS Code Entry/Edit^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1584,1,0)="^^8^8^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1584,1,1,0)="This function allows the coordinator to add new AMIS"
^DIC(19,1584,1,2,0)="codes and edit existing AMIS codes."
^DIC(19,1584,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1584,1,4,0)="When the system is first installed, all necessary entries and"
^DIC(19,1584,1,5,0)="data associated with each entry will be part of the module."
^DIC(19,1584,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1584,1,7,0)="This function should only be used if the AMIS weights are changed"
^DIC(19,1584,1,8,0)="by VACO or if new codes are added by VACO."
^DIC(19,1584,25)="3^RAMAIN"
^DIC(19,1584,"U")="MAJOR AMIS CODE ENTRY/EDIT"
^DIC(19,1585,0)="RA DIAGEDIT^Diagnostic Code Enter/Edit^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1585,1,0)="^^25^25^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1585,1,1,0)="This function allows the coordinator to enter/edit"
^DIC(19,1585,1,2,0)="report diagnostic codes.  These diagnostic codes are entered along"
^DIC(19,1585,1,3,0)="with the interpreting resident and/or staff to indicate an overall"
^DIC(19,1585,1,4,0)="impression stated in the report."
^DIC(19,1585,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1585,1,6,0)="The following is the list of 'diagnostic codes' that are loaded"
^DIC(19,1585,1,7,0)="as part of the initialization process:"
^DIC(19,1585,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1585,1,9,0)="       1) Normal"
^DIC(19,1585,1,10,0)="       2) Minor Abnormality"
^DIC(19,1585,1,11,0)="       3) Major Abnormality, No Attn. Needed"
^DIC(19,1585,1,12,0)="       4) Abnormality, Attn. Needed"
^DIC(19,1585,1,13,0)="       5) Major Abnormality, Physician Aware"
^DIC(19,1585,1,14,0)="       6) Undictated Films Not Returned, 3 Days"
^DIC(19,1585,1,15,0)="       7) Unsatisfactory/Incomplete Exam"
^DIC(19,1585,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1585,1,17,0)="As part of the initialization process, these entries can be deleted."
^DIC(19,1585,1,18,0)="However, once the system is in production, you should not delete any"
^DIC(19,1585,1,19,0)="entries.  The names of entries should also not be changed, once in"
^DIC(19,1585,1,20,0)="production, as this could affect their meaning."
^DIC(19,1585,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1585,1,22,0)="If the site decides to enter a diagnostic code for exams, then"
^DIC(19,1585,1,23,0)="database searches using VA FileMan can be performed using the 'Diagnostic"
^DIC(19,1585,1,24,0)="Code' field of the exam record in the search criteria.  For example,"
^DIC(19,1585,1,25,0)="the database can be searched for all 'Normal' 'CHEST PA&LAT' procedures."
^DIC(19,1585,25)="5^RAMAIN"
^DIC(19,1585,"U")="DIAGNOSTIC CODE ENTER/EDIT"
^DIC(19,1586,0)="RA COMPEDIT^Complication Type Entry/Edit^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1586,1,0)="^^20^20^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1586,1,1,0)="This function allows the coordinator to enter/edit"
^DIC(19,1586,1,2,0)="complication types that may be associated with an exam.  The"
^DIC(19,1586,1,3,0)="user can indicate an exam and a specific complication using the"
^DIC(19,1586,1,4,0)="'Case Number Edit' option."
^DIC(19,1586,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1586,1,6,0)="The most commonly used complication type is a contrast material"
^DIC(19,1586,1,7,0)="reaction complication.  In the case of this complication, the"
^DIC(19,1586,1,8,0)="patient's record in the Allergy Tracking System"
^DIC(19,1586,1,9,0)="will be automatically updated to indicate"
^DIC(19,1586,1,10,0)="the patient has had a contrast material reaction.  As a result,"
^DIC(19,1586,1,11,0)="everytime the patient is registered for a procedure that may involve"
^DIC(19,1586,1,12,0)="contrast material, the receptionist will be warned and he/she should"
^DIC(19,1586,1,13,0)="then take the appropriate action."
^DIC(19,1586,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1586,1,15,0)="When the system is initialized, two complications are loaded into"
^DIC(19,1586,1,16,0)="the module.  They are 'Contrast Material Reaction' and 'No Complication'."
^DIC(19,1586,1,17,0)="Other site specific entries can be added using this function."
^DIC(19,1586,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1586,1,19,0)="Finally, this field can be specified in criteria used when searching"
^DIC(19,1586,1,20,0)="the database using VA FileMan."
^DIC(19,1586,25)="7^RAMAIN"
^DIC(19,1586,"U")="COMPLICATION TYPE ENTRY/EDIT"
^DIC(19,1587,0)="RA FLASHFORM^Label/Header/Footer Formatter^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1587,1,0)="^^23^23^2940609^"
^DIC(19,1587,1,1,0)="This function allows the coordinator to design site"
^DIC(19,1587,1,2,0)="specific formats for the following:"
^DIC(19,1587,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1587,1,4,0)="      1) Flash Cards"
^DIC(19,1587,1,5,0)="      2) Exam Labels"
^DIC(19,1587,1,6,0)="      3) Jacket Labels"
^DIC(19,1587,1,7,0)="      4) Report Headers"
^DIC(19,1587,1,8,0)="      5) Report Footers"
^DIC(19,1587,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1587,1,10,0)="After a format has been entered or edited, the system will display"
^DIC(19,1587,1,11,0)="a test version of the format."
^DIC(19,1587,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1587,1,13,0)="The 'Imaging Locations' file uses this file to obtain the format"
^DIC(19,1587,1,14,0)="specifications for the following location parameters:"
^DIC(19,1587,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1587,1,16,0)="      1) Default Flash Card Format"
^DIC(19,1587,1,17,0)="      2) Default Exam Label Format"
^DIC(19,1587,1,18,0)="      3) Default Jacket Label Format"
^DIC(19,1587,1,19,0)="      4) Default Report Header Format"
^DIC(19,1587,1,20,0)="      5) Default Report Footer Format"
^DIC(19,1587,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1587,1,22,0)="  These parameters are set using the 'Location Parameter Set-Up'"
^DIC(19,1587,1,23,0)="function."
^DIC(19,1587,25)="6^RAMAIN"
^DIC(19,1587,"U")="LABEL/HEADER/FOOTER FORMATTER"
^DIC(19,1588,0)="RA PNL^Rad/Nuc Med Personnel Menu^^M^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1588,1,0)="^^14^14^2940607^^^^"
^DIC(19,1588,1,1,0)="This menu allows the coordinator to enter new department"
^DIC(19,1588,1,2,0)="personnel into the system."
^DIC(19,1588,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1588,1,4,0)="There are currently four classifications the personnel can be"
^DIC(19,1588,1,5,0)="placed under.  They are the following:"
^DIC(19,1588,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1588,1,7,0)="      1) Technologist"
^DIC(19,1588,1,8,0)="      2) Interpreting Resident"
^DIC(19,1588,1,9,0)="      3) Interpreting Staff"
^DIC(19,1588,1,10,0)="      4) Clerk"
^DIC(19,1588,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1588,1,12,0)="The entries in this file are used as allowable choices by the"
^DIC(19,1588,1,13,0)="system when the user enters the corresponding information about"
^DIC(19,1588,1,14,0)="an exam."
^DIC(19,1588,10,0)="^19.01PI^7^5"
^DIC(19,1588,10,3,0)="1578^"
^DIC(19,1588,10,4,0)="1589^"
^DIC(19,1588,10,5,0)="1590^"
^DIC(19,1588,10,6,0)="1591^"
^DIC(19,1588,10,7,0)="6301^"
^DIC(19,1588,10,"B",1578,3)=""
^DIC(19,1588,10,"B",1589,4)=""
^DIC(19,1588,10,"B",1590,5)=""
^DIC(19,1588,10,"B",1591,6)=""
^DIC(19,1588,10,"B",6301,7)=""
^DIC(19,1588,15)=""
^DIC(19,1588,20)=""
^DIC(19,1588,99)="59924,36533"
^DIC(19,1588,"U")="RAD/NUC MED PERSONNEL MENU"
^DIC(19,1589,0)="RA PNLTECH^Technologist List^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1589,1,0)="^^2^2^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1589,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to obtain a list of technologists"
^DIC(19,1589,1,2,0)="as specified by the 'Personnel Menu'."
^DIC(19,1589,25)="2^RAPNL"
^DIC(19,1589,"U")="TECHNOLOGIST LIST"
^DIC(19,1590,0)="RA PNLRES^Interpreting Resident List^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1590,1,0)="^^2^2^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1590,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to obtain a list of the interpreting"
^DIC(19,1590,1,2,0)="residents as specified by the 'Personnel Menu'."
^DIC(19,1590,25)="3^RAPNL"
^DIC(19,1590,"U")="INTERPRETING RESIDENT LIST"
^DIC(19,1591,0)="RA PNLSTAFF^Interpreting Staff List^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1591,1,0)="^^2^2^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1591,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to obtain a list of the interpreting staff"
^DIC(19,1591,1,2,0)="as specified by the 'Personnel Menu'."
^DIC(19,1591,25)="4^RAPNL"
^DIC(19,1591,"U")="INTERPRETING STAFF LIST"
^DIC(19,1592,0)="RA SYSLOC^Location Parameter Set-up^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1592,1,0)="^^15^15^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1592,1,1,0)="The 'Location Parameter Set-Up' function allows the"
^DIC(19,1592,1,2,0)="coordinator to define location parameters."
^DIC(19,1592,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1592,1,4,0)="Within a specific division, there may be a number of physical"
^DIC(19,1592,1,5,0)="locations where a procedure can be performed.  For"
^DIC(19,1592,1,6,0)="example, a division may have its own main department on"
^DIC(19,1592,1,7,0)="the second floor and  a satellite location on the"
^DIC(19,1592,1,8,0)="first floor at an outpatient clinic area."
^DIC(19,1592,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1592,1,10,0)="The module is designed to handle multiple locations within a"
^DIC(19,1592,1,11,0)="division.  Each location will have its own set of parameters"
^DIC(19,1592,1,12,0)="defining such location-specific criteria as printer devices for"
^DIC(19,1592,1,13,0)="flash cards and jacket labels."
^DIC(19,1592,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1592,1,15,0)="A location may only be associated with one division."
^DIC(19,1592,25)="3^RASYS"
^DIC(19,1592,"U")="LOCATION PARAMETER SET-UP"
^DIC(19,1593,0)="RA FAILSOFT^Failsoft Parameters^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1593,1,0)="^^3^3^2950817^"
^DIC(19,1593,1,1,0)="    This function allows IRM to specify location parameters concerning"
^DIC(19,1593,1,2,0)="operating conditions.  The operating conditions are either 'NORMAL' or"
^DIC(19,1593,1,3,0)="'EMERGENCY'."
^DIC(19,1593,25)="3^RASITE"
^DIC(19,1593,"U")="FAILSOFT PARAMETERS"
^DIC(19,1595,0)="RA SYSDIVLIST^Print Division Parameter List^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1595,1,0)="^^2^2^2881230^^^"
^DIC(19,1595,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to obtain a list of division parameters"
^DIC(19,1595,1,2,0)="as specified by the 'Division Parameter Set-Up' function."
^DIC(19,1595,25)="2^RASYS"
^DIC(19,1595,"U")="PRINT DIVISION PARAMETER LIST"
^DIC(19,1596,0)="RA SYSLOCLIST^Location Parameter List^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1596,1,0)="^^2^2^2940606^^^^"
^DIC(19,1596,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to obtain a list of the location"
^DIC(19,1596,1,2,0)="parameters as specified by the 'Location Parameter Set-Up' function."
^DIC(19,1596,25)="4^RASYS"
^DIC(19,1596,"U")="LOCATION PARAMETER LIST"
^DIC(19,1597,0)="RA SYSDEF^System Definition Menu^^M^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1597,1,0)="^^3^3^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1597,1,1,0)="The 'System Definition Menu' provides the coordinator"
^DIC(19,1597,1,2,0)="with functions that allow for the initialization and maintenance of"
^DIC(19,1597,1,3,0)="the division, location, and camera/equip/rm files."
^DIC(19,1597,10,0)="^19.01PI^9^9"
^DIC(19,1597,10,1,0)="1577^"
^DIC(19,1597,10,2,0)="1595^"
^DIC(19,1597,10,3,0)="1592^"
^DIC(19,1597,10,4,0)="1596^"
^DIC(19,1597,10,6,0)="1619^"
^DIC(19,1597,10,7,0)="1638^"
^DIC(19,1597,10,8,0)=14917
^DIC(19,1597,10,9,0)=15004
^DIC(19,1597,10,"B",1577,1)=""
^DIC(19,1597,10,"B",1592,3)=""
^DIC(19,1597,10,"B",1595,2)=""
^DIC(19,1597,10,"B",1596,4)=""
^DIC(19,1597,10,"B",1619,6)=""
^DIC(19,1597,10,"B",1638,7)=""
^DIC(19,1597,10,"B",14917,8)=""
^DIC(19,1597,10,"B",15004,9)=""
^DIC(19,1597,99)="66284,84297"
^DIC(19,1597,"U")="SYSTEM DEFINITION MENU"
^DIC(19,1598,0)="RA SHARING^Sharing Agreement/Contract Entry/Edit^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1598,1,0)="^^5^5^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1598,1,1,0)="This function allows the coordinator to enter new sharing"
^DIC(19,1598,1,2,0)="agreements/contracts into the system and edit existing ones."
^DIC(19,1598,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1598,1,4,0)="A patient whose category of exam is 'Contract' or 'Sharing', must"
^DIC(19,1598,1,5,0)="have an entry from this file associated with the exam."
^DIC(19,1598,25)="8^RAMAIN"
^DIC(19,1598,"U")="SHARING AGREEMENT/CONTRACT ENT"
^DIC(19,1599,0)="RA ADDEXAM^Add Exams to Last Visit^^R^11712^^^^^^^^^1^1"
^DIC(19,1599,1,0)="^^4^4^2940606^^^^"
^DIC(19,1599,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to add exams to a patient's last"
^DIC(19,1599,1,2,0)="visit. It is used in conjunction with the 'Register Patient for"
^DIC(19,1599,1,3,0)="Exams' function.  The user is allowed to add exams to the last visit,"
^DIC(19,1599,1,4,0)="only if the visit was on the current or previous day."
^DIC(19,1599,15)="K RAVSTFLG,RAOPT(""ADDEXAM"")"
^DIC(19,1599,20)="S RAOPT(""ADDEXAM"")="""""
^DIC(19,1599,25)="ADD^RAREG"
^DIC(19,1599,"U")="ADD EXAMS TO LAST VISIT"
^DIC(19,1600,0)="RA EDITCN^Case No. Exam Edit^^R^11712^^^^^^^^^1^1"
^DIC(19,1600,1,0)="^^12^12^2960411^"
^DIC(19,1600,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to edit exams for patients by selecting"
^DIC(19,1600,1,2,0)="either the case number or the patient's name.  If the case number doesn't"
^DIC(19,1600,1,3,0)="exist or is inactive, the system will indicate so with an error message."
^DIC(19,1600,1,4,0)="This function should be used to re-edit fields that have already been"
^DIC(19,1600,1,5,0)="entered but need to be corrected. Only fields where data has previously"
^DIC(19,1600,1,6,0)="been entered will appear for re-edit.  The Status Tracking options should"
^DIC(19,1600,1,7,0)="be used to enter data and insure that exams progress to a status of"
^DIC(19,1600,1,8,0)="'Complete'."
^DIC(19,1600,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1600,1,10,0)="Once an exam is edited and in the 'COMPLETE' status, the associated"
^DIC(19,1600,1,11,0)="request will display a message as follows: ""** Note: Request has been"
^DIC(19,1600,1,12,0)="changed by Radiology/Nuclear Medicine**""."
^DIC(19,1600,15)="K RAOPT(""EDITCN"")"
^DIC(19,1600,20)="S RAOPT(""EDITCN"")="""""
^DIC(19,1600,25)="EDIT^RAEDCN"
^DIC(19,1600,99.1)="57013,51400"
^DIC(19,1600,"U")="CASE NO. EXAM EDIT"
^DIC(19,1601,0)="RA DIAGCN^Diagnostic Code and Interpreter Edit by Case No.^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1601,1,0)="^^4^4^2940603^"
^DIC(19,1601,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to enter a diagnostic code and the"
^DIC(19,1601,1,2,0)="interpreting resident and staff physicians for any case number.  If this"
^DIC(19,1601,1,3,0)="information has already been entered, then this function allows the user"
^DIC(19,1601,1,4,0)="to review and update the information."
^DIC(19,1601,25)="DIAG^RAEDCN"
^DIC(19,1601,"U")="DIAGNOSTIC CODE AND INTERPRETE"
^DIC(19,1602,0)="RA OUTADD^Add Films to Registry^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1602,1,0)="^^2^2^2881230^^"
^DIC(19,1602,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to add new films to the existing"
^DIC(19,1602,1,2,0)="outside films registry."
^DIC(19,1602,25)="1^RAOUT"
^DIC(19,1602,"U")="ADD FILMS TO REGISTRY"
^DIC(19,1603,0)="RA OUTEDIT^Edit Registry^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1603,1,0)="^^3^3^2881230^^^"
^DIC(19,1603,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to edit information pertaining to"
^DIC(19,1603,1,2,0)="a specific outside film that has been registered.  This is how the"
^DIC(19,1603,1,3,0)="user can indicate that films have been returned."
^DIC(19,1603,25)="2^RAOUT"
^DIC(19,1603,"U")="EDIT REGISTRY"
^DIC(19,1604,0)="RA OUTFLAG^Flag Film To Need 'OK' Before Return^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1604,1,0)="^^10^10^2881230^^"
^DIC(19,1604,1,1,0)="This function allows the supervisor to designate specific "
^DIC(19,1604,1,2,0)="outside films as needing his/her return approval before the films "
^DIC(19,1604,1,3,0)="can be sent back to their source."
^DIC(19,1604,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(19,1604,1,5,0)="Many times it is desired to keep certain films on file for reference"
^DIC(19,1604,1,6,0)="while the patient is still an 'inpatient'."
^DIC(19,1604,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(19,1604,1,8,0)="If an entry is flagged as needing an 'ok' before return, then the"
^DIC(19,1604,1,9,0)="user will be asked  whether it"
^DIC(19,1604,1,10,0)="has been approved or not."
^DIC(19,1604,25)="3^RAOUT"
^DIC(19,1604,"U")="FLAG FILM TO NEED 'OK' BEFORE "
^DIC(19,1609,0)="RA PROFSORT^Exam Profile (selected sort)^^R^11740^^^^^^^^^1^1"
^DIC(19,1609,1,0)="^19.06^8^8^3000615^^^^"
^DIC(19,1609,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to list a patient's exam profile."
^DIC(19,1609,1,2,0)="The profile can be sorted by either exam procedure, exam status,"
^DIC(19,1609,1,3,0)="or exam date order."
^DIC(19,1609,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(19,1609,1,5,0)="If the user selects a specific exam, the module switches control"
^DIC(19,1609,1,6,0)="to the 'View Exam by Case No.' function, which will display"
^DIC(19,1609,1,7,0)="very detailed information about the exam, such as the requesting"
^DIC(19,1609,1,8,0)="physician and the technologist who performed the exam."
^DIC(19,1609,15)="K RATECHCO"
^DIC(19,1609,20)="S RATECHCO="""""
^DIC(19,1609,25)="RAPROS"
^DIC(19,1609,"U")="EXAM PROFILE (SELECTED SORT)"
^DIC(19,1610,0)="RA VIEWCN^View Exam by Case No.^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^^^1^1"
^DIC(19,1610,1,0)="^^3^3^2940606^^^^"
^DIC(19,1610,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to examine a case by viewing all "
^DIC(19,1610,1,2,0)="the vital information about the case.  This function also displays"
^DIC(19,1610,1,3,0)="an activity log, status tracking log, and exam report text."
^DIC(19,1610,15)="K RANOSCRN"
^DIC(19,1610,20)="S RANOSCRN="""""
^DIC(19,1610,25)="VIEW^RAEDCN1"
^DIC(19,1610,99)="56384,29759"
^DIC(19,1610,99.1)="58531,48797"
^DIC(19,1610,"U")="VIEW EXAM BY CASE NO."
^DIC(19,1613,0)="RA OUTPROF^Outside Films Profile^^R^11712^^^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1613,1,0)="^^4^4^2881230^^^"
^DIC(19,1613,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to see if films from other "
^DIC(19,1613,1,2,0)="hospitals or institutions have been registered for this patient."
^DIC(19,1613,1,3,0)="Both returned and unreturned films are listed in the profile. "
^DIC(19,1613,1,4,0)="If they have been returned, then the 'Date Returned' is given."
^DIC(19,1613,15)=""
^DIC(19,1613,20)=""
^DIC(19,1613,25)="5^RAOUT"
^DIC(19,1613,"U")="OUTSIDE FILMS PROFILE"
^DIC(19,1614,0)="RA RPTENTRY^Report Entry/Edit^^R^11712^^^^^^^^^1^1"
^DIC(19,1614,1,0)="^^8^8^2940613^^^"
^DIC(19,1614,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to enter and edit reports for registered"
^DIC(19,1614,1,2,0)="exams. These reports are first dictated by the interpreting physician"
^DIC(19,1614,1,3,0)="before the user accesses this function to enter the report into the"
^DIC(19,1614,1,4,0)="system."
^DIC(19,1614,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1614,1,6,0)="Once the report has been verified, the report is available to all"
^DIC(19,1614,1,7,0)="appropriate users of the computer system, i.e. ward clerks, nurses,"
^DIC(19,1614,1,8,0)="and physicians."
^DIC(19,1614,15)="K RANOSCRN,^TMP($J,""RA D-TYPE""),^TMP($J,""RA I-TYPE"")"
^DIC(19,1614,20)="S RANOSCRN="""""
^DIC(19,1614,25)="RARTE"
^DIC(19,1614,99.1)="63608,44125"
^DIC(19,1614,"U")="REPORT ENTRY/EDIT"
^DIC(19,1615,0)="RA EXAMSTATUS^Examination Status Entry/Edit^^R^11712^^^^^^y^^^^"
^DIC(19,1615,1,0)="^^10^10^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1615,1,1,0)="  This function allows the coordinator the option to perform"
^DIC(19,1615,1,2,0)="  the following:"
^DIC(19,1615,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1615,1,4,0)="      1) Add new examination statuses"
^DIC(19,1615,1,5,0)="      2) Edit existing examination statuses"
^DIC(19,1615,1,6,0)="      3) Modify requirement criteria for each status"
^DIC(19,1615,1,7,0)="      4) Modify which prompts appear when using the 'Status Tracking"
^DIC(19,1615,1,8,0)="         of Exams' function"
^DIC(19,1615,1,9,0)="      5) Indicate by status, which exams in each status to use"
^DIC(19,1615,1,10,0)="         in the compilations of the various workload reports"
^DIC(19,1615,15)=""
^DIC(19,1615,20)=""
^DIC(19,1615,25)="1^RAMAIN1"
^DIC(19,1615,"U")="EXAMINATION STATUS ENTRY/EDIT"
^DIC(19,1616,0)="RA DELETEXAM^Exam Deletion^^R^10000000020^RA DELETEXAM^^^^^^^^1^1"
^DIC(19,1616,1,0)="^^16^16^2990624^^"
^DIC(19,1616,1,1,0)="This function allows the coordinator to delete exams from"
^DIC(19,1616,1,2,0)="the system. This function should only be used by the"
^DIC(19,1616,1,3,0)="coordinator."
^DIC(19,1616,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1616,1,5,0)="When this function is executed, a bulletin is sent to members of the"
^DIC(19,1616,1,6,0)="appropriate mail group to notify them of the exam deletion."
^DIC(19,1616,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1616,1,8,0)="Deletion of an exam is prohibited if the exam has an associated"
^DIC(19,1616,1,9,0)="report.  The report must be deleted first before the exam can be"
^DIC(19,1616,1,10,0)="deleted."
^DIC(19,1616,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1616,1,12,0)="Once the examination is 'DELETED', the user will be prompted to"
^DIC(19,1616,1,13,0)="answer with a 'YES'or 'NO' to cancel the request associated with"
^DIC(19,1616,1,14,0)="this exam. If 'YES', the request will also be cancelled and the request"
^DIC(19,1616,1,15,0)="status updated to 'CANCELLED'. If 'NO', the request status will be"
^DIC(19,1616,1,16,0)="updated to 'HOLD' and may be selected for registration at a future date."
^DIC(19,1616,15)="K RANOSCRN,RAOPT(""DELETEXAM"")"
^DIC(19,1616,20)="S RANOSCRN="""",RAOPT(""DELETEXAM"")="""""
^DIC(19,1616,25)="DEL^RAEDCN1"
^DIC(19,1616,99)="56384,33979"
^DIC(19,1616,"U")="EXAM DELETION"
^DIC(19,1617,0)="RA DELINQUENT^Delinquent Status Report^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1617,1,0)="^^4^4^2940606^^"
^DIC(19,1617,1,1,0)="This option allows the supervisor to generate a listing of"
^DIC(19,1617,1,2,0)="examination reports with a status considered delinquent. The only statuses"
^DIC(19,1617,1,3,0)="considered to be delinquent are those designated through the 'Exam Status"
^DIC(19,1617,1,4,0)="Entry/Edit' option."
^DIC(19,1617,25)="RADLQ1"
^DIC(19,1617,"U")="DELINQUENT STATUS REPORT"
^DIC(19,1618,0)="RA LABELTEST^Test Label Printer^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1618,1,0)="^^1^1^2940606^^^^"
^DIC(19,1618,1,1,0)="This function allows the user to test a label printer."
^DIC(19,1618,25)="TEST^RAFLH1"
^DIC(19,1618,"U")="TEST LABEL PRINTER"
^DIC(19,1619,0)="RA SYSEXROOM^Camera/Equip/Rm Entry/Edit^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1619,1,0)="^^14^14^2940606^"
^DIC(19,1619,1,1,0)="The 'Camera/Equip/Rm Enter/Edit' function allows the coordinator to enter"
^DIC(19,1619,1,2,0)="new cameras/equipment/rooms into the system or edit the descriptions and"
^DIC(19,1619,1,3,0)="locations of existing cameras/equip/rms.  These cameras/equip/rms can then"
^DIC(19,1619,1,4,0)="be associated with a location.  Also, unlike the relationship between"
^DIC(19,1619,1,5,0)="divisions and locations, cameras/equip/rms can be associated with more"
^DIC(19,1619,1,6,0)="than one location."
^DIC(19,1619,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1619,1,8,0)="The entries in this file are used by the technologist when he/she"
^DIC(19,1619,1,9,0)="indicates with which camera/equip/rm the exam was performed.  Only"
^DIC(19,1619,1,10,0)="cameras/equipment/rooms associated with the location where the exam was"
^DIC(19,1619,1,11,0)="performed are valid choices."
^DIC(19,1619,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1619,1,13,0)="Use the 'Location Parameter Set-Up' option to associate a camera/equip/rm"
^DIC(19,1619,1,14,0)="with a location."
^DIC(19,1619,25)="5^RASYS"
^DIC(19,1619,"U")="CAMERA/EQUIP/RM ENTRY/EDIT"
^DIC(19,1620,0)="RA DELETERPT^Delete a Report^^R^1^RA RPTMGR^^^^^^^^1^1"
^DIC(19,1620,1,0)="^19.06^7^7^3210629^^^"
^DIC(19,1620,1,1,0)="This option allows the coordinator to delete a report.  This option "
^DIC(19,1620,1,2,0)="should only be used by the coordinator.  When a report is deleted, it"
^DIC(19,1620,1,3,0)="causes a bulletin about the deleted report to be sent to the members of"
^DIC(19,1620,1,4,0)="the appropriate mail group."
^DIC(19,1620,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1620,1,6,0)="To view a list of deleted reports, use the 'Restore a Deleted Report' "
^DIC(19,1620,1,7,0)="option and enter ""??"" at the ""Select Deleted Report to restore:"" prompt."
^DIC(19,1620,15)="K RADELRPT"
^DIC(19,1620,20)="S RADELRPT="""""
^DIC(19,1620,25)="DEL^RARTE1"
^DIC(19,1620,"U")="DELETE A REPORT"
^DIC(19,1621,0)="RA WKL^Personnel Workload Reports^^M^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1621,1,0)="^^6^6^2970805^^^"
^DIC(19,1621,1,1,0)="This menu provides the supervisor with the necessary options"
^DIC(19,1621,1,2,0)="to obtain workload reports for the following personnel:"
^DIC(19,1621,1,3,0)="                     1) Requesting Physician"
^DIC(19,1621,1,4,0)="                     2) Interpreting Resident Physician"
^DIC(19,1621,1,5,0)="                     3) Interpreting Staff Physician"
^DIC(19,1621,1,6,0)="                     4) Technologist"
^DIC(19,1621,10,0)="^19.01PI^13^9"
^DIC(19,1621,10,1,0)="1622^"
^DIC(19,1621,10,3,0)="1623^"
^DIC(19,1621,10,5,0)="1624^"
^DIC(19,1621,10,7,0)="1625^"
^DIC(19,1621,10,8,0)="6292^"
^DIC(19,1621,10,9,0)=10774
^DIC(19,1621,10,10,0)=13281
^DIC(19,1621,10,12,0)=13283
^DIC(19,1621,10,13,0)=13285
^DIC(19,1621,10,"B",1622,1)=""
^DIC(19,1621,10,"B",1623,3)=""
^DIC(19,1621,10,"B",1624,5)=""
^DIC(19,1621,10,"B",1625,7)=""
^DIC(19,1621,10,"B",6292,8)=""
^DIC(19,1621,10,"B",10774,9)=""
^DIC(19,1621,10,"B",13281,10)=""
^DIC(19,1621,10,"B",13283,12)=""
^DIC(19,1621,10,"B",13285,13)=""
^DIC(19,1621,99)="65157,59497"
^DIC(19,1621,"U")="PERSONNEL WORKLOAD REPORTS"
^DIC(19,1622,0)="RA WKLTECH^Technologist Report^^R^11712^^^^^^y^"
^DIC(19,1622,1,0)="^^14^14^2940803^^"
^DIC(19,1622,1,1,0)="This option allows the supervisor to generate a report of workloads for"
^DIC(19,1622,1,2,0)="technologists. If the supervisor has access to more than one division or"
^DIC(19,1622,1,3,0)="imaging type, s/he is prompted to select the divisions and imaging"
^DIC(19,1622,1,4,0)="types to include in the report. The supervisor is prompted to select"
^DIC(19,1622,1,5,0)="the technologists to include in the report. The supervisor may select one,"
^DIC(19,1622,1,6,0)="many or all technologists. The supervisor is prompted to enter a date"
^DIC(19,1622,1,7,0)="range for the exams to be included in the report. The exam status values"
^DIC(19,1622,1,8,0)="that will be included in the report will be displayed by imaging type."
^DIC(19,1622,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1622,1,10,0)="The report contains the following information: procedure, number of"
^DIC(19,1622,1,11,0)="examinations, weighted work units, and percent of total weighted work"
^DIC(19,1622,1,12,0)="units.  A 'summary' report groups all examinations together by"
^DIC(19,1622,1,13,0)="technologist for each imaging type and division. A 'detailed' report gives"
^DIC(19,1622,1,14,0)="information for each individiual procedure performed by each technologist."
^DIC(19,1622,25)="TECH^RAWKL"
^DIC(19,1622,99)="56105,32129"
^DIC(19,1622,"U")="TECHNOLOGIST REPORT"
^DIC(19,1623,0)="RA WKLRES^Resident Report^^R^11712^^^^^^y^"
^DIC(19,1623,1,0)="^^15^15^2940803^"
^DIC(19,1623,1,1,0)="This option allows the supervisor to generate a report of examinations for"
^DIC(19,1623,1,2,0)="interpreting resident physicians. If the supervisor has access to more"
^DIC(19,1623,1,3,0)="than one division or imaging type, s/he is prompted to select the"
^DIC(19,1623,1,4,0)="divisions and imaging types to include in the report. The supervisor"
^DIC(19,1623,1,5,0)="is prompted to select the interpreting resident physicians to include in"
^DIC(19,1623,1,6,0)="the report. The supervisor may select one, many or all interpreting"
^DIC(19,1623,1,7,0)="resident physicians. The supervisor is prompted to enter a date range for"
^DIC(19,1623,1,8,0)="the exams to be included in the report. The exam status values that will"
^DIC(19,1623,1,9,0)="be included in the report are displayed by imaging type."
^DIC(19,1623,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1623,1,11,0)="The report contains the following information: procedure and number of"
^DIC(19,1623,1,12,0)="examinations. A 'summary' report groups all examinations together by"
^DIC(19,1623,1,13,0)="interpreting resident physician for each imaging type and division. A"
^DIC(19,1623,1,14,0)="'detailed' report gives information for each individual procedure"
^DIC(19,1623,1,15,0)="performed by each interpreting resident physician."
^DIC(19,1623,25)="RES^RAWKL"
^DIC(19,1623,"U")="RESIDENT REPORT"
^DIC(19,1624,0)="RA WKLSTAFF^Staff Report^^R^11712^^^^^^y^"
^DIC(19,1624,1,0)="^^15^15^2940803^^^"
^DIC(19,1624,1,1,0)="This option allows the supervisor to generate a report of examinations for"
^DIC(19,1624,1,2,0)="interpreting staff physicians. If the supervisor has access to more than"
^DIC(19,1624,1,3,0)="one division or imaging type, s/he is prompted to select the divisions"
^DIC(19,1624,1,4,0)="and imaging types to include in the report. The supervisor is prompted to"
^DIC(19,1624,1,5,0)="select the interpreting staff physicians to include in the report. The"
^DIC(19,1624,1,6,0)="supervisor may select one, many or all interpreting staff physicians. The"
^DIC(19,1624,1,7,0)="supervisor is prompted to enter a date range for exams to be included in"
^DIC(19,1624,1,8,0)="the report. The exam status values that will be included in the report"
^DIC(19,1624,1,9,0)="will be displayed by imaging type."
^DIC(19,1624,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1624,1,11,0)="The report contains the following information: procedure and number of"
^DIC(19,1624,1,12,0)="exams. A 'summary' report groups all examinations together by interpreting"
^DIC(19,1624,1,13,0)="staff physician for each imaging type and division. A 'detailed' report"
^DIC(19,1624,1,14,0)="gives information for each individual procedure performed by each"
^DIC(19,1624,1,15,0)="interpreting staff physician."
^DIC(19,1624,25)="STAFF^RAWKL"
^DIC(19,1624,"U")="STAFF REPORT"
^DIC(19,1625,0)="RA WKLPHY^Physician Report^^R^11712^^^^^^y^"
^DIC(19,1625,1,0)="^^15^15^2940829^^"
^DIC(19,1625,1,1,0)="This option allows the supervisor to generate a report of examinations for"
^DIC(19,1625,1,2,0)="referring physicians. If the supervisor has access to more than"
^DIC(19,1625,1,3,0)="one division or imaging type, s/he is prompted to select the divisions"
^DIC(19,1625,1,4,0)="and imaging types to include in the report. The supervisor is prompted to"
^DIC(19,1625,1,5,0)="select the referring physicians to include in the report. The"
^DIC(19,1625,1,6,0)="supervisor may select one, many or all referring physicians. The"
^DIC(19,1625,1,7,0)="supervisor is prompted to enter a date range for exams to be included in"
^DIC(19,1625,1,8,0)="the report. The exam status values that will be included in the report"
^DIC(19,1625,1,9,0)="will be displayed by imaging type."
^DIC(19,1625,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1625,1,11,0)="The report contains the following information: procedure and number of"
^DIC(19,1625,1,12,0)="exams. A 'summary' report groups all examinations together by referring"
^DIC(19,1625,1,13,0)="physician for each imaging type and division. A 'detailed' report"
^DIC(19,1625,1,14,0)="gives information for each individual procedure performed by each"
^DIC(19,1625,1,15,0)="referring physician."
^DIC(19,1625,25)="PHY^RAWKL"
^DIC(19,1625,"U")="PHYSICIAN REPORT"
^DIC(19,1626,0)="RA WKLROOM^Camera/Equip/Rm Report^^R^11712^^^^^^y^"
^DIC(19,1626,1,0)="^^16^16^2940803^"
^DIC(19,1626,1,1,0)="This option allows the supervisor to generate a report of workloads for"
^DIC(19,1626,1,2,0)="camera/equipment/rooms. If the supervisor has access to more than one"
^DIC(19,1626,1,3,0)="division or imaging type, s/he is prompted to select the divisions and"
^DIC(19,1626,1,4,0)="imaging types to include in the report. The supervisor is prompted to"
^DIC(19,1626,1,5,0)="select the camera/equipment/rooms to include in the report. The supervisor"
^DIC(19,1626,1,6,0)="may select one, many or all camera/equipment/rooms. The supervisor is"
^DIC(19,1626,1,7,0)="prompted to enter a date range for the exams to be included in the report."
^DIC(19,1626,1,8,0)="The exam status values that will be included in the report will be"
^DIC(19,1626,1,9,0)="displayed by imaging type."
^DIC(19,1626,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1626,1,11,0)="The report contains the following information: procedure, number of"
^DIC(19,1626,1,12,0)="examinations, weighted work units, and percent of total weighted work"
^DIC(19,1626,1,13,0)="units.  A 'summary' report groups all examinations together by"
^DIC(19,1626,1,14,0)="camera/equipment/rooms for each imaging type and division. A 'detailed'"
^DIC(19,1626,1,15,0)="report gives information for each individiual procedure performed by each"
^DIC(19,1626,1,16,0)="camera/equipment/rooms."
^DIC(19,1626,25)="ROOM^RAWKL"
^DIC(19,1626,"U")="CAMERA/EQUIP/RM REPORT"
^DIC(19,1627,0)="RA WKLPROCEDURE^Detailed Procedure Report^^R^11712^^^^^^y^"
^DIC(19,1627,1,0)="^^14^14^2940830^"
^DIC(19,1627,1,1,0)="This option allows the supervisor to generate a workload report"
^DIC(19,1627,1,2,0)="for each 'Detailed Procedure' completed for one imaging type only. If"
^DIC(19,1627,1,3,0)="the supervisor has access to more than one division, s/he is prompted to"
^DIC(19,1627,1,4,0)="select the divisions to include in the report. One, many or all divisions"
^DIC(19,1627,1,5,0)="may be selected. The user is prompted for an imaging type. One imaging"
^DIC(19,1627,1,6,0)="type may be selected. If the user has access to one imaging type only,"
^DIC(19,1627,1,7,0)="then that imaging type will be selected automatically. The user is then"
^DIC(19,1627,1,8,0)="prompted to enter a date range. The examination status values that will"
^DIC(19,1627,1,9,0)="be included in the report are displayed to the user."
^DIC(19,1627,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1627,1,11,0)="The report consists of the following information for each AMIS category:"
^DIC(19,1627,1,12,0)="procedure, number of examinations In and Out, total number of"
^DIC(19,1627,1,13,0)="examinations, percent of exams, weighted work units, and percent of"
^DIC(19,1627,1,14,0)="weighted work units."
^DIC(19,1627,25)="RAPRC"
^DIC(19,1627,"U")="DETAILED PROCEDURE REPORT"
^DIC(19,1628,0)="RA STATRACK^Status Tracking of Exams^^R^11712^^^^^^^^^1^1"
^DIC(19,1628,1,0)="^^20^20^2940603^"
^DIC(19,1628,1,1,0)="This function is used mainly by the technologist to change the"
^DIC(19,1628,1,2,0)="status of an exam."
^DIC(19,1628,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1628,1,4,0)="This function is different than the 'Case No. Exam Edit'"
^DIC(19,1628,1,5,0)="function, since only certain prompts are asked for each status"
^DIC(19,1628,1,6,0)="change, while 'Case No. Exam Edit' always asks the same prompts."
^DIC(19,1628,1,7,0)="The type of data asked for during each status change is"
^DIC(19,1628,1,8,0)="specified by the site.  The number of statuses and names"
^DIC(19,1628,1,9,0)="are also site specific.  However, the choices of what type"
^DIC(19,1628,1,10,0)="of data to be asked is limited."
^DIC(19,1628,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1628,1,12,0)="A status can be flagged not to appear as part of the exam status tracking."
^DIC(19,1628,1,13,0)="A site may not want to display a particular exam status, if the data"
^DIC(19,1628,1,14,0)="needed to change the exam to the next status is usually not entered via"
^DIC(19,1628,1,15,0)="this option.  For example, going from the 'Examined' status to"
^DIC(19,1628,1,16,0)="'Transcribed' status usually requires interpreting physician's data, but"
^DIC(19,1628,1,17,0)="this is usually entered by the transcriptionist while entering the report."
^DIC(19,1628,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1628,1,19,0)="By limiting the statuses that appear under this function,"
^DIC(19,1628,1,20,0)="total system performance is improved because of less processing."
^DIC(19,1628,15)="K RAOPT(""STATRACK"")"
^DIC(19,1628,20)="S RAOPT(""STATRACK"")="""""
^DIC(19,1628,25)="RASTEXT"
^DIC(19,1628,99.1)="56981,36773"
^DIC(19,1628,"U")="STATUS TRACKING OF EXAMS"
^DIC(19,1629,0)="RA TECHMENU^Rad/Nuc Med Technologist Menu^^M^11712^^^^^^^^^1^1"
^DIC(19,1629,1,0)="^^3^3^2940607^^"
^DIC(19,1629,1,1,0)="This menu provides the technologist with functions to enter/edit patients"
^DIC(19,1629,1,2,0)="for procedures, to cancel a procedure, to add procedures,"
^DIC(19,1629,1,3,0)="to display reports and to utilize the 'Exam Status Tracking' option."
^DIC(19,1629,10,0)="^19.01PI^18^12"
^DIC(19,1629,10,1,0)="1560^"
