^DIC(19,1631,0)="RA DEVICE^Device Specifications for Imaging Locations^^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1631,1,0)="^^15^15^2940712^"
^DIC(19,1631,1,1,0)="This function allows IRM to assign device names"
^DIC(19,1631,1,2,0)="to represent divisions and locations."
^DIC(19,1631,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1631,1,4,0)="When a user signs on the system and tries to access the module,"
^DIC(19,1631,1,5,0)="the first action by the module will be to determine which"
^DIC(19,1631,1,6,0)="division and location the user is associated with."
^DIC(19,1631,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1631,1,8,0)="The module uses the device name to do this.  If the current device name"
^DIC(19,1631,1,9,0)="is the same as one of the names you are about to associate with a"
^DIC(19,1631,1,10,0)="particular division and location, then during the entire session the system"
^DIC(19,1631,1,11,0)="will automatically use the parameters that the coordinator has"
^DIC(19,1631,1,12,0)="specified for that division and location."
^DIC(19,1631,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1631,1,14,0)="For example, the user will never be asked how many flash cards to print"
^DIC(19,1631,1,15,0)="or what flash card format to use. The parameters have that information."
^DIC(19,1631,25)="2^RASITE"
^DIC(19,1631,99)="55699,38188"
^DIC(19,1631,"U")="DEVICE SPECIFICATIONS FOR IMAG"
^DIC(19,1633,0)="RA PURGE^Purge Data Function^RA*5.0*198: Radiology data purge not allowed.^R^11712^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,1633,1,0)="^^17^17^2940607^"
^DIC(19,1633,1,1,0)="This option allows IRM to purge rad/nuc med data from the system.  The"
^DIC(19,1633,1,2,0)="following types of data can be purged:"
^DIC(19,1633,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1633,1,4,0)="       1) Activity Logs"
^DIC(19,1633,1,5,0)="       2) Status Tracking Times"
^DIC(19,1633,1,6,0)="       3) Reports (but not impressions)"
^DIC(19,1633,1,7,0)="       4) Clinical Histories"
^DIC(19,1633,1,8,0)="       5) Order Data"
^DIC(19,1633,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1633,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1633,1,11,0)="For each of the above, the user is first asked how many days of on-line"
^DIC(19,1633,1,12,0)="data should be saved. The user is then asked when he wants this job to"
^DIC(19,1633,1,13,0)="run. It should not be executed during normal working hours."
^DIC(19,1633,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(19,1633,1,15,0)="Finally, this routine will produce a large amount of global kills"
^DIC(19,1633,1,16,0)="and as a result, journaling may need to be disabled during this process."
^DIC(19,1633,1,17,0)="Otherwise, many journal tapes may be produced."
^DIC(19,1633,25)="SCH^RAPURGE"
^DIC(19,1633,"U")="PURGE DATA FUNCTION"
