^DIC(19,2235,"U")="NATIONAL DRUG FILE MENU"
^DIC(19,2237,0)="PSNVFY^Verify Matches^^R^11595^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2237,1,0)="5^^7^7^2980922^^^^"
^DIC(19,2237,1,1,0)="Using this option, you can verify, one at a time, the unverified drugs that"
^DIC(19,2237,1,2,0)="have been matched using the option ""Rematch / Match Single Drugs"". The"
^DIC(19,2237,1,3,0)="unverified matches are stored in the National Drug Translation file. It"
^DIC(19,2237,1,4,0)="is not necessary to verify all of the matches at once. It will also allow"
^DIC(19,2237,1,5,0)="you to rematch a drug if you do not like the match. It is a requirement of"
^DIC(19,2237,1,6,0)="the software that all matched drugs be verified. The same person should"
^DIC(19,2237,1,7,0)="not match the drugs and then verify the matches."
^DIC(19,2237,25)="PSNVFY"
^DIC(19,2237,99)="55595,55503"
^DIC(19,2237,"U")="VERIFY MATCHES"
^DIC(19,2238,0)="PSNEXC^Report of Attempted Match Drugs^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2238,1,0)="^^9^9^2980922^^^^"
^DIC(19,2238,1,1,0)="Report of drugs from local file which were not matched successfully using"
^DIC(19,2238,1,2,0)="the option ""Rematch / Match Single Drugs "". Even though these"
^DIC(19,2238,1,3,0)="drugs were not matched, an entry was still made in National Drug"
^DIC(19,2238,1,4,0)="Translation File. This report should be printed after the option ""Verify"
^DIC(19,2238,1,5,0)="Matches"" has been executed and before the option ""Merge National Drug File"
^DIC(19,2238,1,6,0)="Data Into Local File"" has been executed. This is a cumulative report and will"
^DIC(19,2238,1,7,0)="include all entries since the entire matching process was initiated until"
^DIC(19,2238,1,8,0)="the time when these entries are manually classed."
^DIC(19,2238,1,9,0)="This report requires 80 columns."
^DIC(19,2238,25)="PSNEXC"
^DIC(19,2238,"U")="REPORT OF ATTEMPTED MATCH DRUG"
^DIC(19,2239,0)="PSNPFN^VA Product Names Matched Report^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2239,1,0)="^^7^7^2980922^^^^"
^DIC(19,2239,1,1,0)="This option generates a report of all drugs that have been matched. It"
^DIC(19,2239,1,2,0)="lists the name from the Local file, name from the National file, package"
^DIC(19,2239,1,3,0)="size, package type and user's name. This option should be printed before"
^DIC(19,2239,1,4,0)="the option ""Merge National Drug File Data Into Local File"". This report is"
^DIC(19,2239,1,5,0)="also useful after running the automatic match by NDC process to review what"
^DIC(19,2239,1,6,0)="has been matched. The data for this report is stored in the National Drug"
^DIC(19,2239,1,7,0)="Translation File. This report requires 80 columns."
^DIC(19,2239,25)="PSNPFN"
^DIC(19,2239,"U")="VA PRODUCT NAMES MATCHED REPOR"
^DIC(19,2240,0)="PSNDRUG^Rematch / Match Single Drugs^^R^11595^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2240,1,0)="^^4^4^2980922^^^^"
^DIC(19,2240,1,1,0)="User should run this option to match one drug at a time. User is"
^DIC(19,2240,1,2,0)="prompted for the drug name from local file to match with National File."
^DIC(19,2240,1,3,0)="This option can also be used to rematch any drug that was incorrectly"
^DIC(19,2240,1,4,0)="matched or to match any new drug added to your local drug file."
^DIC(19,2240,25)="PSNDRUG"
^DIC(19,2240,"U")="REMATCH / MATCH SINGLE DRUGS"
^DIC(19,2241,0)="PSNMRG^Merge National Drug File Data Into Local File^^R^11595^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2241,1,0)="7^^7^7^2980922^^^^"
^DIC(19,2241,1,1,0)="This option merges the following data from National Drug File into local"
^DIC(19,2241,1,2,0)="drug file: the pointer to VA Generic file, VA Product Name, pointer to"
^DIC(19,2241,1,3,0)="VA Product file, pointer to Package Size and Type, and VA Drug Classification."
^DIC(19,2241,1,4,0)="This option will also print a report listing any drugs in the National Drug"
^DIC(19,2241,1,5,0)="Translation File that were not merged. There must be at least one matched"
^DIC(19,2241,1,6,0)="and verified drug in the National Drug Translation file for the merge to"
^DIC(19,2241,1,7,0)="work. The printout of the ""error report"" will require 80 columns."
^DIC(19,2241,25)="PSNMRG"
^DIC(19,2241,99)="55595,55537"
^DIC(19,2241,"U")="MERGE NATIONAL DRUG FILE DATA "
^DIC(19,2242,0)="PSNCLS^VA Drug Classification^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2242,1,0)="^^5^5^2980922^^^^"
^DIC(19,2242,1,1,0)="This option generates a report that lists all of the VA Drug Classification"
^DIC(19,2242,1,2,0)="Codes and Classes. You are given the option of having the classification"
^DIC(19,2242,1,3,0)="descriptions printed in the report. You can choose to print all of the drug"
^DIC(19,2242,1,4,0)="classifications or a range of classifications. This report requires 80"
^DIC(19,2242,1,5,0)="columns."
^DIC(19,2242,25)="PSNCLS"
^DIC(19,2242,"U")="VA DRUG CLASSIFICATION"
^DIC(19,2243,0)="PSNRPT^NDF Info From Your Local Drug File^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2243,1,0)="^^6^6^2980922^^^^"
^DIC(19,2243,1,1,0)="This option generates a report that contains information either for a"
^DIC(19,2243,1,2,0)="specific range of drugs or for all drugs that have been merged. This option"
^DIC(19,2243,1,3,0)="should be executed after the option ""Merge National Drug File Data Into"
^DIC(19,2243,1,4,0)="Local File"" has been completed. Any drugs that contain no NDF information,"
^DIC(19,2243,1,5,0)="(i.e., the drug has not been matched, verified, and merged), will be"
^DIC(19,2243,1,6,0)="ignored. This report requires 132 columns."
^DIC(19,2243,25)="PSNRPT"
^DIC(19,2243,99)="55070,54671"
^DIC(19,2243,"U")="NDF INFO FROM YOUR LOCAL DRUG "
^DIC(19,2244,0)="PSNLDG^Local Drug File Report^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2244,1,0)="^^6^6^2980922^^^^"
^DIC(19,2244,1,1,0)="This option generates a report that contains selected information about"
^DIC(19,2244,1,2,0)="the drugs in your local drug file. The report prints the local drug name,"
^DIC(19,2244,1,3,0)="inactive date, NDC, and the DEA (Drug Enforcement Agency) value. This"
^DIC(19,2244,1,4,0)="report can be used to determine which drugs have an NDC already assigned"
^DIC(19,2244,1,5,0)="to them. It is recommended that this option be run first. This report"
^DIC(19,2244,1,6,0)="will require 132 columns."
^DIC(19,2244,25)="PSNLDG"
^DIC(19,2244,"U")="LOCAL DRUG FILE REPORT"
^DIC(19,2245,0)="PSNSTCL^Allow Unmatched Drugs To Be Classed^^R^11595^PSNMGR^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2245,1,0)="^^6^6^2980922^^^^"
^DIC(19,2245,1,1,0)="This option allows unmatched drugs to be classed. You may class one drug at"
^DIC(19,2245,1,2,0)="a time by generic name or internal number in your local file or you may"
^DIC(19,2245,1,3,0)="choose to go through a ""looping"" process alphabetically for all drugs that"
^DIC(19,2245,1,4,0)="do not have an inactive date and have not been merged. You may not change"
^DIC(19,2245,1,5,0)="the class of a merged drug. You must use the option ""Rematch / Match"
^DIC(19,2245,1,6,0)="Single Drugs"" to change the class of a merged drug."
^DIC(19,2245,25)="PSNSTCL"
^DIC(19,2245,"U")="ALLOW UNMATCHED DRUGS TO BE CL"
^DIC(19,2302,0)="PSGW ON-DEMAND NURSING EDIT^Enter/Edit Nurses' On-Demand Request (80 column)^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2302,1,0)="^^10^10^2890726^^^^"
^DIC(19,2302,1,1,0)="This option is used to enter an on-demand request by the Nursing"
^DIC(19,2302,1,2,0)="Staff.  An on-demand request is the non-scheduled distribution"
^DIC(19,2302,1,3,0)="of an item to an AOU.  If there is a backorder on the requested"
^DIC(19,2302,1,4,0)="item, the backorder total is displayed, but the user is not"
^DIC(19,2302,1,5,0)="allowed to enter quantity to be dispensed."
^DIC(19,2302,1,6,0)="If the item requested is currently not stocked in that AOU, the"
^DIC(19,2302,1,7,0)="user is NOT allowed to add it with this option.  Requests for"
^DIC(19,2302,1,8,0)="non-standard items must be made through the pharmacy by phone or"
^DIC(19,2302,1,9,0)="form.  After entering the request, the user may print a report"
^DIC(19,2302,1,10,0)="of the request."
^DIC(19,2302,25)="PSGWODRN"
^DIC(19,2302,"U")="ENTER/EDIT NURSES' ON-DEMAND R"
^DIC(19,2303,0)="PSGW ENTER/EDIT AMIS DATA^AMIS Data Enter/Edit (Single Drug)^^E^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2303,1,0)="^^5^5^2910226^^^^"
^DIC(19,2303,1,1,0)="This option allows the entry of AMIS category and conversion number"
^DIC(19,2303,1,2,0)="for those drugs used in the Automatic Replenishment/Ward Stock"
^DIC(19,2303,1,3,0)="package.  The user must select the drug for which data is to be entered."
^DIC(19,2303,1,4,0)="This option is most likely to be used to edit data entered in the"
^DIC(19,2303,1,5,0)="""Enter AMIS Data for All Drugs/All AOUs"" option."
^DIC(19,2303,30)="PSDRUG("
^DIC(19,2303,31)="AEMQ"
^DIC(19,2303,50)="PSDRUG("
^DIC(19,2303,51)="[PSGW ENTER/EDIT AMIS DATA]"
^DIC(19,2303,"U")="AMIS DATA ENTER/EDIT (SINGLE D"
^DIC(19,2304,0)="PSGW PREPARE AMIS DATA^Prepare AMIS Data^^M^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2304,1,0)="^^1^1^2910326^^^^"
^DIC(19,2304,1,1,0)="Main option for preparing data base with AR/WS AMIS data."
^DIC(19,2304,10,0)="^19.01PI^7^7"
^DIC(19,2304,10,1,0)="2303^^7"
^DIC(19,2304,10,2,0)="2305^^3"
^DIC(19,2304,10,3,0)="2306^^1"
^DIC(19,2304,10,4,0)="2307^^5"
^DIC(19,2304,10,5,0)="2308^^9"
^DIC(19,2304,10,6,0)="2309^^13"
^DIC(19,2304,10,7,0)="4460^^11"
^DIC(19,2304,10,"B",2303,1)=""
^DIC(19,2304,10,"B",2305,2)=""
^DIC(19,2304,10,"B",2306,3)=""
^DIC(19,2304,10,"B",2307,4)=""
^DIC(19,2304,10,"B",2308,5)=""
^DIC(19,2304,10,"B",2309,6)=""
^DIC(19,2304,10,"B",4460,7)=""
^DIC(19,2304,99)="62088,37770"
^DIC(19,2304,"U")="PREPARE AMIS DATA"
^DIC(19,2305,0)="PSGW ENTER AMIS DATA/ALL DRUGS^Enter AMIS Data for All Drugs/All AOUs^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2305,1,0)="^^5^5^2870902^^"
^DIC(19,2305,1,1,0)="This routine will display for the user, all drugs in all AOUs,"
^DIC(19,2305,1,2,0)="allowing the entry of data needed for AMIS calculations."
^DIC(19,2305,1,3,0)="The drugs will be displayed alphabetically by ""type""."
^DIC(19,2305,1,4,0)="For each drug, the user will be asked for AMIS category and"
^DIC(19,2305,1,5,0)="AMIS conversion number."
^DIC(19,2305,25)="PSGWADE"
^DIC(19,2305,"U")="ENTER AMIS DATA FOR ALL DRUGS/"
^DIC(19,2306,0)="PSGW PRINT AMIS WORKSHEET^Print AMIS Worksheet (80 column)^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2306,1,0)="^^3^3^2891019^^^"
^DIC(19,2306,1,1,0)="This option prints a worksheet to be used in classifying AR/WS"
^DIC(19,2306,1,2,0)="drugs for AMIS.  The print order is by ""type"", and within type"
^DIC(19,2306,1,3,0)="the drug listing is alphabetical."
^DIC(19,2306,25)="PSGWPAW"
^DIC(19,2306,"U")="PRINT AMIS WORKSHEET (80 COLUM"
^DIC(19,2307,0)="PSGW PRINT DATA FOR AMIS STATS^Data for AMIS Stats - Print (132 column)^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2307,1,0)="^^2^2^2890410^^^"
^DIC(19,2307,1,1,0)="This report will show the current data stored in the Drug File which"
^DIC(19,2307,1,2,0)="will affect AR/WS AMIS statistics."
^DIC(19,2307,25)="PSGWADP"
^DIC(19,2307,"U")="DATA FOR AMIS STATS - PRINT (1"
^DIC(19,2308,0)="PSGW AOU RETURNS & AMIS COUNT^Identify AOU Returns & AMIS Count^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2308,1,0)="^^8^8^2930622^^^^"
^DIC(19,2308,1,1,0)="For AMIS purposes, the system must know how to credit returns."
^DIC(19,2308,1,2,0)="This option allows the user to identify the ""usual"" method of"
^DIC(19,2308,1,3,0)="drug distribution to be credited for each AOU.  ALL returns"
^DIC(19,2308,1,4,0)="from the AOU will be credited to this method."
^DIC(19,2308,1,5,0)="For AMIS purposes, the system must know if the inventories for"
^DIC(19,2308,1,6,0)="each AOU are to be counted in the AR/WS Stats File."
^DIC(19,2308,1,7,0)="MOST AOUs will count on AMIS, however, an AOU used for internal"
^DIC(19,2308,1,8,0)="inventory purposes within the pharmacy should not."
^DIC(19,2308,25)="PSGWAOU"
^DIC(19,2308,"U")="IDENTIFY AOU RETURNS & AMIS CO"
^DIC(19,2309,0)="PSGW AOU RET/AMIS CT PRINT^Show AOU Status for AMIS (80 column)^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2309,1,0)="^^3^3^2890706^^^^"
^DIC(19,2309,1,1,0)="This option shows the method of distribution credited for RETURNS"
^DIC(19,2309,1,2,0)="for each AOU, and if the AOU is to be counted in AMIS stats."
^DIC(19,2309,1,3,0)="This option also displays the INPATIENT SITE designation for the AOU."
^DIC(19,2309,25)="PSGWRAC"
^DIC(19,2309,60)=""
^DIC(19,2309,62)=""
^DIC(19,2309,63)=""
^DIC(19,2309,64)=""
^DIC(19,2309,"U")="SHOW AOU STATUS FOR AMIS (80 C"
^DIC(19,2310,0)="PSGW AMIS^AR/WS AMIS Report^^M^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2310,1,0)="^^2^2^2890126^^^^"
^DIC(19,2310,1,1,0)="Main option for clearing exceptions, printing, and recalculating"
^DIC(19,2310,1,2,0)="the AMIS report."
^DIC(19,2310,10,0)="^19.01PI^3^3"
^DIC(19,2310,10,1,0)="2311^^1"
^DIC(19,2310,10,2,0)="2312^^3"
^DIC(19,2310,10,3,0)="2313^^2"
^DIC(19,2310,10,"B",2311,1)=""
^DIC(19,2310,10,"B",2312,2)=""
^DIC(19,2310,10,"B",2313,3)=""
^DIC(19,2310,99)="62088,37770"
^DIC(19,2310,"U")="AR/WS AMIS REPORT"
^DIC(19,2311,0)="PSGW CLEAR AMIS EXCEPTIONS^Incomplete AMIS Data^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2311,1,0)="^^7^7^2910304^^^^"
^DIC(19,2311,1,1,0)="This option loops through the ""AEX"" - exceptions cross-reference in the"
^DIC(19,2311,1,2,0)="AR/WS Stats File - 58.5.  Drugs in this cross-reference had data"
^DIC(19,2311,1,3,0)="missing from the Drug file at the time the quantity was dispensed,"
^DIC(19,2311,1,4,0)="and thus could not be added to the cumulative AMIS statistics."
^DIC(19,2311,1,5,0)="For the selected date range, the drug will be shown, and the user"
^DIC(19,2311,1,6,0)="will be asked to supply the missing data.  At that time, the routine"
^DIC(19,2311,1,7,0)="will update the AMIS statistics, and delete the ""AEX"" cross-reference."
^DIC(19,2311,25)="PSGWCL"
^DIC(19,2311,"U")="INCOMPLETE AMIS DATA"
^DIC(19,2312,0)="PSGW RECALCULATE AMIS^Recalculate AMIS^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2312,1,0)="^^5^5^2870902^^"
^DIC(19,2312,1,1,0)="This option should be used ONLY after the AMIS report has been run,"
^DIC(19,2312,1,2,0)="results have been found to be in error, and data in the Drug file"
^DIC(19,2312,1,3,0)="has been changed to reflect the correct information.  The purpose"
^DIC(19,2312,1,4,0)="of this option is to correct the AMIS when data entry errors have"
^DIC(19,2312,1,5,0)="caused the results to be inaccurate."
^DIC(19,2312,25)="PSGWRA"
^DIC(19,2312,"U")="RECALCULATE AMIS"
^DIC(19,2313,0)="PSGW PRINT AMIS REPORT^Print AMIS Report (132 column)^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2313,1,0)="^^2^2^2890126^^^^"
^DIC(19,2313,1,1,0)="This option prints the AMIS report.  Right margin should be at 132."
^DIC(19,2313,1,2,0)="The report may be queued to print at a later time."
^DIC(19,2313,25)="PSGWAR"
^DIC(19,2313,99)="53515,48652"
^DIC(19,2313,"U")="PRINT AMIS REPORT (132 COLUMN)"
^DIC(19,2314,0)="PSGW PURGE^Obsolete Data Purge^^M^.5^PSGW PURGE^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2314,1,0)="^^1^1^2880114^^^^"
^DIC(19,2314,1,1,0)="This option is the main menu driver for purging AR/WS files."
^DIC(19,2314,10,0)="^19.01PI^2^2"
^DIC(19,2314,10,1,0)="2315^"
^DIC(19,2314,10,2,0)="2316^"
^DIC(19,2314,10,"B",2315,1)=""
^DIC(19,2314,10,"B",2316,2)=""
^DIC(19,2314,99)="62088,37770"
^DIC(19,2314,"U")="OBSOLETE DATA PURGE"
^DIC(19,2315,0)="PSGW PURGE AMIS^AMIS Data Purge^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2315,1,0)="^^4^4^2910212^^^^"
^DIC(19,2315,1,1,0)="This option allows the user to delete data from File 58.5 - the"
^DIC(19,2315,1,2,0)="AR/WS Stats File.  Data should be kept in this file for at least"
^DIC(19,2315,1,3,0)="one quarter.  The routine will not allow users to delete data"
^DIC(19,2315,1,4,0)="that is less than 100 days old.  The option is automatically queued."
^DIC(19,2315,25)="PSGWAP"
^DIC(19,2315,"U")="AMIS DATA PURGE"
^DIC(19,2316,0)="PSGW PURGE FILES^Purge Dispensing Data^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2316,1,0)="^^5^5^2930624^^^^"
^DIC(19,2316,1,1,0)="This option allows the user to delete data from Files 58.1, 58.3,"
^DIC(19,2316,1,2,0)="and 58.19.  Data should be kept in these files for at least one"
^DIC(19,2316,1,3,0)="quarter.  The routine will not allow users to delete data that is"
^DIC(19,2316,1,4,0)="less than 100 days old.  Since the option is CPU intensive, it should"
^DIC(19,2316,1,5,0)="be queued to run during the ""off"" hours.  "
^DIC(19,2316,10,0)="^19.01IP^0^0"
^DIC(19,2316,25)="PSGWOLD"
^DIC(19,2316,"U")="PURGE DISPENSING DATA"
^DIC(19,2317,0)="PSGW COST PER AOU^Cost Report Per AOU (80 column)^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2317,1,0)="^^10^10^2910221^^^^"
^DIC(19,2317,1,1,0)="For a user selected date range, this report will show all active drugs for"
^DIC(19,2317,1,2,0)="one AOU, several AOUs, or ALL AOUs, with total quantity dispensed and cost."
^DIC(19,2317,1,3,0)="(It will print only Bottom Totals if desired.)"
^DIC(19,2317,1,4,0)="The report gives a total of all quantities dispensed and all drug costs"
^DIC(19,2317,1,5,0)="for that AOU.  Also, if wards/locations and services have been defined"
^DIC(19,2317,1,6,0)="for the AOU, a breakdown report will print.  It shows the defined "
^DIC(19,2317,1,7,0)="wards/locations percentage of total, and cost per ward/location."
^DIC(19,2317,1,8,0)="If services are defined, it shows the defined services, percentage of"
^DIC(19,2317,1,9,0)="ward/location and cost per service.  The report may be queued to print "
^DIC(19,2317,1,10,0)="at a later time."
^DIC(19,2317,25)="PSGWCPA"
^DIC(19,2317,99)="55459,39294"
^DIC(19,2317,"U")="COST REPORT PER AOU (80 COLUMN"
^DIC(19,2318,0)="PSGW SHOW AREA OF USE^Show AOU/Ward/Service (132 column)^^P^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2318,1,0)="^^2^2^2890906^^^^"
^DIC(19,2318,1,1,0)="This option allows the user to see the AOUs/wards/services created in the"
^DIC(19,2318,1,2,0)="""Create the Area of Use"" option."
^DIC(19,2318,60)="PSI(58.1,"
^DIC(19,2318,62)=0
^DIC(19,2318,63)="[PSGW SHOW AREA OF USE]"
^DIC(19,2318,64)="[PSGW SHOW AREA OF USE]"
^DIC(19,2318,65)="FIRST"
^DIC(19,2318,66)="LAST"
^DIC(19,2318,"U")="SHOW AOU/WARD/SERVICE (132 COL"
^DIC(19,2319,0)="PSGW HIGH COST^High Cost Report (80 column)^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2319,1,0)="^^5^5^2910212^^^^"
^DIC(19,2319,1,1,0)="This option allows the user to see drugs/items dispensed in AR/WS"
^DIC(19,2319,1,2,0)="in alphabetical or cost order.  The user selects a date range, and"
^DIC(19,2319,1,3,0)="a ""cut off"" amount for the report.  The report may be calculated for"
^DIC(19,2319,1,4,0)="a single AOU, or cumulatively for all AOUs.  Report may be queued to"
^DIC(19,2319,1,5,0)="print at a later time."
^DIC(19,2319,25)="PSGWHC"
^DIC(19,2319,"U")="HIGH COST REPORT (80 COLUMN)"
^DIC(19,2320,0)="PSGW HIGH VOLUME^High Volume Report (80 column)^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2320,1,0)="^^3^3^2870902^^"
^DIC(19,2320,1,1,0)="For a selected date range, the user may print a report showing"
^DIC(19,2320,1,2,0)="drug usage in decreasing order for either a selected AOU or"
^DIC(19,2320,1,3,0)="for all AOUs combined."
^DIC(19,2320,10,0)="^19.01IP^0^0"
^DIC(19,2320,25)="PSGWHV"
^DIC(19,2320,"U")="HIGH VOLUME REPORT (80 COLUMN)"
^DIC(19,2321,0)="PSGW PRINT SETUP LISTS^Print Set Up Lists^^M^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2321,1,0)="^^2^2^2870902^^"
^DIC(19,2321,1,1,0)="This option contains all ""reports"" or lists associated with setting"
^DIC(19,2321,1,2,0)="up the files for AR/WS."
^DIC(19,2321,10,0)="^19.01PI^6^6"
^DIC(19,2321,10,1,0)="732^^1"
