^DIC(19,2802,0)="FBAA MRA DELETE VENDOR^Delete Vendor MRA^^R^1^FBAA LEVEL 2^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2802,1,0)="^19.06^17^17^3070927^^^^"
^DIC(19,2802,1,1,0)="The 'Delete Vendor MRA' option is used to place a vendor locally"
^DIC(19,2802,1,2,0)="in delete status whenever a vendor becomes inactive or cancels"
^DIC(19,2802,1,3,0)="FEE care.  This option will not send a delete request to the"
^DIC(19,2802,1,4,0)="Central Fee system in Austin."
^DIC(19,2802,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(19,2802,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(19,2802,1,7,0)=" 1)  If the vendor is in delete status on both your system as well as"
^DIC(19,2802,1,8,0)="     Central FEE, you only need to use the 'Reinstate Vendor MRA' option."
^DIC(19,2802,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,2802,1,10,0)=" 2)  If the vendor is in delete status on your system, but no longer"
^DIC(19,2802,1,11,0)="     resides on the Central FEE system, use the 'Update FMS Vendor File "
^DIC(19,2802,1,12,0)="     in Austin' option."
^DIC(19,2802,1,13,0)="  "
^DIC(19,2802,1,14,0)=" 3)  If a vendor which you were now adding to your system somehow"
^DIC(19,2802,1,15,0)="     already resided on the Central FEE system, but in delete status,"
^DIC(19,2802,1,16,0)="     you would need to add the vendor to your systemonly.  Doing so"
^DIC(19,2802,1,17,0)="     will re-activate the vendor in the Central system."
^DIC(19,2802,25)="FBAADV"
^DIC(19,2802,"U")="DELETE VENDOR MRA"
