^DIC(19,2828,"U")="VETERAN MRA MAIN MENU"
^DIC(19,2829,0)="FBAA QUEUE DATA FOR TRANS.^Queue Data for Transmission^^R^1^FBAA LEVEL 2^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2829,1,0)="^19.06^2^2^3080407^^^^"
^DIC(19,2829,1,1,0)="This option is used by the supervisor to transmit to Austin"
^DIC(19,2829,1,2,0)="FEE payments and MRA's via electronic mail."
^DIC(19,2829,25)="FBAAV0"
^DIC(19,2829,"U")="QUEUE DATA FOR TRANSMISSION"
^DIC(19,2830,0)="FBAA MRA VENDOR REINSTATE^Reinstate Vendor MRA^^R^1^FBAA LEVEL 2^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,2830,1,0)="^19.06^14^14^3070920^^^^"
^DIC(19,2830,1,1,0)="The 'Reinstate Vendor MRA' option is used to reactivate a vendor formerly in delete status."
^DIC(19,2830,1,2,0)="  "
^DIC(19,2830,1,3,0)="  "
^DIC(19,2830,1,4,0)=" 1)  If the vendor is in delete status on both your system as well as"
^DIC(19,2830,1,5,0)="     Central FEE, you only need to use the 'Reinstate Vendor MRA' option."
^DIC(19,2830,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,2830,1,7,0)=" 2)  If the vendor is in delete status on your system, but no longer"
^DIC(19,2830,1,8,0)="     resides on the Central FEE system, use the 'Update FMS Vendor File "
^DIC(19,2830,1,9,0)="     in Austin' option."
^DIC(19,2830,1,10,0)="  "
^DIC(19,2830,1,11,0)=" 3)  If a vendor which you were now adding to your system somehow"
^DIC(19,2830,1,12,0)="     already resided on the Central FEE system, but in delete status,"
^DIC(19,2830,1,13,0)="     you would need to add the vendor to your system, transmit data"
^DIC(19,2830,1,14,0)="     to Austin, and then invoke the 'Reinstate Vendor MRA' option."
^DIC(19,2830,25)="FBAARV"
^DIC(19,2830,"U")="REINSTATE VENDOR MRA"
^DIC(19,2833,0)="PRAP 50K CAP CLEARANCE^50K CAP Clearance^^R^.5^^^"
^DIC(19,2833,1,0)="^^7^7^2880218^^^^"
^DIC(19,2833,1,1,0)="This option is used in the Automated tracking procedure for"
^DIC(19,2833,1,2,0)="facilities that have reached their $50,000 limit. This option"
^DIC(19,2833,1,3,0)="comes into play whenever the $50,000 limit has been reached for"
^DIC(19,2833,1,4,0)="either of the two categories:"
^DIC(19,2833,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,2833,1,6,0)="              (1) Research & Development"
^DIC(19,2833,1,7,0)="              (2) Medical"
^DIC(19,2833,25)="PRAPCAP"
^DIC(19,2833,"U")="50K CAP CLEARANCE"
^DIC(19,2837,0)="PRAP PROGRAM AREA INITIATIVES^Program Area Initiatives^^R^.5^^^"
^DIC(19,2837,1,0)="^^3^3^2880115^^"
^DIC(19,2837,1,1,0)="This option is used by MIRMO, and selected personnel to provide"
^DIC(19,2837,1,2,0)="a list, sorted by region/facility/initiative of the initiatives"
^DIC(19,2837,1,3,0)="associated with a particular Program Area."
^DIC(19,2837,25)="PRAPPGM"
^DIC(19,2837,"U")="PROGRAM AREA INITIATIVES"
^DIC(19,2838,0)="PRAP PROGRAM AREA EQUIPMENT^Program Area Equipment^^R^.5^^^"
^DIC(19,2838,1,0)="^^3^3^2880115^^"
^DIC(19,2838,1,1,0)="This option will sort by Region/Facility/Initiative to find initiatives"
^DIC(19,2838,1,2,0)="associated with a certain Program Area, Where a certain Equipment Type"
^DIC(19,2838,1,3,0)="is contained."
^DIC(19,2838,25)="PRAPPGM1"
^DIC(19,2838,"U")="PROGRAM AREA EQUIPMENT"
^DIC(19,2839,0)="PRAP INITIATIVE PURGE^Purge Inactivated Initiatives^^R^.5^^^"
^DIC(19,2839,1,0)="^^6^6^2880125^"
^DIC(19,2839,1,1,0)="This option will automatically, purge any Inactive Iniatiative that has been"
^DIC(19,2839,1,2,0)="inactivated prior to two planning cycles ago. For example if the current"
^DIC(19,2839,1,3,0)="planning cycle is for 1989, Initiatives that were inactivated prior to 1987"
^DIC(19,2839,1,4,0)="shall be deleted from record. Even though initiatives that were inactivated"
^DIC(19,2839,1,5,0)="in the previous planning cycle (i.e. 1988) cannot be reactivated, they will"
^DIC(19,2839,1,6,0)="be kept on record.)"
^DIC(19,2839,25)="PRAPOFF"
^DIC(19,2839,"U")="PURGE INACTIVATED INITIATIVES"
^DIC(19,2841,0)="PRAP SERVICE EQUIPMENT^Equipment Breakdown of Program Area^^R^.5^^^"
^DIC(19,2841,1,0)="^^5^5^2880204^"
^DIC(19,2841,1,1,0)="This report produces a listing by facility, of the total amount of "
^DIC(19,2841,1,2,0)="APPROVED equipment types. It shows a total number of each type, plus"
^DIC(19,2841,1,3,0)="a total dollar figure. It then shows a listing of the Associated,"
^DIC(19,2841,1,4,0)="Primary Program areas/Services, with a listing of dollar amount each,"
^DIC(19,2841,1,5,0)="and what equipment types each Program area/Service is approved for."
^DIC(19,2841,25)="PRAPCRT1"
^DIC(19,2841,"U")="EQUIPMENT BREAKDOWN OF PROGRAM AREA"
^DIC(19,2842,0)="PRAP99^Requested .900 total (facility)^^R^.5^^^"
^DIC(19,2842,1,0)="^^2^2^2880427^^"
^DIC(19,2842,1,1,0)="This option will show the total amount of .900 money a station"
^DIC(19,2842,1,2,0)="has REQUESTED for a given year."
^DIC(19,2842,25)="PRAP99"
^DIC(19,2842,"U")="REQUESTED .900 TOTAL (FACILITY)"
^DIC(19,2843,0)="PRAP9FTE^FACILITY REQUESTED FTEE^^R^.5^^^"
^DIC(19,2843,1,0)="^^1^1^2880218^"
^DIC(19,2843,1,1,0)="Shows the total amount of FTEE a station has requested"
^DIC(19,2843,25)="PRAP9FTE"
^DIC(19,2843,"U")="FACILITY REQUESTED FTEE"
^DIC(19,2846,0)="PRAP RD ERROR^RD & ISC ERROR CHECKER^^R^.5^^^"
^DIC(19,2846,1,0)="^^3^3^2880405^"
^DIC(19,2846,1,1,0)="This is the error checker for the RDs & ISCs. It'll check through the"
^DIC(19,2846,1,2,0)="initiatives, and when any errors are discovered, it will flag them and"
^DIC(19,2846,1,3,0)="show these errors in a report."
^DIC(19,2846,25)="PRAPDE"
^DIC(19,2846,"U")="RD & ISC ERROR CHECKER"
^DIC(19,2847,0)="PRAP RD PRINT INITIATIVES^Print Initiatives^^R^.5^^^"
^DIC(19,2847,1,0)="^^3^3^2880406^"
^DIC(19,2847,1,1,0)="This option allows the user to print RD & ISC initiatives."
^DIC(19,2847,1,2,0)="RDs & ISCs can only look at their own initiatives, while MIRMO"
^DIC(19,2847,1,3,0)="has access to all initiatives."
^DIC(19,2847,25)="PRAPDPT"
^DIC(19,2847,"U")="PRINT INITIATIVES"
^DIC(19,2852,0)="PRAP NEW EQUIPMENT MENU^Equipment data menu^^M^.5^^^^^^^^^1^1"
