^DIC(19,3205,"U")="HINQ MENU (VERSION 4.0)"
^DIC(19,3206,0)="DVB HREQ-STATUSBYPAT^Status of HINQ by Patient^^R^.5^DVBHINQ^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,3206,1,0)="^^5^5^2920117^^^^"
^DIC(19,3206,1,1,0)="This option gives information about entries in the suspense file"
^DIC(19,3206,1,2,0)="by patient name.  The suspense file status, the eligibility status"
^DIC(19,3206,1,3,0)="(from the station's patient file), and the HINQ response message, if"
^DIC(19,3206,1,4,0)="a response has been received, will be displayed for each patient"
^DIC(19,3206,1,5,0)="selected."
^DIC(19,3206,25)="FIND^DVBHQUS"
^DIC(19,3206,"U")="STATUS OF HINQ BY PATIENT"
^DIC(19,3207,0)="DVB HSUSP-VIEWFILE^View the HINQ Suspense File^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,3207,1,0)="^^7^7^2920117^^^^"
^DIC(19,3207,1,1,0)="This option lists HINQ suspense file entries on the screen.  Entries"
^DIC(19,3207,1,2,0)="are displayed in order according to the last status update date and"
^DIC(19,3207,1,3,0)="time, beginning with the most recent.  Only entries whose last status"
^DIC(19,3207,1,4,0)="update date is on or after the last network workday will be shown."
^DIC(19,3207,1,5,0)="For each entry displayed, the following information is given:  patient's"
^DIC(19,3207,1,6,0)="name, SSN, suspense file status, last status update date, and the names"
^DIC(19,3207,1,7,0)="and times of users who requested an entry for the patient."
^DIC(19,3207,25)="DVBHQUE"
^DIC(19,3207,"U")="VIEW THE HINQ SUSPENSE FILE"
^DIC(19,3208,0)="DVB HSUSP-ENTERREQ^Enter a Request in the HINQ Suspense File^DO NOT USE!! - HINQ DECOM - DVB*4.0*71^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,3208,1,0)="^^17^17^2920117^^^^"
^DIC(19,3208,1,1,0)="This option allows HINQ inquiry requests to be entered into the "
^DIC(19,3208,1,2,0)="HINQ suspense file for later transmission to the VBA computer."
^DIC(19,3208,1,3,0)="Entries may be made in the suspense file by users who do not"
^DIC(19,3208,1,4,0)="have the required security to transmit requests to the VBA"
^DIC(19,3208,1,5,0)="computer.  Requests should also be entered in the suspense file"
^DIC(19,3208,1,6,0)="when the VBA computer is not available as during non-VBA "
^DIC(19,3208,1,7,0)="computer workday hours or when the network is disabled because"
^DIC(19,3208,1,8,0)="of a communication problem."
^DIC(19,3208,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,3208,1,10,0)="This option may be made available during the Registration options:"
^DIC(19,3208,1,11,0)="Register Patient and Load/Edit Patient Data by turning the USE"
^DIC(19,3208,1,12,0)="HINQ INQUIRY parameter on.  It can also be placed stand alone in"
^DIC(19,3208,1,13,0)="the ADT menu."
^DIC(19,3208,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(19,3208,1,15,0)="If the patient's eligibility status in the station's patient file"
^DIC(19,3208,1,16,0)="is 'Verified', this will be indicated when an entry is made"
^DIC(19,3208,1,17,0)="in the suspense file."
^DIC(19,3208,25)="DVBHQZ4"
^DIC(19,3208,30)=""
^DIC(19,3208,99)="55460,46927"
^DIC(19,3208,"U")="ENTER A REQUEST IN THE HINQ SU"
