^DIC(19,3955,"U")="PRINT ELECTRON MICROSCOPY REPO"
^DIC(19,3956,0)="LRAPR^Verify/release reports, anat path^^R^10000000020^LRVERIFY^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,3956,1,0)="^^12^12^3080423^"
^DIC(19,3956,1,1,0)="This option is used to verify/release pathology reports.  The user is prompted"
^DIC(19,3956,1,2,0)="for the accession number of the report to be released.  If electronic signature"
^DIC(19,3956,1,3,0)="is not activated, the user is asked if the report is to be released, yes or no. "
^DIC(19,3956,1,4,0)="If electronic signature has been activated, the option is used to"
^DIC(19,3956,1,5,0)="electronically sign and store pathology reports.  It also allows CPT coding to"
^DIC(19,3956,1,6,0)="be performed regardless of the release status of the chosen report.  Another"
^DIC(19,3956,1,7,0)="feature is the ability to print SNOMED codes for the given accession/report."
^DIC(19,3956,1,8,0)="Action alerts are sent automatically to the ordering provider and the "
^DIC(19,3956,1,9,0)="primary physician or PCP at the time the report is released.  If "
^DIC(19,3956,1,10,0)="requested, alerts may be sent to additional person(s) and or mail"
^DIC(19,3956,1,11,0)="group(s).  These additional alerts are also action alerts.  These alerts"
^DIC(19,3956,1,12,0)="are sent whether electronic signature is on or off."
^DIC(19,3956,25)="LRAPR"
^DIC(19,3956,99)="55477,35597"
^DIC(19,3956,"U")="VERIFY/RELEASE REPORTS, ANAT P"
^DIC(19,3957,0)="LRAPTT^Anatomic pathology turnaround time^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,3957,1,0)="^^2^2^2870204^^^"
^DIC(19,3957,1,1,0)="Provides the number of days cases submitted to pathology were in"
^DIC(19,3957,1,2,0)=" the lab before being signed out."
^DIC(19,3957,25)="LRAPTT"
^DIC(19,3957,"U")="ANATOMIC PATHOLOGY TURNAROUND "
^DIC(19,3958,0)="LRAP ADD^Add patient(s) to report print queue^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,3958,1,0)="^^2^2^2880728^^^"
^DIC(19,3958,1,1,0)="This option adds patients to the cumulative report print queue, the"
^DIC(19,3958,1,2,0)="final report queue, or the autopsy protocols print queue."
^DIC(19,3958,20)=""
^DIC(19,3958,25)="N^LRAPP"
^DIC(19,3958,"U")="ADD PATIENT(S) TO REPORT PRINT"
^DIC(19,3959,0)="LRAP DELETE^Delete report print queue^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,3959,1,0)="^^3^3^2880728^^"
^DIC(19,3959,1,1,0)="This option deletes a list of any previous pathology accessions in"
^DIC(19,3959,1,2,0)="surgical path and ctyopath and patients on the cumulative report, "
^DIC(19,3959,1,3,0)="final report, or autopsy protocols print queue."
^DIC(19,3959,20)=""
^DIC(19,3959,25)="D^LRAPP"
^DIC(19,3959,"U")="DELETE REPORT PRINT QUEUE"
^DIC(19,3960,0)="LRAP PRINT SINGLE^Print single report only^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,3960,1,0)="^19.06^8^8^3020826^^^^"
^DIC(19,3960,1,1,0)="Prints a list of any pathology accessions in cytopath, electron microscopy,"
^DIC(19,3960,1,2,0)="and surgical pathology for cumulative reports for micro exams.  Also prints"
^DIC(19,3960,1,3,0)="final reports and completed autopsy reports.  For final reports, if the report"
^DIC(19,3960,1,4,0)="has been electronically signed and stored in TIU, the report will be pulled"
^DIC(19,3960,1,5,0)="from TIU.  Otherwise, the report will be generated from the data stored in the"
^DIC(19,3960,1,6,0)="LAB DATA (#63) file.  The option asks if a 'Final Office Copy' should be"
^DIC(19,3960,1,7,0)="printed.  The 'Final Office Copy' prints SNOMED codes on a separate page"
^DIC(19,3960,1,8,0)="since they are no longer printed on the SF515."
^DIC(19,3960,20)=""
^DIC(19,3960,25)="S^LRAPP"
^DIC(19,3960,"U")="PRINT SINGLE REPORT ONLY"
^DIC(19,3961,0)="LRAP PRINT ALL ON QUEUE^Print all reports on queue^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,3961,1,0)="^19.06^8^8^3020826^^^^"
^DIC(19,3961,1,1,0)="This option prints a report listing the clinical history and gross"
^DIC(19,3961,1,2,0)="description for review for patients on the cumulative report print queue,"
^DIC(19,3961,1,3,0)="as well as final reports for patients and completed autopsy reports.  For final"
^DIC(19,3961,1,4,0)="reports, if the report has been electronically signed and stored in TIU, the"
^DIC(19,3961,1,5,0)="report will be pulled from TIU.  Otherwise, the report will be generated from"
^DIC(19,3961,1,6,0)="the data stored in the LAB DATA (#63) file.  The option asks if a 'Final Office"
^DIC(19,3961,1,7,0)="Copy' should be printed.  The 'Final Office Copy' prints SNOMED codes on a"
^DIC(19,3961,1,8,0)="separate page since they are no longer printed on the SF515."
^DIC(19,3961,20)=""
^DIC(19,3961,25)="P^LRAPP"
^DIC(19,3961,"U")="PRINT ALL REPORTS ON QUEUE"
