^DIC(19,5164,0)="XMMGR-NEW-MAIL-BOX^Create a Mailbox for a user^^R^11748^^^^^^^54^^^^"
^DIC(19,5164,1,0)="^^8^8^2970730^^^^"
^DIC(19,5164,1,1,0)="This option is meant to be used only on systems where Kernel 6 or later"
^DIC(19,5164,1,2,0)="is not running (or when a repair must be made to the 3.7 file).  A mailbox"
^DIC(19,5164,1,3,0)="is created for each new or reinstated user in Kernel 6 and there should be"
^DIC(19,5164,1,4,0)="no need to use this routine unless there was an error setting up the user"
^DIC(19,5164,1,5,0)="or there was a file degradation problem.  Using this option for a user whose"
^DIC(19,5164,1,6,0)="mailbox is partially or wholly set up will not cause data to be lost."
^DIC(19,5164,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5164,1,8,0)="A MAILBOX may be CREATED or REPAIRED using this option."
^DIC(19,5164,20)=""
^DIC(19,5164,25)="NEWMBOX^XM"
^DIC(19,5164,"U")="CREATE A MAILBOX FOR A USER"
^DIC(19,5165,0)="XMMGR-START-BACKGROUND-FILER^START background filer^^R^11748^^^^^^^54^^^^"
^DIC(19,5165,1,0)="^^5^5^2980107^^^^"
^DIC(19,5165,1,1,0)="XMMGR-START-BACKGROUND-FILER reverses the action that was taken when the"
^DIC(19,5165,1,2,0)="option that is its mirror image (XMMGR-STOP-BACKGROUND-FILER) has been"
^DIC(19,5165,1,3,0)="run.  It also will restart the background filer if it disappears from the"
^DIC(19,5165,1,4,0)="system status report.  In order for this option to be effective, the Task"
^DIC(19,5165,1,5,0)="Manager (ZTM) must be running."
^DIC(19,5165,15)=""
^DIC(19,5165,20)=""
^DIC(19,5165,25)="START^XMKPL"
^DIC(19,5165,99)="55010,54425"
^DIC(19,5165,"U")="START BACKGROUND FILER"
^DIC(19,5166,0)="XMMGR-STOP-BACKGROUND-FILER^STOP background filer^^R^11748^^^^^^^54^^^^"
^DIC(19,5166,1,0)="^^6^6^2980107^^"
^DIC(19,5166,1,1,0)="Use this option to STOP the background filer gently at the end of a delivery"
^DIC(19,5166,1,2,0)="before it starts to deliver any further messages.  This only stops local "
^DIC(19,5166,1,3,0)="delivery operations.  ALL LOCAL MAIL DELIVERY WILL STOP until the"
^DIC(19,5166,1,4,0)="XMMGR-START-BACKGROUND-FILER option is run."
^DIC(19,5166,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5166,1,6,0)="STOPS DELIVERY OF LOCAL MAIL GRACEFULLY !!"
^DIC(19,5166,15)=""
^DIC(19,5166,20)=""
^DIC(19,5166,25)="STOP^XMKPL"
^DIC(19,5166,99)="55010,54409"
^DIC(19,5166,"U")="STOP BACKGROUND FILER"
^DIC(19,5167,0)="XMMGR-CHECK-BACKGROUND-FILER^CHECK background filer^^R^11748^^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,5167,1,0)="^^2^2^2891130^"
^DIC(19,5167,1,1,0)="This option tells you if the background filer is running and tells how many"
^DIC(19,5167,1,2,0)="recipients need delivery for each of the messages/responses in the queue."
^DIC(19,5167,25)="CHECK^XMUT5"
^DIC(19,5167,99)="55381,48148"
^DIC(19,5167,"U")="CHECK BACKGROUND FILER"
^DIC(19,5168,0)="XMPURGE-BY-DATE^Purge Messages by Origination Date^^R^11748^XMMGR^^^^^^54^^"
^DIC(19,5168,1,0)="^19.06^60^60^3010514^^^^"
^DIC(19,5168,1,1,0)="You must hold the XMMGR and XMSTAR keys to run this option."
^DIC(19,5168,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,3,0)="XMPURGE-BY-DATE will delete *all* messages originating before a cutoff"
^DIC(19,5168,1,4,0)="date. It will delete those messages from users' mailboxes, and then delete"
^DIC(19,5168,1,5,0)="them from the MESSAGE file, along with any responses chained to them. This"
^DIC(19,5168,1,6,0)="flexible option can be run interactively or scheduled to run on a"
^DIC(19,5168,1,7,0)="recurring basis, the cutoff date can be controlled, users may or may not"
^DIC(19,5168,1,8,0)="be sent a warning bulletin to warn them of the purge ahead of time, and"
^DIC(19,5168,1,9,0)="the option may produce a report to show how many messages and responses it"
^DIC(19,5168,1,10,0)="deleted."
^DIC(19,5168,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,12,0)="When the option is run interactively:"
^DIC(19,5168,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,14,0)="1) It asks for the cutoff date. The default is based on the DATE PURGE"
^DIC(19,5168,1,15,0)="CUTOFF DAYS field (10.03) in the MAILMAN SITE PARAMETERS file (4.3). If"
^DIC(19,5168,1,16,0)="that field is null, it defaults to 730 days (2 years) in the past."
^DIC(19,5168,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,18,0)="2) It asks whether to run the option in Test mode. In Test mode, the"
^DIC(19,5168,1,19,0)="option will not purge any messages, just report how many and which would"
^DIC(19,5168,1,20,0)="have been purged."
^DIC(19,5168,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,22,0)="3) It asks for the output device on which to print the report. The purge"
^DIC(19,5168,1,23,0)="and report can be queued here to run later."
^DIC(19,5168,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,25,0)="4) If it's queued more than 3 days in the future, the option immediately"
^DIC(19,5168,1,26,0)="broadcasts the XM DATE PURGE WARNING bulletin to all users to notify them"
^DIC(19,5168,1,27,0)="of the upcoming purge and give them a chance to save off old messages"
^DIC(19,5168,1,28,0)="beforehand."
^DIC(19,5168,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,30,0)="5) If it's queued less than 3 days in the future, or is not queued, no"
^DIC(19,5168,1,31,0)="bulletin is sent."
^DIC(19,5168,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,33,0)="When the option is scheduled:"
^DIC(19,5168,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,35,0)="1) The option runs at the scheduled time, as specified by the QUEUED TO"
^DIC(19,5168,1,36,0)="RUN AT WHAT TIME field (2) of the OPTION SCHEDULING file (19.2)."
^DIC(19,5168,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,38,0)="2) If the RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY field (6) of file 19.2 is set, the option"
^DIC(19,5168,1,39,0)="is scheduled to run repeatedly."
^DIC(19,5168,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,41,0)="3) It uses the DATE PURGE CUTOFF DAYS field, or the default of 730 days if"
^DIC(19,5168,1,42,0)="it's empty, to calculate the cutoff date."
^DIC(19,5168,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,44,0)="4) It does not run in Test mode."
^DIC(19,5168,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,46,0)="5) If the DATE PURGE GRACE PERIOD field (10.04) of file 4.3 is empty, the"
^DIC(19,5168,1,47,0)="purge runs at the time for which the option is scheduled."
^DIC(19,5168,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,49,0)="6) Otherwise, at the scheduled time the option only broadcasts the XM DATE"
^DIC(19,5168,1,50,0)="PURGE WARNING bulletin to all users and queues a second task to perform"
^DIC(19,5168,1,51,0)="the date purge GRACE PERIOD number of days later."
^DIC(19,5168,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,53,0)="7) If the DEVICE FOR QUEUED JOB OUTPUT field (3) of file 19.2 is empty,"
^DIC(19,5168,1,54,0)="the purge runs without printing a report."
^DIC(19,5168,1,55,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,56,0)="8) Otherwise it prints the report on the selected device."
^DIC(19,5168,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5168,1,58,0)="*Messages in SHARED,MAIL's mailbox and messages in the POSTMASTER's"
^DIC(19,5168,1,59,0)="remote transmit queues and server baskets (including released patch"
^DIC(19,5168,1,60,0)="messages on FORUM) are exempt from the purge."
^DIC(19,5168,25)="ENTER^XMA32"
^DIC(19,5168,99)="55684,50992"
^DIC(19,5168,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,5168,"U")="PURGE MESSAGES BY ORIGINATION "
