^DIC(19,5281,0)="ECTQ RPT SEMI ANNUAL^Summary of Occurrence Screening^^R^.5^^^^^^^189^^1"
^DIC(19,5281,1,0)="^^5^5^2901123^^"
^DIC(19,5281,1,1,0)="This option calls the QA entry point PSM0^QAOSXTRN to produce the"
^DIC(19,5281,1,2,0)="Summary of Occurrence Screening Semi-Annual Report.  The report is"
^DIC(19,5281,1,3,0)="the same as attachment A in circular 10-88-71 supplement number 2."
^DIC(19,5281,1,4,0)="Users may use the 'List QA Screens' option to determine the meaning"
^DIC(19,5281,1,5,0)="of the screen code displayed on this report."
^DIC(19,5281,20)="S X=""QAOSXTRN"" X ^%ZOSF(""TEST"") E  S XQUIT=1 W !,X,"" routine does not exist on your system!,"",!"
^DIC(19,5281,25)="PSM0^QAOSXTRN"
^DIC(19,5281,99)="54740,36815"
^DIC(19,5281,"U")="SUMMARY OF OCCURRENCE SCREENIN"
^DIC(19,5282,0)="ECTQ RPT ADVERSE FINDINGS^Adverse Findings^^R^.5^^^^^^^189^^1"
^DIC(19,5282,1,0)="^^7^7^2901123^^^^"
^DIC(19,5282,1,1,0)="This option calls the QA entry point PAD0^QAOSXTRN to produce the"
^DIC(19,5282,1,2,0)="Adverse Findings report.  This report does not display names or codes"
^DIC(19,5282,1,3,0)="of the involved practitioner.  The report displays occurrences with"
^DIC(19,5282,1,4,0)="care level findings of two or three.  Fields shown include: patient"
^DIC(19,5282,1,5,0)="identification, occurrence date, screen code, status, and level."
^DIC(19,5282,1,6,0)="Users may use the 'List QA Screens' option to determine the meaning"
^DIC(19,5282,1,7,0)="of the screen code displayed on this report."
^DIC(19,5282,20)="S X=""QAOSXTRN"" X ^%ZOSF(""TEST"") E  S XQUIT=1 W !,X,"" routine does not exist on your system!,"",!"
^DIC(19,5282,25)="PAD0^QAOSXTRN"
^DIC(19,5282,99)="54739,41678"
^DIC(19,5282,"U")="ADVERSE FINDINGS"
^DIC(19,5283,0)="ECTS BEDSECTION^Bedsection Workload^^R^.5^^^^^^^189"
^DIC(19,5283,1,0)="^^13^13^2901217^^^^"
^DIC(19,5283,1,1,0)="The user may choose to print this report for a single selected"
^DIC(19,5283,1,2,0)="AMIS segment, or for all segments in the AMIS 334-341 file."
^DIC(19,5283,1,3,0)="If all segments are chosen, the user may select the AMIS"
^DIC(19,5283,1,4,0)="month/year date range for the report.  A separate page prints"
^DIC(19,5283,1,5,0)="for each AMIS month/year selected.  For each segment, the"
^DIC(19,5283,1,6,0)="following totals are shown: operating beds at the end of the month,"
^DIC(19,5283,1,7,0)="discharges, and patient days of care.  The discharge total is"
^DIC(19,5283,1,8,0)="comprised of 'DEATHS, BO AND ABO' plus 'DISCHARGE TO OPT/NSC'"
^DIC(19,5283,1,9,0)="plus 'DISCHARGES NOT OPT/NSC' plus 'TRANSFER OUT'."
^DIC(19,5283,1,10,0)="Alternatively, the user may choose to print the report for a"
^DIC(19,5283,1,11,0)="single segment.  After choosing the segment, the user may"
^DIC(19,5283,1,12,0)="select the AMIS month/year date range.  The same fields will"
^DIC(19,5283,1,13,0)="be displayed for the selected AMIS segment."
^DIC(19,5283,20)=""
^DIC(19,5283,25)="ECTSBED"
^DIC(19,5283,99)="54696,49989"
^DIC(19,5283,"U")="BEDSECTION WORKLOAD"
^DIC(19,5284,0)="ECTS AMIS 334^AMIS 334-341 Hospital Inpatient Data^^R^.5^^^^^^^189"
^DIC(19,5284,1,0)="^^13^13^2901214^^^"
^DIC(19,5284,1,1,0)="When a station loads the new MAS version 5, this option will print the"
^DIC(19,5284,1,2,0)="Hospital Inpatient AMIS from that package.  Until version 5 is loaded,"
^DIC(19,5284,1,3,0)="the option presents, for a user selected month/year, the following"
^DIC(19,5284,1,4,0)="fields:"
^DIC(19,5284,1,5,0)="Total admissions, transfers in, changes in bedsection, deaths, BO and"
^DIC(19,5284,1,6,0)="ABO, discharge to OPT/NSC, discharges not OPT/NSC, transfer out,"
^DIC(19,5284,1,7,0)="changes in bedsection, bed occupants EOM, absent bed occupant EOM,"
^DIC(19,5284,1,8,0)="patient days of care, days of auth absence <96 hrs, wait list in"
^DIC(19,5284,1,9,0)="hospital, wait list not in hospital, wait list service connected,"
^DIC(19,5284,1,10,0)="scheduled admis OPT/NSC status, operating beds EOM, female patients"
^DIC(19,5284,1,11,0)="remaining EOM, 1 day hemodialysis inpatients, and patient days of"
^DIC(19,5284,1,12,0)="care >45.  These fields are displayed by AMIS segment, and within"
^DIC(19,5284,1,13,0)="segment, by division."
^DIC(19,5284,25)="ECTS334"
^DIC(19,5284,99)="54740,38076"
^DIC(19,5284,"U")="AMIS 334-341 HOSPITAL INPATIEN"
^DIC(19,5285,0)="ECTS AMIS 345^AMIS 345-346 NHCU/DOM Patient Data^^R^.5^^^^^^^189"
^DIC(19,5285,1,0)="^^11^11^2901119^"
^DIC(19,5285,1,1,0)="When a station loads the new MAS version 5, this option will print the"
^DIC(19,5285,1,2,0)="AMIS 345-346 from that package.  Until version 5 is loaded,"
^DIC(19,5285,1,3,0)="the option presents, for a user selected month/year, the following"
^DIC(19,5285,1,4,0)="fields:"
^DIC(19,5285,1,5,0)="Admis after rehosp >30 days, admissions--all others, transfers to"
^DIC(19,5285,1,6,0)="similar facil, from ASIH, discharges, deaths, transfers out-similar"
^DIC(19,5285,1,7,0)="facil, to ASIH, bed occupant, absent bed occupants, ASIH, female"
^DIC(19,5285,1,8,0)="bed occupants remaining, discharges-ASIH, died-ASIH, patient days of"
^DIC(19,5285,1,9,0)="care, days of auth abs <96hrs, operating beds EOM, waiting list"
^DIC(19,5285,1,10,0)="EOM (SC), and waiting list EOM (NSC).  These fields are displayed by"
^DIC(19,5285,1,11,0)="AMIS segment, and within segment by division."
^DIC(19,5285,25)="ECTS345"
^DIC(19,5285,99)="54740,38081"
^DIC(19,5285,"U")="AMIS 345-346 NHCU/DOM PATIENT "
^DIC(19,5286,0)="ECTS AMIS 401^AMIS 401 - Patient Care by Vet. Category^^R^.5^^^^^^^189"
^DIC(19,5286,1,0)="^^9^9^2901119^^"
^DIC(19,5286,1,1,0)="Data for this report is pulled from the AMIS Segment file.  For a"
^DIC(19,5286,1,2,0)="selected date range, sorted by division, the report displays the"
^DIC(19,5286,1,3,0)="following fields:  patient classification category, number of"
^DIC(19,5286,1,4,0)="applications for care, inpatient hospital care received,"
^DIC(19,5286,1,5,0)="outpatient care received, and the acceptance rate."
^DIC(19,5286,1,6,0)="Acceptance rate is calculated by this formula:"
^DIC(19,5286,1,7,0)="((hospital care received + NHCU care received + domiciliary care"
^DIC(19,5286,1,8,0)="received + outpatient care received) divided by the total number"
^DIC(19,5286,1,9,0)="of applications for care)."
^DIC(19,5286,25)="ECTSCAT"
^DIC(19,5286,99)="54741,40100"
^DIC(19,5286,"U")="AMIS 401 - PATIENT CARE BY VET"
^DIC(19,5287,0)="ECTS WKLD INP^Inpatient Workload Trends^^R^.5^^^^^^^189"
^DIC(19,5287,1,0)="^^3^3^2901109^^"
^DIC(19,5287,1,1,0)="This report prints the number of discharges for all inpatient locations"
^DIC(19,5287,1,2,0)="for a selected range of fiscal years.  Up to a five year range may be"
^DIC(19,5287,1,3,0)="displayed on the report."
^DIC(19,5287,25)="ECTSNP"
^DIC(19,5287,"U")="INPATIENT WORKLOAD TRENDS"
^DIC(19,5288,0)="ECTS WKLD OP^Outpatient Workload Trends^^R^.5^^^^^^^189"
^DIC(19,5288,1,0)="^^3^3^2901109^"
^DIC(19,5288,1,1,0)="This report prints the number of visits for all outpatient locations"
^DIC(19,5288,1,2,0)="for a selected range of fiscal years.  Up to a five year range may be"
^DIC(19,5288,1,3,0)="displayed on the report."
^DIC(19,5288,25)="ECTSOP"
^DIC(19,5288,"U")="OUTPATIENT WORKLOAD TRENDS"
^DIC(19,5289,0)="ECTD NUR STATS^Nursing Workload/AMIS 1106^^R^.5^^^^^^^189^^1"
^DIC(19,5289,1,0)="^^5^5^2900928^^^"
^DIC(19,5289,1,1,0)="This option displays data from the Nursing Service Workload/ AMIS 1106"
^DIC(19,5289,1,2,0)="Report.  The report is a workload statistics summary for the entire"
^DIC(19,5289,1,3,0)="service based upon the patient classification data accrued for the"
^DIC(19,5289,1,4,0)="AMIS 1106 Report.  The report indicates FTEE statistics on patients"
^DIC(19,5289,1,5,0)="classified no later than 3 PM."
^DIC(19,5289,20)="S ECT1=""NUR"""
^DIC(19,5289,25)="ECTDIR"
^DIC(19,5289,99)="54738,53778"
^DIC(19,5289,"U")="NURSING WORKLOAD/AMIS 1106"
^DIC(19,5290,0)="ECTD LAB STATS^Laboratory Workload^^R^.5^^^^^^^189"
^DIC(19,5290,1,0)="^^5^5^2910105^^^^"
^DIC(19,5290,1,1,0)="This report allows the user to specify the range of accession areas"
^DIC(19,5290,1,2,0)="and the date range.  For the selected areas and dates, the report"
^DIC(19,5290,1,3,0)="displays the total number of samples or specimens, and"
^DIC(19,5290,1,4,0)="the total number of tests performed.  There is a subcount for each"
^DIC(19,5290,1,5,0)="accession area, and a total for all areas for the date range."
^DIC(19,5290,25)="ECTDLAB"
^DIC(19,5290,"U")="LABORATORY WORKLOAD"
^DIC(19,5291,0)="ECTD SUR STATS^Surgery Workload^^R^.5^^^^^^^189"
^DIC(19,5291,1,0)="^^3^3^2901114^^^"
^DIC(19,5291,1,1,0)="For a user selected date range, this report displays number of"
^DIC(19,5291,1,2,0)="completed surgery cases, cancelled surgery cases, and the percent "
^DIC(19,5291,1,3,0)="cancelled. The report is sorted by surgical specialty."
^DIC(19,5291,25)="ECTDSUR"
^DIC(19,5291,"U")="SURGERY WORKLOAD"
^DIC(19,5292,0)="ECTMGR^DHCP Interim Management Support^^M^.5^^^^^^^189^^1"
^DIC(19,5292,1,0)="^^6^6^2910115^^^^"
^DIC(19,5292,1,1,0)="This option is the primary menu driver for the DHCP Interim Management"
^DIC(19,5292,1,2,0)="Support software.  The purpose of the package is to provide "
^DIC(19,5292,1,3,0)="management at the VAMC with easily accessible, reliable, and"
^DIC(19,5292,1,4,0)="useful information about the center, its workload, and its"
^DIC(19,5292,1,5,0)="resources.  The data is primarily from the DHCP software"
^DIC(19,5292,1,6,0)="applications and associated files."
^DIC(19,5292,10,0)="^19.01PI^10^10"
