^DIC(19,5359,0)="LA WATCH^Watch the data in the LA global.^^R^.5^LRVERIFY^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,5359,1,0)="^^2^2^2870204^"
^DIC(19,5359,1,1,0)="This option allows you to watch the accumulation of data in the LA"
^DIC(19,5359,1,2,0)="global.  You may also delete all data stored in a global."
^DIC(19,5359,25)="LAWATCH"
^DIC(19,5359,"U")="WATCH THE DATA IN THE LA GLOBA"
^DIC(19,5360,0)="LA LAB TEST^Test the interface ^^R^.5^LRLIASON^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,5360,1,0)="^^1^1^2900914^^^^"
^DIC(19,5360,1,1,0)="A test mode for the lab interface to show the messages."
^DIC(19,5360,25)="LABTEST"
^DIC(19,5360,"U")="TEST THE INTERFACE "
^DIC(19,5361,0)="LA KB DIFF^Keypad differential for CRT's^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,5361,1,0)="^^40^40^2900913^^^^"
^DIC(19,5361,1,1,0)="This is an option for entering differential counts in hematology using"
^DIC(19,5361,1,2,0)="a CRT keyboard.  It functions very much like an automated instrument"
^DIC(19,5361,1,3,0)="that is connected to the LSI.  The parameters that define what characters"
^DIC(19,5361,1,4,0)="on the keyboard represent what portions of the differential are defined"
^DIC(19,5361,1,5,0)="in the AUTO INSTRUMENT file under the entry KEYBOARD DIFF.  For each"
^DIC(19,5361,1,6,0)="test there are 3 parameters (PARAM).  PARAM 3 is the character on the key-"
^DIC(19,5361,1,7,0)="board that represents that test.  For example, if the test SEGS had a "
^DIC(19,5361,1,8,0)="PARAM 3 equal to 1, then whenever the character 1 was pressed, a SEG would"
^DIC(19,5361,1,9,0)="be added to the total count of SEGS.  Tests that occupy internal numbers"
^DIC(19,5361,1,10,0)="1-27 in the AUTO INSTRUMENT file at the level CHEM TESTS are used in the"
^DIC(19,5361,1,11,0)="entry of the WBC count.  WBC count occupies three rows of characters: (1-9),"
^DIC(19,5361,1,12,0)="(10-18), (19-27).  The keys '-', '!', '?' are reserved functions."
^DIC(19,5361,1,13,0)="  If PARAM 2 is equal to 1 for these tests, then"
^DIC(19,5361,1,14,0)="these tests will be used in the total count of WBC cells."
^DIC(19,5361,1,15,0)="PARAM 2 equal to 2 means that the test is not included in the total count."
^DIC(19,5361,1,16,0)="PARAM 1 is used to change the value of V, which is the value of the test"
^DIC(19,5361,1,17,0)="you are counting or editing.  For example, using the previous example,"
^DIC(19,5361,1,18,0)="whenever you press 1, you are adding 1 to the total count of SEGS, so the"
^DIC(19,5361,1,19,0)="value of SEGS (V at this point) is changed to a percentage of total WBC"
^DIC(19,5361,1,20,0)="cells counted."
^DIC(19,5361,1,21,0)="RBC Morphology tests are located at internal numbers 31-58 occupying"
^DIC(19,5361,1,22,0)="3 rows on the keyboard (31-39), (40-48), (49-58).  "
^DIC(19,5361,1,23,0)="The backslach '\' is used to display the WBC values."
^DIC(19,5361,1,24,0)="To verify data entered with this option use the EA option."
^DIC(19,5361,1,25,0)="The conditions of reviewing and"
^DIC(19,5361,1,26,0)="verifying data entered with this option are the same as any other"
^DIC(19,5361,1,27,0)="automated instrument.  The LOAD/WORK LIST field entries used to test"
^DIC(19,5361,1,28,0)="this option are as follows:"
^DIC(19,5361,1,29,0)="NAME: DIFF"
^DIC(19,5361,1,30,0)="LOAD TRANSFORM: UNIVERSAL"
^DIC(19,5361,1,31,0)="TYPE: SEQUENCE/BATCH"
^DIC(19,5361,1,32,0)="CUPS PER TRAY: 0"
^DIC(19,5361,1,33,0)="FULL TRAY'S ONLY: NO"
^DIC(19,5361,1,34,0)="VERIFY BY: ACCESSION"
^DIC(19,5361,1,35,0)="PROFILE: DIFF"
^DIC(19,5361,1,36,0)="ACCESSION AREA: (what ever is appropriate)"
^DIC(19,5361,1,37,0)="TEST: (what ever is appropriate)"
^DIC(19,5361,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5361,1,39,0)="This option will only work with CRT's that have cursor addressing"
^DIC(19,5361,1,40,0)="capabilities."
^DIC(19,5361,25)="LAKDIFF"
^DIC(19,5361,"U")="KEYPAD DIFFERENTIAL FOR CRT'S"
^DIC(19,5362,0)="LA DOWN^Download a load list to an Instrument.^^R^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,5362,1,0)="^^32^32^2900315^^^"
^DIC(19,5362,1,1,0)="This option invokes a instrument specific routine to take a load list"
^DIC(19,5362,1,2,0)="and prepare it for sending (downloading) to the instrument."
^DIC(19,5362,1,3,0)="The option first asks what instrument to work on, Then tells what load"
^DIC(19,5362,1,4,0)="list will be used.  There is a question asking if the job should be "
^DIC(19,5362,1,5,0)="queued to the background.  Then each cup of each tray that has been"
^DIC(19,5362,1,6,0)="built into the load list is worked on by the instrument specific"
^DIC(19,5362,1,7,0)="routine to prepare it for sending.  The data from this pass is saved"
^DIC(19,5362,1,8,0)="in the load list file in node 2 of the cup entry.  This means that"
^DIC(19,5362,1,9,0)="only one instrument can use the load list at a time.  The lab techs"
^DIC(19,5362,1,10,0)="MUST be carefull in managment of the load list for the instrument."
^DIC(19,5362,1,11,0)="At this time all cups that are on the load list will be sent so that"
^DIC(19,5362,1,12,0)="care must be taken to see that only accessions that should be sent"
^DIC(19,5362,1,13,0)="are built and that after sending the load list is unloaded and"
^DIC(19,5362,1,14,0)="these accessions are not built to the load list when setting up the"
^DIC(19,5362,1,15,0)="load list for the next run."
^DIC(19,5362,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5362,1,17,0)="Tech notes:  This is done in a two pass operation."
^DIC(19,5362,1,18,0)="1. This pass gets the accession and tests from the load list and"
^DIC(19,5362,1,19,0)="builds records for the instrument that are stored in node 2 of the"
^DIC(19,5362,1,20,0)="cup entry (see DD listing)."
^DIC(19,5362,1,21,0)="2. In this pass the data from pass 1 is put together in the form"
^DIC(19,5362,1,22,0)="that is needed for the protocall. For the Ektachem700, LAEKT7D"
^DIC(19,5362,1,23,0)="builds the records that need to be sent, and LAKERM2 adds"
^DIC(19,5362,1,24,0)="the kermit file headers, record head and checksum, and file trailer."
^DIC(19,5362,1,25,0)="This is all controled by LADOWN along with the autoinstrument file."
^DIC(19,5362,1,26,0)="The entry points into LAKERM2 or other protocall routines have"
^DIC(19,5362,1,27,0)="fixed names: START^LAxxx is called once before the first data call."
^DIC(19,5362,1,28,0)="NEXT^LAxxx is called once for each tray before the cup data is "
^DIC(19,5362,1,29,0)="started. (with the ektachem each tray is a file.)"
^DIC(19,5362,1,30,0)="DATA^LAxxx (both parts from the file) is called for each record"
^DIC(19,5362,1,31,0)="found in the load list."
^DIC(19,5362,1,32,0)="END^LAxxx is called once at the end to close out the file."
^DIC(19,5362,25)="LADOWN"
^DIC(19,5362,"U")="DOWNLOAD A LOAD LIST TO AN INS"
^DIC(19,5363,0)="LA MI MICROSCAN L/W BUILD^MicroScan Load Worklist (Build)^^R^.5^^^^^^^53"
^DIC(19,5363,1,0)="^^1^1^2900327^"
^DIC(19,5363,1,1,0)=" This option will build the load worklist for down loading to the Microscan"
^DIC(19,5363,25)="LAMILL"
^DIC(19,5363,"U")="MICROSCAN LOAD WORKLIST (BUILD"
^DIC(19,5364,0)="LA MI VITEK L/W BUILD^Vitek Load Worklist (Build)^^R^.5^^^^^^^53"
^DIC(19,5364,1,0)="^^1^1^2900327^"
^DIC(19,5364,1,1,0)=" This option will build the load worklist for down load to th Vitek."
^DIC(19,5364,25)="LAMIAUT7"
^DIC(19,5364,"U")="VITEK LOAD WORKLIST (BUILD)"
^DIC(19,5365,0)="LA MI VERIFY AUTO^Verify Micro Auto Data^^R^.5^^^^^^^53"
^DIC(19,5365,1,0)="^^6^6^2900913^^^"
^DIC(19,5365,1,1,0)=" This routine allow for the review,editing, and deletion of data produced"
^DIC(19,5365,1,2,0)="by Microbiology Automated Instrumentation."
^DIC(19,5365,1,3,0)="  After the above steps the data can be verified. The steps involved are"
^DIC(19,5365,1,4,0)="patterned after the standard chemistry verification procedures. Simular to"
^DIC(19,5365,1,5,0)="the EA option for chemistry/hematology type instrumentation. Refer"
^DIC(19,5365,1,6,0)="the Microbiology Auto verification guide for more information."
^DIC(19,5365,25)="LAMIAUT0"
^DIC(19,5365,"U")="VERIFY MICRO AUTO DATA"
^DIC(19,5366,0)="LA MI SPECIAL CHARCTER LOAD^Load Vitek Special Characters^^R^.5^^^^^^^53"
^DIC(19,5366,1,0)="^^4^4^2900327^"
^DIC(19,5366,1,1,0)="  There are some code used by Vitek instrumentation which can not"
^DIC(19,5366,1,2,0)="be loaded into the file by Fileman. The character have a special meaning"
^DIC(19,5366,1,3,0)="to Fileman which will prevent them from being loaded into the file."
^DIC(19,5366,1,4,0)="This option provides means for getting this type of data into the file."
^DIC(19,5366,25)="LAMICRA"
^DIC(19,5366,"U")="LOAD VITEK SPECIAL CHARACTERS"
^DIC(19,5367,0)="LA MI MENU^Automated Microbiology Menu^^M^.5^^^^^^^53"
^DIC(19,5367,1,0)="^^2^2^2900327^^"
^DIC(19,5367,1,1,0)=" This menu contains the option associated with Automated Microbiology"
^DIC(19,5367,1,2,0)="interfacing. Appropriate lock should be place on each option if necessary."
^DIC(19,5367,10,0)="^19.01PI^5^5"
^DIC(19,5367,10,1,0)="5363^"
^DIC(19,5367,10,2,0)="5366^"
^DIC(19,5367,10,3,0)="5364^"
^DIC(19,5367,10,4,0)="5365^"
^DIC(19,5367,10,5,0)=5362
^DIC(19,5367,10,"B",5362,5)=""
^DIC(19,5367,10,"B",5363,1)=""
^DIC(19,5367,10,"B",5364,3)=""
^DIC(19,5367,10,"B",5365,4)=""
^DIC(19,5367,10,"B",5366,2)=""
^DIC(19,5367,99)="62728,38009"
^DIC(19,5367,"U")="AUTOMATED MICROBIOLOGY MENU"
^DIC(19,5368,0)="LA ERR PRINT^Lab Error Trap Listing^^R^.5^^^^^^^53"
^DIC(19,5368,1,0)="^^20^20^2900913^^^"
^DIC(19,5368,1,1,0)=" This option is used to list system error involving the Auto Instruments"
^DIC(19,5368,1,2,0)="routines. When an error occurs, LABERR routines stores the variables in"
^DIC(19,5368,1,3,0)="the ^%ZTSK global. The amount of time before these variables are auto"
^DIC(19,5368,1,4,0)="maticly purged is controlled by the field 606 in file 69.9 file."
^DIC(19,5368,1,5,0)="  This option will first present a list of error contained in"
^DIC(19,5368,1,6,0)="the error trap. This is serves as an index giving some basic informa"
^DIC(19,5368,1,7,0)="tion about the error. A complete listing of the errors list can"
^DIC(19,5368,1,8,0)="be obtained byentering '?'."
^DIC(19,5368,1,9,0)="  One can then select a specific error for a detailed listing of"
^DIC(19,5368,1,10,0)="variables. This option does not allow for the restoring of variables"
^DIC(19,5368,1,11,0)="to the user's partition."
^DIC(19,5368,1,12,0)="   NOTE: The Y variable is consumed by the ^%ZTLOAD ROUTINES, therefore"
^DIC(19,5368,1,13,0)="those variables are stored under LABZY(x). However if you enter 'Y'"
^DIC(19,5368,1,14,0)="you will be presented with correct Y(x) variables even though they"
^DIC(19,5368,1,15,0)="are not shown in the conplete display function."
^DIC(19,5368,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(19,5368,1,17,0)="   This option is primarily for programmers or advanced power users."
^DIC(19,5368,1,18,0)="This option is generally of little use to the casual user. But this"
^DIC(19,5368,1,19,0)="does allow the user to relay information to support persons not on the "
^DIC(19,5368,1,20,0)="system."
^DIC(19,5368,25)="LABERRP"
^DIC(19,5368,"U")="LAB ERROR TRAP LISTING"
^DIC(19,5369,0)="LA DIR JOB^Direct Connect Auto-Instrument  Start^^R^.5^^^^^^^53"
^DIC(19,5369,1,0)="^^7^7^2900914^^^"
^DIC(19,5369,1,1,0)=" This option allows one to view Auto-Instrument which are not connected"
^DIC(19,5369,1,2,0)="to the LSI. These instruments are connected directly to the CPU."
^DIC(19,5369,1,3,0)="  USE LRJOB TO VIEW INSTRUMENTS ON THE LSI."
^DIC(19,5369,1,4,0)="      Note:  This only function properly if the instrument is connected"
^DIC(19,5369,1,5,0)="to this CPU, not another. Other words, both the user and the instrument"
^DIC(19,5369,1,6,0)="must be operating on the same CPU.  Beckman CX5 is a direct connect in"
^DIC(19,5369,1,7,0)="strument."
^DIC(19,5369,10,0)="^19.01IP^0^0"
^DIC(19,5369,25)="LADJOB"
^DIC(19,5369,"U")="DIRECT CONNECT AUTO-INSTRUMENT"
^DIC(19,5370,0)="LA AP FICHE^AP Microfiche Archive^^R^.5^^^^^^^53"
^DIC(19,5370,1,0)="^^4^4^2900818^"
^DIC(19,5370,1,1,0)="  This option allow one to archive Anatomical Pathology Reports"
^DIC(19,5370,1,2,0)="to a Microfiche. The tape drive must be previously defined and made"
^DIC(19,5370,1,3,0)="ready before the use of this option. Refer to documentation for "
^DIC(19,5370,1,4,0)="specifics."
^DIC(19,5370,25)="LAPFICH"
^DIC(19,5370,"U")="AP MICROFICHE ARCHIVE"
