^DIC(19,6349,"U")="ALPHA/BETA TEST OPTION USAGE M"
^DIC(19,6350,0)="XMQDOMAINS^Compare Domains in System Against Released List^^R^11748^^^^^^y^54"
^DIC(19,6350,1,0)="^19.06^4^4^3020509^^^^"
^DIC(19,6350,1,1,0)="This option compares the domains in the DOMAIN file with the list of"
^DIC(19,6350,1,2,0)="domains in routine XMUDCHK, and generates a report of domains in"
^DIC(19,6350,1,3,0)="XMUDCHK which are not in the DOMAIN file.  Site managers should consider"
^DIC(19,6350,1,4,0)="whether the missing domains should be added to the DOMAIN file."
^DIC(19,6350,25)="VALID8^XMUDCHK"
^DIC(19,6350,"U")="COMPARE DOMAINS IN SYSTEM AGAI"
^DIC(19,6351,0)="XQALERT DELETE OLD^Delete Old (>14 d) Alerts^^R^1^^^^^^^^^1"
^DIC(19,6351,1,0)="^^11^11^3240430^"
^DIC(19,6351,1,1,0)="WARNING: Failure to run this task daily would create a patient safety "
^DIC(19,6351,1,2,0)="issue!"
^DIC(19,6351,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,6351,1,4,0)="This option must be scheduled to run daily as it not only purges old "
^DIC(19,6351,1,5,0)="alerts, but it is also responsible for forwarding unprocessed alerts to"
^DIC(19,6351,1,6,0)="surrogates, service chiefs and backup reviewers."
^DIC(19,6351,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,6351,1,8,0)="When scheduling, the TASK PARAMETERS field is used to set the number of"
^DIC(19,6351,1,9,0)="retention days. The system will default to a value of 14 if this is not "
^DIC(19,6351,1,10,0)="set. Failure to set this field could result in alerts as recent as 15 days"
^DIC(19,6351,1,11,0)="old being purged from all users."
^DIC(19,6351,2)="n"
^DIC(19,6351,20)="W:'$D(ZTQUEUED) !,""***MUST USE TASKMAN. SEE OPTION DESCRIPTION FOR MORE INFO.***"" D:$D(ZTQUEUED) OLDDEL^XQALERT"
^DIC(19,6351,25)=""
^DIC(19,6351,99)="66956,26945"
^DIC(19,6351,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,6351,"U")="DELETE OLD (>14 D) ALERTS"
^DIC(19,6352,0)="XUSERBLK^Grant Access by Profile^^R^1039^XUMGR^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,6352,1,0)="^^11^11^2901231^"
^DIC(19,6352,1,1,0)="This option allows the adding or editing of one or more users according"
^DIC(19,6352,1,2,0)="to an existing user profile.  The complete profile of the actual or"
^DIC(19,6352,1,3,0)="dummy user, menus and keys included, is copied to the other users.  For"
^DIC(19,6352,1,4,0)="new users, security forms will be generated.  (Use the Help Processor"
^DIC(19,6352,1,5,0)="menu to edit the XUSER COMPUTER ACCOUNT help frame containing the text"
^DIC(19,6352,1,6,0)="of the forms.)  To route forms, be sure that the user profile has a"
^DIC(19,6352,1,7,0)="service/section and that the corresponding entry in the Service/Section"
^DIC(19,6352,1,8,0)="file has a Coordinator.  "
^DIC(19,6352,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,6352,1,10,0)="This option is locked with the XUMGR key and is restricted for use by"
^DIC(19,6352,1,11,0)="systems management staff."
^DIC(19,6352,25)="XUSERBLK"
^DIC(19,6352,99)="55628,33483"
^DIC(19,6352,99.1)="54814,47307"
^DIC(19,6352,"U")="GRANT ACCESS BY PROFILE"
^DIC(19,6353,0)="XTSUMBLD-CHECK^Calculate and Show Checksum Values^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^163"
^DIC(19,6353,1,0)="^^3^3^3060321^"
^DIC(19,6353,1,1,0)="This option calls CHCKSUM^XTSUMBLD to calculate and show the checksum"
^DIC(19,6353,1,2,0)="value for one or more routines in the current account.  This value"
^DIC(19,6353,1,3,0)="will be referenced in Patch Module description for routine patches."
^DIC(19,6353,25)="CHCKSUM^XTSUMBLD"
^DIC(19,6353,"U")="CALCULATE AND SHOW CHECKSUM VA"
^DIC(19,6354,0)="XTLATSET^VAX DSM Device Set-up^^R^.5^XUMGR^^^^^^163^^1"
^DIC(19,6354,1,0)=23
^DIC(19,6354,1,1,0)="Do not run this option without first understanding how it works and what"
^DIC(19,6354,1,2,0)="will result.  It assumes the existence of a SYSPRINT.COM file, a VMS"
^DIC(19,6354,1,3,0)="command file originally distributed by the DHCP Cookbook team.  The"
^DIC(19,6354,1,4,0)="LAT$STARTUP file is also involved in the process."
^DIC(19,6354,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,6354,1,6,0)="This option runs the XTLATSET routine.  The purpose is allow system"
^DIC(19,6354,1,7,0)="managers to keep the Kernel and VMS device tables synchronized with the"
^DIC(19,6354,1,8,0)="least amount of effort.  Those who prefer to use the VMS editor to"
^DIC(19,6354,1,9,0)="to modify the VMS device tables according to changes in the Kernel Device"
^DIC(19,6354,1,10,0)="file will not want to use this option."
^DIC(19,6354,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(19,6354,1,12,0)="This option may be use when first moving the Kernel to a VMS"
^DIC(19,6354,1,13,0)="environment.  It may be used thereafter to rebuild the files if they"
^DIC(19,6354,1,14,0)="are not in sync.  When running this option, it is critical to be in the"
^DIC(19,6354,1,15,0)="configuration that has a complete Kernel Device file, one with all the"
^DIC(19,6354,1,16,0)="VMS devices used by any other configuration.  The VMS files that are built"
^DIC(19,6354,1,17,0)="will automatically be used at next VMS startup."
^DIC(19,6354,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(19,6354,1,19,0)="This option runs the XTLATSET routine to build VMS command"
^DIC(19,6354,1,20,0)="files to coordinate the Kernel and VMS device tables.  It reads from the"
^DIC(19,6354,1,21,0)="Kernel's Device file for _LTA devices and writes three VMS command files."
^DIC(19,6354,1,22,0)="The first file, LT_LOAD.COM, sets up printers in LATCP.  The second,"
^DIC(19,6354,1,23,0)="LT_PRT.DAT, is read by SYSPRINT.COM to set VMS parameters for printers"
^DIC(19,6354,1,24,0)="and other devices and can optionally set up VMS spooling.  The third,"
^DIC(19,6354,1,25,0)="TSC_LOAD.COM, establishes printer parameters to be used in the DECserver's"
^DIC(19,6354,1,26,0)="device tables."
^DIC(19,6354,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(19,6354,1,28,0)="This option should be used with care.  The process should be reviewed"
^DIC(19,6354,1,29,0)="beforehand to be sure that other VMS device settings will not be altered"
^DIC(19,6354,1,30,0)="in an unexpected way.  It is assumed that the system has been"
^DIC(19,6354,1,31,0)="configured with knowledge of DHCP Cookbook recommendations."
^DIC(19,6354,20)="S DIR(0)=""Y"",DIR(""A"")=""Want to proceed"",DIR(""A"",1)=""Do not use unless you are in the startup account"",DIR(""A"",2)=""where the correct VMS files are present!"",DIR(""B"")=""No"",DIR(""?"")=""See option description"" D ^DIR K DIR S:Y'=1!$D(DIRUT) XQUIT="""""
^DIC(19,6354,25)="XTLATSET"
^DIC(19,6354,"U")="VAX DSM DEVICE SET-UP"
^DIC(19,6355,0)="XTMOVE^Move Routines across Volume Sets^^R^.5^XUPROGMODE^^^^^^163"
^DIC(19,6355,1,0)="^^6^6^2910131^^"
^DIC(19,6355,1,1,0)="This option runs the %ZTMOVE routine.  It is used to move routines from one"
^DIC(19,6355,1,2,0)="volume set to another.  A specified set of routines may be moved to a"
^DIC(19,6355,1,3,0)="specified UCI on a different volume set in one step (automatically) or in"
^DIC(19,6355,1,4,0)="two steps.  The second step requires use of the XTMOVE-IN option (Bring in"
^DIC(19,6355,1,5,0)="Sent Routines) in the destination UCI/Volume Set.  This second option will"
^DIC(19,6355,1,6,0)="bring in the sent routines by running IN^%ZTMOVE."
^DIC(19,6355,25)="%ZTMOVE"
^DIC(19,6355,"U")="MOVE ROUTINES ACROSS VOLUME SE"
^DIC(19,6356,0)="XTRDEL^Delete Routines^^R^.5^XUPROGMODE^^^^^^163"
^DIC(19,6356,1,0)="^^1^1^2910130^"
^DIC(19,6356,1,1,0)="This option runs the %ZTRDEL routine to delete one or more routines."
^DIC(19,6356,25)="%ZTRDEL"
^DIC(19,6356,"U")="DELETE ROUTINES"
^DIC(19,6357,0)="XTMOVE-IN^Bring in Sent Routines^^R^.5^XUPROGMODE^^^^^^163"
^DIC(19,6357,1,0)="^^3^3^2910131^^"
^DIC(19,6357,1,1,0)="This option is only to be used after invoking the XTMOVE option (Move"
^DIC(19,6357,1,2,0)="Routines across Volume Sets).  When in the destination UCI/Volume Set,"
^DIC(19,6357,1,3,0)="this option will install the routines that were previously sent."
^DIC(19,6357,25)="IN^%ZTMOVE"
^DIC(19,6357,"U")="BRING IN SENT ROUTINES"
^DIC(19,6358,0)="XTRGRPE^Group Routine Edit^^R^.5^XUPROGMODE^^^^^^163"
^DIC(19,6358,1,0)="^^2^2^2910130^^"
^DIC(19,6358,1,1,0)="This option calls the XTRGRPE routine to edit a group of routines.  Once"
^DIC(19,6358,1,2,0)="several routines are identified, the Kernel %Z editor is called."
^DIC(19,6358,25)="XTRGRPE"
^DIC(19,6358,"U")="GROUP ROUTINE EDIT"
^DIC(19,6359,0)="DI DDUCHK^Check/Fix DD Structure^^R^1^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,6359,1,0)="^^4^4^2930125^"
