^DIC(19,7169,"U")="HL7 MAIN MENU"
^DIC(19,7170,0)="HL TRANSMISSION LOG^Start/Stop Log of HL7 Transmissions^^R^11741^^^^^^^304"
^DIC(19,7170,1,0)="^^9^9^2990726^^"
^DIC(19,7170,1,1,0)="This option is used to start/stop the log of HL7 transmissions.  The log"
^DIC(19,7170,1,2,0)="should normally only be started when you are testing the HL7 interface."
^DIC(19,7170,1,3,0)="After testing is finished, the log should be stopped to save disk space"
^DIC(19,7170,1,4,0)="and reduce global sets.  The log data is stored descendant from the"
^DIC(19,7170,1,5,0)="^TMP(""HL"",ION) global node, where ION is equal to the name of the HL7"
^DIC(19,7170,1,6,0)="Device that was entered into the HL7 Non-DHCP Application Parameter file."
^DIC(19,7170,1,7,0)="It can be purged at any time by killing the ^TMP(""HL"",ION) global.  You"
^DIC(19,7170,1,8,0)="are also asked if you want to purge the data whenever you start/stop the"
^DIC(19,7170,1,9,0)="log."
^DIC(19,7170,25)="LOG^HLUOPT"
^DIC(19,7170,"U")="START/STOP LOG OF HL7 TRANSMIS"
^DIC(19,7171,0)="HL TASK^Initiate Background Task^^R^11741^^^^^^^304"
^DIC(19,7171,1,0)="^^3^3^2920130^"
^DIC(19,7171,1,1,0)="This option creates a background task to start up the lower level protocol"
^DIC(19,7171,1,2,0)="routine for a specific non-DHCP application.  It checks to make sure a"
^DIC(19,7171,1,3,0)="background task does not already exist in Taskmanager."
^DIC(19,7171,25)="HLTASK"
^DIC(19,7171,"U")="INITIATE BACKGROUND TASK"
^DIC(19,7172,0)="HL PURGE TRANSMISSIONS^Purge Messages^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^304"
^DIC(19,7172,1,0)="^19.06^31^31^3010910^^"
^DIC(19,7172,1,1,0)="This option purges entries from the HL7 message files:"
^DIC(19,7172,1,2,0)=" 773 - HL7 MESSAGE ADMINISTRATION"
^DIC(19,7172,1,3,0)=" 772 - HL7 MESSAGE TEXT"
^DIC(19,7172,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7172,1,5,0)="These files contain a record of all outgoing HL7 transmissions and their"
^DIC(19,7172,1,6,0)="status.  Messages are purged if they are in a certain status and are a"
^DIC(19,7172,1,7,0)="certain number of days old.  The default parameters (number of days) are"
^DIC(19,7172,1,8,0)="taken from fields in file 869.3, HL COMMUNICATION SERVER PARAMETERS.  The"
^DIC(19,7172,1,9,0)="fields should be set such that a balance is struck between the need to"
^DIC(19,7172,1,10,0)="keep disk space from filling up and the need to keep messages around long"
^DIC(19,7172,1,11,0)="enough so that they can be investigated in case problems arise."
^DIC(19,7172,1,12,0)="Please see the descriptions of these fields for more information:"
^DIC(19,7172,1,13,0)="  41 - PURGE COMPLETED MESSAGES"
^DIC(19,7172,1,14,0)="  42 - PURGE AWAITING ACK MESSAGES"
^DIC(19,7172,1,15,0)="  43 - PURGE ALL MESSAGES"
^DIC(19,7172,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7172,1,17,0)="Note that the number of days in field 43 must be greater than or equal"
^DIC(19,7172,1,18,0)="to the number of days in field 42, which must be greater than or equal"
^DIC(19,7172,1,19,0)="to the number of days in field 41.  If any of the fields violates this"
^DIC(19,7172,1,20,0)="rule, then the default values of these fields will be used, instead."
^DIC(19,7172,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7172,1,22,0)="To purge entries in an error status, run this option directly and answer"
^DIC(19,7172,1,23,0)="'Yes' to the question about purging them.  It is recommended that entries"
^DIC(19,7172,1,24,0)="in an error status be reviewed before purging.  For this reason, such"
^DIC(19,7172,1,25,0)="messages are NOT purged by automatically recurring scheduled runs of this"
^DIC(19,7172,1,26,0)="option."
^DIC(19,7172,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7172,1,28,0)="It is recommended that this option be scheduled to run once a day to keep"
^DIC(19,7172,1,29,0)="the files from getting too large.  On TaskMan's 'Edit Option Schedule',"
^DIC(19,7172,1,30,0)="the TASK PARAMETERS field is ignored.  Instead, the parameters are taken"
^DIC(19,7172,1,31,0)="from the fields in file 869.3, noted above."
^DIC(19,7172,25)="PURGE^HLUOPT1"
^DIC(19,7172,99)="55644,54515"
^DIC(19,7172,200)="^^1D"
^DIC(19,7172,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,7172,"U")="PURGE MESSAGES"
^DIC(19,7173,0)="HL PRINT PENDING TRANS^Awaiting/Pending Transmission Report (non-TCP)^^R^11741^^^^^^^304"
