^DIC(19,7182,10,"B",9988,9)=""
^DIC(19,7182,99)="59254,80398"
^DIC(19,7182,"U")="TRANSMISSION MANAGEMENT"
^DIC(19,7183,0)="DGYP SD GLOBAL ESTIMATOR^Global Estimator for Scheduling^^A^.5^DGYP IRM^^^^^^307^^1^1"
^DIC(19,7183,1,0)="^^60^60^3050103"
^DIC(19,7183,1,1,0)="In previous versions of PIMS, a patient's outpatient information has"
^DIC(19,7183,1,2,0)="been stored in various files in the VistA database. With the"
^DIC(19,7183,1,3,0)="requirement to checkout all outpatient encounters, it was necessary"
^DIC(19,7183,1,4,0)="to consolidate much of the common outpatient information into one"
^DIC(19,7183,1,5,0)="outpatient encounter file."
^DIC(19,7183,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,7,0)="In PIMS v5.3, the data will reside in the new OUTPATIENT"
^DIC(19,7183,1,8,0)="ENCOUNTER(#409.68) file as well as in the old data structures."
^DIC(19,7183,1,9,0)="This file will hold encounter data for all checked out encounters."
^DIC(19,7183,1,10,0)="This will include information from the following:"
^DIC(19,7183,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,12,0)="         o appointments:  SDAPI - Appointment API"
^DIC(19,7183,1,13,0)="         o add/edits   :  ^SDV()"
^DIC(19,7183,1,14,0)="         o dispositions:  ^DPT(patient,""DIS"",date/time)"
^DIC(19,7183,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,16,0)="The MUMPS global for this file is ^SCE."
^DIC(19,7183,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,19,0)="Also, as part of the checkout process, questions regarding"
^DIC(19,7183,1,20,0)="whether the encounter was related to a service-connected disability,"
^DIC(19,7183,1,21,0)="Agent Orange, ionization and environmental contaminants from the"
^DIC(19,7183,1,22,0)="Persian Gulf war, will be asked when appropriate."
^DIC(19,7183,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,24,0)="This data will be stored in the new OUTPATIENT CLASSIFICATION"
^DIC(19,7183,1,25,0)="(#409.42) file in the ^SDD(409.42) global node."
^DIC(19,7183,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,28,0)="The purpose of this utility is the following:"
^DIC(19,7183,1,29,0)="             1. estimate a one year rate of growth for"
^DIC(19,7183,1,30,0)="                ^SCE using as a base the encounter data"
^DIC(19,7183,1,31,0)="                for the previous 365 days"
^DIC(19,7183,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,33,0)="             2. estimate a one year rate of growth for"
^DIC(19,7183,1,34,0)="                ^SDD(409.42) using as a base the encounter data"
^DIC(19,7183,1,35,0)="                for the previous 365 and the patient demographic"
^DIC(19,7183,1,36,0)="                information"
^DIC(19,7183,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,38,0)="Using these estimates, you can make a better determination"
^DIC(19,7183,1,39,0)="as to where to place this new ^SCE global and how large the"
^DIC(19,7183,1,40,0)="existing ^SDD global will grow."
^DIC(19,7183,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,42,0)="This utility will not affect the current v5.2 functionality in any"
^DIC(19,7183,1,43,0)="way. However, it is recommended that it be queued to run at non-peak"
^DIC(19,7183,1,44,0)="hours.  After the estimations are calculated, the results will be"
^DIC(19,7183,1,45,0)="reported to the user via a MailMan message."
^DIC(19,7183,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,47,0)="Finally, in v5.3, the site will have the ability to capture provider"
^DIC(19,7183,1,48,0)="and diagnostic data as part of the checkout process. Capturing this"
^DIC(19,7183,1,49,0)="data will be site selectable. It is estimated that each provider and"
^DIC(19,7183,1,50,0)="each diagnosis captured for an encounter will use .05 1K blocks."
^DIC(19,7183,1,51,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,52,0)="NOTE: If the site does choose to capture provider data then nurses,"
^DIC(19,7183,1,53,0)="social workers and other providers of care will need to have entries"
^DIC(19,7183,1,54,0)="in the NEW PERSON file and be assigned the PROVIDER security key."
^DIC(19,7183,1,55,0)="Assigning this key will allow selection of these providers during the"
^DIC(19,7183,1,56,0)="checkout process."
^DIC(19,7183,1,57,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7183,1,59,0)="The option should be executed by the IRM staff and is locked with the"
^DIC(19,7183,1,60,0)="DGYP IRM security key."
^DIC(19,7183,15)="Q"
^DIC(19,7183,20)="D EN^DGYPSDE0"
^DIC(19,7183,99)="55642,39748"
^DIC(19,7183,"U")="GLOBAL ESTIMATOR FOR SCHEDULIN"
^DIC(19,7184,0)="DGYP REG CFL REP^Claim Folder Location Conversion Report^^A^.5^^^^^^^307^^1"
^DIC(19,7184,1,0)="35^^38^38^2930714^^^"
^DIC(19,7184,1,1,0)="As part of the PIMS v5.3 installation, the current field in the"
^DIC(19,7184,1,2,0)="v5.2 field (#.312, a free text field) in the PATIENT FILE (#2)"
^DIC(19,7184,1,3,0)="will be renamed to *CLAIMS FOLDER LOCATION.  A new field, CLAIMS "
^DIC(19,7184,1,4,0)="FOLDER LOCATION (#.314, a pointer to the INSTITUTION File (#4)) will"
^DIC(19,7184,1,5,0)="be used by PIMS instead."
^DIC(19,7184,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7184,1,7,0)="During the post init of PIMS v5.3, the Claims Folder Location"
^DIC(19,7184,1,8,0)="conversion will populate this new field.  Only those fields"
^DIC(19,7184,1,9,0)="that are formatted according to the AMIE specification will"
^DIC(19,7184,1,10,0)="be converted.  To be convertible, field #.312 must begin"
^DIC(19,7184,1,11,0)="with the station number of the Claims Folder Location.  The"
^DIC(19,7184,1,12,0)="data in the free-text field will not be deleted as part of"
^DIC(19,7184,1,13,0)="the PIMS v5.3 installation; the data will be deleted, along"
^DIC(19,7184,1,14,0)="with the field at some future release."
^DIC(19,7184,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7184,1,16,0)="If a record is not convertible, users will see UNANSWERED"
^DIC(19,7184,1,17,0)="for the new CLAIMS FOLDER LOCATION on the"
^DIC(19,7184,1,18,0)="ELIGIBILITY STATUS DATA, SCREEN <7> of Registration after"
^DIC(19,7184,1,19,0)="the PIMS v5.3 installation.  It is possible that some sites"
^DIC(19,7184,1,20,0)="will have a large number of unconvertible records.  It is"
^DIC(19,7184,1,21,0)="preferred, but not required that all records be corrected"
^DIC(19,7184,1,22,0)="prior to PIMS v5.3 installation.  Unconvertible records are"
^DIC(19,7184,1,23,0)="not used by AMIE currently; the same condition will exist"
^DIC(19,7184,1,24,0)="after the installation.  This report may help the sites"
^DIC(19,7184,1,25,0)="prioritize their efforts by listing most recently seen"
^DIC(19,7184,1,26,0)="patients first."
^DIC(19,7184,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7184,1,28,0)="The MAS ADPAC should run this option, review the listing"
^DIC(19,7184,1,29,0)="and make any necessary corrections. NO DATA WILL BE CHANGED"
^DIC(19,7184,1,30,0)="as a result of running this report. It is the responsibility"
^DIC(19,7184,1,31,0)="of the MAS ADPAC to review the report and determine if any"
^DIC(19,7184,1,32,0)="changes need to be made."
^DIC(19,7184,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7184,1,34,0)="This report will be delivered in the form of a MailMan message to the"
^DIC(19,7184,1,35,0)="user who selected this option."
^DIC(19,7184,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7184,1,37,0)="This is a queued task.  Since this searches the entire PATIENT File,"
^DIC(19,7184,1,38,0)="you may wish to run it during off-hours."
^DIC(19,7184,20)="D CFLQUE^DGYPREG4"
^DIC(19,7184,99)="55642,55463"
^DIC(19,7184,"U")="CLAIM FOLDER LOCATION CONVERSI"
^DIC(19,7185,0)="DGYP REG TOTVACHK REP^Monetary Benefit Amounts Conversion Report^^A^.5^^^^^^^307^^1^"
^DIC(19,7185,1,0)="39^^40^40^2930714^^"
^DIC(19,7185,1,1,0)="As part of the PIMS v5.3 installation, the current monetary"
^DIC(19,7185,1,2,0)="benefit amount fields (#.3621, AMOUNT OF AID & ATTENDANCE;"
^DIC(19,7185,1,3,0)="#.3622, AMOUNT OF HOUSEBOUND; #.303, AMOUNT OF VA DISABILITY;"
^DIC(19,7185,1,4,0)="#.3624, AMOUNT OF VA PENSION) will be replaced by a new field,"
^DIC(19,7185,1,5,0)="#.36295, TOTAL ANNUAL VA CHECK AMOUNT in the PATIENT File (#2)."
^DIC(19,7185,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7185,1,7,0)="As part of the PIMS v5.3 post init, field #.36295 will be"
^DIC(19,7185,1,8,0)="populated by the value of one of the current monetary benefit"
^DIC(19,7185,1,9,0)="amount fields (#.3621, AMOUNT OF AID & ATTENDANCE; #.3622, AMOUNT OF "
^DIC(19,7185,1,10,0)="HOUSEBOUND; #.303, AMOUNT OF VA DISABILITY;  or #.3624, AMOUNT OF VA "
^DIC(19,7185,1,11,0)="PENSION) if exactly one of them has a positive dollar amount.  Those "
^DIC(19,7185,1,12,0)="records which have two or more of these fields with a positive dollar "
^DIC(19,7185,1,13,0)="amount will not be convertible and the new field will not be "
^DIC(19,7185,1,14,0)="populated.  No data will be deleted as part of this conversion."
^DIC(19,7185,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7185,1,16,0)="This report prints in patient activity order to assist"
^DIC(19,7185,1,17,0)="ADPACs in prioritizing their efforts.  The MAS ADPAC should"
^DIC(19,7185,1,18,0)="run this option, review the listing and make any"
^DIC(19,7185,1,19,0)="necessary corrections."
^DIC(19,7185,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7185,1,21,0)="Some of the older records may have some inconsistent data.  If the "
^DIC(19,7185,1,22,0)="receiving income field (#.36205, RECEIVING A&A BENEFITS?; #.36215, "
^DIC(19,7185,1,23,0)="RECEIVING HOUSEBOUND BENEFITS?; #.36235, RECEIVING A VA PENSION?; or "
^DIC(19,7185,1,24,0)="#.3025,RECEIVING VA DISABILITY?) has been entered 'NO' there should"
^DIC(19,7185,1,25,0)="be no entry in the corresponding dollar  amount field.  The current "
^DIC(19,7185,1,26,0)="software prevents this from happening; however, there may be old data "
^DIC(19,7185,1,27,0)="in which this occurs.  This report will treat these cases as not "
^DIC(19,7185,1,28,0)="having an entry in the dollar amount field.  With the installation of "
^DIC(19,7185,1,29,0)="PIMS v5.3, these inconsistent dollar entries will be deleted."
^DIC(19,7185,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7185,1,31,0)="It is the responsibility of the MAS ADPAC to review the report and "
^DIC(19,7185,1,32,0)="determine if any changes need to be made.  It is possible to run HINQs"
^DIC(19,7185,1,33,0)="on patients to verify amounts and enter this amount or combined"
^DIC(19,7185,1,34,0)="amounts under one of the above monetary benefit amount fields."
^DIC(19,7185,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7185,1,36,0)="This report will be delivered in the form of a MailMan message to the"
^DIC(19,7185,1,37,0)="user who selected this option."
^DIC(19,7185,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7185,1,39,0)="This is a queued task.  Since this searches the entire PATIENT File,"
^DIC(19,7185,1,40,0)="you may wish to run it during off-hours."
^DIC(19,7185,15)=""
^DIC(19,7185,20)="D MBQUE^DGYPREG4"
^DIC(19,7185,99)="55642,56003"
^DIC(19,7185,"U")="MONETARY BENEFIT AMOUNTS CONVE"
^DIC(19,7192,0)="XQSPING^TCP/IP Type Ping Server^^S^1039^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,7192,1,0)="^^3^3^2950214^"
^DIC(19,7192,1,1,0)="This is a PING server that works like PING under TCP/IP.  If you send"
^DIC(19,7192,1,2,0)="a message to this sever it will send it back to you, thereby showing"
^DIC(19,7192,1,3,0)="that the network mail channel is open."
^DIC(19,7192,25)="XTSPING"
^DIC(19,7192,220)="^R^^N^Y^E"
^DIC(19,7192,"U")="TCP/IP TYPE PING SERVER"
^DIC(19,7193,0)="XQLOCK1^All the Keys a User Needs^^R^1039^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,7193,1,0)="^^3^3^2941026^"
^DIC(19,7193,1,1,0)="This option envolkes a routine that follows the menu trees of a user"
^DIC(19,7193,1,2,0)="collects all the keys in to a list that will be needed to effectively"
^DIC(19,7193,1,3,0)="use a menu."
^DIC(19,7193,25)="EN1^XQLOCK"
^DIC(19,7193,"U")="ALL THE KEYS A USER NEEDS"
^DIC(19,7194,0)="XQLOCK2^Keys For a Given Menu Tree^^R^11748^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,7194,1,0)="^^2^2^2941026^"
^DIC(19,7194,1,1,0)="This option runs a routine that searches the children of a given parent"
^DIC(19,7194,1,2,0)="option and compiles a list of the keys needed for that menu tree."
^DIC(19,7194,25)="EN2^XQLOCK"
^DIC(19,7194,"U")="KEYS FOR A GIVEN MENU TREE"
^DIC(19,7195,0)="XQSCHK^Server-type Option Test Server^^S^1039^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,7195,1,0)="^^4^4^2950214^"
^DIC(19,7195,1,1,0)="This server-type option is used to test other servers by examining"
^DIC(19,7195,1,2,0)="the host Option File and returning the data associated with the"
^DIC(19,7195,1,3,0)="target server.  A message is sent to the host site with the name"
^DIC(19,7195,1,4,0)="of the server option to be examined on the first line of the message."
^DIC(19,7195,25)="XQSRV5"
^DIC(19,7195,220)="^R^^^N"
^DIC(19,7195,"U")="SERVER-TYPE OPTION TEST SERVER"
^DIC(19,7196,0)="XQDIAGMENU^Menu Diagrams^^M^.5^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,7196,1,0)="^^2^2^2921022^"
^DIC(19,7196,1,1,0)=" "
^DIC(19,7196,1,2,0)="This menu contains the various methods of diagramming menus."
^DIC(19,7196,10,0)="^19.01PI^3^3"
^DIC(19,7196,10,1,0)="7^"
^DIC(19,7196,10,2,0)="3485^"
^DIC(19,7196,10,3,0)="3484^"
