^DIC(19,8442,10,"C",3,3)=""
^DIC(19,8442,10,"C",4,4)=""
^DIC(19,8442,20)="D ^LRPARAM"
^DIC(19,8442,99)="56214,30164"
^DIC(19,8442,"U")="LMIP REPORTS/DATA COLLECTION"
^DIC(19,8443,0)="LR WKLD LMIP 1^PHASE 1: Move data from 64.1 to 67.9.^^R^.5^LRSUPER^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8443,1,0)="^^8^8^2940509^^^^"
^DIC(19,8443,1,1,0)="  This option performs the first step in producing your monthly report"
^DIC(19,8443,1,2,0)="for LMIP and management. This option's function is to extract from your"
^DIC(19,8443,1,3,0)="workload file (#64.1) ^LRO(64.1, which contains your daily workload, and "
^DIC(19,8443,1,4,0)="roll up the data in a condensed form. The condensed data is stored in the "
^DIC(19,8443,1,5,0)="LAB MONTHLY WORKLOADS file (#67.9)  ^LRO(67.9 )."
^DIC(19,8443,1,6,0)=" This option should be used two days after the last day of the month"
^DIC(19,8443,1,7,0)="you wish to collect data for. Refer to your package documentation for more "
^DIC(19,8443,1,8,0)="information."
^DIC(19,8443,25)="LRCAPAM1"
^DIC(19,8443,"U")="PHASE 1: MOVE DATA FROM 64.1 T"
^DIC(19,8444,0)="LR WKLD LMIP 2^PHASE 2: Collect data for transmit to NDB.^^R^.5^LRSUPER^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8444,1,0)="^^7^7^2940509^^^^"
^DIC(19,8444,1,1,0)=" This option is the second phase of LMIP data reporting. In this step,"
^DIC(19,8444,1,2,0)="data is condensed further and formatted for transmission to the National"
^DIC(19,8444,1,3,0)="Data base. This formatted message is stored in a temporary global from"
^DIC(19,8444,1,4,0)="which a review report will be created for your certification. Care should"
^DIC(19,8444,1,5,0)="be taken with who has access to this menu."
^DIC(19,8444,1,6,0)="  The Laboratory Manager or the Chief Technologist should control this"
^DIC(19,8444,1,7,0)="option."
^DIC(19,8444,25)="LRCAPAM2"
^DIC(19,8444,"U")="PHASE 2: COLLECT DATA FOR TRAN"
^DIC(19,8445,0)="LR WKLD LMIP 3^PHASE 3: Print of data to be sent to NDB.^^R^.5^LRSUPER^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8445,1,0)="^^11^11^2940912^^^^"
^DIC(19,8445,1,1,0)="  This option produces a printable report of the data the system"
^DIC(19,8445,1,2,0)="has collected for the requested reporting period. This data is in"
^DIC(19,8445,1,3,0)="a format which allow transmission to the National Data center. In"
^DIC(19,8445,1,4,0)="order for you to be able to review the compiled data it must be"
^DIC(19,8445,1,5,0)="converted to human readable format."
^DIC(19,8445,1,6,0)="  This report allows you to have a hard copy of the LMIP data for"
^DIC(19,8445,1,7,0)="review. This data cannot be edited. The files which the"
^DIC(19,8445,1,8,0)="data is extracted are editable to a limited degree."
^DIC(19,8445,1,9,0)="  If this report does not conform to your manual workload tally"
^DIC(19,8445,1,10,0)="procedures, a package implementation review may be required."
^DIC(19,8445,1,11,0)="  Consult your Package documentation for further information."
^DIC(19,8445,25)="LRCAPAM3"
^DIC(19,8445,"U")="PHASE 3: PRINT OF DATA TO BE S"
^DIC(19,8446,0)="LR WKLD LMIP 4^PHASE 4: Create E-mail message for NDB.^^R^.5^LRSUPER^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8446,1,0)="12^^12^12^2940509^^"
^DIC(19,8446,1,1,0)=" This is the last phase of data collection leading to the creation"
^DIC(19,8446,1,2,0)="of a mail message containing LMIP data. This option will take the"
^DIC(19,8446,1,3,0)="formatted data from the temporary file and place the data into "
^DIC(19,8446,1,4,0)="appropriately formatted mail message. The mail message will be sent only"
^DIC(19,8446,1,5,0)="to the user creating the message. The User must forward the message"
^DIC(19,8446,1,6,0)="via mailman options to the National Data location."
^DIC(19,8446,1,7,0)="  Consult LMIP directive for the proper forwarding procedures."
^DIC(19,8446,1,8,0)="  If for some reason the message creation fails, this option can be"
^DIC(19,8446,1,9,0)="ran multiple times. The National Data center will only accept 1 "
^DIC(19,8446,1,10,0)="data message for a single month. Send only one message to the National"
^DIC(19,8446,1,11,0)="Data base. The second one for any month will not be processed."
^DIC(19,8446,1,12,0)="  Consult your package documentation for more information."
^DIC(19,8446,25)="LRCAPAM4"
^DIC(19,8446,"U")="PHASE 4: CREATE E-MAIL MESSAGE"
^DIC(19,8447,0)="LRLISTE^Summary list (extended supervisors')^^R^.5^LRSUPER^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8447,1,0)="^^2^2^2930301^"
^DIC(19,8447,1,1,0)="All results for a given accession area(s) for a given date and range of"
^DIC(19,8447,1,2,0)="accession numbers."
^DIC(19,8447,25)="LRLISTE"
^DIC(19,8447,"U")="SUMMARY LIST (EXTENDED SUPERVI"
^DIC(19,8448,0)="LRMITS^Microbiology Trend Report^^R^10000000020^^2877^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8448,1,0)="^19.06^8^8^3050511^^^^"
^DIC(19,8448,1,1,0)="The antimicrobial trend report is used to compare counts of organisms and"
^DIC(19,8448,1,2,0)="patterns of antibiotic susceptibility.  Different types of reports can"
^DIC(19,8448,1,3,0)="be generated.  The types of reports are categorized by: organism, specimen,"
^DIC(19,8448,1,4,0)="collection sample, patient, physician, and location.  Specific criteria"
^DIC(19,8448,1,5,0)="can be applied to all report types.  Criteria include: specific types"
^DIC(19,8448,1,6,0)="of organisms, isolates collected after a specified time from admission,"
^DIC(19,8448,1,7,0)="merge criteria, antibiotic patterns, and detailed reports.  These reports"
^DIC(19,8448,1,8,0)="can be printed by division or for selected divisions."
^DIC(19,8448,25)="LRMITS"
^DIC(19,8448,99)="55431,33599"
^DIC(19,8448,"U")="MICROBIOLOGY TREND REPORT"
^DIC(19,8449,0)="LRCAPMA^Workload Statistics by Major Section^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8449,1,0)="^^1^1^2940331^^"
^DIC(19,8449,1,1,0)="Workload report summed by LAB division, major section and subsection."
^DIC(19,8449,25)="LRCAPMA"
^DIC(19,8449,"U")="WORKLOAD STATISTICS BY MAJOR S"
^DIC(19,8450,0)="LRCAPDL^WKLD log file download^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8450,1,0)="^^9^9^2940509^^^^"
^DIC(19,8450,1,1,0)="  This option can be used to download data from the WKLD LOG FILE (64.03) to"
^DIC(19,8450,1,2,0)="spread sheets. The user is able to select the character used to separate"
^DIC(19,8450,1,3,0)="data to match the spread sheet used. The '^' character is not allowed as "
^DIC(19,8450,1,4,0)="a field separator and the character may not be null. The output can be "
^DIC(19,8450,1,5,0)="captured in an ASCII file to be later imported into a spread sheet."
^DIC(19,8450,1,6,0)="  Not all sites will make use of the option or this file. The field"
^DIC(19,8450,1,7,0)="that controls the collection of the data into the file is located"
^DIC(19,8450,1,8,0)="in the LABORATORY SITE file (#69.9) COLLECT WKLD LOG FILE DATA (#616)."
^DIC(19,8450,1,9,0)="  To stop data transfer, press return/enter key"
^DIC(19,8450,25)="LRCAPDL"
^DIC(19,8450,99)="55621,30605"
^DIC(19,8450,"U")="WKLD LOG FILE DOWNLOAD"
^DIC(19,8451,0)="LRRP8^Workload statistics by accession area and shift^^R^.5^LRSUPER^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8451,1,0)="^^11^11^2940328^^^^"
^DIC(19,8451,1,1,0)="This report is a summary of workload statistics broken down by work shifts,"
^DIC(19,8451,1,2,0)="time ranges, accession areas, WKLD codes and date ranges.  The user is asked"
^DIC(19,8451,1,3,0)="for the institution, accession areas, date range, WKLD codes and a time range"
^DIC(19,8451,1,4,0)="or a set of shifts, each with a specific time range.  The statistics will"
^DIC(19,8451,1,5,0)="show subtotal WKLD code counts for each shift/time range and counts for each"
^DIC(19,8451,1,6,0)="WKLD code within a shift.  A percentage for each CAP code within a shift"
^DIC(19,8451,1,7,0)="subtotal will be calculated.  This information will be summarized for each"
^DIC(19,8451,1,8,0)="accession area, then an all-inclusive summary will be shown.  After the"
^DIC(19,8451,1,9,0)="detailed and summary sections, a section on workload data entered manually"
^DIC(19,8451,1,10,0)="(Standard, QC, Repeat and Manual) will print and finally a section on"
^DIC(19,8451,1,11,0)="workload comments."
^DIC(19,8451,25)="EN^LRRP8"
^DIC(19,8451,99)="54900,30168"
^DIC(19,8451,"U")="WORKLOAD STATISTICS BY ACCESSI"
^DIC(19,8452,0)="LRRP5^Lab orders by collection type^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8452,1,0)="^^2^2^2940328^^^^"
^DIC(19,8452,1,1,0)="Print a report of ordered tests for a collection type (LAB COLLECT, SEND"
^DIC(19,8452,1,2,0)="PATIENT or WARD COLLECT) and a date."
^DIC(19,8452,25)="LRRP5"
^DIC(19,8452,"U")="LAB ORDERS BY COLLECTION TYPE"
^DIC(19,8453,0)="LRCAPAM5^RCS-CDR/LMIP REPORT^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8453,1,0)="^^2^2^2940331^^^^"
^DIC(19,8453,1,1,0)="  This option will provide a report based on treating specialty codes."
^DIC(19,8453,1,2,0)="This report is derived from the LAB MONTHLY WORKLOADS (#67.9) file."
^DIC(19,8453,25)="LRCAPAM5"
^DIC(19,8453,"U")="RCS-CDR/LMIP REPORT"
^DIC(19,8454,0)="LRCAPD^Workload code list^^R^.5^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,8454,25)="LRCAPD"
^DIC(19,8454,"U")="WORKLOAD CODE LIST"
