^DIC(19,9895,"U")="REMINDER TEST"
^DIC(19,9898,0)="PXRR CASELOAD PROFILE BY CL^Caseload Profile by Clinic^^R^10958^^^^^^y^^^1"
^DIC(19,9898,1,0)="^^48^48^2960809^"
^DIC(19,9898,1,1,0)="This report generates a profile of the patients in a clinic's caseload"
^DIC(19,9898,1,2,0)="given a selected date range.  One or more clinics or a stop code may be"
^DIC(19,9898,1,3,0)="selected to represent the caseload. If stop code is selected, a report is"
^DIC(19,9898,1,4,0)="generated for each clinic within that stop code.  The percent and overall"
^DIC(19,9898,1,5,0)="mean calculations are based on the patient data for all of the clinics"
^DIC(19,9898,1,6,0)="selected.  Where only one clinic is selected, these values are not"
^DIC(19,9898,1,7,0)="applicable."
^DIC(19,9898,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9898,1,9,0)="Note: There must be at least one PCE encounter within the selected date"
^DIC(19,9898,1,10,0)="  range, or the report will not be generated, even though there may be"
^DIC(19,9898,1,11,0)="  lab, radiology, and outpatient pharmacy occasions of service within the"
^DIC(19,9898,1,12,0)="  other timeframes (selected date range plus six and twelve months"
^DIC(19,9898,1,13,0)="  previous to the range)"
^DIC(19,9898,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9898,1,15,0)="This report combines PCE encounter, Lab, Radiology, Outpatient"
^DIC(19,9898,1,16,0)="Pharmacy and Admissions data.  It provides a profile of the patients"
^DIC(19,9898,1,17,0)="making up a clinic's caseload, over a representative period of time."
^DIC(19,9898,1,18,0)="Clinical staff will decide the appropriate date range.  Report areas are"
^DIC(19,9898,1,19,0)="demographics of clinic caseload, preventive medicine, quality of care"
^DIC(19,9898,1,20,0)="markers, and utilization.   Patient age, diagnosis, gender, Lab assay, RX,"
^DIC(19,9898,1,21,0)="and procedure are all used to generate the patient profile."
^DIC(19,9898,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9898,1,23,0)="There are three separate timeframes for the report:"
^DIC(19,9898,1,24,0)="      SELECTED DATE RANGE"
^DIC(19,9898,1,25,0)="      SIX MONTHS PREVIOUS TO THE SELECTED ENDING DATE"
^DIC(19,9898,1,26,0)="      TWELVE MONTHS PREVIOUS TO THE SELECTED ENDING DATE"
^DIC(19,9898,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9898,1,28,0)="Search ranges are listed at the top of each report section:"
^DIC(19,9898,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9898,1,30,0)="  DEMOGRAPHICS are based on the selected date range. "
^DIC(19,9898,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9898,1,32,0)="  PREVENTIVE MEDICINE is based on 1)ICD codes recorded in PCE encounter"
^DIC(19,9898,1,33,0)="diagnoses and 2) Radiology results for the twelve months previous to the"
^DIC(19,9898,1,34,0)="selected ending date."
^DIC(19,9898,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9898,1,36,0)="  QUALITY OF CARE MARKERS are based on Laboratory results, PCE encounter"
^DIC(19,9898,1,37,0)="diagnoses, and Scheduling data for the six months previous to the selected"
^DIC(19,9898,1,38,0)="ending date."
^DIC(19,9898,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9898,1,40,0)="  UTILIZATION data is based on PCE encounters, and outpatient pharmacy"
^DIC(19,9898,1,41,0)="prescriptions for the twelve months previous to selected ending date in "
^DIC(19,9898,1,42,0)="the selected date range."
^DIC(19,9898,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9898,1,44,0)="The six and twelve month range profiles would not be expected to change"
^DIC(19,9898,1,45,0)="much from month to month.  How long the report takes to run will vary"
^DIC(19,9898,1,46,0)="depending upon the number of selected clinics, the number of encounters"
^DIC(19,9898,1,47,0)="within that clinic, and the complexity of the patient data for any"
^DIC(19,9898,1,48,0)="selected clinic."
^DIC(19,9898,20)="S PXRRDEMG=1,PXRRCNUM="""""
^DIC(19,9898,25)="PXRRPCE"
^DIC(19,9898,"U")="CASELOAD PROFILE BY CLINIC"
^DIC(19,9899,0)="PXRR LOCATION ENCOUNTER COUNTS^Location Encounter Counts^^R^10958^^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,9899,1,0)="^^29^29^2960515^"
^DIC(19,9899,1,1,0)="This report provides the number of PCE outpatient encounters within an"
^DIC(19,9899,1,2,0)="encounter date range, by location."
^DIC(19,9899,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9899,1,4,0)="The location report selection criteria can be based on facility, hospital"
^DIC(19,9899,1,5,0)="location(s), or clinic stop(s). The selection criteria are:"
^DIC(19,9899,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9899,1,7,0)="     Facility - select the facilities encounters to include in the report."
^DIC(19,9899,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9899,1,9,0)="     Service Category - only encounters with the specified service"
^DIC(19,9899,1,10,0)="     category or categories will be used to generate the report. This"
^DIC(19,9899,1,11,0)="     defaults to ""AI"" for Ambulatory encounters and clinic encounters"
^DIC(19,9899,1,12,0)="     where the patient had an inpatient status."
^DIC(19,9899,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9899,1,14,0)="     Encounter Date Range - only encounters that fall within the specified"
^DIC(19,9899,1,15,0)="     date range will be used to generate the report."
^DIC(19,9899,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9899,1,17,0)="     Location criteria can specify All Hospital Locations, Selected"
^DIC(19,9899,1,18,0)="     Hospital Locations, All Clinic Stops, or Selected Clinic Stops."
^DIC(19,9899,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9899,1,20,0)="         Hospital Locations - only encounters, where the"
^DIC(19,9899,1,21,0)="         encounter's hospital location is the same as one of the selected"
^DIC(19,9899,1,22,0)="         hospital locations, will be used to generate the report."
^DIC(19,9899,1,23,0)="         "
^DIC(19,9899,1,24,0)="         Clinic Stops - only encounters, where the encounter's clinic stop"
^DIC(19,9899,1,25,0)="         is the same as one of the selected clinic stops, will be used to"
^DIC(19,9899,1,26,0)="         generate the report."
^DIC(19,9899,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9899,1,28,0)="The report lists the number of encounters alphabetically by the location"
^DIC(19,9899,1,29,0)="criteria selected. "
^DIC(19,9899,20)=""
^DIC(19,9899,25)="MAIN^PXRRLCD"
^DIC(19,9899,"U")="LOCATION ENCOUNTER COUNTS"
^DIC(19,9900,0)="PXRR MOST FREQUENT DIAGNOSES^Diagnosis Ranked by Frequency^^R^10958^^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,9900,1,0)="^^67^67^2960515^"
^DIC(19,9900,1,1,0)="This report produces two lists: most frequent diagnoses (ICD) and most"
^DIC(19,9900,1,2,0)="frequent diagnostic categories.  The list entries are ordered with the"
^DIC(19,9900,1,3,0)="most frequent encounter diagnosis first.  The most frequent"
^DIC(19,9900,1,4,0)="diagnosis categories list is based on the ICD diagnostic category related"
^DIC(19,9900,1,5,0)="to each diagnosis in the frequent diagnosis list."
^DIC(19,9900,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,7,0)="The report can be generated using a number of different selection"
^DIC(19,9900,1,8,0)="criteria. The selection criteria are:"
^DIC(19,9900,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,10,0)="  Facility - select the facilities encounters to include in the report."
^DIC(19,9900,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,12,0)="  Primary Diagnoses only or All Diagnoses - if primary is selected then"
^DIC(19,9900,1,13,0)="  only primary diagnosis associated with an encounter will be included in"
^DIC(19,9900,1,14,0)="  the report.  All diagnosis will include Primary and secondary diagnoses"
^DIC(19,9900,1,15,0)="  associated with an encounter.  "
^DIC(19,9900,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,17,0)="  Encounter Date Range - only encounters that fall within the specified"
^DIC(19,9900,1,18,0)="  date range will be used to generate the report."
^DIC(19,9900,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,20,0)="  Number of most frequent diagnoses - this will determine how many"
^DIC(19,9900,1,21,0)="  diagnoses and diagnoses categories will be listed on the report. For"
^DIC(19,9900,1,22,0)="  example, if 20 was input for this criteria, the report would list up to"
^DIC(19,9900,1,23,0)="  20 of the most frequent diagnoses found associated with encounters.  The"
^DIC(19,9900,1,24,0)="  diagnoses are ranked from most frequent to least frequent.  The same is"
^DIC(19,9900,1,25,0)="  true for diagnostic categories.  If the encounters contained less than"
^DIC(19,9900,1,26,0)="  20 different diagnoses, then the report would list all the different"
^DIC(19,9900,1,27,0)="  diagnoses that were found."
^DIC(19,9900,1,28,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,29,0)="The remaining criteria are optional for singling out diagnosis entries"
^DIC(19,9900,1,30,0)="based on other encounter or patient data. The user can accept the default"
^DIC(19,9900,1,31,0)="""other"" encounter/patient criteria which is all VA Clinic encounters"
^DIC(19,9900,1,32,0)="(Service Category of ""A"" or ""I"") for all patients."
^DIC(19,9900,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,34,0)="Other encounter/patient report selection criteria:"
^DIC(19,9900,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,36,0)="   Service Category - only encounters with the specified service"
^DIC(19,9900,1,37,0)="   category or categories will be used to generate the report. This"
^DIC(19,9900,1,38,0)="   defaults to ""AI"" for Ambulatory encounters and encounters at a clinic"
^DIC(19,9900,1,39,0)="   where the patient had an inpatient status."
^DIC(19,9900,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,41,0)="   Clinic Stop Code - only encounters with the specified list of clinic"
^DIC(19,9900,1,42,0)="   stop codes will be used to generate the report."
^DIC(19,9900,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,44,0)="   Provider criteria can specify All Providers, Primary"
^DIC(19,9900,1,45,0)="   Providers, Selected Providers, or Selected Provider Classes."
^DIC(19,9900,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,47,0)="        Providers - only encounters, where one of the encounter providers"
^DIC(19,9900,1,48,0)="        is the same as one of the providers selected, will be used to"
^DIC(19,9900,1,49,0)="        generate the report."
^DIC(19,9900,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,51,0)="        Primary Providers - only encounters, where one of the encounter"
^DIC(19,9900,1,52,0)="        providers is designated as a Primary provider, will be used to"
^DIC(19,9900,1,53,0)="        generate the report."
^DIC(19,9900,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,55,0)="        Provider class - only encounters, where one of the encounter"
^DIC(19,9900,1,56,0)="        providers has the same provider class as one of the providers"
^DIC(19,9900,1,57,0)="        classes selected, will be used to generate the report."
^DIC(19,9900,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,59,0)="   Patient Date of Birth Range - only encounters, where the patient's date"
^DIC(19,9900,1,60,0)="   of birth falls in the specified range, will be used to generate the"
^DIC(19,9900,1,61,0)="   report."
^DIC(19,9900,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,63,0)="   Patient Sex - only encounters, where the patient's sex matches the"
^DIC(19,9900,1,64,0)="   specified sex, will be used to generate the report."
^DIC(19,9900,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9900,1,66,0)="To include all encounters, ignoring all defaults for the other criteria,"
^DIC(19,9900,1,67,0)="the user may specify ""A"" for All Encounters at the Other criteria prompt."
^DIC(19,9900,20)=""
^DIC(19,9900,25)="MAIN^PXRRFDD"
^DIC(19,9900,"U")="DIAGNOSIS RANKED BY FREQUENCY"
^DIC(19,9901,0)="PXRR PROVIDER ENCOUNTER COUNTS^Provider Encounter Counts^^R^10958^^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,9901,1,0)="^^46^46^2960515^"
^DIC(19,9901,1,1,0)="This report provides the number of PCE outpatient encounters within an"
^DIC(19,9901,1,2,0)="encounter date range, by provider.  The user specifies report selection"
^DIC(19,9901,1,3,0)="criteria and then chooses either a summary report or detailed report."
^DIC(19,9901,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,5,0)="The report can be generated using a number of different selection"
^DIC(19,9901,1,6,0)="criteria. The selection criteria are:"
^DIC(19,9901,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,8,0)="    Facility - select the facilities encounters to include in the report."
^DIC(19,9901,1,9,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,10,0)="    Service Category - only encounters with the specified service"
^DIC(19,9901,1,11,0)="    category or categories will be used to generate the report. This"
^DIC(19,9901,1,12,0)="    defaults to ""AI"" for Ambulatory encounters and clinic encounters"
^DIC(19,9901,1,13,0)="    where the patient had an inpatient status."
^DIC(19,9901,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,15,0)="    Provider criteria can specify All Providers, Primary Providers,"
^DIC(19,9901,1,16,0)="    Selected Providers, or Selected Provider Classes."
^DIC(19,9901,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,18,0)="        Providers - only encounters, where one of the encounter providers"
^DIC(19,9901,1,19,0)="        is the same as one of the providers selected, will be used to"
^DIC(19,9901,1,20,0)="        generate the report."
^DIC(19,9901,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,22,0)="        Primary Providers - only encounters, where one of the encounter"
^DIC(19,9901,1,23,0)="        providers is designated as a Primary provider, will be used to"
^DIC(19,9901,1,24,0)="        generate the report."
^DIC(19,9901,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,26,0)="        Provider class - only encounters, where one of the encounter"
^DIC(19,9901,1,27,0)="        providers has the same provider class as one of the providers"
^DIC(19,9901,1,28,0)="        classes selected, will be used to generate the report."
^DIC(19,9901,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,30,0)="    Encounter Date Range - only encounters that fall within the specified"
^DIC(19,9901,1,31,0)="    date range will be used to generate the report."
^DIC(19,9901,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,34,0)="Once the report criteria is specified, the user can request a detailed"
^DIC(19,9901,1,35,0)="or a summary report."
^DIC(19,9901,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,37,0)="The detailed report lists the number of encounters by encounter date and"
^DIC(19,9901,1,38,0)="hospital location for each provider. The clinic stop code for the hospital"
^DIC(19,9901,1,39,0)="location is in parenthesis, followed by a string of letters corresponding"
^DIC(19,9901,1,40,0)="to the service categories represented by the encounters found.  The legend"
^DIC(19,9901,1,41,0)="for the service categories is included on the top of the report. For"
^DIC(19,9901,1,42,0)="example, if on a particular day the provider had three ambulatory"
^DIC(19,9901,1,43,0)="encounters and two telecommunications encounters, the string would be ""AT"""
^DIC(19,9901,1,44,0)="and the number of encounters would be five."
^DIC(19,9901,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9901,1,46,0)="The summary report lists the total number of encounters for each provider."
^DIC(19,9901,20)=""
^DIC(19,9901,25)="MAIN^PXRRPRD"
^DIC(19,9901,"U")="PROVIDER ENCOUNTER COUNTS"
^DIC(19,9902,0)="PX REPORT PARAMETER EDIT^PCE Report Parameter Edit^^E^10958^^^^^^^507^"
^DIC(19,9902,1,0)="^^9^9^2960418^"
^DIC(19,9902,1,1,0)="This option is used to define parameters that will be used by the PCE"
^DIC(19,9902,1,2,0)="Report Module.  The user will need to identify which clinics are viewed by"
^DIC(19,9902,1,3,0)="clinicians as being Emergency Room clinics.  The user will also need to"
^DIC(19,9902,1,4,0)="identify the lab test names that are used by your site to identify the"
^DIC(19,9902,1,5,0)="following types of Lab tests: Glucose, Cholesterol, LDL Cholesterol, and"
^DIC(19,9902,1,6,0)="HBA1C."
^DIC(19,9902,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9902,1,8,0)="To get a print out of current definitions in the PCE Parameters fields for"
^DIC(19,9902,1,9,0)="these fields, use the PCE HS/RPT Parameters Print."
^DIC(19,9902,30)="PX(815,"
^DIC(19,9902,31)="QAMEZL"
^DIC(19,9902,50)="PX(815,"
^DIC(19,9902,51)="801:805"
^DIC(19,9902,53)="BACKOUTOK"
^DIC(19,9902,"U")="PCE REPORT PARAMETER EDIT"
^DIC(19,9903,0)="PXCE ENCOUNTER ENTRY SUPER^PCE Encounter Data Entry - Supervisor^^A^1^^^^^^^507^^1^1"
^DIC(19,9903,1,0)="^19.06^14^14^3070806^^^^"
^DIC(19,9903,1,1,0)="This option allows for the add/edit/deleting of information on certain"
^DIC(19,9903,1,2,0)="encounters that most users should not be changing and the other PCE"
^DIC(19,9903,1,3,0)="options will not allow to be changed. This option also does not"
^DIC(19,9903,1,4,0)="conditionally not ask some fields, i.e. it always ask all of the fields."
^DIC(19,9903,1,5,0)="In addition this option allows users to document a clinical encounter in"
^DIC(19,9903,1,6,0)="the V-files (visit related files), and can also delete any V-File"
^DIC(19,9903,1,7,0)="encounter entries, even though they are not the creator of the entries."
^DIC(19,9903,1,8,0)="The data entered via this option includes visit information (where and"
^DIC(19,9903,1,9,0)="when), and the following clinical data related to the visit: providers of"
^DIC(19,9903,1,10,0)="care, problems treated, procedures and treatments done, and immunizations,"
^DIC(19,9903,1,11,0)="skin tests, and patient education given."
^DIC(19,9903,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9903,1,13,0)="This option is intended for the Coordinator for PCE and/or supervisor of"
^DIC(19,9903,1,14,0)="the encounter data entry staff."
^DIC(19,9903,10.1)="SUP"
^DIC(19,9903,15)="K SDSCEDIT"
^DIC(19,9903,20)="S SDSCEDIT=1 D EN^PXCE(""S"")"
^DIC(19,9903,99.1)="56179,36316"
^DIC(19,9903,"U")="PCE ENCOUNTER DATA ENTRY - SUP"
^DIC(19,9904,0)="PX IRM MAIN MENU^PCE IRM Main Menu^^M^10958^^^^^^^507"
