^DIC(19,9984,0)="PRCN TURN WHSE MENU^Warehouse Turn-In Menu^^M^11601^PRCNWHSE^^^^^^508^^^1^^1"
^DIC(19,9984,1,0)="^^2^2^2960823^^^^"
^DIC(19,9984,1,1,0)="This menu option is to be assigned to the Warehouse users for"
^DIC(19,9984,1,2,0)="turn-ins."
^DIC(19,9984,10,0)="^19.01IP^2^2"
^DIC(19,9984,10,1,0)="9966^^1"
^DIC(19,9984,10,2,0)="9980^^2"
^DIC(19,9984,10,"B",9966,1)=""
^DIC(19,9984,10,"B",9980,2)=""
^DIC(19,9984,15)="K STA"
^DIC(19,9984,20)=""
^DIC(19,9984,26)="S STA=22 D TMSG^PRCNUTL"
^DIC(19,9984,99)="62195,30816"
^DIC(19,9984,99.1)="56691,41425"
^DIC(19,9984,"U")="WAREHOUSE TURN-IN MENU"
^DIC(19,9985,0)="PRCN NX CONC MENU^Equipment Concurring Official Menu^^M^11601^^^^^^^508^^^^^1"
^DIC(19,9985,1,0)="^^2^2^2960823^^"
^DIC(19,9985,1,1,0)="This menu option is to be assigned to those individuals who may"
^DIC(19,9985,1,2,0)="act as concurring officials for equipment requests."
^DIC(19,9985,10,0)="^19.01IP^1^1"
^DIC(19,9985,10,1,0)="9970^^1"
^DIC(19,9985,10,"B",9970,1)=""
^DIC(19,9985,20)=""
^DIC(19,9985,26)="S STA=9 D EMSG^PRCNUTL"
^DIC(19,9985,99)="62195,30816"
^DIC(19,9985,"U")="EQUIPMENT CONCURRING OFFICIAL "
^DIC(19,9986,0)="PRCN NX ENG MENU^Engineering Equipment Request Menu^^M^11601^PRCNEN^^^^^^508^^^^^1"
^DIC(19,9986,1,0)="^^3^3^2960823^^"
^DIC(19,9986,1,1,0)="This menu option is the main menu option for Engineering"
^DIC(19,9986,1,2,0)="personnel who may review and process non-expendable equipment"
^DIC(19,9986,1,3,0)="requests."
^DIC(19,9986,10,0)="^19.01IP^1^1"
^DIC(19,9986,10,1,0)="9964^^1"
^DIC(19,9986,10,"B",9964,1)=""
^DIC(19,9986,20)=""
^DIC(19,9986,26)="F STA=8,26,30 D EMSG^PRCNUTL"
^DIC(19,9986,99)="62195,30816"
^DIC(19,9986,99.1)="56797,45581"
^DIC(19,9986,"U")="ENGINEERING EQUIPMENT REQUEST "
^DIC(19,9987,0)="SCDX AMBCAR RETRANS SEL REJ^Selective Retransmission of NPCDB Rejections^This functionality is now accomplished by CDW/VSSC.^R^11289^SD SUPERVISOR^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,9987,1,0)="^^6^6^2961016^^"
^DIC(19,9987,1,1,0)="This option will present the user with a list of patients who currently"
^DIC(19,9987,1,2,0)="have rejections from the National Patient Care Database on file.  The user"
^DIC(19,9987,1,3,0)="can selectively choose which patients' encounters should be marked for"
^DIC(19,9987,1,4,0)="retransmission."
^DIC(19,9987,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9987,1,6,0)="Note:  Encounters that are marked for retransmission are screened out"
^DIC(19,9987,25)="EN^SCDXRT02"
^DIC(19,9987,"U")="SELECTIVE RETRANSMISSION OF NP"
^DIC(19,9988,0)="XMSCRIPTOUT^Toggle a script out of service^^R^11748^^^^^^^54"
^DIC(19,9988,1,0)="^19.06^3^3^3020312^^^^"
^DIC(19,9988,1,1,0)="This options lets you edit the OUT OF SERVICE field for a Transmission"
^DIC(19,9988,1,2,0)="Script in the Domain file. You can also requeue the Domain for transmission"
^DIC(19,9988,1,3,0)="from this option."
^DIC(19,9988,25)="OUT^XMCE"
^DIC(19,9988,"U")="TOGGLE A SCRIPT OUT OF SERVICE"
^DIC(19,9989,0)="ACKQAS VISIT ENTRY^New Clinic Visits^^R^11720^^^^^^^509^^1^1"
^DIC(19,9989,1,0)="^^145^145^2991202^"
^DIC(19,9989,1,1,0)="The New Clinic Visits option allows you to enter A&SP clinic visits "
^DIC(19,9989,1,2,0)="into the computer. When entering a new visit, if all required "
^DIC(19,9989,1,3,0)="information is not typed in, the entire visit is deleted. This is "
^DIC(19,9989,1,4,0)="done to eliminate errors caused by incomplete data."
^DIC(19,9989,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9989,1,6,0)="After you identify the division and clinic location, the software asks you"
^DIC(19,9989,1,7,0)="for the visit date. QUASAR defaults to today's date and will accept any"
^DIC(19,9989,1,8,0)="DHCP date format except a future date."
^DIC(19,9989,1,9,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9989,1,10,0)="At the ""Select A&SP Patient Name"" prompt, enter the patient's name. "
^DIC(19,9989,1,11,0)="If a new name is entered (i.e., a name not previously in the A&SP "
^DIC(19,9989,1,12,0)="PATIENT file (#509850.2)), QUASAR asks if you want to add the new "
^DIC(19,9989,1,13,0)="patient to the file. The software also gives you the cumulative count "
^DIC(19,9989,1,14,0)="of unique patients entered in the file."
^DIC(19,9989,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,16,0)="If the selected patient does not have a Primary Eligibility the system"
^DIC(19,9989,1,17,0)="displays an error message to this effect and returns to the division"
^DIC(19,9989,1,18,0)="prompt."
^DIC(19,9989,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,20,0)="If you have not selected an existing visit and the Send to PCE value on"
^DIC(19,9989,1,21,0)="the Site Parameters file for the selected division is set to true the"
^DIC(19,9989,1,22,0)="system checks to see if there are any appointments set up for this patient"
^DIC(19,9989,1,23,0)="on this date.  If there are they are displayed, you have the option to"
^DIC(19,9989,1,24,0)="select one.  If you select an appointment the appointment time is used to"
^DIC(19,9989,1,25,0)="populate the visit time field in the visit record.  If there are no"
^DIC(19,9989,1,26,0)="appointments for the patient the system then checks if there are any PCE"
^DIC(19,9989,1,27,0)="visits for the patient on the selected day.  If there are they are"
^DIC(19,9989,1,28,0)="displayed and you are given the option to select one.  If one is selected"
^DIC(19,9989,1,29,0)="data from the PCE visit (that is valid within QUASAR) is used to populate"
^DIC(19,9989,1,30,0)="the visit record."
^DIC(19,9989,1,31,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9989,1,32,0)="Next, QUASAR provides a brief patient inquiry excerpt, a list of rated "
^DIC(19,9989,1,33,0)="disabilities, Service Connected data and the A&SP problem list if any"
^DIC(19,9989,1,34,0)="diagnostic codes have been entered."
^DIC(19,9989,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,36,0)="You are then required to enter a visit time."
^DIC(19,9989,1,37,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9989,1,38,0)="You are asked to enter the initial visit date. If the patient is a "
^DIC(19,9989,1,39,0)="new patient, the initial visit date is the date of the patient's first "
^DIC(19,9989,1,40,0)="A&SP clinic visit."
^DIC(19,9989,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,42,0)="If the USE ASP CLINIC FILE NUMBER parameter is set to YES for the"
^DIC(19,9989,1,43,0)="Division, the system shall prompt you to enter the Local Clinic Number for"
^DIC(19,9989,1,44,0)="the Patient."
^DIC(19,9989,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,46,0)="If the USE C&P parameter is set to YES for the Division, then the system"
^DIC(19,9989,1,47,0)="shall look for an open C&P request for the Patient. If one is found then"
^DIC(19,9989,1,48,0)="the system will prompt if the Visit you are entering is a C&P Exam."
^DIC(19,9989,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,50,0)="If you have selected a PCE Visit then the system will have retrieved"
^DIC(19,9989,1,51,0)="all the Diagnosis Codes from the PCE Visit that are valid for QUASAR and"
^DIC(19,9989,1,52,0)="these codes shall be displayed. You will not have to re-enter the same"
^DIC(19,9989,1,53,0)="Diagnosis Codes into QUASAR."
^DIC(19,9989,1,54,0)="QUASAR asks for a diagnostic code (i.e., ICD-9-CM code). For evaluations, "
^DIC(19,9989,1,55,0)="the disease codes are those conditions found to be present during the "
^DIC(19,9989,1,56,0)="evaluation. For treatment and therapy visits, the disease codes are those "
^DIC(19,9989,1,57,0)="conditions which are TREATED. Conditions previously diagnosed during an "
^DIC(19,9989,1,58,0)="evaluation but not treated during the visit are NOT entered. The "
^DIC(19,9989,1,59,0)="first code entered is always assumed to be the primary complaint. "
^DIC(19,9989,1,60,0)="Disease codes are added to the Problem List.  You should exercise "
^DIC(19,9989,1,61,0)="caution when entering disease codes."
^DIC(19,9989,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,63,0)="If the Send to PCE parameter for the Division is set to NO the Visit"
^DIC(19,9989,1,64,0)="Eligibility will not be prompted."
^DIC(19,9989,1,65,0)="If the Send to PCE parameter for the Division is set to YES and the"
^DIC(19,9989,1,66,0)="Patient is not defined as Service Connected then the system will set the"
^DIC(19,9989,1,67,0)="Visit Eligibility to the Patient's Primary Eligibility and this field will"
^DIC(19,9989,1,68,0)="not be displayed."
^DIC(19,9989,1,69,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9989,1,70,0)="If the Send to PCE parameter for the Patient is set to YES and the Patient"
^DIC(19,9989,1,71,0)="is Service Connected the system will prompt for the Visit Eligibility. It"
^DIC(19,9989,1,72,0)="will display all the Patient's Eligibilities. If the list of Eligibilities"
^DIC(19,9989,1,73,0)="does not include NSC (Non-Service Connected) then this will also be"
^DIC(19,9989,1,74,0)="displayed. The system shall prompt the user to select an Eligibility for"
^DIC(19,9989,1,75,0)="the Visit from those displayed."
^DIC(19,9989,1,76,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,77,0)="If the Send To PCE parameter is set to YES for the Division, and the"
^DIC(19,9989,1,78,0)="Patient is Service Connected then the system shall prompt if the Visit's"
^DIC(19,9989,1,79,0)="Treatment was Service Connected. "
^DIC(19,9989,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,81,0)="If the Send To PCE parameter is set to YES for the Division, the Visit's"
^DIC(19,9989,1,82,0)="Treatment is Service Connected and the Patient is classified as having"
^DIC(19,9989,1,83,0)="been exposed to Agent Orange, the system shall prompt if the Visit's"
^DIC(19,9989,1,84,0)="Treatment was related to Agent Orange Exposure. "
^DIC(19,9989,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,86,0)="If the Send To PCE parameter is set to YES for the Division, the Visit's"
^DIC(19,9989,1,87,0)="Treatment is Service Connected and the Patient is classified as having"
^DIC(19,9989,1,88,0)="been exposed to Radiation, the system shall prompt if the Visit's"
^DIC(19,9989,1,89,0)="Treatment was related to Radiation Exposure. "
^DIC(19,9989,1,90,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,91,0)="If the Send To PCE parameter is set to YES for the Division, the Visit's"
^DIC(19,9989,1,92,0)="Treatment is Service Connected and the Patient is classified as having"
^DIC(19,9989,1,93,0)="been exposed to Environmental Contaminants, the system shall prompt if the"
^DIC(19,9989,1,94,0)="Visit's Treatment was related to Environmental Contaminants. "
^DIC(19,9989,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,96,0)="Depending on your site parameter settings, the software may ask for"
^DIC(19,9989,1,97,0)="audiometric data. These data fields are used to enter audiometric "
^DIC(19,9989,1,98,0)="thresholds and word recognition scores. The audiometric fields appear "
^DIC(19,9989,1,99,0)="for all C&P exams (even when a code for normal hearing [389.8] is "
^DIC(19,9989,1,100,0)="entered) and for any routine audiometric evaluation where a hearing "
^DIC(19,9989,1,101,0)="loss code is entered in the diagnostic code field. The audiometric "
^DIC(19,9989,1,102,0)="data field does not appear when a code for normal hearing (389.8) or "
^DIC(19,9989,1,103,0)="when a non-hearing loss code (e.g., dizziness 780.4) is entered in "
^DIC(19,9989,1,104,0)="the diagnostic code field. Enter a whole number between -10 and 105. "
^DIC(19,9989,1,105,0)="Missing data is coded as 1. No response at the limits of the "
^DIC(19,9989,1,106,0)="audiometer or 105 dB HL, whichever is lower, is coded as 110."
^DIC(19,9989,1,107,0)="Note: VACO prohibits presentation of audiometric stimuli."
^DIC(19,9989,1,108,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,109,0)="If the user selected a PCE Visit, the system shall copy the Providers"
^DIC(19,9989,1,110,0)="associated with the PCE Visit over to QUASAR, discarding any that are not"
^DIC(19,9989,1,111,0)="defined as active on the A&SP Staff file. Prior to prompting for the"
^DIC(19,9989,1,112,0)="Providers for this visit, the system shall display the Providers copied"
^DIC(19,9989,1,113,0)="over from PCE."
^DIC(19,9989,1,114,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9989,1,115,0)="Next, you are prompted for Primary Provider, Secondary Provider and"
^DIC(19,9989,1,116,0)="Student. The Primary Provider field contains the name of the primary A&SP"
^DIC(19,9989,1,117,0)="Provider who participated in the exam. If a second Provider was involved"
^DIC(19,9989,1,118,0)="with the visit, enter his or her name.  If a Student was involved with"
^DIC(19,9989,1,119,0)="this visit, enter the student's name. A screen allows you to select only"
^DIC(19,9989,1,120,0)="Providers and Students, who are active on the exam visit date."
^DIC(19,9989,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,122,0)="If the you selected a PCE Visit, the system shall copy the Procedure"
^DIC(19,9989,1,123,0)="codes and any associated CPT Modifiers and Procedure Volumes, for that"
^DIC(19,9989,1,124,0)="Visit over to QUASAR, discarding any that are not defined as active on the"
^DIC(19,9989,1,125,0)="A&SP Procedure file or the A&SP CPT Modifier File. Prior to asking you to"
^DIC(19,9989,1,126,0)="enter the Procedures for this visit, the system shall display any"
^DIC(19,9989,1,127,0)="Procedures (with CPT Modifiers and Volume) copied over from PCE."
^DIC(19,9989,1,128,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,129,0)="QUASAR asks for a procedure code (i.e., CPT-4 code)."
^DIC(19,9989,1,130,0)="After entering a CPT Procedure code the system shall prompt for any CPT"
^DIC(19,9989,1,131,0)="Modifiers (if appropriate) and a Volume, before returning to ask for"
^DIC(19,9989,1,132,0)="another CPT Procedure Code."
^DIC(19,9989,1,133,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,134,0)="The final prompt is for the total time spent during the clinic visit. "
^DIC(19,9989,1,135,0)="Time is recorded in minutes and is to include direct (e.g., face-to-face) "
^DIC(19,9989,1,136,0)="and indirect time (e.g., paperwork, documentation, administration)."
^DIC(19,9989,1,137,0)=" "
^DIC(19,9989,1,138,0)="If the Send to PCE parameter is set to YES for the Division the system"
^DIC(19,9989,1,139,0)="shall ensure that the each of the required PCE fields has had data"
^DIC(19,9989,1,140,0)="entered.  If any required fields have not had data entered they are"
^DIC(19,9989,1,141,0)="displayed.  You then have the option to return to the amend the visit or"
^DIC(19,9989,1,142,0)="quit and therefore delete the visit."
^DIC(19,9989,1,143,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9989,1,144,0)="The New Clinic Visits option is not used to edit visits. Existing "
^DIC(19,9989,1,145,0)="clinic visits can be edited with the Edit an Existing Visit option."
^DIC(19,9989,15)="K ACKSITE,ACKCSC"
^DIC(19,9989,20)="W @IOF,!,""This option is used to enter new A&SP clinic visits.  Existing clinic"",!,""visits should be updated with the Edit an Existing Visit option."",!"
^DIC(19,9989,25)="VISIT^ACKQAS"
^DIC(19,9989,"U")="NEW CLINIC VISITS"
^DIC(19,9990,0)="ACKQAS MASTER^Audiology & Speech Visit Tracking System^^M^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,9990,1,0)="^^4^4^2990802^^^"
^DIC(19,9990,1,1,0)="The Audiology & Speech Visit Tracking System menu is assigned to "
^DIC(19,9990,1,2,0)="Audiology and Speech Pathology personnel who enter or edit clinic visit "
^DIC(19,9990,1,3,0)="data and generate reports. This menu contains all options exported with "
^DIC(19,9990,1,4,0)="the QUASAR package except for the supervisory specific options."
^DIC(19,9990,10,0)="^19.01PI^4^4"
^DIC(19,9990,10,1,0)="9989^^1"
^DIC(19,9990,10,2,0)="9991^^5"
^DIC(19,9990,10,3,0)="9992^^10"
^DIC(19,9990,10,4,0)="9997^^15"
^DIC(19,9990,10,"B",9989,1)=""
^DIC(19,9990,10,"B",9991,2)=""
^DIC(19,9990,10,"B",9992,3)=""
^DIC(19,9990,10,"B",9997,4)=""
^DIC(19,9990,99)="62195,30800"
^DIC(19,9990,99.1)="54530,56018"
^DIC(19,9990,"U")="AUDIOLOGY & SPEECH VISIT TRACK"
^DIC(19,9991,0)="ACKQAS VISIT EDIT^Edit an Existing Visit^^R^11720^^^^^^^509^^^1"
^DIC(19,9991,1,0)="^^5^5^2990818^^"
^DIC(19,9991,1,1,0)="The Edit an Existing Visit option is used to modify an existing "
^DIC(19,9991,1,2,0)="clinic visit when the data is incorrect, incomplete, or needs to be "
^DIC(19,9991,1,3,0)="updated.  This option is not to be used to enter a new visit."
^DIC(19,9991,1,4,0)="Any A&SP staff member designated as a supervisor can delete a "
^DIC(19,9991,1,5,0)="clinic visit entered in error."
^DIC(19,9991,15)="K ACKSITE,ACKCSC"
^DIC(19,9991,25)="ACKQAS2"
^DIC(19,9991,"U")="EDIT AN EXISTING VISIT"
^DIC(19,9992,0)="ACKQAS PAT INQ^Inquire - A&SP Patient^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,9992,1,0)="^^13^13^2991213^^"
^DIC(19,9992,1,1,0)="The Inquire - A&SP Patient option displays demographic information "
^DIC(19,9992,1,2,0)="for an A&SP patient which includes date of birth, social security "
^DIC(19,9992,1,3,0)="number, eligibility, and initial visit date.  Additionally the option "
^DIC(19,9992,1,4,0)="shows inpatient status and diagnostic history.  Output can be sent to "
^DIC(19,9992,1,5,0)="a printer."
^DIC(19,9992,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9992,1,7,0)="After selecting the A&SP patient's name, you are given an"
^DIC(19,9992,1,8,0)="opportunity to update the diagnostic history. The Problem List is"
^DIC(19,9992,1,9,0)="recompiled using this logic:  All clinic visits for the patient "
^DIC(19,9992,1,10,0)="are examined. Unique diagnostic codes and the earliest date for "
^DIC(19,9992,1,11,0)="each code are determined. The A&SP PATIENT file is updated with "
^DIC(19,9992,1,12,0)="these codes and dates. Also, the earliest diagnostic date found "
^DIC(19,9992,1,13,0)="becomes the INITIAL VISIT DATE."
^DIC(19,9992,25)="ACKQNQ"
^DIC(19,9992,"U")="INQUIRE - A&SP PATIENT"
^DIC(19,9993,0)="ACKQAS VISITS BY DIAG^Visits by Diagnosis^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,9993,1,0)="^^11^11^2960108^^"
^DIC(19,9993,1,1,0)="The Visits by Diagnosis report can be printed for a date range "
^DIC(19,9993,1,2,0)="you select.  You can print the report for Audiology only, Speech "
^DIC(19,9993,1,3,0)="Pathology only, or both Audiology and Speech Pathology."
^DIC(19,9993,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9993,1,5,0)="You can choose to print the report for one or all clinician(s), other "
^DIC(19,9993,1,6,0)="provider(s), or student(s)."
^DIC(19,9993,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9993,1,8,0)="The report lists clinic visits for the date range sorted by ICD-9CM "
^DIC(19,9993,1,9,0)="diagnostic codes.  Since the diagnostic code field is a multiple "
^DIC(19,9993,1,10,0)="field, the visit shows up once under each diagnostic code entered for "
^DIC(19,9993,1,11,0)="that visit."
^DIC(19,9993,25)="ACKQR3"
^DIC(19,9993,"U")="VISITS BY DIAGNOSIS"
^DIC(19,9994,0)="ACKQAS CDR^Generate A&SP Service CDR^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,9994,1,0)="^^19^19^3000201^^^"
^DIC(19,9994,1,1,0)="The Generate A&SP Service CDR option generates and prints the RCS "
^DIC(19,9994,1,2,0)="10-0141 report for Audiology and Speech Pathology."
^DIC(19,9994,1,3,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9994,1,4,0)="If your CDR is reported by Division, you must enter the Division"
^DIC(19,9994,1,5,0)="for which the report is to be generated."
^DIC(19,9994,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9994,1,7,0)="You must then enter the month for which the report is to be generated."
^DIC(19,9994,1,8,0)="The total number of clinic visit hours for the month is displayed. You "
^DIC(19,9994,1,9,0)="are prompted for the total number of paid hours. "
^DIC(19,9994,1,10,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9994,1,11,0)="You can enter a flat number of hours to be distributed among all "
^DIC(19,9994,1,12,0)="education/training and research accounts or you can enter hours for "
^DIC(19,9994,1,13,0)="each account individually. You are then asked for pass through "
^DIC(19,9994,1,14,0)="account hours. When entering hours for these accounts, keep in mind "
^DIC(19,9994,1,15,0)="the number of clinic visit hours. Do not let the number of hours "
^DIC(19,9994,1,16,0)="remaining go below the total number of clinic visit hours."
^DIC(19,9994,1,17,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9994,1,18,0)="The A&SP CDR is an 80 column report which displays only the CDR "
^DIC(19,9994,1,19,0)="account numbers with activity during the date range."
^DIC(19,9994,25)="ACKQCDR"
^DIC(19,9994,"U")="GENERATE A&SP SERVICE CDR"
^DIC(19,9995,0)="ACKQAS PROC STATS^Statistics by Procedure^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,9995,1,0)="^19.06^11^11^3001013^^"
^DIC(19,9995,1,1,0)="The Statistics by Procedure report can be printed for a date range "
^DIC(19,9995,1,2,0)="you select.  You can print the report for Audiology only, Speech "
^DIC(19,9995,1,3,0)="Pathology only, or both Audiology and Speech Pathology."
^DIC(19,9995,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9995,1,5,0)="You can choose to print the report for one or all clinician(s), other "
^DIC(19,9995,1,6,0)="provider(s), or student(s)."
^DIC(19,9995,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9995,1,8,0)="The report lists clinic visits for the date range sorted by CPT-4 "
^DIC(19,9995,1,9,0)="procedure codes.  Since the procedure code field is a multiple "
^DIC(19,9995,1,10,0)="field, the visit shows up once under each procedure code entered for "
^DIC(19,9995,1,11,0)="that visit."
^DIC(19,9995,25)="ACKQR2"
^DIC(19,9995,"U")="STATISTICS BY PROCEDURE"
^DIC(19,9996,0)="ACKQAS PAT BY CITY^Patients by City^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,9996,1,0)="^^3^3^2960108^^^^"
^DIC(19,9996,1,1,0)="The Patients by City option generates a patient count report "
^DIC(19,9996,1,2,0)="for a selected date range. The report shows the number of patients "
^DIC(19,9996,1,3,0)="seen, sorted by city of residence."
^DIC(19,9996,25)="ACKQR1"
^DIC(19,9996,"U")="PATIENTS BY CITY"
^DIC(19,9997,0)="ACKQAS REPORTS^A&SP Reports^^M^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,9997,1,0)="^19.06^3^3^3001013^^^^"
^DIC(19,9997,1,1,0)="The A&SP Reports menu contains options to print Audiology and Speech "
^DIC(19,9997,1,2,0)="Pathology reports. This menu is assigned to users who do not enter or "
^DIC(19,9997,1,3,0)="modify A&SP data, but require read only access."
^DIC(19,9997,10,0)="^19.01IP^11^8"
^DIC(19,9997,10,1,0)="9993^^1"
^DIC(19,9997,10,3,0)="9996^^5"
