^DIC(19,9997,99.1)="55957,22224"
^DIC(19,9997,"U")="A&SP REPORTS"
^DIC(19,9998,0)="ACKQAS SUPER^A&SP Supervisor Menu^^M^11720^^^^^^^509^^1"
^DIC(19,9998,1,0)="^^5^5^2990915^^^^"
^DIC(19,9998,1,1,0)="The A&SP Supervisor Menu is designed for Audiology and Speech"
^DIC(19,9998,1,2,0)="Pathology supervisory personnel.  This menu contains all options"
^DIC(19,9998,1,3,0)="exported with the QUASAR package.  It contains options for setting"
^DIC(19,9998,1,4,0)="up and maintaining the package, generating the CDR and capitation"
^DIC(19,9998,1,5,0)="reports, as well as adequating C&P exams."
^DIC(19,9998,10,0)="^19.01PI^12^5"
^DIC(19,9998,10,1,0)="9990^^5"
^DIC(19,9998,10,6,0)="10004^^15"
^DIC(19,9998,10,9,0)="10007^^1"
^DIC(19,9998,10,10,0)="10009^^10"
^DIC(19,9998,10,12,0)=11862
^DIC(19,9998,10,"B",9990,1)=""
^DIC(19,9998,10,"B",10004,6)=""
^DIC(19,9998,10,"B",10007,9)=""
^DIC(19,9998,10,"B",10009,10)=""
^DIC(19,9998,10,"B",11862,12)=""
^DIC(19,9998,20)="D INTRO^ACKQUTL"
^DIC(19,9998,99)="62195,30800"
^DIC(19,9998,99.1)="67804,41143"
^DIC(19,9998,"U")="A&SP SUPERVISOR MENU"
^DIC(19,9999,0)="ACKQAS SITE PARAMS^A&SP Site Parameters^^E^11720^^^^^^^509^^1^1"
^DIC(19,9999,1,0)="^^72^72^2990701^"
^DIC(19,9999,1,1,0)="The A&SP Site Parameters option allows you to enter data into the"
^DIC(19,9999,1,2,0)="A&SP SITE PARAMETERS file (#509850.8). This data determines how"
^DIC(19,9999,1,3,0)="QUASAR behaves when entering Visit information at your site."
^DIC(19,9999,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9999,1,5,0)="After entering your site name you will be asked whether you wish"
^DIC(19,9999,1,6,0)="QUASAR to INTERFACE WITH PCE. If you answer YES then the overnight"
^DIC(19,9999,1,7,0)="batch transmission job that sends the data to PCE will be activated."
^DIC(19,9999,1,8,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9999,1,9,0)="Next you must define each Division for which Visit data is recorded"
^DIC(19,9999,1,10,0)="at your site. For each Division you will then be asked whether or"
^DIC(19,9999,1,11,0)="not data for this Division should be sent to PCE, whether or not to"
^DIC(19,9999,1,12,0)="use Local File numbers to identify patients, whether or not to use "
^DIC(19,9999,1,13,0)="the AMIE C&P Interface, whether or not to require audiometric data "
^DIC(19,9999,1,14,0)="for hearing loss Diagnosis Codes, and the names of all the clinics "
^DIC(19,9999,1,15,0)="at which the visits take place."
^DIC(19,9999,1,16,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9999,1,17,0)="In order to use Quasar to record visit data for a Division, the "
^DIC(19,9999,1,18,0)="Division must be defined on this file and have a status of ACTIVE."
^DIC(19,9999,1,19,0)="The Status should be set to INACTIVE if you no longer record visits"
^DIC(19,9999,1,20,0)="for a Division or you have entered a Division by mistake. (You can "
^DIC(19,9999,1,21,0)="not delete a Division from this file but changing the status to "
^DIC(19,9999,1,22,0)="INACTIVE has the same effect). The Division status referred to here"
^DIC(19,9999,1,23,0)="applies only to Quasar and has no effect on any other packages."
^DIC(19,9999,1,24,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9999,1,25,0)="If the parameter INTERFACE WITH PCE is set to YES, then visit data "
^DIC(19,9999,1,26,0)="will be transmitted to PCE for all Divisions that have the SEND TO"
^DIC(19,9999,1,27,0)="PCE parameter set to YES. This means the interface may be turned off"
^DIC(19,9999,1,28,0)="for a single Division by setting the SEND TO PCE parameter for that"
^DIC(19,9999,1,29,0)="Division to NO. If the INTERFACE TO PCE parameter is set to NO then"
^DIC(19,9999,1,30,0)="NO DATA will be sent to PCE for any Division."
^DIC(19,9999,1,31,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9999,1,32,0)="Answer YES or NO to the USE ASP CLINIC FILE NUMBER field. Some sites "
^DIC(19,9999,1,33,0)="have existing LOCAL (not medical center) file numbers associated with "
^DIC(19,9999,1,34,0)="their Audiology and Speech Pathology patients and wish to continue "
^DIC(19,9999,1,35,0)="using these numbers. If you answer YES, you can cross-reference "
^DIC(19,9999,1,36,0)="QUASAR visit entries to your current file numbering system."
^DIC(19,9999,1,37,0)="    "
^DIC(19,9999,1,38,0)="The USE C&P field can be answered YES or NO. Answer YES if you wish "
^DIC(19,9999,1,39,0)="to use QUASAR's AMIE/C&P interface. If you use a different reporting"
^DIC(19,9999,1,40,0)="procedure and do not wish to use the AMIE/C&P interface, answer NO."
^DIC(19,9999,1,41,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9999,1,42,0)="The AMIE linkage feature allows entry of text and audiometric data"
^DIC(19,9999,1,43,0)="in the AMIE format, adequation of the results, and hand-off of the "
^DIC(19,9999,1,44,0)="report to the AMIE Compensation and Pension package. If this option "
^DIC(19,9999,1,45,0)="is enabled, QUASAR is informed when an Audiology C&P exam is "
^DIC(19,9999,1,46,0)="scheduled. When an entry is made for the patient, the user is asked "
^DIC(19,9999,1,47,0)="""Is this a C&P exam?"" If the user responds yes, in addition to the "
^DIC(19,9999,1,48,0)="usual QUASAR information, narrative data is requested for generating"
^DIC(19,9999,1,49,0)="the AMIE report."
^DIC(19,9999,1,50,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9999,1,51,0)="If the C&P exam prompt does not appear, the patient entered is either "
^DIC(19,9999,1,52,0)="(1) not a C&P patient, (2) Veterans Affairs Regional Office (VARO)"
^DIC(19,9999,1,53,0)="did not request an AUDIO exam (see Form 2507), or (3) the patient's "
^DIC(19,9999,1,54,0)="C&P claim has been closed by the C&P Unit. Users should contact their "
^DIC(19,9999,1,55,0)="C&P Unit. If it is determined that the patient has a C&P visit, the "
^DIC(19,9999,1,56,0)="C&P prompt can be turned on by entering ^C after the patient "
^DIC(19,9999,1,57,0)="identifying information is entered."
^DIC(19,9999,1,58,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9999,1,59,0)="Answer YES or NO to the BYPASS AUDIOMETRICS field. Certain diagnosis "
^DIC(19,9999,1,60,0)="codes (i.e., hearing loss codes) are flagged to require audiometric "
^DIC(19,9999,1,61,0)="data to be entered when those codes are used for a visit. By "
^DIC(19,9999,1,62,0)="answering YES for the BYPASS AUDIOMETRICS field, you allow users to "
^DIC(19,9999,1,63,0)="bypass the entry of that data.  If you answer NO, users are not "
^DIC(19,9999,1,64,0)="allowed to bypass the entry of audiometric data."
^DIC(19,9999,1,65,0)="  "
^DIC(19,9999,1,66,0)="The final prompt is for CLINIC LOCATION. Clinics can be established "
^DIC(19,9999,1,67,0)="by name (e.g., Audiology or Speech Pathology), by function (e.g., "
^DIC(19,9999,1,68,0)="Hearing Aid Clinic or Dysphagia Clinic), or by clinician (e.g., "
^DIC(19,9999,1,69,0)="Audiology-Smith). Only clinic locations established by MAS can be "
^DIC(19,9999,1,70,0)="selected. Contact MAS for further information. Multi-divisional sites "
^DIC(19,9999,1,71,0)="or those with more than one A&SP location are entered. There must be "
^DIC(19,9999,1,72,0)="at least one clinic entered for this field."
^DIC(19,9999,15)="K ACKLAYGO,DLAYGO"
^DIC(19,9999,20)="S ACKLAYGO="""",DLAYGO=509850.8 W @IOF,!,""This option allows you to configure the QUASAR package to meet facility needs."",!"
^DIC(19,9999,30)="ACK(509850.8,"
^DIC(19,9999,31)="AEMQ"
^DIC(19,9999,50)="ACK(509850.8,"
^DIC(19,9999,51)="[ACKQAS SITE]"
^DIC(19,9999,"U")="A&SP SITE PARAMETERS"
^DIC(19,10000,0)="ACKQAS WKLD GEN MAN^Compile A&SP Capitation Data^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,10000,1,0)="^^15^15^2990701^"
^DIC(19,10000,1,1,0)="The Workload Options distributed with QUASAR V. 1.0 contained useful "
^DIC(19,10000,1,2,0)="information.  Due to insufficient resources for development and "
^DIC(19,10000,1,3,0)="support of the central data base, the QUASAR V. 1.0 workload rollup "
^DIC(19,10000,1,4,0)="report has been discontinued.  However, because the data is vital to "
^DIC(19,10000,1,5,0)="local managers, the functionality remains in QUASAR V. 2.0 and is "
^DIC(19,10000,1,6,0)="available in the Capitation Report."
^DIC(19,10000,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10000,1,8,0)="The Compile A&SP Capitation Data option is used to generate capitation "
^DIC(19,10000,1,9,0)="data for a selected Division or Divisions and a selected month. If data"
^DIC(19,10000,1,10,0)="has previously been compiled for the selected Division or Divisions and"
^DIC(19,10000,1,11,0)="the selected month, you are asked if you wish to continue.  If you do so,"
^DIC(19,10000,1,12,0)="the previously compiled data is deleted and the information will be"
^DIC(19,10000,1,13,0)="recalculated.  The compilation takes place in the background, and you are"
^DIC(19,10000,1,14,0)="notified by an E-Mail message when the task is finished.  You can use the"
^DIC(19,10000,1,15,0)="Print A&SP Capitation Report to review the data."
^DIC(19,10000,25)="ACKQDWL"
^DIC(19,10000,"U")="COMPILE A&SP CAPITATION DATA"
^DIC(19,10001,0)="ACKQAS WKLD VERIFY^Print A&SP Capitation Report^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,10001,1,0)="^^7^7^2990701^"
^DIC(19,10001,1,1,0)="When the Compile A&SP Capitation Data option has generated information for"
^DIC(19,10001,1,2,0)="selected Division(s) and selected month, you are notified by an E-Mail"
^DIC(19,10001,1,3,0)="message.  You can then use the Print A&SP Capitation Report to review the"
^DIC(19,10001,1,4,0)="data.  This option produces a three-part report for each Division which"
^DIC(19,10001,1,5,0)="includes demographic, diagnostic and procedure data followed by a summary"
^DIC(19,10001,1,6,0)="(not separated by Division) that includes demographic, diagnostic and"
^DIC(19,10001,1,7,0)="procedure data."
^DIC(19,10001,25)="ACKQDWLP"
^DIC(19,10001,"U")="PRINT A&SP CAPITATION REPORT"
^DIC(19,10002,0)="ACKQAS ADHOC^Tailor-Made A&SP Reports^^A^11720^ACKQ ADHOC^^^^^^509^^1"
^DIC(19,10002,1,0)="^^15^15^2990909^^^^"
^DIC(19,10002,1,1,0)="The Tailor-Made A&SP Reports option allows you to generate reports "
^DIC(19,10002,1,2,0)="with a small amount of VA FileMan training. Reports can be generated "
^DIC(19,10002,1,3,0)="from the A&SP CLINIC VISIT file (#509850.6) or the A&SP PATIENT file "
^DIC(19,10002,1,4,0)="(#509850.2). You must be familiar with VA FileMan's PRINT and SORT "
^DIC(19,10002,1,5,0)="functions as well as the structure of the file from which the data is "
^DIC(19,10002,1,6,0)="printed."
^DIC(19,10002,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10002,1,8,0)="Access to this option is controlled by the ACKQ ADHOC security key. "
^DIC(19,10002,1,9,0)="Allocation of this key is at the discretion of the IRM chief. The "
^DIC(19,10002,1,10,0)="option may not be available at all sites. If available, this option "
^DIC(19,10002,1,11,0)="can be a powerful tool to provide various statistical reports from "
^DIC(19,10002,1,12,0)="the QUASAR package. However, its indiscriminate use could have a "
^DIC(19,10002,1,13,0)="negative impact on system performance. Complicated sorts or reports "
^DIC(19,10002,1,14,0)="that could be expected to impact system performance should be queued "
^DIC(19,10002,1,15,0)="to run during off-hours."
^DIC(19,10002,20)="S DIR(0)=""SB^P:Patient;V:Visit"",DIR(""A"")=""Print From Which File"",DIR(""B"")=""V"",DIR(""?"")=""P=Patient; V=Visit"" D ^DIR K DIR Q:$D(DIRUT)  S:Y=""P"" BY="".01"",DHIT=""W !"" S DIC=$S(Y=""V"":""^ACK(509850.6,"",1:""^ACK(509850.2,""),L=0 D EN1^DIP"
^DIC(19,10002,"U")="TAILOR-MADE A&SP REPORTS"
^DIC(19,10003,0)="ACKQAS CLINICIAN ENTRY^Staff (Enter/Edit)^^R^10000000216^^^^^^^509^^1^1"
^DIC(19,10003,1,0)="^19.06^23^23^3071115^^^^"
^DIC(19,10003,1,1,0)="The Staff (Enter/Edit) option allows you to enter data for "
^DIC(19,10003,1,2,0)="clinicians, fee-basis personnel, other providers (e.g., health "
^DIC(19,10003,1,3,0)="technician), and students into the A&SP STAFF file (#509850.3). The "
^DIC(19,10003,1,4,0)="information includes the staff person's name, activation and "
^DIC(19,10003,1,5,0)="inactivation dates, status, and an ID number for sites that choose to "
^DIC(19,10003,1,6,0)="use code numbers."
^DIC(19,10003,1,7,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10003,1,8,0)="Names added to the A&SP STAFF file (#509850.3) must be in the NEW "
^DIC(19,10003,1,9,0)="PERSON file (#200). The A&SP Service Chief should contact IRM if an "
^DIC(19,10003,1,10,0)="entry needs to be made to the NEW PERSON file."
^DIC(19,10003,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10003,1,12,0)="An activation date is required to associate the staff member with a "
^DIC(19,10003,1,13,0)="clinic visit. The activation date is the date the staff member became "
^DIC(19,10003,1,14,0)="an active member. For the staff member to receive credit for a patient "
^DIC(19,10003,1,15,0)="visit, he or she must have been active on or before the visit date."
^DIC(19,10003,1,16,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10003,1,17,0)="Inactive staff members should never be deleted because entries in the "
^DIC(19,10003,1,18,0)="A&SP CLINIC VISIT file (#509850.6) reference them. This option is used "
^DIC(19,10003,1,19,0)="to activate and inactivate staff members as appropriate."
^DIC(19,10003,1,20,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10003,1,21,0)="Selected clinicians can be designated as supervisors. Supervisors "
^DIC(19,10003,1,22,0)="have access to certain functionality that is not available to other "
^DIC(19,10003,1,23,0)="staff members (e.g., adequating any C&P exam)."
^DIC(19,10003,15)="K ACKLAYGO,DLAYGO"
^DIC(19,10003,20)="S ACKLAYGO="""",DLAYGO=509850.3 D NMVD^ACKQCLED W @IOF,!,""This option allows you to enter data for A&SP staff members."",!,""This includes name, activation/inactivation dates, and status."",!"
^DIC(19,10003,25)="EN^ACKQCLED"
^DIC(19,10003,30)=""
^DIC(19,10003,31)=""
^DIC(19,10003,32)=""
^DIC(19,10003,34)=""
^DIC(19,10003,50)=""
^DIC(19,10003,51)=""
^DIC(19,10003,"U")="STAFF (ENTER/EDIT)"
^DIC(19,10004,0)="ACKQAS CP ADEQ^C&P Exam Adequation^^R^11720^^^^^^^509^^"
^DIC(19,10004,1,0)="^^16^16^2990809^^^"
^DIC(19,10004,1,1,0)="This option allows you to adequate a C&P exam. Only exams that are "
^DIC(19,10004,1,2,0)="complete (i.e., having a status of AWAITING ADEQUATION) and signed "
^DIC(19,10004,1,3,0)="off on can be adequated."
^DIC(19,10004,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10004,1,5,0)="When an audiologist provides his or her electronic signature to a C&P "
^DIC(19,10004,1,6,0)="exam, the chief adequator sees a list of exams waiting to be "
^DIC(19,10004,1,7,0)="adequated. He or she can review, print, or edit the report using the "
^DIC(19,10004,1,8,0)="Edit an Existing Visit option. Finally, he or she can provide an "
^DIC(19,10004,1,9,0)="electronic signature using the C&P Exam Adequation option to release "
^DIC(19,10004,1,10,0)="the report to the AMIE package.  Entering the electronic signature to "
^DIC(19,10004,1,11,0)="adequate an exam causes all exam results to be transferred to the "
^DIC(19,10004,1,12,0)="AMIE C&P package and the exam is marked CLOSED.  The results are made "
^DIC(19,10004,1,13,0)="available to the regional office. Non-supervisory clinicians can "
^DIC(19,10004,1,14,0)="adequate their own C&P exams.  A clinician designated as a supervisor "
^DIC(19,10004,1,15,0)="in the A&SP STAFF file (#509850.3) can adequate other clinicians' C&P "
^DIC(19,10004,1,16,0)="exams."
^DIC(19,10004,20)=""
^DIC(19,10004,25)="ADEQ^ACKQCP"
^DIC(19,10004,"U")="C&P EXAM ADEQUATION"
^DIC(19,10005,0)="ACKQAS COST ENTRY^Enter Cost Information for Procedures^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,10005,1,0)="^^13^13^2991022^^^^"
^DIC(19,10005,1,1,0)="The Enter Cost Information for Procedures option allows you to enter"
^DIC(19,10005,1,2,0)="cost data for each procedure code in the A&SP PROCEDURE CODE file"
^DIC(19,10005,1,3,0)="(#509850.4). You can selected a single CPT-4 code, or you can edit"
^DIC(19,10005,1,4,0)="all procedure codes. If you choose to edit all procedures, each"
^DIC(19,10005,1,5,0)="procedure is displayed consecutively, and the current approximate"
^DIC(19,10005,1,6,0)="private sector cost can be entered."
^DIC(19,10005,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10005,1,8,0)="You can obtain fee schedules from public or private sector clinics "
^DIC(19,10005,1,9,0)="and hospitals, calculate their real costs, or use insurance "
^DIC(19,10005,1,10,0)="reimbursement rates (e.g., Medicare/Medicaid or insurance UCRs)."
^DIC(19,10005,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10005,1,12,0)="Procedure cost information is used in generating the Cost Comparison "
^DIC(19,10005,1,13,0)="Report on the A&SP Reports menu."
^DIC(19,10005,25)="ACKQAS3"
^DIC(19,10005,"U")="ENTER COST INFORMATION FOR PRO"
^DIC(19,10006,0)="ACKQAS PRINT COST COMPARE^Cost Comparison Report^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,10006,1,0)="^^6^6^2960216^^^"
^DIC(19,10006,1,1,0)="The Cost Comparison Report option produces a report of all CPT-4 "
^DIC(19,10006,1,2,0)="procedure codes used within a selected date range and their "
^DIC(19,10006,1,3,0)="associated costs. The cost linked to a CPT code is based upon "
^DIC(19,10006,1,4,0)="approximate private sector cost. Cost is entered by local A&SP "
^DIC(19,10006,1,5,0)="supervisors using the Enter Cost Information for Procedures option on "
^DIC(19,10006,1,6,0)="the Set Up/Maintenance menu."
^DIC(19,10006,25)="ACKQR4"
^DIC(19,10006,"U")="COST COMPARISON REPORT"
^DIC(19,10007,0)="ACKQAS SET UP MENU^Set Up/Maintenance^^M^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,10007,1,0)="^^5^5^2991014^^^^"
^DIC(19,10007,1,1,0)="There are four tasks on the Set Up/Maintenance menu which must be"
^DIC(19,10007,1,2,0)="completed to set up and maintain the package.  These tasks are (1) Enter"
^DIC(19,10007,1,3,0)="Audiology and Speech Pathology Staff, (2) Establish Local Site Parameters,"
^DIC(19,10007,1,4,0)="(3) Update File Data at the Direction of VACO and (4) Update CPT Modifiers"
^DIC(19,10007,1,5,0)="per CO Directive."
^DIC(19,10007,10,0)="^19.01IP^8^6"
^DIC(19,10007,10,1,0)="10003^^1"
^DIC(19,10007,10,4,0)="9999^^5"
^DIC(19,10007,10,5,0)="10008^^15"
^DIC(19,10007,10,6,0)="10010^^20"
^DIC(19,10007,10,7,0)=11861
^DIC(19,10007,10,8,0)=10005
^DIC(19,10007,10,"B",9999,4)=""
^DIC(19,10007,10,"B",10003,1)=""
^DIC(19,10007,10,"B",10005,8)=""
^DIC(19,10007,10,"B",10008,5)=""
^DIC(19,10007,10,"B",10010,6)=""
^DIC(19,10007,10,"B",11861,7)=""
^DIC(19,10007,99)="62195,30800"
^DIC(19,10007,"U")="SET UP/MAINTENANCE"
^DIC(19,10008,0)="ACKQAS VACO DIRECTIVE^Update Files per CO Directive^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,10008,1,0)="^^15^15^2990701^^^^"
^DIC(19,10008,1,1,0)="In order to use this option, you must be designated as an active "
^DIC(19,10008,1,2,0)="supervisor in the A&SP STAFF file (#509850.3)."
^DIC(19,10008,1,3,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10008,1,4,0)="The Update Files per CO Directive option is to be used with extreme "
^DIC(19,10008,1,5,0)="caution. Data in the CDR ACCOUNT file (#509850), the A&SP DIAGNOSTIC "
^DIC(19,10008,1,6,0)="CONDITION file (#509850.1), and the A&SP PROCEDURE CODE file "
^DIC(19,10008,1,7,0)="(#509850.4) are standardized for roll-up to central data bases (e.g., "
^DIC(19,10008,1,8,0)="DSS).  File entries should be added or modified ONLY by directive "
^DIC(19,10008,1,9,0)="from the Director, Audiology and Speech Pathology Service (VAHQ)."
^DIC(19,10008,1,10,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10008,1,11,0)="After selecting the file you wish to work with, you can choose to "
^DIC(19,10008,1,12,0)="inactivate selected entries or add data for a new entry. When a new "
^DIC(19,10008,1,13,0)="entry is added, all fields for that entry must be answered in order "
^DIC(19,10008,1,14,0)="to maintain data base integrity. If data is incomplete, the entry is "
^DIC(19,10008,1,15,0)="automatically deleted."
^DIC(19,10008,25)="ACKQFIL"
^DIC(19,10008,"U")="UPDATE FILES PER CO DIRECTIVE"
^DIC(19,10009,0)="ACKQAS MANAGEMENT REPORTS^Management Reports A&SP^^M^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,10009,1,0)="^^4^4^2990802^"
^DIC(19,10009,1,1,0)="The Management Reports A&SP menu allows you to compile and print "
^DIC(19,10009,1,2,0)="the Audiology and Speech Pathology CDR, and to compile and print the"
^DIC(19,10009,1,3,0)="A&SP Capitation report. This data is stored in the A&SP WORKLOAD "
^DIC(19,10009,1,4,0)="file (#509850.7)."
^DIC(19,10009,10,0)="^19.01IP^4^4"
^DIC(19,10009,10,1,0)="9994^^1"
^DIC(19,10009,10,2,0)="10000^^5"
^DIC(19,10009,10,3,0)="10001^^10"
^DIC(19,10009,10,4,0)="11860^^2"
^DIC(19,10009,10,"B",9994,1)=""
^DIC(19,10009,10,"B",10000,2)=""
^DIC(19,10009,10,"B",10001,3)=""
^DIC(19,10009,10,"B",11860,4)=""
^DIC(19,10009,99)="62195,30800"
^DIC(19,10009,"U")="MANAGEMENT REPORTS A&SP"
^DIC(19,10010,0)="ACKQAS FILE PRINT^Print A&SP File Entries^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,10010,1,0)="^^3^3^2960226^^"
^DIC(19,10010,1,1,0)="The Print A&SP File Entries option lists the file entries from "
^DIC(19,10010,1,2,0)="the CDR ACCOUNT file, the A&SP PROCEDURE CODE file, or the A&SP"
^DIC(19,10010,1,3,0)="DIAGNOSTIC CONDITION file."
^DIC(19,10010,25)="ACKQFILP"
^DIC(19,10010,"U")="PRINT A&SP FILE ENTRIES"
^DIC(19,10014,0)="LR WKLD LOCATION^Create Laboratory OOS Locations^^R^10958^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,10014,1,0)="^^18^18^2961024^^"
^DIC(19,10014,1,1,0)="Occasion Of Service (OOS)"
^DIC(19,10014,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10014,1,3,0)=" This option is used to create new/addtional LAB OOS LOCATIONS in the"
^DIC(19,10014,1,4,0)="HOSPTIAL LOCATION (#44) file. This maybe required if other services are"
^DIC(19,10014,1,5,0)="using the Laboratory Package for patient result data entry."
^DIC(19,10014,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10014,1,7,0)="You are able to create locations for different divisions or locations with"
^DIC(19,10014,1,8,0)="different Stop Codes. For example you may want to create a location for"
^DIC(19,10014,1,9,0)="Surgery Blood Gases with the stop code for GENERAL SURGERY (401)."
^DIC(19,10014,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10014,1,11,0)="Example:"
^DIC(19,10014,1,12,0)="site number=XXX"
^DIC(19,10014,1,13,0)="Stop code = 401"
^DIC(19,10014,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10014,1,15,0)="New location name = 'LAB DIV XXX OOS ID 401'"
^DIC(19,10014,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10014,1,17,0)="NOTE: ONCE LOCATION HAVE BEEN CREATED, THEY SHOULD NOT BE DELETED."
^DIC(19,10014,1,18,0)="Extra locations do not create any system problems."
^DIC(19,10014,25)="LRCAPPH2"
^DIC(19,10014,"U")="CREATE LABORATORY OOS LOCATION"
^DIC(19,10015,0)="LR WKLD ACC AREA LOCATION^Edit ACC Area OOS Locations^^R^10958^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,10015,1,0)="^^15^15^2961024^^"
^DIC(19,10015,1,1,0)="Occasion Of Service (OOS)"
^DIC(19,10015,1,2,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10015,1,3,0)=" This option is used to edit Accession Area's Laboratory OOS Location."
^DIC(19,10015,1,4,0)="If the Accession area is not defined, the system will prompt with the"
^DIC(19,10015,1,5,0)="DEFAULT LAB OOS LOCATION."
^DIC(19,10015,1,6,0)=" If the Accession Area already has a LAB OOS LOCATION, the system will"
^DIC(19,10015,1,7,0)="display the details about the location before you make a selection."
^DIC(19,10015,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10015,1,9,0)="Use this option when you want to assign a different Stop Code to a given"
^DIC(19,10015,1,10,0)="Accession Area for NPCDB workload purposes. The DEFAULT LAB OOS LOCATION"
^DIC(19,10015,1,11,0)="is used if the Accession Area has no LAB OOS LOCATION defined."
^DIC(19,10015,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10015,1,13,0)="The location you want to select must first exist it the HOSPITAL LOCATION"
^DIC(19,10015,1,14,0)="file. You may create new LAB OOS LOCATIONS using the [LR WKLD LOCATION]"
^DIC(19,10015,1,15,0)="option. You may use ?? at the Location prompt to view possible selection."
^DIC(19,10015,25)="ACC^LRCAPPH2"
^DIC(19,10015,"U")="EDIT ACC AREA OOS LOCATIONS"
^DIC(19,10017,0)="DENTPURGE^Purge Dental AMIS^DAS turned off^R^11595^^^^^^^58"
^DIC(19,10017,1,0)="6^^5^5^2960814^^^^"
^DIC(19,10017,1,1,0)="This option allows the purging of dental data on Dental Treatment"
^DIC(19,10017,1,2,0)="file #221, Dental Fee Basis file #222, Dental Class I-VI file #223,"
^DIC(19,10017,1,3,0)="Dental Personnel file #224, and Dental Non Clinical Time file #226."
^DIC(19,10017,1,4,0)="Five years of dental data will remain after purge.  The data is not"
^DIC(19,10017,1,5,0)="archived but is permanently purged from the system."
^DIC(19,10017,25)="DENTPUR"
^DIC(19,10017,200.9)=""
^DIC(19,10017,"U")="PURGE DENTAL AMIS"
^DIC(19,10018,0)="DENTBATCH^Enter Batch Screening/Complete Exam^DAS turned off^R^11595^^^^^^^58"
^DIC(19,10018,1,0)="^^2^2^2960930^^"
^DIC(19,10018,1,1,0)="This option allows the user to enter a batch of screening Dental"
^DIC(19,10018,1,2,0)="Treatments at once."
^DIC(19,10018,25)="DENTSCR"
^DIC(19,10018,200.9)=""
^DIC(19,10018,"U")="ENTER BATCH SCREENING/COMPLETE"
^DIC(19,10019,0)="SRO PCE STATUS^PCE Filing Status Report^^R^10000000049^^^^^^^167^^1^1"
^DIC(19,10019,1,0)="^19.06^28^28^3050712^^"
^DIC(19,10019,1,1,0)="This option provides a report of the PCE filing status of completed cases "
^DIC(19,10019,1,2,0)="performed during the selected date range.  The report may be printed for "
^DIC(19,10019,1,3,0)="OR surgical cases, non-OR procedures or both.  Also, the report may be "
^DIC(19,10019,1,4,0)="printed for all specialties or for a single specialty only.  "
^DIC(19,10019,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10019,1,6,0)="This report is intended to be used as a tool in the review of Surgery "
^DIC(19,10019,1,7,0)="case information that is passed to PCE.  The report uses 2 status "
^DIC(19,10019,1,8,0)="categories: "
^DIC(19,10019,1,9,0)="  (1) FILED - This status indicates that case information has already been"
^DIC(19,10019,1,10,0)="      filed with PCE.  "
^DIC(19,10019,1,11,0)="  (2) NOT FILED - This status indicates that the case information has not"
^DIC(19,10019,1,12,0)="      been filed with PCE.  The case may or may not be missing information"
^DIC(19,10019,1,13,0)="      needed to file with PCE.  "
^DIC(19,10019,1,14,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10019,1,15,0)="Two forms of the report are available, the long and the short. The long "
^DIC(19,10019,1,16,0)="form uses a 132 column format and prints case information including the "
^DIC(19,10019,1,17,0)="surgeon/provider, the attending, the specialty, the principal post-op "
^DIC(19,10019,1,18,0)="diagnosis, and the principal procedure.  If the PCE filing status is "
^DIC(19,10019,1,19,0)="FILED, the CPT codes and ICD diagnosis codes will be printed.  If the "
^DIC(19,10019,1,20,0)="filing status is NOT FILED, information fields needed for PCE filing that "
^DIC(19,10019,1,21,0)="do not contain data will be printed.  At the end of the report, the "
^DIC(19,10019,1,22,0)="number of cases in each PCE filing status will be printed, plus the "
^DIC(19,10019,1,23,0)="number of CPT and ICD codes for cases with a status of FILED.  "
^DIC(19,10019,1,24,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10019,1,25,0)="The short form uses an 80 column format and does not include "
^DIC(19,10019,1,26,0)="surgeon/provider, attending, principal post-op diagnosis and CPT and ICD "
^DIC(19,10019,1,27,0)="code information.  The totals printed at the end will show only the total "
^DIC(19,10019,1,28,0)="cases for each status."
^DIC(19,10019,15)="D EXIT^SROVAR"
^DIC(19,10019,20)="D ^SROVAR"
^DIC(19,10019,22)="Q"
^DIC(19,10019,25)="SROPCE0"
^DIC(19,10019,"U")="PCE FILING STATUS REPORT"
^DIC(19,10020,0)="LRAR ARCHIVE SEARCH^Search for lab data to archive^^R^10958^^^^^^^510"
^DIC(19,10020,1,0)="^^5^5^2950530^^^^"
^DIC(19,10020,1,1,0)="Data to be archived must be older than the beginning of the month three"
^DIC(19,10020,1,2,0)="months ago, on a patient not currently on a ward, and on a permanent page."
^DIC(19,10020,1,3,0)="If the data is prior to the time specified above it will be purged if"
^DIC(19,10020,1,4,0)="unverified."
^DIC(19,10020,1,5,0)="Microbiology, Anatomic Pathology, and Blood Bank data are not archived."
^DIC(19,10020,25)="SEARCH^LRARCHIV"
^DIC(19,10020,"U")="SEARCH FOR LAB DATA TO ARCHIVE"
^DIC(19,10021,0)="LRAR ARCHIVE PURGE^Purge data found in the Search option^^R^10958^^^^^^^510"
^DIC(19,10021,1,0)="^^6^6^2950411^^^^"
^DIC(19,10021,1,1,0)="Data found in the Search archive option is stored in the ^LAR global."
^DIC(19,10021,1,2,0)="Data is removed from the Lab Data file 63 (^LR global) based on the"
^DIC(19,10021,1,3,0)="data in the ^LAR global.  The ^LAR data must be written to separate media,"
^DIC(19,10021,1,4,0)="the Clear archive option run, the data read back from the media, then"
^DIC(19,10021,1,5,0)="this option may be run to complete the archive."
^DIC(19,10021,1,6,0)="Note that the data is removed from both the ^LR and the ^LAR globals."
^DIC(19,10021,25)="PURGE^LRARCHIV"
^DIC(19,10021,"U")="PURGE DATA FOUND IN THE SEARCH"
^DIC(19,10022,0)="LRAR ARCHIVE WRITE MEDIA^Write data to off-line media^^A^10958^^^^^^^510^^1"
^DIC(19,10022,1,0)="^^2^2^2870204^^"
^DIC(19,10022,1,1,0)="After having created entries in the ^LAR global, the data should be"
^DIC(19,10022,1,2,0)="written to off-line media for purposes of long term storage."
^DIC(19,10022,20)="W !,""The site manager should determine the method of data storage of the"",!,""^LAR global."""
^DIC(19,10022,"U")="WRITE DATA TO OFF-LINE MEDIA"
^DIC(19,10023,0)="LRAR ARCHIVE READ MEDIA^Read data from off-line media^^A^10958^^^^^^^510^^1"
^DIC(19,10023,1,0)="^^2^2^2870203^^^"
^DIC(19,10023,1,1,0)="After having Cleared the ^LAR global, the data should be read back in to"
^DIC(19,10023,1,2,0)="verify and purge what has been archived."
^DIC(19,10023,20)="W !,""The site manager should determine the method of data retrieval of the"",!,""^LAR global."""
^DIC(19,10023,"U")="READ DATA FROM OFF-LINE MEDIA"
^DIC(19,10024,0)="LRAR ARCHIVE RESTORE^Restore archived data to LR global^^R^10958^^^^^^^510"
^DIC(19,10024,1,0)="^^1^1^2950411^^^"
^DIC(19,10024,1,1,0)="Used to restore data into the LR global that has been archived."
^DIC(19,10024,25)="LRARCHD"
^DIC(19,10024,"U")="RESTORE ARCHIVED DATA TO LR GL"
^DIC(19,10025,0)="LRAR ARCHIVE CLEAR^Clear data from the LAR global^^R^10958^^^^^^^510"
^DIC(19,10025,1,0)="^^2^2^2950411^^^"
^DIC(19,10025,1,1,0)="Data found in the Search archive option is temporarily removed by this"
^DIC(19,10025,1,2,0)="option."
^DIC(19,10025,25)="CLEAN^LRARCHIV"
^DIC(19,10025,99.1)="54228,80501"
^DIC(19,10025,"U")="CLEAR DATA FROM THE LAR GLOBAL"
^DIC(19,10026,0)="LRAR ARCHIVE DATA^Find patient's archived data^^R^10958^^^^^^^510"
^DIC(19,10026,1,0)="^^3^3^2950411^^^"
^DIC(19,10026,1,1,0)="Once data for a patient has been archived, the storage location of the data"
^DIC(19,10026,1,2,0)="is saved with the patient's remaining data.  This information can be"
^DIC(19,10026,1,3,0)="found using this option."
^DIC(19,10026,25)="FIND^LRARCHD"
^DIC(19,10026,"U")="FIND PATIENT'S ARCHIVED DATA"
