^DIC(19,10348,"U")="UNIVERSAL INTERFACE CONTACT ME"
^DIC(19,10349,0)="XMMGR-TERMINATE-ONE^Terminate one mail user^^R^11748^^^^^^^54"
^DIC(19,10349,1,0)="^19.06^18^18^3020509^^^^"
^DIC(19,10349,1,1,0)="This option lets you remove the mailbox of any user who meets the criteria of"
^DIC(19,10349,1,2,0)="either the XMMGR-TERMINATE-MANY option or the XMMGR-TERMINATE-SUGGEST option. "
^DIC(19,10349,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(19,10349,1,4,0)="Remove means:"
^DIC(19,10349,1,5,0)=" - Delete user's private mail groups"
^DIC(19,10349,1,6,0)=" - Remove user from membership in all groups"
^DIC(19,10349,1,7,0)=" - Remove user as an authorized sender from all groups"
^DIC(19,10349,1,8,0)=" - Remove user from anyone's list of surrogates"
^DIC(19,10349,1,9,0)=" - Delete user's latered-messages list"
^DIC(19,10349,1,10,0)=" - Delete user's mail box"
^DIC(19,10349,1,11,0)=""
^DIC(19,10349,1,12,0)="As a result, the user will not receive any mail."
^DIC(19,10349,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(19,10349,1,14,0)="Remember,"
^DIC(19,10349,1,15,0)=" - Whenever you give a user a new access code, the system gives the user a"
^DIC(19,10349,1,16,0)="mailbox if he doesn't already have one. "
^DIC(19,10349,1,17,0)=" - Whenever a user logs on, the system gives the user a mailbox if he doesn't"
^DIC(19,10349,1,18,0)="already have one. "
^DIC(19,10349,25)="CHOOSE^XMUTERM"
^DIC(19,10349,"U")="TERMINATE ONE MAIL USER"
^DIC(19,10350,0)="XMMGR-TERMINATE-MANY^Terminate many mail users^^R^11748^^^^^^^54"
^DIC(19,10350,1,0)="^19.06^39^39^3010731^^^^"
^DIC(19,10350,1,1,0)="This option goes through the MAIL BOX global and removes any mailbox if"
^DIC(19,10350,1,2,0)=" - the user is not in the NEW PERSON file."
^DIC(19,10350,1,3,0)=" - the user has no access code and was not terminated."
^DIC(19,10350,1,4,0)=" - the user has no access code and was terminated w/o mailbox retention."
^DIC(19,10350,1,5,0)=" - the user has an access code, but no primary menu."
^DIC(19,10350,1,6,0)=" - the user has an access code and primary menu, but no verify code, AND"
^DIC(19,10350,1,7,0)="   - has never signed on or used mail, since being added before a cutoff date."
^DIC(19,10350,1,8,0)="   OR"
^DIC(19,10350,1,9,0)="   - last signed on or used mail before a cutoff date."
^DIC(19,10350,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(19,10350,1,11,0)="However, if the user meets one of the last two conditions above, but has"
^DIC(19,10350,1,12,0)="a forwarding address, the user's mailbox will not be removed.  The fact"
^DIC(19,10350,1,13,0)="will be noted on the report, and the user should be investigated further."
^DIC(19,10350,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(19,10350,1,15,0)="Remove means:"
^DIC(19,10350,1,16,0)=" - Delete user's private mail groups"
^DIC(19,10350,1,17,0)=" - Remove user from membership in all groups"
^DIC(19,10350,1,18,0)=" - Remove user as an authorized sender from all groups"
^DIC(19,10350,1,19,0)=" - Remove user from anyone's list of surrogates"
^DIC(19,10350,1,20,0)=" - Delete user's latered-messages list"
^DIC(19,10350,1,21,0)=" - Delete user's mail box"
^DIC(19,10350,1,22,0)=""
^DIC(19,10350,1,23,0)="As a result, the user will not receive any mail."
^DIC(19,10350,1,24,0)=""
^DIC(19,10350,1,25,0)="This option can be run in 'test' or 'real' mode."
^DIC(19,10350,1,26,0)=""
^DIC(19,10350,1,27,0)="The report lists, in DUZ order:"
^DIC(19,10350,1,28,0)=" - The user's DUZ and name"
^DIC(19,10350,1,29,0)=" - Whether the user has an access code, verify code, and primary menu"
^DIC(19,10350,1,30,0)=" - When the user was added to the NEW PERSON file"
^DIC(19,10350,1,31,0)=" - When the user last signed on or used mail"
^DIC(19,10350,1,32,0)=" - When the user was terminated (if applicable)"
^DIC(19,10350,1,33,0)=" - If the user was terminated, then whether the site manager chose to"
^DIC(19,10350,1,34,0)="   delete the user's mailbox.  (It's generally a good idea to go ahead"
^DIC(19,10350,1,35,0)="   and delete the mailbox upon termination.)"
^DIC(19,10350,1,36,0)=" - If the user has an access code and a forwarding address, the user"
^DIC(19,10350,1,37,0)="   is marked with '***', and the forwarding address is shown."
^DIC(19,10350,1,38,0)="   (Again, the mailbox is not deleted in this case, but the user should"
^DIC(19,10350,1,39,0)="   be investigated further.)"
^DIC(19,10350,25)="ALL1^XMUTERM"
^DIC(19,10350,"U")="TERMINATE MANY MAIL USERS"
^DIC(19,10351,0)="XMMGR-TERMINATE-SUGGEST^Terminate mail user suggestions^^R^11748^^^^^^^54"
^DIC(19,10351,1,0)="^19.06^37^37^3020509^^^^"
^DIC(19,10351,1,1,0)="This option goes through the MailBox global and reports on users who"
^DIC(19,10351,1,2,0)="*perhaps* should have their mail access terminated."
^DIC(19,10351,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10351,1,4,0)="Users are included in the report if"
^DIC(19,10351,1,5,0)=" - the user was DISUSER'd."
^DIC(19,10351,1,6,0)=" - the user was terminated before a manager-supplied cutoff date"
^DIC(19,10351,1,7,0)="   and allowed to keep a mailbox."
^DIC(19,10351,1,8,0)=" - the user has an access code, verify code, and primary menu,"
^DIC(19,10351,1,9,0)="   but last signed on or used mail before a manager-supplied cutoff date."
^DIC(19,10351,1,10,0)=" - the user has an access code, verify code, and primary menu,"
^DIC(19,10351,1,11,0)="   was added before a manager-supplied cutoff date, but has never signed on"
^DIC(19,10351,1,12,0)="   or used mail."
^DIC(19,10351,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10351,1,14,0)="This option does not terminate mail access."
^DIC(19,10351,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10351,1,16,0)="The report page breaks on Service/Section and includes the following"
^DIC(19,10351,1,17,0)="information:"
^DIC(19,10351,1,18,0)=" - User's DUZ and name"
^DIC(19,10351,1,19,0)=" - Whether the user has an access code, a verify code, and a primary menu"
^DIC(19,10351,1,20,0)=" - When the user last signed on or used mail"
^DIC(19,10351,1,21,0)=" - When the user was terminated (if applicable)"
^DIC(19,10351,1,22,0)=" - If the user was terminated, then whether the site manager chose to"
^DIC(19,10351,1,23,0)="   delete the user's mailbox.  (Remember, you should usually answer 'yes'"
^DIC(19,10351,1,24,0)="   to this question, unless the user is coming back and needs to have his"
^DIC(19,10351,1,25,0)="   mail retained.)"
^DIC(19,10351,1,26,0)=" - Whether the user was DISUSER'd"
^DIC(19,10351,1,27,0)=" - How many new messages the user has.  (New messages are never purged,"
^DIC(19,10351,1,28,0)="   except during purge-by-date purges.)"
^DIC(19,10351,1,29,0)=" - If the user has any surrogates, the first surrogate is shown."
^DIC(19,10351,1,30,0)=" - If the user has an access code and a forwarding address, the forwarding"
^DIC(19,10351,1,31,0)="   address is shown."
^DIC(19,10351,1,32,0)=""
^DIC(19,10351,1,33,0)="Besides being of interest to the Site Manager, this report is also"
^DIC(19,10351,1,34,0)="designed to be submitted to other services. The intent is that the"
^DIC(19,10351,1,35,0)="other services would check each of their users listed in the report,"
^DIC(19,10351,1,36,0)="annotate whether MailMan or VistA access should be terminated, and"
^DIC(19,10351,1,37,0)="return the report to the Site Manager to act on. "
^DIC(19,10351,25)="ALL2^XMUTERM"
^DIC(19,10351,"U")="TERMINATE MAIL USER SUGGESTION"
^DIC(19,10352,0)="XMMGR-PURGE-MESSAGE^Purge a message^^R^11748^^^^^^^54"
^DIC(19,10352,1,0)="^19.06^9^9^3020509^^^"
^DIC(19,10352,1,1,0)="This option enables you to purge any message."
^DIC(19,10352,1,2,0)=""
^DIC(19,10352,1,3,0)="Purge means:"
^DIC(19,10352,1,4,0)=" -delete the message from all user mailboxes"
^DIC(19,10352,1,5,0)=" -delete the message from the MESSAGE file 3.9"
^DIC(19,10352,1,6,0)=" -delete all responses from the MESSAGE file 3.9"
^DIC(19,10352,1,7,0)=" -delete the message from the MESSAGES TO BE NEW AT A LATER DATE file 3.73"
^DIC(19,10352,1,8,0)=""
^DIC(19,10352,1,9,0)="Purge is not reversible.  The message is gone forever."
^DIC(19,10352,25)="MESSAGE^XMUTERM"
^DIC(19,10352,"U")="PURGE A MESSAGE"
