^DIC(19,10572,0)="SCDX AMBCAR XMIT HIST FOR PAT^Transmission History for Patient^^R^1253^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10572,1,0)="^^7^7^2970722^"
^DIC(19,10572,1,1,0)="This option will produce the ACRP transmission history of all encounters"
^DIC(19,10572,1,2,0)="that a patient had during a given time frame."
^DIC(19,10572,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10572,1,4,0)="Note: All transmissions of the encounter are included, even if the"
^DIC(19,10572,1,5,0)="transmission occured after the date range selected.  This is because the"
^DIC(19,10572,1,6,0)="date range limits the encounters printed, not when the encounter was"
^DIC(19,10572,1,7,0)="transmitted."
^DIC(19,10572,25)="PATHIST^SCDXPRN1"
^DIC(19,10572,"U")="TRANSMISSION HISTORY FOR PATIE"
^DIC(19,10573,0)="SCDX AMBCAR XMIT REPORTS^Transmission Reports^^M^1253^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10573,1,0)="^^1^1^2970929^^^"
^DIC(19,10573,1,1,0)="Menu that contains all ACRP transmission reports"
^DIC(19,10573,10,0)="^19.01IP^2^2"
^DIC(19,10573,10,1,0)="10572^PAT"
^DIC(19,10573,10,2,0)="10574^FULL"
^DIC(19,10573,10,"B",10572,1)=""
^DIC(19,10573,10,"B",10574,2)=""
^DIC(19,10573,10,"C","FULL",2)=""
^DIC(19,10573,10,"C","PAT",1)=""
^DIC(19,10573,99)="57272,55125"
^DIC(19,10573,"U")="TRANSMISSION REPORTS"
^DIC(19,10574,0)="SCDX AMBCAR XMIT HIST FULL^Transmission History Report - Full^^R^1253^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10574,1,0)="^^3^3^2970813^"
^DIC(19,10574,1,1,0)="Complete transmission history report.  User allowed to select which"
^DIC(19,10574,1,2,0)="division(s), clinic(s), and patient(s) to include in the report and will"
^DIC(19,10574,1,3,0)="also be prompted for a transmission date range."
^DIC(19,10574,25)="FULLHIST^SCDXPRN2"
^DIC(19,10574,"U")="TRANSMISSION HISTORY REPORT - "
^DIC(19,10575,0)="SCDX AMBCAR PURGE ACRP FILES^Purge Ambulatory Care Reporting files^^R^1253^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10575,1,0)="^^5^5^2970908^^^"
^DIC(19,10575,1,1,0)="This option will purge the Transmitted Outpatient Encounter file (#409.73)"
^DIC(19,10575,1,2,0)="of all encounters that occurred during a user supplied date range.  This"
^DIC(19,10575,1,3,0)="will result in the deletion of corresponding entries in the Deleted"
^DIC(19,10575,1,4,0)="Outpatient Encounter file (#409.74), the Transmitted Outpatient Encounter"
^DIC(19,10575,1,5,0)="Error file (#409.75), and the ACRP Transmission History file (#409.77)."
^DIC(19,10575,25)="MAIN^SCDXPRG0"
^DIC(19,10575,"U")="PURGE AMBULATORY CARE REPORTIN"
^DIC(19,10576,0)="PXRR PATIENT ACTIVITY BY LOC^Patient Activity by Location^^R^10958^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,10576,1,0)="^^76^76^2970616^^^"
^DIC(19,10576,1,1,0)="This report may be run for either selected hospital locations, all"
^DIC(19,10576,1,2,0)="hospital locations, selected clinics, or all clinics. The report format"
^DIC(19,10576,1,3,0)="is a summary by patient for each selected location. For each location,"
^DIC(19,10576,1,4,0)="Scheduling data is used to identify patients with appointments during"
^DIC(19,10576,1,5,0)="the Patient Appointment Date Range. (The user can specify whether or not"
^DIC(19,10576,1,6,0)="each location should be started on a new page.  This is useful for"
^DIC(19,10576,1,7,0)="clerks printing and then distributing the reports to multiple"
^DIC(19,10576,1,8,0)="locations.)"
^DIC(19,10576,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(19,10576,1,10,0)="VISTA data for these patients is then examined for possible patient"
^DIC(19,10576,1,11,0)="activities during the Patient Activity Date Range.  Patient"
^DIC(19,10576,1,12,0)="activities include inpatient stays, emergency room encounters and"
^DIC(19,10576,1,13,0)="critical lab values.  A summary of each of these follows."
^DIC(19,10576,1,14,0)=""
^DIC(19,10576,1,15,0)="Inpatient stays:  All inpatient activities within the Patient Activity Date"
^DIC(19,10576,1,16,0)="Range are reported.  These include admissions and corresponding discharge, if"
^DIC(19,10576,1,17,0)="there is one, discharges and corresponding admission, and current"
^DIC(19,10576,1,18,0)="in-patient status."
^DIC(19,10576,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,20,0)="Emergency Room encounters:  All encounters within the Patient Activity"
^DIC(19,10576,1,21,0)="Date Range that have an identified Emergency Room location are"
^DIC(19,10576,1,22,0)="reported. Emergency rooms are identified through the PCE PARAMETERS"
^DIC(19,10576,1,23,0)="file.  This data is entered by the clinical coordinator or IRM staff"
^DIC(19,10576,1,24,0)="through the 'PCE Report Parameter Setup' option."
^DIC(19,10576,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,26,0)="Critical Lab Values:  All critical lab values reported within the"
^DIC(19,10576,1,27,0)="Patient Activity Date Range are presented, along with a column to identify"
^DIC(19,10576,1,28,0)="whether the value is critically high or critically low."
^DIC(19,10576,1,29,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,30,0)="Finally a search for future appointments is made within the Future"
^DIC(19,10576,1,31,0)="Appointment Date Range.  Any future appointments within this date range"
^DIC(19,10576,1,32,0)="are listed."
^DIC(19,10576,1,33,0)=""
^DIC(19,10576,1,34,0)="Within each location the patients are listed alphabetically followed by"
^DIC(19,10576,1,35,0)="a list of their appointments and activities.  Only patients with"
^DIC(19,10576,1,36,0)="activities will be included in the report."
^DIC(19,10576,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,38,0)="This report was developed as a measure of continuity of care. If a"
^DIC(19,10576,1,39,0)="provider of record has his or her care-giving interrupted through"
^DIC(19,10576,1,40,0)="clinical rotation, leave, reassignment, or for any other reason, this"
^DIC(19,10576,1,41,0)="report may be used to get an update on patient activities in his/her"
^DIC(19,10576,1,42,0)="caseload. This report is also useful when care is not interrupted."
^DIC(19,10576,1,43,0)="Clinical staff may wish to review patient activity by location for"
^DIC(19,10576,1,44,0)="events  which they may be unaware of."
^DIC(19,10576,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,46,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,47,0)="Technical Description:"
^DIC(19,10576,1,48,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,49,0)="Patient appointments are found by examining the appointment multiple of"
^DIC(19,10576,1,50,0)="the Hospital Location file for the specified locations during the time"
^DIC(19,10576,1,51,0)="frame specified by the Patient Appointment Date Range."
^DIC(19,10576,1,52,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,53,0)="Admissions and discharges that occurred during the Patient Activity Date"
^DIC(19,10576,1,54,0)="Range are found using the ATT1 and ATT3 cross-references of the"
^DIC(19,10576,1,55,0)="Patient Movement file.  A search for the corresponding discharge or"
^DIC(19,10576,1,56,0)="admission is made using the IN5^VADPT call.  Current inpatient status"
^DIC(19,10576,1,57,0)="is determined using this same call."
^DIC(19,10576,1,58,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,59,0)="Emergency room locations must be defined in field 801 of the PCE"
^DIC(19,10576,1,60,0)="PARAMETERS file, which is a multiple pointing to the HOSPITAL LOCATION"
^DIC(19,10576,1,61,0)="file. The ER clinic names are stored permanently at the global"
^DIC(19,10576,1,62,0)="location: ^PX(815,D0,RR1,D1,0). The Visit File is examined for"
^DIC(19,10576,1,63,0)="encounters during the Patient Activity Date Range which have a location"
^DIC(19,10576,1,64,0)="matching one of the defined emergency room locations."
^DIC(19,10576,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10576,1,66,0)="Laboratory data assessed for critical values is based on the Subfile 63.04"
^DIC(19,10576,1,67,0)="of the Lab DATA file (63), which stores results from Chemistry,"
^DIC(19,10576,1,68,0)="Hematology, Toxicology, RIA, Serology, and others.  Critical values are"
^DIC(19,10576,1,69,0)="identified through a pattern match of a numeric value followed by a ""*""."
^DIC(19,10576,1,70,0)="The global location read is ^LR(LRDFN,""CH"",INVERSE LAB DATE, LAB TEST"
^DIC(19,10576,1,71,0)="FIELD NUMBER). Piece one contains the result. Piece 2 indicates a critical"
^DIC(19,10576,1,72,0)="value and if it is high or low (e.g. *H).  This search is confined to"
^DIC(19,10576,1,73,0)="the Patient Activity Date Range."
^DIC(19,10576,1,74,0)=""
^DIC(19,10576,1,75,0)="Future appointments are found using the SDA^VADPT call for each patient"
^DIC(19,10576,1,76,0)="within the Future Appointment Date Range."
^DIC(19,10576,25)="PXRRPAD"
^DIC(19,10576,"U")="PATIENT ACTIVITY BY LOCATION"
^DIC(19,10577,0)="PRCH PA STATS DAILY^Purchasing Agent Statistics by Date^^P^11740^^^^^^^^^1"
^DIC(19,10577,1,0)="^^3^3^2970814^^^^"
^DIC(19,10577,1,1,0)="This option prints detailed total line counts and total dollar values for"
^DIC(19,10577,1,2,0)="purchasing agents for a given time period.  A single PA or a range of"
^DIC(19,10577,1,3,0)="PAs can be specified."
^DIC(19,10577,20)="S DIPCRIT=1"
