^DIC(19,10663,0)="SCRPW CLINICUTILIZATION SUMM^Clinic Utilization Statistical Summary^^R^11281^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10663,1,0)="^^2^2^2971221^"
^DIC(19,10663,1,1,0)="Option for printing clinic utilization statistics for a specified date "
^DIC(19,10663,1,2,0)="range."
^DIC(19,10663,25)="SCRPW2"
^DIC(19,10663,99.1)="56424,56047"
^DIC(19,10663,"U")="CLINIC UTILIZATION STATISTICAL"
^DIC(19,10664,0)="SCRPW ACTION REQUIRED REPORT^Encounter 'Action Required' Report^^R^11281^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10664,1,0)="^^2^2^2970410^"
^DIC(19,10664,1,1,0)="Option for printing facility 'action required' encounters in detailed or"
^DIC(19,10664,1,2,0)="statistics only format."
^DIC(19,10664,25)="SCRPW16"
^DIC(19,10664,99.1)="57079,34730"
^DIC(19,10664,"U")="ENCOUNTER 'ACTION REQUIRED' RE"
^DIC(19,10665,0)="SCRPW OUT ENC WORKLOAD STATS^Outpatient Encounter Workload Statistics^^R^11281^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10665,1,0)="^^108^108^2971223^"
^DIC(19,10665,1,1,0)="This report is based on ""parent"" encounters in the OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER"
^DIC(19,10665,1,2,0)="file.  The term ""parent"" in this case is used to refer to records where"
^DIC(19,10665,1,3,0)="the PARENT ENCOUNTER field is null (""child"" encounters are OUTPATIENT"
^DIC(19,10665,1,4,0)="ENCOUNTER records that contain a pointer in this field to another "
^DIC(19,10665,1,5,0)="OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER record). "
^DIC(19,10665,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,7,0)="Facility workload, via transmission to NPCDB, is derived from ""parent"""
^DIC(19,10665,1,8,0)="encounters that have a status of CHECKED OUT and have been referred to"
^DIC(19,10665,1,9,0)="the transmission process.  Information contained in ""child"" encounters"
^DIC(19,10665,1,10,0)="is not referred directly to the transmission process, but rather, "
^DIC(19,10665,1,11,0)="gathered with the ""parent"" encounter when the ""parent"" encounter is"
^DIC(19,10665,1,12,0)="transmitted."
^DIC(19,10665,1,13,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,14,0)="The OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER WORKLOAD section of the report is a count of"
^DIC(19,10665,1,15,0)="""parent"" OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTERS by status values that are considered"
^DIC(19,10665,1,16,0)="to be ""for credit"".  These statuses include CHECKED IN, CHECKED OUT,"
^DIC(19,10665,1,17,0)="NO ACTION TAKEN, FUTURE, and ACTION REQUIRED.  Only statuses found"
^DIC(19,10665,1,18,0)="in the database for the date range are reflected on the report."
^DIC(19,10665,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,20,0)="Only encounters in the OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER WORKLOAD section (encounters"
^DIC(19,10665,1,21,0)="with ""for credit"" statuses) are used to calculate visits and uniques as"
^DIC(19,10665,1,22,0)="reflected in the FACILITY OUTPATIENT VISITS and FACILITY OUTPATIENT"
^DIC(19,10665,1,23,0)="UNIQUES sections of this report."
^DIC(19,10665,1,24,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,25,0)="The NON-WORKLOAD section of the report is a count of ""parent"" encounters"
^DIC(19,10665,1,26,0)="by statuses that are not given outpatient workload credit (nationally)."
^DIC(19,10665,1,27,0)="These include DELETED, NON-COUNT, INPATIENT APPOINTMENT, NO-SHOW, and"
^DIC(19,10665,1,28,0)="CANCELLED statuses.  Only statuses that are found will appear on the"
^DIC(19,10665,1,29,0)="report."
^DIC(19,10665,1,30,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,31,0)="Within the CHECKED OUT category of the OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER WORKLOAD"
^DIC(19,10665,1,32,0)="section, encounters are further sub-categorized by transmission status."
^DIC(19,10665,1,33,0)="Only sub-categories that are found will appear on the report.  These"
^DIC(19,10665,1,34,0)="sub-categories include:"
^DIC(19,10665,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,36,0)="   'No transmission record' - These are ""parent"" encounters that are"
^DIC(19,10665,1,37,0)="    checked out but have not been referred to the transmission "
^DIC(19,10665,1,38,0)="    process (which should have happened when the record was checked"
^DIC(19,10665,1,39,0)="    out).  "
^DIC(19,10665,1,40,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,41,0)="    'Rejected for transmission' - Encounters in this category have failed"
^DIC(19,10665,1,42,0)="    to pass the checks for data elements required for transmission of"
^DIC(19,10665,1,43,0)="    workload to Austin."
^DIC(19,10665,1,44,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,45,0)="    'Not required, not transmitted' - These are encounters that have"
^DIC(19,10665,1,46,0)="    been referred to the transmission process (they have a record in"
^DIC(19,10665,1,47,0)="    the TRANSMITTED OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER file) but are not flagged to"
^DIC(19,10665,1,48,0)="    be transmitted, nor have they been transmitted. "
^DIC(19,10665,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,50,0)="    'Awaiting transmission' - These are records that have been referred"
^DIC(19,10665,1,51,0)="    to the transmission process since the last nightly transmission.  "
^DIC(19,10665,1,52,0)="    They will be sent in the next nightly transmission if they pass the"
^DIC(19,10665,1,53,0)="    the pre-transmission screening requirements."
^DIC(19,10665,1,54,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,55,0)="    'Transmitted, no acknowledgement' - These are encounters that have"
^DIC(19,10665,1,56,0)="    been referred to HL7 for transmission to Austin.  If there were no"
^DIC(19,10665,1,57,0)="    problems with HL7, they have been sent to Austin.  The number in "
^DIC(19,10665,1,58,0)="    this category should roughly match the average number of encounters"
^DIC(19,10665,1,59,0)="    produced by a facility on any given work day.  If these numbers are"
^DIC(19,10665,1,60,0)="    substantially greater than the facility's average daily workload,"
^DIC(19,10665,1,61,0)="    it may indicate a problem with HL7 has caused a failure to transmit"
^DIC(19,10665,1,62,0)="    data to Austin; or, it may indicate a problem with the incoming"
^DIC(19,10665,1,63,0)="    filer that processes the acknowledgment messages returning from"
^DIC(19,10665,1,64,0)="    Austin."
^DIC(19,10665,1,65,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,66,0)="    'Transmitted, rejected' - These are encounters that have been sent"
^DIC(19,10665,1,67,0)="    to Austin but have failed the requirements for filing into NPCDB."
^DIC(19,10665,1,68,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,69,0)="    'Transmitted, error' - One of the possible Austin acknowledgement"
^DIC(19,10665,1,70,0)="    statuses (not currently in use)."
^DIC(19,10665,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,72,0)="    'Transmitted, accepted' - These are encounters that have been"
^DIC(19,10665,1,73,0)="    sent to Austin, processed, and an acknowledgment message indicating"
^DIC(19,10665,1,74,0)="    acceptance has been returned to the facility.  This indicates the"
^DIC(19,10665,1,75,0)="    encounter has been recorded in NPCDB for national facility workload"
^DIC(19,10665,1,76,0)="    credit."
^DIC(19,10665,1,77,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,78,0)="The FACILITY OUTPATIENT VISITS section of the report is a count of one"
^DIC(19,10665,1,79,0)="per patient per day (regardless of the number of encounters a patient"
^DIC(19,10665,1,80,0)="may have had on a given day).  For multi-divisional sites, the station"
^DIC(19,10665,1,81,0)="totals are not the sum of all divisions.  If a patient was seen at more"
^DIC(19,10665,1,82,0)="than one division on a single day, they reflect as a visit to each "
^DIC(19,10665,1,83,0)="division; however, they are still just a single visit for the facility"
^DIC(19,10665,1,84,0)="on that date (as calculated by this report)."
^DIC(19,10665,1,85,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,86,0)="A patient visit will accrue to only one of the sub-categories in this"
^DIC(19,10665,1,87,0)="section.  If a patient had multiple encounters on a single day and as"
^DIC(19,10665,1,88,0)="few as one of those encounters has a ""transmitted, accepted"" status,"
^DIC(19,10665,1,89,0)="the patient's visit will accrue in the 'Transmitted, accepted visits'"
^DIC(19,10665,1,90,0)="sub-category.  If none of the patient's encounters on that date have"
^DIC(19,10665,1,91,0)="have a ""transmitted, accepted"" status, the visit will accrue to the"
^DIC(19,10665,1,92,0)="'Act. Req./not accepted' sub-category."
^DIC(19,10665,1,93,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,94,0)="The FACILITY OUTPATIENT UNIQUES section of the report is a count of one"
^DIC(19,10665,1,95,0)="per patient for the entire date range (regardless of the number of visits"
^DIC(19,10665,1,96,0)="a patient had).  For multi-divisional sites, the station totals are not"
^DIC(19,10665,1,97,0)="a sum of all of the divisions.  If a patient was seen at more than one"
^DIC(19,10665,1,98,0)="division during the date range, they reflect as a unique patient for"
^DIC(19,10665,1,99,0)="each division; however, they are still counted as a single unique for"
^DIC(19,10665,1,100,0)="the facility (as calculated by this report)."
^DIC(19,10665,1,101,0)=" "
^DIC(19,10665,1,102,0)="The unique patient will accrue to only one of the sub-categories in this"
^DIC(19,10665,1,103,0)="section.  If the patient had multiple visits during the date range and"
^DIC(19,10665,1,104,0)="as few as one of those visits had an encounter with a ""transmitted,"
^DIC(19,10665,1,105,0)="accepted"" status, the unique will accrue to the 'Transmitted, accepted"
^DIC(19,10665,1,106,0)="unique pts.' sub-category.  If none of the patient's visits had any"
^DIC(19,10665,1,107,0)="encounters with a ""transmitted, accepted"" status, the unique will accrue"
^DIC(19,10665,1,108,0)="to the 'Act. Req./not accepted unique pts.' sub-category."
^DIC(19,10665,25)="SCRPW8"
^DIC(19,10665,99.1)="57359,46699"
^DIC(19,10665,"U")="OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER WORKLOAD "
^DIC(19,10666,0)="SCRPW PTACTBYAPPTFREQ^Patient Activity by Appointment Frequency^^R^11281^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10666,1,0)="^^2^2^2970811^^"
^DIC(19,10666,1,1,0)="Option for printing patient appointment activity for a selected "
^DIC(19,10666,1,2,0)="range of clinic stop codes, sorted in the order of decreasing frequency."
^DIC(19,10666,25)="SCRPW11"
^DIC(19,10666,99.1)="56046,29762"
^DIC(19,10666,"U")="PATIENT ACTIVITY BY APPOINTMEN"
^DIC(19,10667,0)="SCRPW LIST PT ENCOUNTERS^Patient Encounter List^^R^11281^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10667,1,0)="^^2^2^2971221^^"
^DIC(19,10667,1,1,0)="Option for listing patient encounters in reverse chronological order"
^DIC(19,10667,1,2,0)="including date, location, number, check out and transmission status."
^DIC(19,10667,25)="SCRPW7"
^DIC(19,10667,"U")="PATIENT ENCOUNTER LIST"
^DIC(19,10668,0)="SCRPW REV SCH/PCE/VISIT DATA^Review of Scheduling/PCE/Problem List Data^^R^11281^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10668,1,0)="^^2^2^2971221^"
^DIC(19,10668,1,1,0)="Option for printing all scheduling/patient care encounter/visit tracking"
^DIC(19,10668,1,2,0)="data for a selected patient outpatient activity date."
^DIC(19,10668,25)="SCRPW1"
^DIC(19,10668,99.1)="56526,49278"
^DIC(19,10668,"U")="REVIEW OF SCHEDULING/PCE/PROBL"
^DIC(19,10669,0)="SCRPW TREND FACILITY UNIQUES^Trend of Facility Uniques by 12 Month Date Ranges^^R^11281^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10669,1,0)="^^4^4^2971221^^"
^DIC(19,10669,1,1,0)="Option for trending facility outpatient uniques by overlapping 12 month"
^DIC(19,10669,1,2,0)="date ranges for the past 5 years.  Data prior to 10/01/96 is derived"
^DIC(19,10669,1,3,0)="from the OPC file, data for dates following 10/01/96 is based on "
^DIC(19,10669,1,4,0)="'checked out' OUTPATIENT ENCOUNTER file reocrds."
^DIC(19,10669,25)="SCRPW6"
^DIC(19,10669,"U")="TREND OF FACILITY UNIQUES BY 1"
^DIC(19,10670,0)="SCRPW CLINIC GROUP MAINT^Clinic Group Maintenance for Reports^^R^11281^SD SUPERVISOR^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10670,1,0)="^^2^2^2971221^"
^DIC(19,10670,1,1,0)="Option for entering, editing, and printing clinic groups and clinic "
^DIC(19,10670,1,2,0)="group assignments for reports."
^DIC(19,10670,25)="SCRPW10"
^DIC(19,10670,"U")="CLINIC GROUP MAINTENANCE FOR R"
^DIC(19,10671,0)="SCRPW ENCOUNTER ACTIVITY RPT^Encounter Activity Report^^R^11281^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,10671,1,0)="^^7^7^2970618^"
^DIC(19,10671,1,1,0)="Option for producing encounter, visit, and unique patient statistics by"
^DIC(19,10671,1,2,0)="selected clinic, provider, or stop code perspective.  In summary format"
^DIC(19,10671,1,3,0)="output can be ranked alphabetically or by frequency of encounters, visits,"
^DIC(19,10671,1,4,0)="or uniques.  Detailed format allows the selection of specific clinics,"
^DIC(19,10671,1,5,0)="providers, or stop codes and will produce frequency ranked statistics of"
^DIC(19,10671,1,6,0)="diagnosises and procedures recorded in addition to encounters, visits and"
^DIC(19,10671,1,7,0)="uniques."
^DIC(19,10671,25)="SCRPW14"
^DIC(19,10671,99.1)="57250,43002"
^DIC(19,10671,"U")="ENCOUNTER ACTIVITY REPORT"
^DIC(19,10672,0)="VAFH PIVOT PURGE^Purge PIMS HL7 PIVOT file^^R^11740^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,10672,1,0)="^^24^24^2991213^^^^"
^DIC(19,10672,1,1,0)="This option will purge all entries from the PIMS HL7 PIVOT file "
^DIC(19,10672,1,2,0)="(#391.71) that are older than a specific number of days as determined"
^DIC(19,10672,1,3,0)="by the site.  There is no user input required."
^DIC(19,10672,1,4,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10672,1,5,0)="A field in the MAS PARAMETERS file (#43) is used in conjunction with"
^DIC(19,10672,1,6,0)="this option.  The name of the field is PIVOT FILE DAYS TO RETAIN and"
^DIC(19,10672,1,7,0)="the field number is 391.702.  The field may be updated with a numeric"
^DIC(19,10672,1,8,0)="value between 30 and 999 using the Enter/Edit option of VA FileMan.  "
^DIC(19,10672,1,9,0)="This value represents the number of days worth of data to retain "
^DIC(19,10672,1,10,0)="in file #391.71 when the VAFH PIVOT PURGE option is run."
^DIC(19,10672,1,11,0)="  "
^DIC(19,10672,1,12,0)="For example, if the site updates this field with a value of 100, then"
^DIC(19,10672,1,13,0)="any record with a date earlier than TODAY-100 days will be deleted"
^DIC(19,10672,1,14,0)="during the purge.  If the site does not update this field (i.e., the"
^DIC(19,10672,1,15,0)="field value remains null), then the VAFH PIVOT PURGE option will use"
^DIC(19,10672,1,16,0)="a default value of 547 days (approximately 18 months)."
^DIC(19,10672,1,17,0)="   "
^DIC(19,10672,1,18,0)="However, before any file #391.71 record is deleted two checks will"
^DIC(19,10672,1,19,0)="be performed on the record.  (1) If the internal entry number of the"
^DIC(19,10672,1,20,0)="record exists in the ""AXMIT"" cross-reference, it will not be deleted."
^DIC(19,10672,1,21,0)="(2) If the TYPE OF EVENT field (#.04) of the record is ""1"" (i.e.,"
^DIC(19,10672,1,22,0)="INPATIENT EVENTS) and if the PATIENT MOVEMENT file (#405) does not"
^DIC(19,10672,1,23,0)="reflect a discharge for the admission, the file #391.71 record will"
^DIC(19,10672,1,24,0)="not be deleted."
^DIC(19,10672,25)="EN^VAFHPURG"
^DIC(19,10672,"U")="PURGE PIMS HL7 PIVOT FILE"
^DIC(19,10673,0)="VAFH BATCH OUTPATIENT^OUTPATIENT BATCH JOB^^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,10673,1,0)="^^10^10^2970612^^^^"
^DIC(19,10673,1,1,0)="DO NOT SCHEDULE THIS OPTION UNLESS THERE IS A SPECIFIC APPLICATION THAT"
^DIC(19,10673,1,2,0)="REQUIRES NOTIFICATION OF SCHEDULING APPOINTMENTS WITH A HL7 MESSAGE."
^DIC(19,10673,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(19,10673,1,4,0)="This option is not intended to be run from programmer mode.  No output to"
^DIC(19,10673,1,5,0)="the screen is intended.  When this job is scheduled through TaskMan  "
^DIC(19,10673,1,6,0)="a routine will loop through the Hospital Location file ""S"" node and"
^DIC(19,10673,1,7,0)="generate an A08 HL7 v2.2 message for all appointments for today that"
^DIC(19,10673,1,8,0)="have a status of ""No action taken"" or ""Future""."
^DIC(19,10673,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(19,10673,1,10,0)="It should be scheduled to run after midnight but before 0400 hours."
^DIC(19,10673,25)="EN^VAFHCOPT"
^DIC(19,10673,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,10673,"U")="OUTPATIENT BATCH JOB"
^DIC(19,10674,0)="VAFH BATCH UPDATE^UPDATE BATCH JOB^^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,10674,1,0)="^^10^10^2970612^^^^"
^DIC(19,10674,1,1,0)="This option is not intended to be run from programmer mode.  No output to"
^DIC(19,10674,1,2,0)="the screen is intended.  When this job is scheduled through TaskMan it"
^DIC(19,10674,1,3,0)="will collect and transmitt all the entries in the PIVOT file that are of"
^DIC(19,10674,1,4,0)="an update to patient information.  The job will build PIMS A08 HL7 messages"
^DIC(19,10674,1,5,0)="and broadcast them to any subscriber."
^DIC(19,10674,1,6,0)=""
^DIC(19,10674,1,7,0)="The job should be re-scheduled to run about every 10 minutes.  The task"
^DIC(19,10674,1,8,0)="interval will determine approximately the maximum time it takes for an"
^DIC(19,10674,1,9,0)="update to patient information to be broadcast in a HL7 message."
^DIC(19,10674,1,10,0)=""
^DIC(19,10674,25)="EN^VAFHBGJ"
^DIC(19,10674,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,10674,"U")="UPDATE BATCH JOB"
^DIC(19,10675,0)="VAFC BATCH UPDATE^UPDATE BATCH JOB FOR HL7 v2.3^^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,10675,1,0)="^^9^9^2970612^^^^"
^DIC(19,10675,1,1,0)="This option is not intended to be run from programmer mode.  No output to"
^DIC(19,10675,1,2,0)="the screen is intended.  When this job is scheduled through TaskMan it"
^DIC(19,10675,1,3,0)="will collect and transmitt all the entries in the PIVOT file that are of"
^DIC(19,10675,1,4,0)="an update to patient information.  The job will build PIMS A08 HL7 v2.3"
^DIC(19,10675,1,5,0)="messages and broadcast them to any subscriber."
^DIC(19,10675,1,6,0)=""
^DIC(19,10675,1,7,0)="The job should be re-scheduled to run about every 10 minutes.  The task"
^DIC(19,10675,1,8,0)="interval will determine approximately the maximum time it takes for an"
^DIC(19,10675,1,9,0)="update to patient information to be broadcast in a HL7 message."
^DIC(19,10675,25)="MAIN^VAFCMSG"
^DIC(19,10675,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,10675,"U")="UPDATE BATCH JOB FOR HL7 V2.3"
^DIC(19,10676,0)="VAFC BATCH OUTPATIENT^OUTPATIENT BATCH JOB HL7 v2.3^^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,10676,1,0)="^^10^10^2970612^^^^"
^DIC(19,10676,1,1,0)="DO NOT SCHEDULE THIS OPTION UNLESS THERE IS A SPECIFIC APPLICATION THAT"
^DIC(19,10676,1,2,0)="REQUIRES NOTIFICATION OF SCHEDULING APPOINTMENTS WITH A HL7 A08 v2.3 MESSAGE."
^DIC(19,10676,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(19,10676,1,4,0)="This option is not intended to be run from programmer mode.  No output to"
^DIC(19,10676,1,5,0)="the screen is intended.  When this job is scheduled through TaskMan"
^DIC(19,10676,1,6,0)="a routine will loop through the Hospital Location file ""S"" node and"
^DIC(19,10676,1,7,0)="generate an A08 HL7 v2.3 message for all appointments for today that"
^DIC(19,10676,1,8,0)="have a status of ""No action taken"" or ""Future""."
^DIC(19,10676,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(19,10676,1,10,0)="It should be scheduled to run after midnight but before 0400 hours."
^DIC(19,10676,25)="EN^VAFCCOPT"
^DIC(19,10676,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,10676,"U")="OUTPATIENT BATCH JOB HL7 V2.3"
