^DIC(19,11182,0)="PSU PBM JOB CHECK^Pharmacy Background Job Check^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^367"
^DIC(19,11182,1,0)="^19.06^6^6^3040505^^^"
^DIC(19,11182,1,1,0)="This option will check to see if the monthly PBM statistics ran to"
^DIC(19,11182,1,2,0)="completion.  A MailMan message will be sent to the local PSU PBM mail"
^DIC(19,11182,1,3,0)="group and to the National PBM group at Hines if the report has not"
^DIC(19,11182,1,4,0)="completed in 6 days.  This option is scheduled automatically by the"
^DIC(19,11182,1,5,0)="PSU PBM AUTO option and normally does not need user intervention.  In case"
^DIC(19,11182,1,6,0)="of computer outage, it could be run manually."
^DIC(19,11182,25)="PSUCP2"
^DIC(19,11182,"U")="PHARMACY BACKGROUND JOB CHECK"
^DIC(19,11183,0)="TIUF NATL CS UTILITY^NATL Edit Document Definitions^^A^11712^^^^^^n^516^^1^1"
^DIC(19,11183,1,0)="^^222^222^2981013^"
^DIC(19,11183,1,1,0)="This is an EXTREMELY POWERFUL option for NATIONAL PROGRAMMERS only.  It"
^DIC(19,11183,1,2,0)="may also be used by CUSTOMER SERVICE, AFTER they have consulted with TIU"
^DIC(19,11183,1,3,0)="developers.  "
^DIC(19,11183,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,5,0)="           **** Who Should Use this Option *****"
^DIC(19,11183,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,7,0)="If a site has arranged with Customer Service to move Consult Titles from a"
^DIC(19,11183,1,8,0)="separate CLASS to Progress Notes, Customer Service may choose to give this"
^DIC(19,11183,1,9,0)="option to the person doing the moves.  Such persons should NEVER say YES"
^DIC(19,11183,1,10,0)="to an Override prompt except for the Missing Fields override, as noted"
^DIC(19,11183,1,11,0)="towards the bottom of this message.  If Customer Service has altered"
^DIC(19,11183,1,12,0)="this option before giving it to someone, they should restore it to its"
^DIC(19,11183,1,13,0)="original condition when the person has finished."
^DIC(19,11183,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,15,0)="In all other cases, Customer Service is requested to use the option"
^DIC(19,11183,1,16,0)="themselves rather than giving it to a site."
^DIC(19,11183,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,18,0)="Since this is NOT a site option, please do NOT give instructions for its"
^DIC(19,11183,1,19,0)="use in NOIS, in FORUM group messages, etc."
^DIC(19,11183,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,21,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,22,0)="This option is the same as TIUFH EDIT DDEFS MGR except much more powerful."
^DIC(19,11183,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,24,0)="It permits:"
^DIC(19,11183,1,25,0)="       Changing entries to/from National Standard"
^DIC(19,11183,1,26,0)="       Moving Titles between CLASSES"
^DIC(19,11183,1,27,0)="       Changing field OK TO DISTRIBUTE (# .13)"
^DIC(19,11183,1,28,0)="       "
^DIC(19,11183,1,29,0)="If user answers Yes to an override/bypass prompt, it also permits:"
^DIC(19,11183,1,30,0)="       Editing entries without INACTIVATING them"
^DIC(19,11183,1,31,0)="       Adding an item that is IN USE"
^DIC(19,11183,1,32,0)="       Deleting an item that is IN USE"
^DIC(19,11183,1,33,0)="       Selecting an item of the WRONG TYPE to add to a parent"
^DIC(19,11183,1,34,0)="       Moving documents to a faulty Title"
^DIC(19,11183,1,35,0)="       Moving a Title to a FAULTY Document Class"
^DIC(19,11183,1,36,0)="       Moving a FAULTY Title"
^DIC(19,11183,1,37,0)="       Moving a Title which will lack Technical Fields under the move"
^DIC(19,11183,1,38,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,39,0)="It does NOT permit:"
^DIC(19,11183,1,40,0)="       Most actions on National entries"
^DIC(19,11183,1,41,0)="       Adding an item you don't OWN to a parent"
^DIC(19,11183,1,42,0)="       Moving DOCUMENTS between CLASSES"
^DIC(19,11183,1,43,0)="       Adding ACTIVE items to a parent"
^DIC(19,11183,1,44,0)="       Deleting ACTIVE items from a parent"
^DIC(19,11183,1,45,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,46,0)="The above actions which are not permitted can still be done by changing"
^DIC(19,11183,1,47,0)="the offending property.  For example, to move documents between classes,"
^DIC(19,11183,1,48,0)="first move titles so that the documents are in the same class."
^DIC(19,11183,1,49,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,50,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,51,0)="WARNING: This tool permits actions under circumstances which are dangerous"
^DIC(19,11183,1,52,0)="and may have never been tested.  It is up to CUSTOMER SERVICE to consult"
^DIC(19,11183,1,53,0)="with TIU developers to find out what preparatory/followup actions may be"
^DIC(19,11183,1,54,0)="necessary IN ADDITION TO THOSE LISTED HERE, and to test all actions before"
^DIC(19,11183,1,55,0)="using this option in a live account.  Remember that moving entries in the"
^DIC(19,11183,1,56,0)="hierarchy can affect inherited Business Rules, Document Parameters, and"
^DIC(19,11183,1,57,0)="Basic/Technical/Upload Fields, and possibly hard code, for certain"
^DIC(19,11183,1,58,0)="entries."
^DIC(19,11183,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,60,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,61,0)="  ******* General Instructions for Moving Titles between Classes *********"
^DIC(19,11183,1,62,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,63,0)="Moving Titles between Classes should be undertaken only after consulting"
^DIC(19,11183,1,64,0)="TIU developers and/or Customer Service, and in close cooperation with IRM"
^DIC(19,11183,1,65,0)="at the site.  It may require programmer expertise."
^DIC(19,11183,1,66,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,67,0)="The option TIUF NATL CS UTILITY takes you into the Edit Document"
^DIC(19,11183,1,68,0)="Definitions screen.  Use the Copy/Move action: Move Title.  You will be"
^DIC(19,11183,1,69,0)="able to select Document Classes OUTSIDE the original class.  This does NOT"
^DIC(19,11183,1,70,0)="require answering YES to an override prompt."
^DIC(19,11183,1,71,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,72,0)="After you move a title, the program will attempt to update documents using"
^DIC(19,11183,1,73,0)="the moved title.  If a document is being edited while this program is"
^DIC(19,11183,1,74,0)="attempting to update it, the screen will write the IFN of the document not"
^DIC(19,11183,1,75,0)="updated, the document IFN will be saved as DA in"
^DIC(19,11183,1,76,0)="        ^XTMP(""TIUFMOVEN""_TITLEDA,DA),"
^DIC(19,11183,1,77,0)="and the document will be skipped.  The class the Title was moved FROM will"
^DIC(19,11183,1,78,0)="be saved as OLDCLASS in"
^DIC(19,11183,1,79,0)="        ^XTMP(""TIUFMOVEN""_TITLEDA)=OLDCLASS."
^DIC(19,11183,1,80,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,81,0)="At the end of the Move Title action, if all documents have been updated,"
^DIC(19,11183,1,82,0)="the screen will so state.  If not, the user will be asked to update them"
^DIC(19,11183,1,83,0)="using action U, 'Update Documents'. This Update (as well as the Move Title"
^DIC(19,11183,1,84,0)="action) must be done through this option [TIUF NATL CS UTILITY] in order"
^DIC(19,11183,1,85,0)="to update both Parent Document Type, AND Class cross-references. It may be"
^DIC(19,11183,1,86,0)="necessary to Update more than once.  The action so states when all"
^DIC(19,11183,1,87,0)="documents have been successfully updated."
^DIC(19,11183,1,88,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,89,0)="The first global, above, is updated with every Update action, and"
^DIC(19,11183,1,90,0)="increases the efficiency of subsequent Updates."
^DIC(19,11183,1,91,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,92,0)="The second global is ESSENTIAL to the process of updating after moving a"
^DIC(19,11183,1,93,0)="title between classes, since it stores OLDCLASS, which is required for"
^DIC(19,11183,1,94,0)="updating cross references."
^DIC(19,11183,1,95,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,96,0)="These globals will exist for 30 days after the title is moved or updated"
^DIC(19,11183,1,97,0)="(or until another national move is done on this title, if that time is"
^DIC(19,11183,1,98,0)="shorter than 30 days).  So please finish your updating within that time"
^DIC(19,11183,1,99,0)="period."
^DIC(19,11183,1,100,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,101,0)="         ******* Updating Documents, One at a Time *******"
^DIC(19,11183,1,102,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,103,0)="This is an ALTERNATIVE to the Update action described above.  In some"
^DIC(19,11183,1,104,0)="cases, it may be more convenient to update a single document from"
^DIC(19,11183,1,105,0)="programmer mode rather than using action Update Documents, which updates"
^DIC(19,11183,1,106,0)="ALL documents using the title."
^DIC(19,11183,1,107,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,108,0)="After moving the title, print out global    ^XTMP(""TIUFMOVEN""_TITLEDA, and"
^DIC(19,11183,1,109,0)="save it.  It has the form: "
^DIC(19,11183,1,110,0)="                      ^XTMP(""TIUFMOVEN""_TITLEDA)=OLDCLASS"
^DIC(19,11183,1,111,0)="                      ^XTMP(""TIUFMOVEN""_TITLEDA,DA)="""", where"
^DIC(19,11183,1,112,0)="     TITLEDA is the IFN in 8925.1 of the moved title"
^DIC(19,11183,1,113,0)="     OLDCLASS is the IFN in 8925.1 of the class the title was moved FROM"
^DIC(19,11183,1,114,0)="     DA is the IFN in 8925 of the document using the title"
^DIC(19,11183,1,115,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,116,0)="Then use DDEF options to look up XDCDA = the IFN of the Document Class the"
^DIC(19,11183,1,117,0)="title was moved TO.  Repeat, moved TO.  "
^DIC(19,11183,1,118,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,119,0)="Now, for every document DA in the above ^XTMP global, call"
^DIC(19,11183,1,120,0)="  MTRPT1^TIUFHA8(TITLEDA,DA,XDCDA,OLDCLASS)."
^DIC(19,11183,1,121,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,122,0)="When every document has been successfully updated using this call, you are"
^DIC(19,11183,1,123,0)="done."
^DIC(19,11183,1,124,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,125,0)="          ****** Adding/Deleting Titles which are IN USE ******"
^DIC(19,11183,1,126,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,127,0)="If you delete a Title which is IN USE from its parent Document Class, the"
^DIC(19,11183,1,128,0)="documents using it will not function.  However, there have been cases"
^DIC(19,11183,1,129,0)="where this is the best way to correct a hierarchy which has been"
^DIC(19,11183,1,130,0)="abnormally altered.  "
^DIC(19,11183,1,131,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,132,0)="When deleting such an item, note the CLASS it was in.  Then add it to the"
^DIC(19,11183,1,133,0)="proper Document Class.  Then do Update Parent Document Type for the Title."
^DIC(19,11183,1,134,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,135,0)="NOTE: If Parent Document Type is not correct for a document, the document"
^DIC(19,11183,1,136,0)="will not appear properly in Parent Document Type Cross Reference ADCPT. At"
^DIC(19,11183,1,137,0)="present the only known consequence of this is generating/failing to"
^DIC(19,11183,1,138,0)="generate CWAD alerts.  However, future changes, national or local, may"
^DIC(19,11183,1,139,0)="create other consequences, so please update this field."
^DIC(19,11183,1,140,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,141,0)="If the Title has changed CLASS under this ""move"", you will ALSO need to"
^DIC(19,11183,1,142,0)="call the following code: D TLDOCMTS^TIUFHA8(TITLEDA,OLDCLASS), where"
^DIC(19,11183,1,143,0)="TITLEDA is the IEN of the ""moved"" Title and OLDCLASS is the IEN of the old"
^DIC(19,11183,1,144,0)="Class the title was in.  Do this AFTER the title is where you want it in"
^DIC(19,11183,1,145,0)="the hierarchy; it will get its NEW class from its current position in the"
^DIC(19,11183,1,146,0)="hierarchy.  This code sets the new class nodes for all documents using"
^DIC(19,11183,1,147,0)="TITLEDA, for cross references APTCL, APTCL38, ACLSB, ACLPT, ACLAU, and"
^DIC(19,11183,1,148,0)="ACLEC.  If OLDCLASS is not 0, it first kills the nodes for the old class."
^DIC(19,11183,1,149,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,150,0)="(Simply reindexing documents will not kill old nodes, since the old class"
^DIC(19,11183,1,151,0)="is unknown to the computer.)"
^DIC(19,11183,1,152,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,153,0)="If the Title you are adding as an item was never IN A CLASS, follow the"
^DIC(19,11183,1,154,0)="above instructions with OLDCLASS=0."
^DIC(19,11183,1,155,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,156,0)="NOTE: If a document was never in a class or if it has changed classes"
^DIC(19,11183,1,157,0)="without calling the above code, it may not appear under appropriate"
^DIC(19,11183,1,158,0)="options, e.g., Review Progress Notes.  Or it may mistakenly appear under"
^DIC(19,11183,1,159,0)="some other option."
^DIC(19,11183,1,160,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,161,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,162,0)="      ******* Moving Consult Titles to Progress Notes ******"
^DIC(19,11183,1,163,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,164,0)="These are steps to be followed when moving consult titles which are"
^DIC(19,11183,1,165,0)="already IN USE from CLASS Consults to a new Consults document class under"
^DIC(19,11183,1,166,0)="class Progress Notes."
^DIC(19,11183,1,167,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,168,0)="1) Inactivate class Consults if you have not already done so."
^DIC(19,11183,1,169,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,170,0)="2) Create a new document class ZZCONSULTS under Progress Notes. (Call it,"
^DIC(19,11183,1,171,0)="say, ZZCONSULTS for now so it won't confuse Joel's code which looks for a"
^DIC(19,11183,1,172,0)="CL or DC called ""CONSULTS."")  Leave it INACTIVE."
^DIC(19,11183,1,173,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,174,0)="3) Set up basic fields, upload fields, TIU document parameters, and"
^DIC(19,11183,1,175,0)="business rules for ZZCONSULTS so that values inherited by titles under it"
^DIC(19,11183,1,176,0)="will be correct.  (Technical fields can be set up later, using option TIU"
^DIC(19,11183,1,177,0)="DEFINE CONSULTS.)"
^DIC(19,11183,1,178,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,179,0)="4) Check titles presently under Class Consults to make sure you want them"
^DIC(19,11183,1,180,0)="all and that they are named correctly."
^DIC(19,11183,1,181,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,182,0)="5) Choose a time when users are not likely to be editing existing"
^DIC(19,11183,1,183,0)="consult documents. Use option TIUF NATL CS UTILITY to move Consult"
^DIC(19,11183,1,184,0)="titles from step 3), one at a time, to DC ZZCONSULTS.  If Technical fields"
^DIC(19,11183,1,185,0)="are missing, answer YES when asked if you want to move the title even"
^DIC(19,11183,1,186,0)="though it is missing technical fields.  You will take care of these fields"
^DIC(19,11183,1,187,0)="later. "
^DIC(19,11183,1,188,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,189,0)="The option then updates document class ZZCONSULTS, the moved title,"
^DIC(19,11183,1,190,0)="and the documents using the title. Documents using the title are updated"
^DIC(19,11183,1,191,0)="with the new Parent Document Type (field # .04).  Class cross-references"
^DIC(19,11183,1,192,0)="for the document are killed and reset."
^DIC(19,11183,1,193,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,194,0)="If some document was not available (locked) at the time the move code"
^DIC(19,11183,1,195,0)="attempted to update it, you will see a message to that effect when code"
^DIC(19,11183,1,196,0)="has finished moving the title.  If so, use option TIUF NATL CS UTILITY "
^DIC(19,11183,1,197,0)="and run action Update documents, under Copy/Move, for its title.  You may"
^DIC(19,11183,1,198,0)="have to run it more than once."
^DIC(19,11183,1,199,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,200,0)="6) Delete Business Rules and TIU Document Parameters for (old) Consult"
^DIC(19,11183,1,201,0)="Document Classes under (old) Class Consults, and for (old) Class Consults"
^DIC(19,11183,1,202,0)="itself."
^DIC(19,11183,1,203,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,204,0)="7) Delete (old) Consult Document Classes under Class Consults and then"
^DIC(19,11183,1,205,0)="(old) Class Consults itself."
^DIC(19,11183,1,206,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,207,0)="8) Change name of document class ZZCONSULTS to CONSULTS."
^DIC(19,11183,1,208,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,209,0)="9) Rerun option TIU DEFINE CONSULTS.  This option was included in patch"
^DIC(19,11183,1,210,0)="TIU*1*4.  It should find the new document class CONSULTS and set"
^DIC(19,11183,1,211,0)="appropriate technical fields.  Patch TIU*1*4 also includes instructions on"
^DIC(19,11183,1,212,0)="business rules and TIU document parameters for CONSULTS.  If they have not"
^DIC(19,11183,1,213,0)="already been set up, do this now.  If this option has already been run for"
^DIC(19,11183,1,214,0)="class CONSULTS, those technical fields may be manually copied into"
^DIC(19,11183,1,215,0)="document class CONSULTS as an alternative to rerunning the option."
^DIC(19,11183,1,216,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,217,0)="10) Check existing consult documents.  Make sure they display in the CPRS"
^DIC(19,11183,1,218,0)="NOTES tab of the CPRS chart."
^DIC(19,11183,1,219,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11183,1,220,0)="11) Activate document class CONSULTS and then the titles below it. Make"
^DIC(19,11183,1,221,0)="sure you can create a consult note and link it to a consult request from"
^DIC(19,11183,1,222,0)="the NOTES tab of the CPRS chart."
^DIC(19,11183,15)="K TIUFPRIV"
^DIC(19,11183,20)="Q:'$G(TIUFPRIV)  N TIUFWHO,TIUFMOVE S (TIUFWHO,TIUFMOVE)=""N"" D EN^TIUFH"
^DIC(19,11183,99)="56434,85597"
^DIC(19,11183,"U")="NATL EDIT DOCUMENT DEFINITIONS"
^DIC(19,11184,0)="TIUFZZ8 UPDATE PARENT DOC TYPE^ZZ Update Parent Document Type^^A^11712^^^^^^^^^1"
^DIC(19,11184,1,0)="^^4^4^2980818^^^^"
^DIC(19,11184,1,1,0)="Updates PARENT DOCUMENT TYPE (#.04) for TIU DOCUMENT FILE (#8925) for"
^DIC(19,11184,1,2,0)="all documents, one title at a time.  Must be run by sites that have moved"
^DIC(19,11184,1,3,0)="documents prior to patch TIU*1*27.  Should be deleted when finished.  May"
^DIC(19,11184,1,4,0)="be run over itself, although this is not efficient."
^DIC(19,11184,20)="D ZZUPDATE^TIUFZZ8"
^DIC(19,11184,"U")="ZZ UPDATE PARENT DOCUMENT TYPE"
^DIC(19,11185,0)="ECXPRO^Prosthetics Extract^^R^10000000216^^^^^^^513"
^DIC(19,11185,1,0)="^^1^1^2980715^"
^DIC(19,11185,1,1,0)="This option will execute the Prosthetics extract."
^DIC(19,11185,10.1)="Prosthetics Extract"
^DIC(19,11185,25)="BEG^ECXPRO"
^DIC(19,11185,"U")="PROSTHETICS EXTRACT"
^DIC(19,11186,0)="ECX PRO SOURCE AUDIT^Prosthetics (PRO) Extract Audit^^R^10000000216^^^^^^^513"
^DIC(19,11186,1,0)="^^2^2^2980715^"
^DIC(19,11186,1,1,0)="This option will generate an audit report of the prosthetics information"
^DIC(19,11186,1,2,0)="that has been extracted."
^DIC(19,11186,10.1)="PRO Extract Audit"
^DIC(19,11186,25)="BEGIN^ECXAPRO"
^DIC(19,11186,"U")="PROSTHETICS (PRO) EXTRACT AUDI"
^DIC(19,11187,0)="PRCH CHARGE CARD REG. EXCEPT^Charge Card Reg. Exception^^R^11740^^^^^^^121"
^DIC(19,11187,1,0)="^^1^1^2980908^^"
^DIC(19,11187,1,1,0)="This is a charge card registration exception list."
^DIC(19,11187,25)="EN3^PRCH2A"
^DIC(19,11187,"U")="CHARGE CARD REG. EXCEPTION"
^DIC(19,11188,0)="PRCH INACTIVATE EXP CHAR CARD^Inactivate Expired Charge Cards^^R^11740^^^^^^^121"
^DIC(19,11188,1,0)="^19.06^1^1^3000607^^^"
^DIC(19,11188,1,1,0)="This option is used to inactivate the expired charge cards."
^DIC(19,11188,25)="EN^PRCH3A"
^DIC(19,11188,"U")="INACTIVATE EXPIRED CHARGE CARD"
^DIC(19,11189,0)="ORCM LIST ORDER MENUS^List Primary Order Menus^^R^11712^^^^^^^170"
^DIC(19,11189,1,0)="^^3^3^2981104^^"
^DIC(19,11189,1,1,0)="This option will print a list of users, locations, divisions etc. that"
^DIC(19,11189,1,2,0)="have a specified order menu assigned for use in the List Manager"
^DIC(19,11189,1,3,0)="interface."
^DIC(19,11189,25)="AOPAR^ORCMEDT5"
^DIC(19,11189,"U")="LIST PRIMARY ORDER MENUS"
^DIC(19,11190,0)="IBCN INSURANCE BUFFER PROCESS^Process Insurance Buffer^^R^10000000033^^^^^^^192"
^DIC(19,11190,1,0)="^^1^1^2980416^^"
^DIC(19,11190,1,1,0)="Display screens and processing actions for the Insurance Buffer."
^DIC(19,11190,25)="EN^IBCNBLL"
^DIC(19,11190,"U")="PROCESS INSURANCE BUFFER"
^DIC(19,11191,0)="IBCN OUTPUT INS BUFF ACTIVITY^Insurance Buffer Activity^^R^1^^^^^^^192"
^DIC(19,11191,1,0)="^^5^5^3211008^"
^DIC(19,11191,1,1,0)="This report provides a summary of the activity within the Insurance "
^DIC(19,11191,1,2,0)="Buffer. Counts, percentages, and average processing times are included "
^DIC(19,11191,1,3,0)="for both processed and unprocessed entries.  The report can be printed "
^DIC(19,11191,1,4,0)="with totals for previous completed months or with totals for a selected "
^DIC(19,11191,1,5,0)="date range."
^DIC(19,11191,25)="IBCNBOA"
^DIC(19,11191,99.1)="62867,39035"
^DIC(19,11191,"U")="INSURANCE BUFFER ACTIVITY"
^DIC(19,11192,0)="IBCN OUTPUT INS BUFF EMPLOYEE^Insurance Buffer Employee^^R^1^^^^^^^192"
^DIC(19,11192,1,0)="^^7^7^3211026^"
^DIC(19,11192,1,1,0)="This report provides a summary of entries in the Insurance Buffer by"
^DIC(19,11192,1,2,0)="employee. There are two variations of this report. One is for those"
^DIC(19,11192,1,3,0)="employees that create/enter new Buffer entries. The other variation is for"
^DIC(19,11192,1,4,0)="those employees that process (accept/reject) Buffer entries. The report"
^DIC(19,11192,1,5,0)="may be printed for one selected employee or all employees using the"
^DIC(19,11192,1,6,0)="Buffer. Counts and percentages are included and can be printed for"
^DIC(19,11192,1,7,0)="completed previous months or for a specified date range."
^DIC(19,11192,25)="IBCNBOE"
^DIC(19,11192,99.1)="62867,39085"
^DIC(19,11192,"U")="INSURANCE BUFFER EMPLOYEE"
^DIC(19,11193,0)="IBCN INSURANCE BUFFER PURGE^Purge Insurance Buffer^^R^10000000033^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11193,1,0)="^^2^2^2981016^^^^"
^DIC(19,11193,1,1,0)="This option may be used to purge the Insurance Buffer of entries that "
^DIC(19,11193,1,2,0)="were processed (accepted or rejected) at least one year ago."
^DIC(19,11193,25)="IBCNBPG"
^DIC(19,11193,"U")="PURGE INSURANCE BUFFER"
