^DIC(19,11226,0)="DGEN ENROLLEES BY STATUS^Enrollees by Status,Priority,Preferred Facility^^R^1253^^^^^^^114"
^DIC(19,11226,1,0)="^^4^4^2980619^"
^DIC(19,11226,1,1,0)="The report provides counts of patients by enrollment status, priority, and"
^DIC(19,11226,1,2,0)="preferred facility.  The user can select the statuses, priorities, and"
^DIC(19,11226,1,3,0)="facilities to include in the report.  An optional patient listing of those"
^DIC(19,11226,1,4,0)="patients included in the statistics can also be requested."
^DIC(19,11226,10.1)="Enrollee Statistics"
^DIC(19,11226,25)="REPORT^DGENRPC1"
^DIC(19,11226,"U")="ENROLLEES BY STATUS,PRIORITY,P"
^DIC(19,11227,0)="DGEN APPTS,NOT ENROLLED^Upcoming Appointments without Enrollment^^R^1253^^^^^^^114"
^DIC(19,11227,1,0)="^^3^3^2980619^"
^DIC(19,11227,1,1,0)="This is a report of patients with appointments that are not enrolled and do"
^DIC(19,11227,1,2,0)="not have pending enrollment applications.  The report is by division and"
^DIC(19,11227,1,3,0)="clinic."
^DIC(19,11227,25)="REPORT^DGENRPD1"
^DIC(19,11227,"U")="UPCOMING APPOINTMENTS WITHOUT "
^DIC(19,11228,0)="DGEN ENROLLED VETERANS^Enrolled Veterans Report^^R^1253^^^^^^y^114"
^DIC(19,11228,1,0)="^^3^3^2970722^^^^"
^DIC(19,11228,1,1,0)="This option will be used to produce the ENROLLED VETERANS REPORT."
^DIC(19,11228,1,2,0)="This report contains a summary of the number of patients in each"
^DIC(19,11228,1,3,0)="enrollment priority group."
^DIC(19,11228,25)="REPORT^DGENRPA1"
^DIC(19,11228,99)="57141,36573"
^DIC(19,11228,"U")="ENROLLED VETERANS REPORT"
^DIC(19,11229,0)="SCMC PATIENT ASSIGN/UNASSIGN^Team/Position Assignment/Re-Assignment^This functionality is now accomplished by the PCMM Web Application.^A^1^SC PCMM ROLL^^^^^^16^^1"
^DIC(19,11229,1,0)="^^22^22^3040423^"
^DIC(19,11229,1,1,0)="Determines patient's Primary Care status.  Based on status it will prompt"
^DIC(19,11229,1,2,0)="the user to select from the following choices:"
^DIC(19,11229,1,3,0)="      "
^DIC(19,11229,1,4,0)="       o  Assign patient to Primary Care or non-primary care team  "
^DIC(19,11229,1,5,0)="          (if not currently assigned)"
^DIC(19,11229,1,6,0)="·      o Assign patient to PC or non-primary care  Practitioner position "
^DIC(19,11229,1,7,0)="         (if assigned to a team, but not PC practitioner).  User can look-up by "
^DIC(19,11229,1,8,0)="        either position name or the current practitioner assigned to the position."
^DIC(19,11229,1,9,0)="       o  Unassign from team (if assigned to a PC or non-PC team).  If patient is"
^DIC(19,11229,1,10,0)="          assigned to PC position, both the PC position and PC team will be unassigned."
^DIC(19,11229,1,11,0)="       o  Unassign from position "
^DIC(19,11229,1,12,0)="      "
^DIC(19,11229,1,13,0)="     While assigning/unassigning from a position: If the position has an"
^DIC(19,11229,1,14,0)="     Associated Clinic, the user will be prompted to enroll/discharge the"
^DIC(19,11229,1,15,0)="     patient from that Associated Clinic."
^DIC(19,11229,1,16,0)="      "
^DIC(19,11229,1,17,0)="     Limitations:"
^DIC(19,11229,1,18,0)="       o  Does not provide edit or delete functionality.  "
^DIC(19,11229,1,19,0)="       o  Does not allow for re-assignment for patients with future PC"
^DIC(19,11229,1,20,0)="          assignments."
^DIC(19,11229,1,21,0)="       o  Requires that position has a practitioner currently assigned to it."
^DIC(19,11229,1,22,0)="    To overcome the above limitations, the PCMM GUI must be used."
^DIC(19,11229,20)="D EN^SCMCQK"
^DIC(19,11229,99)="57544,58472"
^DIC(19,11229,99.1)="59389,47775"
^DIC(19,11229,"U")="TEAM/POSITION ASSIGNMENT/RE-AS"
^DIC(19,11230,0)="SCMC MU MASS TEAM UNASSIGNMENT^Mass Team/Position Unassignment^This functionality is now accomplished by the PCMM Web Application.^A^1^^^^^^^16^^1"
^DIC(19,11230,1,0)="^^16^16^2980915^^^^"
^DIC(19,11230,1,1,0)=" The Mass Team/Position Unassignment option can be used to unassign a large"
^DIC(19,11230,1,2,0)=" number of patients from an active team or an active position using the List"
^DIC(19,11230,1,3,0)=" Manager functionality.  It is recommended that distribution of this option be"
^DIC(19,11230,1,4,0)=" limited."
^DIC(19,11230,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11230,1,6,0)=" The effective date you choose for the unassignment may be in the past, today,"
^DIC(19,11230,1,7,0)=" or in the future.  The list of patients displayed contains all patients with"
^DIC(19,11230,1,8,0)=" assignments to the selected team/position, as of the selected effective date"
^DIC(19,11230,1,9,0)=" or after the effective date.  Those with assignment dates in the future will"
^DIC(19,11230,1,10,0)=" show an asterisk (*) next to the assigned date. "
^DIC(19,11230,1,11,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11230,1,12,0)=" When patients are unassigned from the team, they are also automatically"
^DIC(19,11230,1,13,0)=" unassigned from any associated position.  If a position is associated with"
^DIC(19,11230,1,14,0)=" a clinic, you are given the opportunity to also discharge patients from"
^DIC(19,11230,1,15,0)=" the clinic."
^DIC(19,11230,1,16,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11230,20)="D EN^SCMCMU"
^DIC(19,11230,99.1)="59389,47775"
^DIC(19,11230,"U")="MASS TEAM/POSITION UNASSIGNMEN"
^DIC(19,11231,0)="SC PCMM POSITION ASSIGN REVIEW^Patient Team Position Assignment Review^^R^11281^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,11231,1,0)="^^31^31^2990709^^^^"
^DIC(19,11231,1,1,0)="This option compares all PATIENT TEAM POSITION ASSIGNMENT (#404.43) file"
^DIC(19,11231,1,2,0)="entries with the corresponding PATIENT TEAM ASSIGNMENT (#404.42) file entries."
^DIC(19,11231,1,3,0)="The comparison checks to make sure that the position assignment active "
^DIC(19,11231,1,4,0)="timeframe is within the team assignment active timeframe."
^DIC(19,11231,1,5,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11231,1,6,0)="This report lists those position assignments that fall outside the team"
^DIC(19,11231,1,7,0)="assignment active timeframe."
^DIC(19,11231,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11231,1,9,0)="For example, the following situation would be listed on the report since"
^DIC(19,11231,1,10,0)="the team assignment is inactive but the position assignment is still"
^DIC(19,11231,1,11,0)="active."
^DIC(19,11231,1,12,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11231,1,13,0)="                         Assigned              Unassigned"
^DIC(19,11231,1,14,0)="                           Date                   Date"
^DIC(19,11231,1,15,0)="                         --------              ----------"
^DIC(19,11231,1,16,0)="   Team Assignment      01/01/1997             10/31/1997"
^DIC(19,11231,1,17,0)="   Position Assignment  02/15/1997               <none>"
^DIC(19,11231,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11231,1,19,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11231,1,20,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11231,1,21,0)="Note: The PCMM software has been changed to prevent this and similar"
^DIC(19,11231,1,22,0)="      situations from occurring. However, older versions of PCMM did"
^DIC(19,11231,1,23,0)="      allow these assignment timeframe problems to occur. This report"
^DIC(19,11231,1,24,0)="      should help the site correct these problem assignments."
^DIC(19,11231,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11231,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11231,1,27,0)="Note: Currently, this report can only be run in a 'diagnostic' mode."
^DIC(19,11231,1,28,0)="      In the future, the report maybe enhanced to run in a 'fix' mode."
^DIC(19,11231,1,29,0)="      The 'fix' mode option would also correct the problem assignments"
^DIC(19,11231,1,30,0)="      based on criteria the user specifies."
^DIC(19,11231,1,31,0)="      "
^DIC(19,11231,25)="EN^SCMCTPU3"
^DIC(19,11231,99.1)="57964,82917"
^DIC(19,11231,"U")="PATIENT TEAM POSITION ASSIGNME"
