^DIC(19,11391,"U")="MST OUTPUTS"
^DIC(19,11392,0)="DGMST SUMMARY REPORT^MST Summary Report^MST reports are available at vssc.domain.ext^R^1^^^^^^y^"
^DIC(19,11392,1,0)="^^5^5^2990208^^"
^DIC(19,11392,1,1,0)="This report will print a summary of the Military Sexual Trauma (MST)"
^DIC(19,11392,1,2,0)="status information broken down by gender and status.  For Male and Female"
^DIC(19,11392,1,3,0)="gender, the report will display total count for each status and percent of"
^DIC(19,11392,1,4,0)="total.  The report will also include total patient count and percentage of"
^DIC(19,11392,1,5,0)="total."
^DIC(19,11392,25)="EN^DGMSTR1"
^DIC(19,11392,"U")="MST SUMMARY REPORT"
^DIC(19,11393,0)="DGMST STATISTICAL PRINT^Print Statistical Report^MST reports are available at vssc.domain.ext^R^1^^^^^^y^"
^DIC(19,11393,1,0)="^^7^7^2990204^^"
^DIC(19,11393,1,1,0)="Prints the MST Statistical Report."
^DIC(19,11393,1,2,0)="This report contains both Outpatient and Inpatient statistics."
^DIC(19,11393,1,3,0)="The number of encounters/movements related to MST and those not related"
^DIC(19,11393,1,4,0)="to MST are calculated.  Averages are also calculated for encounters related and not related to MST."
^DIC(19,11393,1,5,0)="For inpatients, the Total Length of Stay for MST related episodes is"
^DIC(19,11393,1,6,0)="determined.  Also, a breakdown for each ICD-9 code assigned to a "
^DIC(19,11393,1,7,0)="patient movement or encounter, by patient sex, is calculated."
^DIC(19,11393,25)="EN^DGMSTR3"
^DIC(19,11393,99.1)="63265,37066"
^DIC(19,11393,"U")="PRINT STATISTICAL REPORT"
^DIC(19,11394,0)="DGMST HISTORY REPORT^MST History Report by Patient^MST reports are available at vssc.domain.ext^A^1^^^^^^^114^^1"
^DIC(19,11394,1,0)="^^4^4^2990208^"
^DIC(19,11394,1,1,0)="This will print the contents of the MST HISTORY File (29.11) for selected"
^DIC(19,11394,1,2,0)="patients sorted by name, with the most recent status entry first.  For"
^DIC(19,11394,1,3,0)="each status, the status change date, status, provider who determined"
^DIC(19,11394,1,4,0)="the status, and the user who entered the status will be displayed."
^DIC(19,11394,20)="D EN^DGMSTR4"
^DIC(19,11394,99.1)="61185,35431"
^DIC(19,11394,"U")="MST HISTORY REPORT BY PATIENT"
^DIC(19,11395,0)="DGMST DETAILED REPORT^Detailed Demographic Report^MST reports are available at vssc.domain.ext^A^1^^^^^^^114^^1"
^DIC(19,11395,1,0)="^^4^4^2990324^^"
^DIC(19,11395,1,1,0)="This will provide detailed demographic data for selected MST status codes"
^DIC(19,11395,1,2,0)="for user specified date ranges.  Additional selection criteria include "
^DIC(19,11395,1,3,0)="gender and period of service.  This report will sort by patient name"
^DIC(19,11395,1,4,0)="or period of service/patient name."
^DIC(19,11395,20)="D EN^DGMSTR2"
^DIC(19,11395,99.1)="63265,37036"
^DIC(19,11395,"U")="DETAILED DEMOGRAPHIC REPORT"
^DIC(19,11396,0)="DG MEANS TEST SPEC INCOME RPT^Means Test Specific Income Amount Report^^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11396,1,0)="^^4^4^2990217^"
^DIC(19,11396,1,1,0)="This report wil print veteran information for those who reported a specific"
^DIC(19,11396,1,2,0)="dollar amount.  The user will be asked for a date range and income range."
^DIC(19,11396,1,3,0)="Those veterans who fall within the entered criteria will have their Name,"
^DIC(19,11396,1,4,0)="SSN, Income Amount, and the Date MT was Completed, printed."
^DIC(19,11396,25)="ENSDA^DGMTARR"
^DIC(19,11396,99.1)="57757,40550"
^DIC(19,11396,"U")="MEANS TEST SPECIFIC INCOME AMO"
^DIC(19,11397,0)="DG MEANS TEST INC < THRESH RPT^Means Test Specific Income Less Threshold Report^^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11397,1,0)="^^5^5^2990217^"
^DIC(19,11397,1,1,0)="This report will print veterans who's income fell below the threshold"
^DIC(19,11397,1,2,0)="amount by a specified dollar amount.  The user will be asked to enter"
^DIC(19,11397,1,3,0)="the dollar range which they would like reported.  The report will"
^DIC(19,11397,1,4,0)="print veterans Name, SSN, Dollars below Threshold, and Means Test"
^DIC(19,11397,1,5,0)="Completion Date/Time."
^DIC(19,11397,25)="ENLTT^DGMTARR"
^DIC(19,11397,99.1)="57757,40550"
^DIC(19,11397,"U")="MEANS TEST SPECIFIC INCOME LES"
^DIC(19,11398,0)="DGEN EGT IMPACT REPORT^EGT Impact Report^^R^11281^^^^^^y^114"
^DIC(19,11398,1,0)="^^7^7^2990524^"
^DIC(19,11398,1,1,0)="This option will let the user choose to run one of four EGT Impact"
^DIC(19,11398,1,2,0)="Reports: EGT Preliminary Summary Impact Report, EGT Preliminary Detailed"
^DIC(19,11398,1,3,0)="Impact Report, EGT Actual Summary Impact Report, and EGT Actual Detailed"
^DIC(19,11398,1,4,0)="Impact Report. According to the criteria selected by the user, these four"
^DIC(19,11398,1,5,0)="reports will provide either a summarized count or the detailed information"
^DIC(19,11398,1,6,0)="of the patients who are either potentially or actually affected by the EGT"
^DIC(19,11398,1,7,0)="change."
^DIC(19,11398,25)="DGENRPT"
^DIC(19,11398,"U")="EGT IMPACT REPORT"
^DIC(19,11399,0)="DG MISSING NEW PERSON FILE SSN^Missing New Person File SSN Report^^P^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11399,1,0)="^^4^4^2990104^"
^DIC(19,11399,1,1,0)="This option produces a list of active users without a social security"
^DIC(19,11399,1,2,0)="number defined in the NEW PERSON (#200) file.  A social security number is"
^DIC(19,11399,1,3,0)="required to access a PATIENT (#2) file if parameter prohibiting access to"
^DIC(19,11399,1,4,0)="your own PATIENT (#2) file record is enabled."
^DIC(19,11399,60)="VA(200,"
^DIC(19,11399,61)=1
^DIC(19,11399,62)=0
^DIC(19,11399,63)="[DG MISSING SSN PRINT]"
^DIC(19,11399,64)="[DG MISSING SSN SORT]"
^DIC(19,11399,"U")="MISSING NEW PERSON FILE SSN RE"
^DIC(19,11400,0)="DGMTH HARDSHIPS^Hardships^^A^11281^DG MEANSTEST^^^^^^114^^1^1"
^DIC(19,11400,1,0)="^^1^1^2990617^"
^DIC(19,11400,1,1,0)="Allows the user to grant, edit, and delete hardships for the current means tests."
^DIC(19,11400,15)="K DGMTYPT"
^DIC(19,11400,20)="D HARDSHIP^DGMTHL"
^DIC(19,11400,"U")="HARDSHIPS"
^DIC(19,11401,0)="IVM FINANCIAL QUERY^IVM Financial Query^^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11401,1,0)="^^4^4^2980615^^^^"
^DIC(19,11401,1,1,0)="This option permits financial queries to be sent to the Health Eligibility"
^DIC(19,11401,1,2,0)="Center (HEC).  This option is used to query the HEC for a patient's most"
^DIC(19,11401,1,3,0)="recent financial information.  This financial information may include"
^DIC(19,11401,1,4,0)="Means Test, Copay Test, and Income Screening data."
^DIC(19,11401,25)="OPT^IVMCQ"
^DIC(19,11401,"U")="IVM FINANCIAL QUERY"
^DIC(19,11402,0)="SCRPW CLINIC APP AVA RPT^Clinic Appointment Availability Report^^R^.5^^^^^^^16"
^DIC(19,11402,1,0)="^^4^4^2990430^"
^DIC(19,11402,1,1,0)="Option for printing clinic appointment availability and utilization"
^DIC(19,11402,1,2,0)="statistics.  This report can be used to validate data transmitted to"
^DIC(19,11402,1,3,0)="Austin in the 'Clinic Waiting Time' extracts distributed in patch"
^DIC(19,11402,1,4,0)="SD*5.3*192."
^DIC(19,11402,25)="SCRPW70"
^DIC(19,11402,"U")="CLINIC APPOINTMENT AVAILABILIT"
^DIC(19,11403,0)="SCMC PC ATTENDING CONVERSION^PC Attending Conversion Utility^This functionality is now accomplished by the PCMM Web Application.^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11403,1,0)="^^13^13^2990623^^^"
^DIC(19,11403,1,1,0)="This tool will allow the user to convert current and future PC"
^DIC(19,11403,1,2,0)="Attending assignments to PC Practitioner assignments.  Any assignment"
^DIC(19,11403,1,3,0)="that is not current, discharged, will not be affected.  This"
^DIC(19,11403,1,4,0)="utility can be run in one of two modes CHECK or FIX.  CHECK will"
^DIC(19,11403,1,5,0)="go through the same procedures and checks that the FIX mode does"
^DIC(19,11403,1,6,0)="only it will not convert the assignments.   It will provide the"
^DIC(19,11403,1,7,0)="same report for the user to review."
^DIC(19,11403,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11403,1,9,0)="It is strongly recommended that the CHECK method be utilized first."
^DIC(19,11403,1,10,0)="This will give the user an understanding of how many records are"
^DIC(19,11403,1,11,0)="affected.  When the decission is made to run in FIX mode, it is"
^DIC(19,11403,1,12,0)="reommened that a small set of teams or positions be selected first."
^DIC(19,11403,1,13,0)="After the report comes back check the results before moving on."
^DIC(19,11403,25)="MAIN^SCMCCV1"
^DIC(19,11403,"U")="PC ATTENDING CONVERSION UTILIT"
^DIC(19,11404,0)="SCMC PRECEPTOR MIGRATION RPT^Preceptor Migration Report^This functionality is now accomplished by the PCMM Web Application.^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11404,1,0)="^^13^13^2990517^"
^DIC(19,11404,1,1,0)="The Preceptor Migration Report loops through the Team file.  For every"
^DIC(19,11404,1,2,0)="active team with entries in the Team Position file that have an entry in"
^DIC(19,11404,1,3,0)="the Preceptor field, the report validates the position and the preceptor"
^DIC(19,11404,1,4,0)="position against the standards for a preceptor link which will be"
^DIC(19,11404,1,5,0)="effective with the release of Scheduling patch SD*5.3*177 (PCMM Phase II"
^DIC(19,11404,1,6,0)="Enhancements). If the Team Position-Preceptor Team Position 'Link' meets"
^DIC(19,11404,1,7,0)="Phase II standards, the report entry  will show 'Preceptor Link OK'."
^DIC(19,11404,1,8,0)="Else, the report entry will show ""Position:"" or ""Preceptor:"" and detail"
^DIC(19,11404,1,9,0)="the faults(s).  Any entry tagged as 'Preceptor Link OK' will be migrated"
^DIC(19,11404,1,10,0)="by the Post Init of Scheduling patch SD*5.3*177 to the *new* Preceptor"
^DIC(19,11404,1,11,0)="History file.  The intent of the report is to allow sites to glean"
^DIC(19,11404,1,12,0)="existing Preceptor assignments prior to migration to the new format.  The"
^DIC(19,11404,1,13,0)="report is automatically queued and delivered via Mailman to the user."
^DIC(19,11404,25)="ENMAIN^SCMCCV3(23)"
^DIC(19,11404,"U")="PRECEPTOR MIGRATION REPORT"
^DIC(19,11405,0)="SCMC PC ATTENDING ASGN RPT^PC Attending Assignment Report^This functionality is now accomplished by the PCMM Web Application.^R^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11405,25)="MAIN^SCMCCV4"
^DIC(19,11405,"U")="PC ATTENDING ASSIGNMENT REPORT"
^DIC(19,11406,0)="SCMC CONVERSION TOOLS MENU^PC Attending tools menu^This functionality is now accomplished by the PCMM Web Application.^M^11281^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11406,1,0)="^^4^4^2990527^^^^"
^DIC(19,11406,1,1,0)="This menu contains options necessary to aid the user in evaluating the number"
^DIC(19,11406,1,2,0)="of PC Attending Assignments at their site.  It also provides a report to"
^DIC(19,11406,1,3,0)="evaluate any preceptor links that may exists between the positions on the PCMM"
^DIC(19,11406,1,4,0)="teams."
^DIC(19,11406,10,0)="^19.01IP^4^4"
