^DIC(19,11414,0)="SCMC PCMM HL7 TRANSMIT^PCMM HL7 Transmission^This functionality is now accomplished by CDW/VSSC.^A^11740^^^^^^^16^^1"
^DIC(19,11414,1,0)="^19.06^3^3^3000828^^^^"
^DIC(19,11414,1,1,0)="This menu option should be queued to run nightly. It will go thru"
^DIC(19,11414,1,2,0)="the ""AACXMIT"" xref on the PCMM HL7 EVENT file and send an HL7"
^DIC(19,11414,1,3,0)="message to the NPCD in Austin for each entry."
^DIC(19,11414,20)="D MAIN^SCMCHL(1)"
^DIC(19,11414,25)="MAIN^SCMCHL(1)"
^DIC(19,11414,"U")="PCMM HL7 TRANSMISSION"
^DIC(19,11415,0)="SCMC PRECEPTOR CONVERSION^PRECEPTOR CONVERSION^This functionality is now accomplished by the PCMM Web Application.^R^11281^SC PCMM SETUP^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11415,1,0)="^^6^6^2990803^^^"
^DIC(19,11415,1,1,0)="This option allows the user to QUEUE off a job that will build the preceptor"
^DIC(19,11415,1,2,0)="histories.  It will be based upon what is currently in your PCMM preceptor"
^DIC(19,11415,1,3,0)="precepty relationships.  Before each of the histories can be set up, all of"
^DIC(19,11415,1,4,0)="the business rules pertaining to preceptor relationships will be checked."
^DIC(19,11415,1,5,0)=""
^DIC(19,11415,1,6,0)="This is the same job that was run as part of the post init for patch SD*5.3*177"
^DIC(19,11415,20)=""
^DIC(19,11415,25)="ENMAIN^SCMCCV3(21)"
^DIC(19,11415,"U")="PRECEPTOR CONVERSION"
^DIC(19,11423,0)="RGPR PRE-IMP SSN REPORT^Pseudo-SSN Report^^R^10000000033^^^^^^^525"
^DIC(19,11423,1,0)="^19.06^6^6^3010613^^^"
^DIC(19,11423,1,1,0)="This is the standard Pseudo-SSN (Social Security Number) report."
^DIC(19,11423,1,2,0)="Users should run this report to a 132-column printer, call the "
^DIC(19,11423,1,3,0)="patients and get the correct SSN, and then update via use of "
^DIC(19,11423,1,4,0)="the Load/Edit Patient Data option [DG LOAD PATIENT DATA] in "
^DIC(19,11423,1,5,0)="the Patient Information Management System (PIMS) software "
^DIC(19,11423,1,6,0)="Registration Menu option [DG REGISTRATION MENU]."
^DIC(19,11423,25)="RGPRSSN"
^DIC(19,11423,"U")="PSEUDO-SSN REPORT"
^DIC(19,11427,0)="DG172 PRE-IMP MAR STAT MAP^Marital Status File - Map Non-Standard Entries^^R^11281^^^^^^^114"
^DIC(19,11427,1,0)="^^14^14^2980909^^^^"
^DIC(19,11427,1,1,0)="This option will identify non-standard MARITAL STATUS file (#11) entries"
^DIC(19,11427,1,2,0)="and then allow the user to designate, for each non-standard entry, a"
^DIC(19,11427,1,3,0)="standard entry which this utility will re-point with associated patients."
^DIC(19,11427,1,4,0)="For example, you will be able to map all patients with a marital status"
^DIC(19,11427,1,5,0)="of SINGLE to NEVER MARRIED."
^DIC(19,11427,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11427,1,7,0)="This mapping will be used during the re-pointing and file clean-up process,"
^DIC(19,11427,1,8,0)="the Begin Religion/Marital Status Conversion [DG172 PRE-IMP START"
^DIC(19,11427,1,9,0)="CONVERSION] option."
^DIC(19,11427,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11427,1,11,0)="The option (1) provides a list of non-standard MARITAL STATUS file entries"
^DIC(19,11427,1,12,0)="to the screen or a printer, (2) prompts the user for a non-standard entry,"
^DIC(19,11427,1,13,0)="and (3) then prompts for the standard entry which the utility will re-"
^DIC(19,11427,1,14,0)="point with associated patients."
^DIC(19,11427,25)="EDIT^DG17204(11)"
^DIC(19,11427,"U")="MARITAL STATUS FILE - MAP NON-"
^DIC(19,11428,0)="DG172 PRE-IMP RELIGION MAP^Religion File - Map Non-Standard Entries^^R^11281^^^^^^^114"
^DIC(19,11428,1,0)="^^14^14^2980909^^^"
^DIC(19,11428,1,1,0)="This option will identify non-standard RELIGION file (#13) entries and"
^DIC(19,11428,1,2,0)="then allows the user to designate, for each non-standard entry, a"
^DIC(19,11428,1,3,0)="standard entry which this utility will re-point with associated patients."
^DIC(19,11428,1,4,0)="For example, you will be able to map all patients with a religion of "
^DIC(19,11428,1,5,0)="XXXXXX to UNKNOWN/NO PREFERENCE."
^DIC(19,11428,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11428,1,7,0)="This mapping will be used during the re-pointing and file clean-up process,"
^DIC(19,11428,1,8,0)="the Begin Religion/Marital Status Conversion [DG172 PRE-IMP START"
^DIC(19,11428,1,9,0)="CONVERSION] option."
^DIC(19,11428,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11428,1,11,0)="The option (1) provides a list of non-standard RELIGION file entries to the"
^DIC(19,11428,1,12,0)="screen or a pointer, (2) prompts the user for a non-standard entry, and (3)"
^DIC(19,11428,1,13,0)="then prompts for the standard entry which the utility will re-point with"
^DIC(19,11428,1,14,0)="associated patients."
^DIC(19,11428,25)="EDIT^DG17204(13)"
^DIC(19,11428,"U")="RELIGION FILE - MAP NON-STANDA"
^DIC(19,11429,0)="DG172 PRE-IMP START CONVERSION^Begin Religion/Marital Status Conversion^^R^11281^^^^^^^114"
^DIC(19,11429,1,0)="^^15^15^2980923^^^^"
^DIC(19,11429,1,1,0)="After mapping of non-standard entries is complete, this conversion"
^DIC(19,11429,1,2,0)="process is run in order to actually re-point patient records from"
^DIC(19,11429,1,3,0)="non-standard entries to the specified standard entries. A mail"
^DIC(19,11429,1,4,0)="bulletin with summary information will be generated at the end "
^DIC(19,11429,1,5,0)="of the process and sent to the user."
^DIC(19,11429,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11429,1,7,0)="The conversion process will re-point those patients associated with"
^DIC(19,11429,1,8,0)="non-standard entries to standard entries, delete the non-standard"
^DIC(19,11429,1,9,0)="entries in the MARITAL STATUS and RELIGION files, and will finally"
^DIC(19,11429,1,10,0)="delete the four options related to this process. Options Pseudo-SSN"
^DIC(19,11429,1,11,0)="Report [RGPR PRE-IMP SSN REPORT], Eligibility Code Files Report"
^DIC(19,11429,1,12,0)="[RGPR PRE-IMP ELIG REPORT], and CIRN Master of Record Menu [RGCIRN"
^DIC(19,11429,1,13,0)="CMOR MAIN] will remain on the CIRN Pre-Implementation Menu [RGPR PRE-"
^DIC(19,11429,1,14,0)="IMP MENU].  The process can be repeated ONLY if the DG*5.3*172 patch"
^DIC(19,11429,1,15,0)="is re-applied."
^DIC(19,11429,25)="JOB^DG17202"
^DIC(19,11429,"U")="BEGIN RELIGION/MARITAL STATUS "
^DIC(19,11430,0)="DG172 PRE-IMP STOP CONVERSION^Stop Religion/Marital Status Conversion^^R^11281^^^^^^^114"
^DIC(19,11430,1,0)="^^8^8^2980909^^"
^DIC(19,11430,1,1,0)="This option will stop the conversion process associated with the Begin"
^DIC(19,11430,1,2,0)="Religion/Marital Status Conversion [DG172 PRE-IMP START CONVERSION] option."
^DIC(19,11430,1,3,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11430,1,4,0)="A bulletin will be delivered to the user of the option after the conversion"
^DIC(19,11430,1,5,0)="process has been stopped.  The system stores the internal entry number(IEN)"
^DIC(19,11430,1,6,0)="of the last entry processed.  To restart the process, simply choose the "
^DIC(19,11430,1,7,0)="Begin Religion/Marital Status Conversion option again.  The system will "
^DIC(19,11430,1,8,0)="then resume with the next patient record."
^DIC(19,11430,25)="STOP^DG17202"
^DIC(19,11430,"U")="STOP RELIGION/MARITAL STATUS C"
^DIC(19,11432,0)="PRCAZ DMC FLAG SET^Set DMC Flag^^E^11613^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11432,1,0)="^^1^1^2991110^^^"
^DIC(19,11432,1,1,0)="This is a class III option to flag a debtor as at DMC."
^DIC(19,11432,30)="RCD(340,"
^DIC(19,11432,31)="AEMQ"
^DIC(19,11432,50)="RCD(340,"
^DIC(19,11432,51)="[PRCAZ DMC FLAG SET]"
^DIC(19,11432,"U")="SET DMC FLAG"
^DIC(19,11433,0)="HL START/STOP LINK MANAGER^TCP Link Manager Start/Stop^^R^11741^^^^^^^304^y"
^DIC(19,11433,1,0)="^^3^3^2991118^^"
^DIC(19,11433,1,1,0)="This option is used to start/restart the Link Manager.  Under normal"
^DIC(19,11433,1,2,0)="conditions, the Link Manager should automatically start along with all"
^DIC(19,11433,1,3,0)="options flagged for special queuing."
^DIC(19,11433,25)="STRTSTOP^HLCSLM"
^DIC(19,11433,"U")="TCP LINK MANAGER START/STOP"
^DIC(19,11434,0)="HL AUTOSTART LINK MANAGER^Autostart Link Manager^^R^10958^^^^^^^304^n"
^DIC(19,11434,1,0)="^^44^44^2990609^^^^"
^DIC(19,11434,1,1,0)="This option is invoked through TaskMan's Special Queuing feature.  When"
^DIC(19,11434,1,2,0)="TaskMan starts through the normal startup and not through the Restart"
^DIC(19,11434,1,3,0)="option, this task will start as a persistent task checking the HL7 message"
^DIC(19,11434,1,4,0)="queues for message(s) to be delivered via non-persistent LLPs.  The"
^DIC(19,11434,1,5,0)="primary job of the Link Manager is to insure that an LLP is available when"
^DIC(19,11434,1,6,0)="messages in the Message Queue are ready to be delivered.  If there are no"
^DIC(19,11434,1,7,0)="existing LLPs available, the Link Manager will task off a Link"
^DIC(19,11434,1,8,0)="Sub-manager which in turn will become an LLP to deliver message(s) for a"
^DIC(19,11434,1,9,0)="specific message queue requiring a non-persistent connection."
^DIC(19,11434,1,10,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,11,0)="In order to set up this option to startup when the system/TaskMan starts,"
^DIC(19,11434,1,12,0)="please find the following HL7 options to create an entry"
^DIC(19,11434,1,13,0)="in the OPTION SCHEDULING file:"
^DIC(19,11434,1,14,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,15,0)=" STEP 1:  Taskman Management ..."
^DIC(19,11434,1,16,0)=" STEP 2:  Schedule/Unschedule Options"
^DIC(19,11434,1,17,0)=" STEP 3 (Create the following entry):"
^DIC(19,11434,1,18,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,19,0)="Select OPTION to schedule or reschedule: HL AUTOSTART LINK MANAGER"
^DIC(19,11434,1,20,0)="  Are you adding 'HL AUTOSTART LINK MANAGER' as "
^DIC(19,11434,1,21,0)="    a new OPTION SCHEDULING (the 12TH)? No// Y"
^DIC(19,11434,1,22,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,23,0)=" STEP 4 (And then you will enter the FileMan ScreenMan form"
^DIC(19,11434,1,24,0)="        as follows and you should edit the 'SPECIAL QUEUEING' field "
^DIC(19,11434,1,25,0)="        to have a value of 'Startup Persistent'):"
^DIC(19,11434,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,27,0)="                          Edit Option Schedule"
^DIC(19,11434,1,28,0)="    Option Name: HL AUTOSTART LINK MANAGER     "
^DIC(19,11434,1,29,0)="    Menu Text: Autostart Link Manager                    TASK ID:"
^DIC(19,11434,1,30,0)="  __________________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(19,11434,1,31,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,32,0)="  QUEUED TO RUN AT WHAT TIME:"
^DIC(19,11434,1,33,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,34,0)="DEVICE FOR QUEUED JOB OUTPUT:"
^DIC(19,11434,1,35,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,36,0)=" QUEUED TO RUN ON VOLUME SET:"
^DIC(19,11434,1,37,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,38,0)="      RESCHEDULING FREQUENCY:"
^DIC(19,11434,1,39,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,40,0)="             TASK PARAMETERS:"
^DIC(19,11434,1,41,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,42,0)="            SPECIAL QUEUEING: Startup Persistent  "
^DIC(19,11434,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11434,1,44,0)="_______________________________________________________________________________"
^DIC(19,11434,25)="EN^HLCSLM"
^DIC(19,11434,200.9)="s"
^DIC(19,11434,"U")="AUTOSTART LINK MANAGER"
^DIC(19,11435,0)="XM FILTER EDIT^Message Filter Edit^^R^11748^^3154^^^^^54"
^DIC(19,11435,1,0)="^19.06^24^24^3020509^^^^"
^DIC(19,11435,1,1,0)="The filter is used by MailMan to determine into which basket to place a"
^DIC(19,11435,1,2,0)="message."
^DIC(19,11435,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(19,11435,1,4,0)="Messages can be filtered based on up to three criteria which are 'and'ed"
^DIC(19,11435,1,5,0)="together:"
^DIC(19,11435,1,6,0)=" - Subject contains"
^DIC(19,11435,1,7,0)=" - Message is from"
^DIC(19,11435,1,8,0)=" - Message is to"
^DIC(19,11435,1,9,0)=""
^DIC(19,11435,1,10,0)="For example, if you specify 'subject contains' and 'message is from', the"
^DIC(19,11435,1,11,0)="filter takes effect only if the subject contains the string you specify AND"
^DIC(19,11435,1,12,0)="the message is from the person you specify. "
^DIC(19,11435,1,13,0)=""
^DIC(19,11435,1,14,0)="If you wish the filter to take effect upon 'subject contains' OR 'message"
^DIC(19,11435,1,15,0)="is from' you must create two filters, one with 'subject contains', and the"
^DIC(19,11435,1,16,0)="other with 'message is from'."
^DIC(19,11435,1,17,0)=""
^DIC(19,11435,1,18,0)="Filtering takes place during message delivery and can also be selected as a"
^DIC(19,11435,1,19,0)="basket action. "
^DIC(19,11435,1,20,0)=""
^DIC(19,11435,1,21,0)="The filter is ignored during delivery under the following conditions:"
^DIC(19,11435,1,22,0)=" - The message already exists in one of your baskets."
^DIC(19,11435,1,23,0)=" - The message is from you, and you specified a basket (other than the IN"
^DIC(19,11435,1,24,0)="basket) at the transmit prompt."
^DIC(19,11435,25)="FILTER^XMVVITA"
^DIC(19,11435,"U")="MESSAGE FILTER EDIT"
^DIC(19,11436,0)="XM PERSONAL MENU^Personal Preferences^^M^11748^^3204^^^^^54"
^DIC(19,11436,1,0)="^19.06^1^1^3020509^^^^"
^DIC(19,11436,1,1,0)="This menu has various options to let you configure MailMan to your liking."
^DIC(19,11436,10,0)="^19.01IP^8^8"
^DIC(19,11436,10,1,0)="70^^1"
