^DIC(19,11623,1,2,0)="corrections to be made on DICOM image files which failed during"
^DIC(19,11623,1,3,0)="the downloading processes.  The routine, MAGDIR1, used to download DICOM"
^DIC(19,11623,1,4,0)="files directly from Radiology modalities (CT, MRI, etc.) sometime will "
^DIC(19,11623,1,5,0)="fail to match exactly on the patients name, ssn or Radiology case number."
^DIC(19,11623,1,6,0)="A reference to the files which failed the matching will be written"
^DIC(19,11623,1,7,0)="to the MAGD(2006.575 global --- (please note that only a reference to  "
^DIC(19,11623,1,8,0)="the file is being made; the actual DICOM file will remain in the"
^DIC(19,11623,1,9,0)="IMAGE_IN DOS directory on the DICOM Image server.)  "
^DIC(19,11623,1,10,0)="The MAGDLB9 routine will use the ""F"" cross  reference to loop"
^DIC(19,11623,1,11,0)="through the entries needing corrections.  This  cross reference is"
^DIC(19,11623,1,12,0)="on the Unique Study Identification number assigned  by the Radiology"
^DIC(19,11623,1,13,0)="modalitiy."
^DIC(19,11623,25)="START^MAGDLB9"
^DIC(19,11623,"U")="CORRECT RAD-DICOM FILE ENTRIES"
^DIC(19,11624,0)="MAG SYS-WIN WRKS^Display Workstation information^^B^20095^^^^^^^"
