^DIC(19,11742,0)="LRCAPCPTI^InActive WKLD CODE File CPT Codes Print^^R^11740^^^^^^^26"
^DIC(19,11742,1,0)="^^41^41^3000128^"
^DIC(19,11742,1,1,0)="This option will scan the WKLD CODE (#64) file for CPT codes that are"
^DIC(19,11742,1,2,0)="InActive in the VA CPT code (#81) file. This option maybe useful when new"
^DIC(19,11742,1,3,0)="CPT Code files are installed. New CPT Code files are usually distributed"
^DIC(19,11742,1,4,0)="annually.  "
^DIC(19,11742,1,5,0)="  "
^DIC(19,11742,1,6,0)=" When a new CPT code file is released, it may contain codes that are no"
^DIC(19,11742,1,7,0)="longer allowed and are inactive in the CPT file. The Laboratory Package"
^DIC(19,11742,1,8,0)="PCE interface checks each CPT code in the WKLD CODE (#64) file before"
^DIC(19,11742,1,9,0)="sending workload to the PCE API. If the CPT code defined in WKLD CODE file"
^DIC(19,11742,1,10,0)="is deemed inactive in the CPT Code files, the software will enter a date"
^DIC(19,11742,1,11,0)="in the INACTIVE DATE field for that particular code. A message is sent to"
^DIC(19,11742,1,12,0)="the local G.LMI mail group informing the LIM that the CPT Code is no"
^DIC(19,11742,1,13,0)="longer active.  "
^DIC(19,11742,1,14,0)="  "
^DIC(19,11742,1,15,0)=" This option can be used to print all of the WKLD CODE file CPT Codes that"
^DIC(19,11742,1,16,0)="are INACTIVE and require a different CPT Code to be entered in order to"
^DIC(19,11742,1,17,0)="capture PCE Workload."
^DIC(19,11742,1,18,0)="  "
^DIC(19,11742,1,19,0)=" The report will identify the WKLD CODE that contains the inappropriate"
^DIC(19,11742,1,20,0)="CPT Code. It will list the offending CPT code(s). It will indicate why the"
^DIC(19,11742,1,21,0)="CPT code is inappropriate. It will then give a list of LABORATORY TEST"
^DIC(19,11742,1,22,0)="names that are linked to this WKLD CODE. The LABORATORY TEST listed will"
^DIC(19,11742,1,23,0)="NOT receive PCE Workload credit."
^DIC(19,11742,1,24,0)="  "
^DIC(19,11742,1,25,0)=" Example: "
