^DIC(19,11860,0)="ACKQAS CDR PRINT^Print A&SP Service CDR^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,11860,1,0)="^^9^9^3000201^^^"
^DIC(19,11860,1,1,0)="The Print A&SP Service CDR option prints the RCS 10-014 report for Audiology"
^DIC(19,11860,1,2,0)="and Speech Pathology."
^DIC(19,11860,1,3,0)="  "
^DIC(19,11860,1,4,0)="Use this option to reprint the CDR report that you have generated using the"
^DIC(19,11860,1,5,0)="Generate A&SP Service CDR option."
^DIC(19,11860,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(19,11860,1,7,0)="If your CDR is reported by Division, you must select the Division(s) to be "
^DIC(19,11860,1,8,0)="printed. You must then enter the month that you wish to print. The report"
^DIC(19,11860,1,9,0)="will print the CDR for the month and Divisions that have been generated."
^DIC(19,11860,25)="ACKQCDRP"
^DIC(19,11860,"U")="PRINT A&SP SERVICE CDR"
^DIC(19,11861,0)="ACKQAS UPDATE CPT MODIFIERS^Update CPT Modifiers per CO Directive^^E^10000000020^^^^^^^509^^1"
^DIC(19,11861,1,0)="^19.06^15^15^3040227^^^^"
^DIC(19,11861,1,1,0)="The system shall allows the user to select any Modifier already defined in"
^DIC(19,11861,1,2,0)="the A&SP Modifier file for edit. The system allows selection of CPT"
^DIC(19,11861,1,3,0)="Modifiers or a HCPCS Modifiers from the CPT Modifier File #81.3 that are"
^DIC(19,11861,1,4,0)="defined as a type 'C' or type 'H'."
^DIC(19,11861,1,5,0)="The system prevents the user from adding to the A&SP Modifier File any"
^DIC(19,11861,1,6,0)="Modifier that is defined as Inactive on the CPT Modifier File #81.3."
^DIC(19,11861,1,7,0)="The system also prevents the user from deleting a Modifier from the A&SP"
^DIC(19,11861,1,8,0)="Modifier File."
^DIC(19,11861,1,9,0)="The system then prompts the user to enter the Status of the Modifier in"
^DIC(19,11861,1,10,0)="QUASAR. Valid entries are '1' for Active or '0' for Inactive."
^DIC(19,11861,1,11,0)="If a new Modifier is selected from the CPT Modifier File the Modifier"
^DIC(19,11861,1,12,0)="Status shall default to Active."
^DIC(19,11861,1,13,0)="If an existing Modifier is selected from the A&SP Modifier File then the"
^DIC(19,11861,1,14,0)="system shall display the current status of the Modifier as the default"
^DIC(19,11861,1,15,0)="value."
^DIC(19,11861,20)="S ACKLAYGO="""",DLAYGO=509850.5 W @IOF,!,""This option allows you to enter new Procedure Modifiers or amend the status of  existing ones."",!"
^DIC(19,11861,30)="ACK(509850.5,"
^DIC(19,11861,31)="AEMQL"
^DIC(19,11861,35)="W """",$$MODTXT^ACKQUTL8(Y,""""),?48,$$GET1^DIQ(81.3,Y,.04)"
^DIC(19,11861,50)="ACK(509850.5,"
^DIC(19,11861,51)="[ACKQAS ENTER/EDIT MODIFIERS]"
^DIC(19,11861,"U")="UPDATE CPT MODIFIERS PER CO DI"
^DIC(19,11862,0)="ACKQAS DELETE VISIT^Delete an A&SP Clinic Visit^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,11862,1,0)="^^10^10^2990917^"
^DIC(19,11862,1,1,0)="This option allows you to delete an A&SP Clinic Visit"
^DIC(19,11862,1,2,0)="that has been entered in error."
^DIC(19,11862,1,3,0)=""
^DIC(19,11862,1,4,0)="If the selected visit has been sent across to PCE then "
^DIC(19,11862,1,5,0)="this function will also attempt to delete the visit from"
^DIC(19,11862,1,6,0)="PCE. If the PCE Deletion fails you will see an Error "
^DIC(19,11862,1,7,0)="message displayed. You may then choose to continue or "
^DIC(19,11862,1,8,0)="abort the deletion. If you continue, the Quasar Visit "
^DIC(19,11862,1,9,0)="will be deleted but you will have to use the PCE package"
^DIC(19,11862,1,10,0)="to delete the same visit from PCE."
^DIC(19,11862,25)="ACKQAS4"
^DIC(19,11862,"U")="DELETE AN A&SP CLINIC VISIT"
^DIC(19,11863,0)="ACKQAS PCE EXCEPTION REPORT^PCE Exception Report^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,11863,1,0)="^^23^23^2991223^^"
^DIC(19,11863,1,1,0)="This report will list all A&SP Clinic Visits whose Visit Date falls"
^DIC(19,11863,1,2,0)="after the PCE Interface Start Date for the Division, that have not"
^DIC(19,11863,1,3,0)="been successfully updated in PCE."
^DIC(19,11863,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11863,1,5,0)="A Visit will be included on the report if it falls into one of the"
^DIC(19,11863,1,6,0)="following two categories:-"
^DIC(19,11863,1,7,0)="1. The last time QUASAR attempted to send the Visit to PCE, the Visit"
^DIC(19,11863,1,8,0)="   was rejected. In this case the report will include the error "
^DIC(19,11863,1,9,0)="   messages returned by the PCE Interface."
^DIC(19,11863,1,10,0)="2. The Visit has been edited in Quasar but the new Visit data has not"
^DIC(19,11863,1,11,0)="   been sent to PCE because the PCE Interface has been switched off."
^DIC(19,11863,1,12,0)="   In this case the report will show the date/time of the last QUASAR"
^DIC(19,11863,1,13,0)="   update versus the date/time of the last time the Visit was sent to "
^DIC(19,11863,1,14,0)="   PCE."
^DIC(19,11863,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11863,1,16,0)="To remove a Visit from the Exception report, the PCE Interface must be"
^DIC(19,11863,1,17,0)="activated for the Site, and for the Division in which the Visit took "
^DIC(19,11863,1,18,0)="place. Then in order for QUASAR to send the new Visit data you must"
^DIC(19,11863,1,19,0)="edit the Visit using the Edit An Existing Visit option. At the end of"
^DIC(19,11863,1,20,0)="the Edit option, Quasar will attempt to send the new Visit data to "
^DIC(19,11863,1,21,0)="PCE. Once the Visit data is the same in both systems, the visit will"
^DIC(19,11863,1,22,0)="be removed from the PCE Exception Report."
^DIC(19,11863,1,23,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11863,25)="ACKQPCX"
^DIC(19,11863,"U")="PCE EXCEPTION REPORT"
^DIC(19,11864,0)="ACKQAS EC PROC STATS^Statistics by Event Capture Procedure^^R^11720^^^^^^^509"
^DIC(19,11864,1,0)="^^10^10^3001013^"
^DIC(19,11864,1,1,0)="The Event Capture Statistics by Procedure report can be printed for a date"
^DIC(19,11864,1,2,0)="range you select.  You can print the report for Audiology only, Speech"
^DIC(19,11864,1,3,0)="Pathology only, or both Audiology and Speech Pathology."
^DIC(19,11864,1,4,0)="You can choose to print the report for one or all clinician(s), other "
^DIC(19,11864,1,5,0)="provider(s), or student(s)."
^DIC(19,11864,1,6,0)=" "
^DIC(19,11864,1,7,0)="The report lists clinic visits for the date range sorted by Event Capture "
^DIC(19,11864,1,8,0)="procedure codes.  Since the EC Procedure Code field is a multiple field,"
^DIC(19,11864,1,9,0)="the visit shows up once under each EC Procedure Code entered for that"
^DIC(19,11864,1,10,0)="visit."
^DIC(19,11864,25)="ACKQR5"
^DIC(19,11864,"U")="STATISTICS BY EVENT CAPTURE PR"
^DIC(19,11865,0)="FHCTF5^Inpatient Monitor Scan^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,11865,1,0)="^19.06^4^4^3011115^^^^"
^DIC(19,11865,1,1,0)="This option is designed to be run automatically once a day to"
^DIC(19,11865,1,2,0)="scan each inpatient for compliance with established monitors."
^DIC(19,11865,1,3,0)="Patients needing examination will be placed both in the monitor"
^DIC(19,11865,1,4,0)="files as well as into the Tickler file."
^DIC(19,11865,25)="FHCTF5"
^DIC(19,11865,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,11865,"U")="INPATIENT MONITOR SCAN"
^DIC(19,11866,0)="TIU TEMPLATE USER DELETE^Delete user's TIU templates.^^A^10000000020^^^^^^^516^^1"
^DIC(19,11866,1,0)="^19.06^4^4^3010103^^"
^DIC(19,11866,1,1,0)="This option calls code to remove all TIU templates for a user, except"
^DIC(19,11866,1,2,0)="those who are not orphans (i.e., also used by some other user).  It relies"
^DIC(19,11866,1,3,0)="on Kernel's XU USER TERMINATE option to set the variable XUIFN in order "
^DIC(19,11866,1,4,0)="to identify the terminated user."
^DIC(19,11866,20)="D KUSER^TIUSRVT3"
^DIC(19,11866,25)=""
^DIC(19,11866,"U")="DELETE USER'S TIU TEMPLATES."
^DIC(19,11867,0)="TIU TEMPLATE CAC USER DELETE^Delete TIU templates for selected user.^^A^10000000020^^^^^^^516^^1"
^DIC(19,11867,1,0)="^19.06^2^2^3010314^^"
^DIC(19,11867,1,1,0)="This option accepts user input for an individual from the NEW PERSON file,"
^DIC(19,11867,1,2,0)="then deletes non-shared TIU templates for that user."
^DIC(19,11867,20)="D SELUSR^TIUSRVT3"
^DIC(19,11867,"U")="DELETE TIU TEMPLATES FOR SELEC"
^DIC(19,11868,0)="TIU TEMPLATE USER DELETE PARAM^Edit auto template cleanup parameter.^^A^10000000020^^^^^^^516^^1"
^DIC(19,11868,1,0)="^19.06^4^4^3010315^^"
^DIC(19,11868,1,1,0)="This option accesses the TIU TEMPLATE USER AUTO DELETE parameter and"
^DIC(19,11868,1,2,0)="toggles the entry on or off, providing for automatic deletion of"
^DIC(19,11868,1,3,0)="non-shared TIU templates for a user upon termination - or skipping any"
^DIC(19,11868,1,4,0)="such automatic action."
^DIC(19,11868,20)="D PARSET^TIUSRVT4"
^DIC(19,11868,"U")="EDIT AUTO TEMPLATE CLEANUP PAR"
^DIC(19,11869,0)="TIU IRM TEMPLATE MGMT^TIU Template Mgmt Functions^^M^10000000020^^^^^^^516"
^DIC(19,11869,1,0)="^19.06^3^3^3010314^^"
^DIC(19,11869,1,1,0)="This option is a menu option which contains other options providing TIU"
^DIC(19,11869,1,2,0)="template management functions to CACs or other managers with access to the"
^DIC(19,11869,1,3,0)="TIU IRM MAINTENANCE MENU option."
^DIC(19,11869,10,0)="^19.01IP^5^5"
