^DIC(19,12154,1,2,0)="used for the ^JUMP.  Whenever an item in a menu is modified, the tree"
^DIC(19,12154,1,3,0)="must get rebuilt.  This will happen automatically the first time it is"
^DIC(19,12154,1,4,0)="referenced, but forcing the rebuild can often save time."
^DIC(19,12154,1,5,0)="The rebuilding of all trees can be queued."
^DIC(19,12154,25)="BUILD^XQ81"
^DIC(19,12154,"U")="BUILD PRIMARY MENU TREES"
^DIC(19,12155,0)="XQSHOWBUILDS^Most Recent Menu Rebuilds^^R^10000000020^^^^^^y^163^y"
^DIC(19,12155,1,0)="^^4^4^3000928^"
^DIC(19,12155,1,1,0)="        This option runs the program ^XQ84 which formats the data stored"
^DIC(19,12155,1,2,0)="in the global ^XUTL(""XQ"",""BUILDS"") the 20 most recent menu rebuilds,"
^DIC(19,12155,1,3,0)="including complete live rebuilds, micro surgery episodes, and tasked"
^DIC(19,12155,1,4,0)="rebuilds."
^DIC(19,12155,25)="SHOW^XQ84"
^DIC(19,12155,"U")="MOST RECENT MENU REBUILDS"
^DIC(19,12156,0)="XQKICKMICRO^Kick Off Micro Surgery^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^^y^1"
^DIC(19,12156,1,0)="^^9^9^3001124^"
^DIC(19,12156,1,1,0)="     When certain changes are made to the Option File those changes are"
^DIC(19,12156,1,2,0)="recorded in the cross-reference ^DIC(19,""AT"").  Micro surgery is the"
^DIC(19,12156,1,3,0)="software in ^XQ83* that uses this data to rebuild the compiled menu trees"
^DIC(19,12156,1,4,0)="in ^DIC(19,""AXQ"").  Micro surgery is normally triggered when a user logs"
^DIC(19,12156,1,5,0)="into a system, but this option allows the programmer to start it manually"
^DIC(19,12156,1,6,0)="if minor changes are made to the Option File which do not merit a complete"
^DIC(19,12156,1,7,0)="rebuild.  If there is nothing in the ""AT"" cross reference to work on the"
^DIC(19,12156,1,8,0)="option responds: ""Nothing to rebuild."", if there is work to do then the"
^DIC(19,12156,1,9,0)="option responds with ""Done."" meaning that Micro surgery has been started."
^DIC(19,12156,20)="W !!,?5,$S($D(^DIC(19,""AT"")):""Done."",1:""Nothing to rebuild."")"
^DIC(19,12156,25)="CHEK^XQ83"
^DIC(19,12156,"U")="KICK OFF MICRO SURGERY"
^DIC(19,12157,0)="XQRIGHTNOW^Is there a menu rebuild running right now?^^R^10000000020^^^^^^y^^y"
^DIC(19,12157,1,0)="^^2^2^3001017^"
^DIC(19,12157,1,1,0)="     This option checks the various flags set in ^DIC(19,""AXQ"",""P0"") to"
^DIC(19,12157,1,2,0)="determine if there is menu rebuild activity on your system right now."
^DIC(19,12157,25)="NOW^XQ84"
^DIC(19,12157,"U")="IS THERE A MENU REBUILD RUNNIN"
^DIC(19,12158,0)="XUEXKEY^Allocate/De-Allocate Exclusive Key(s)^^R^10000000020^XUEXKEY^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,12158,1,0)="^^2^2^3020510^"
^DIC(19,12158,1,1,0)="This option can be used to just edit the 'MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE KEYS'"
^DIC(19,12158,1,2,0)="multiple of the 'SECURITY KEY' file."
^DIC(19,12158,25)="EXCLUSE^XQ6B"
^DIC(19,12158,99.1)="58864,3615"
^DIC(19,12158,"U")="ALLOCATE/DE-ALLOCATE EXCLUSIVE"
^DIC(19,12159,0)="XQAL SET BACKUP REVIEWER^Set Backup Reviewer for Alerts^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^163"
^DIC(19,12159,1,0)="^^8^8^3010706^"
^DIC(19,12159,1,1,0)="This option provides a mechanism for a user to set entries into the"
^DIC(19,12159,1,2,0)="Parameter file which will assign an individual as Backup Reviewer"
^DIC(19,12159,1,3,0)="for Alerts if there is a date specified for Days For Backup Reviewer"
^DIC(19,12159,1,4,0)="in the Alert.  If this is the case, an alert which remains unread"
^DIC(19,12159,1,5,0)="for the indicated number of days will be forwarded to the Backup"
^DIC(19,12159,1,6,0)="Reviewer found for the lowest level for the user in the Parameter"
^DIC(19,12159,1,7,0)="file starting with User, and progressing through OERR Team, Team,"
^DIC(19,12159,1,8,0)="Service, Division, up to System."
^DIC(19,12159,25)="BKUPREVW^XQALDEL"
^DIC(19,12159,"U")="SET BACKUP REVIEWER FOR ALERTS"
^DIC(19,12160,0)="XUMF IMF ADD EDIT^IMF edit^LOG REMEDY TICKET TO CHANGE NATIONAL ENTRY^R^10000000216^XUMF INSTITUTION^^^^^^163"
^DIC(19,12160,1,0)="^19.06^6^6^3101006^^^"
^DIC(19,12160,1,1,0)="This option is used to edit this facility's (or associated facility's) "
^DIC(19,12160,1,2,0)="address information.  The edits will update your local INSTITUTION (#4) "
^DIC(19,12160,1,3,0)="file AND the Institution Master File (IMF) on FORUM."
^DIC(19,12160,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(19,12160,1,5,0)="WARNING:  Use extreme care updating this information, because you will be "
^DIC(19,12160,1,6,0)="updating not just your own database but the national database as well."
^DIC(19,12160,25)=""
^DIC(19,12160,"U")="IMF EDIT"
^DIC(19,12161,0)="XUMF DMIS ID LOAD^Load DMIS ID's^^R^10000000216^XUMF INSTITUTION^^^^^^163"
^DIC(19,12161,1,0)="^^3^3^3020930^"
^DIC(19,12161,1,1,0)="This option is used to queue a background job that will query the "
^DIC(19,12161,1,2,0)="Institution Master File (IMF) and get the DOD DMIS ID facilities and "
^DIC(19,12161,1,3,0)="populate the local INSTITUTION (#4) file with them."
^DIC(19,12161,25)="DMIS^XUMF04Q"
^DIC(19,12161,"U")="LOAD DMIS ID'S"
^DIC(19,12162,0)="JET CAMP PATIENT ENTRY^Enter Camp Patients^^E^10000000020"
^DIC(19,12162,30)="DPT("
^DIC(19,12162,31)="AEMQL"
^DIC(19,12162,50)="DPT("
^DIC(19,12162,51)="[CAMPENTER]"
^DIC(19,12162,99.1)="59233,53691"
^DIC(19,12162,"U")="ENTER CAMP PATIENTS"
^DIC(19,12163,0)="ORB3 FORWARD BACKUP REVIEWER^Forward Unprocessed Notification to Bkup Reviewer^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^170"
^DIC(19,12163,1,0)="^^11^11^3020408^"
^DIC(19,12163,1,1,0)="The number of days to hold a notification before it is forwarded to a"
^DIC(19,12163,1,2,0)="recipient's backup reviewer. The maximum is 30 days.  If not indicated or"
^DIC(19,12163,1,3,0)="zero, the notification will not be forwarded.  For example, if a"
^DIC(19,12163,1,4,0)="notification has a value of 14 for this parameter, it will be forwarded to"
^DIC(19,12163,1,5,0)="the backup reviewer of each recipient who hasn't processed the"
^DIC(19,12163,1,6,0)="notification after 14 days.  Determination of recipients who have not"
^DIC(19,12163,1,7,0)="processed the notification and who their supervisors are is made by the"
^DIC(19,12163,1,8,0)="Kernel Alert Utility.  It will not be forwarded to the backup reviewer of"
^DIC(19,12163,1,9,0)="recipients who have processed the alert within 14 days.  If the value of"
^DIC(19,12163,1,10,0)="this parameter is zero or non-existent, the alert/notification will never"
^DIC(19,12163,1,11,0)="be forwarded to the backup reviewer."
^DIC(19,12163,25)="FREVIEW^ORB3MGR1"
^DIC(19,12163,"U")="FORWARD UNPROCESSED NOTIFICATI"
^DIC(19,12164,0)="GMTS OBJ ENTER/EDIT^Create/Modify Health Summary Object^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,12164,1,0)="^19.06^4^4^3021023^^^^"
^DIC(19,12164,1,1,0)="This option allows the user to create or modify a Health "
^DIC(19,12164,1,2,0)="Summary Object.  Objects are Health Summaries that may have "
^DIC(19,12164,1,3,0)="their headers suppressed so they may be inserted into another"
^DIC(19,12164,1,4,0)="document."
^DIC(19,12164,25)="OBJ^GMTSOBJ"
^DIC(19,12164,"U")="CREATE/MODIFY HEALTH SUMMARY O"
^DIC(19,12165,0)="GMTS OBJ TEST^Test a Health Summary Object^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,12165,1,0)="^19.06^3^3^3020910^^^"
^DIC(19,12165,1,1,0)="This option allows the user test a Health Summary Object by "
^DIC(19,12165,1,2,0)="displaying the Object to the screen exactly as it would appear "
^DIC(19,12165,1,3,0)="inserted in another document."
^DIC(19,12165,25)="TEST^GMTSOBJ"
^DIC(19,12165,"U")="TEST A HEALTH SUMMARY OBJECT"
^DIC(19,12166,0)="GMTS OBJ MENU^Health Summary Objects Menu^^M^10000000020^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,12166,1,0)="^19.06^4^4^3020910^^^^"
^DIC(19,12166,1,1,0)="Use this option to access utilities to add/edit a Health Summary "
^DIC(19,12166,1,2,0)="Object, display the characteristics of a Health Summary Object, "
^DIC(19,12166,1,3,0)="to test a Health Summary Object or to export/import a Health"
^DIC(19,12166,1,4,0)="Summary Object."
^DIC(19,12166,10,0)="^19.01IP^6^5"
^DIC(19,12166,10,1,0)="12164^1^1"
^DIC(19,12166,10,2,0)="12165^3^3"
^DIC(19,12166,10,4,0)="12168^4^4"
^DIC(19,12166,10,5,0)="12167^2^2"
^DIC(19,12166,10,6,0)="12171^5^5"
