^DIC(19,12939,1,0)="^19.06^46^46^3170911^^"
^DIC(19,12939,1,1,0)=" This option allows the DSS extract manager to create the CLINICS AND"
^DIC(19,12939,1,2,0)=" STOP CODES file (#728.44) which will contain clinics, the stop codes"
^DIC(19,12939,1,3,0)=" assigned to those clinics by PIMS, and the stop codes used for those"
^DIC(19,12939,1,4,0)=" clinics by DSS.  The process by which new clinic entries are added and "
^DIC(19,12939,1,5,0)=" existing clinic entries are edited is as follows:"
^DIC(19,12939,1,6,0)="  "
^DIC(19,12939,1,7,0)=" NEW CLINIC ENTRIES"
^DIC(19,12939,1,8,0)="  1. The HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44) is searched for all clinics.  "
^DIC(19,12939,1,9,0)="     Clinics that are currently inactive are ignored.  "
^DIC(19,12939,1,10,0)="  2. New clinic entries to the CLINICS AND STOP CODES file (#728.44) are "
^DIC(19,12939,1,11,0)="     added with the following field defaults:"
^DIC(19,12939,1,12,0)="     a. STOP CODE field (#1) = STOP CODE NUMBER field (#8) in HOSPITAL "
^DIC(19,12939,1,13,0)="        LOCATION file (#44)"
^DIC(19,12939,1,14,0)="     b. CREDIT STOP CODE field (#2) = CREDIT STOP CODE field (#2503) in "
^DIC(19,12939,1,15,0)="        HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44)"
^DIC(19,12939,1,16,0)="     c. DSS STOP CODE field (#3)= STOP CODE NUMBER field (#8) in HOSPITAL "
^DIC(19,12939,1,17,0)="        LOCATION file (#44)"
^DIC(19,12939,1,18,0)="     d. DSS CREDIT STOP CODE field (#4) = CREDIT STOP CODE field (#2503) "
^DIC(19,12939,1,19,0)="        in HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44)"
^DIC(19,12939,1,20,0)="     e. ACTION TO SEND field (#5) = "
^DIC(19,12939,1,21,0)="        ""5"" (SEND BOTH AS ONE RECORD WITHOUT NATIONAL CODE) for clinics "
^DIC(19,12939,1,22,0)="            not meeting the requirements to be assigned a value of ""6"""
^DIC(19,12939,1,23,0)="        ""6"" (DO NOT SEND) if clinic is flagged as a ""non-count"" "
^DIC(19,12939,1,24,0)="            clinic in the HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44)"
^DIC(19,12939,1,25,0)=" "
^DIC(19,12939,1,26,0)=" EXISTING CLINIC ENTRIES"
^DIC(19,12939,1,27,0)="  1. All pre-existing clinics are checked against their counterpart in "
^DIC(19,12939,1,28,0)="     the HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44) to be sure that the STOP CODE "
^DIC(19,12939,1,29,0)="     field (#1) in the CLINICS AND STOP CODES file (#728.44) matches the "
^DIC(19,12939,1,30,0)="     STOP CODE NUMBER field (#8) in the HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44).  "
^DIC(19,12939,1,31,0)="     The same check is made on the CREDIT STOP CODE field (#2) to be sure "
^DIC(19,12939,1,32,0)="     that it matches the CREDIT STOP CODE field (#2503) in the HOSPITAL "
^DIC(19,12939,1,33,0)="     LOCATION file (#44). The same check is made for the DSS STOP CODE "
^DIC(19,12939,1,34,0)="     field (#3) to be sure that it matches the STOP CODE NUMBER field (#8)"
^DIC(19,12939,1,35,0)="     in the HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44).  The same check is made for the"
^DIC(19,12939,1,36,0)="     DSS CREDIT STOP CODE field (#4) to be sure that it matches the CREDIT"
^DIC(19,12939,1,37,0)="     STOP CODE field (#2503) in the HOSPITAL LOCATION file (#44)."
^DIC(19,12939,1,38,0)="  2. Any pre-existing clinic that has had a change to its active status,"
^DIC(19,12939,1,39,0)="     occasion of service status or non-count status in the HOSPITAL"
^DIC(19,12939,1,40,0)="     LOCATION file (#44) will be reported in the 'UNREVIEWED CLINCS'"
^DIC(19,12939,1,41,0)="     report option of the 'Clinics and DSS Stop Codes Print' menu option."
^DIC(19,12939,1,42,0)="  3. Any stop code changes to pre-existing clinics will delete the DATE"
^DIC(19,12939,1,43,0)="     LAST REVIEWED field (#6) in the CLINICS AND STOP CODES file"
^DIC(19,12939,1,44,0)="     (#728.44).  This will ensure that the edited clinics will print out"
^DIC(19,12939,1,45,0)="     as ""unreviewed"" the next time the clinic worksheet (from the ""Clinics"
^DIC(19,12939,1,46,0)="     and DSS Stop Codes Print"") is produced."
^DIC(19,12939,25)="EN^ECXSCLD"
^DIC(19,12939,"U")="CREATE DSS CLINIC STOP CODE FI"
^DIC(19,12940,0)="ECXSCEDIT^Enter/Edit Clinic Parameters^^R^11720^ECXMGR^^^^^^513"
^DIC(19,12940,1,0)="^19.06^8^8^3170911^^"
^DIC(19,12940,1,1,0)="This option displays the existing stop code and credit stop code values "
^DIC(19,12940,1,2,0)="associated with the clinic. The user is then prompted to update the "
^DIC(19,12940,1,3,0)="following fields:"
^DIC(19,12940,1,4,0)=" "
^DIC(19,12940,1,5,0)="     -  Action to Send;"
^DIC(19,12940,1,6,0)="     -  MCA Labor Code;"
^DIC(19,12940,1,7,0)="     -  Non-OR DSS Identifier;"
^DIC(19,12940,1,8,0)="     -  DSS Product Department."
^DIC(19,12940,25)="EDIT^ECXSCLD"
^DIC(19,12940,"U")="ENTER/EDIT CLINIC PARAMETERS"
^DIC(19,12941,0)="ECXADM^Admissions Extract^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^513"
^DIC(19,12941,1,0)="^^4^4^2950417^^^^"
^DIC(19,12941,1,1,0)="This option provides the extract manager the ability to extract the"
^DIC(19,12941,1,2,0)="patient admissions data for a selected date range. This data is stored"
^DIC(19,12941,1,3,0)="in the ADMISSION EXTRACT file (#727.802) until the data is transmitted"
^DIC(19,12941,1,4,0)="to the commercial vendor."
^DIC(19,12941,3.91,0)="^19.391^^0"
^DIC(19,12941,3.92,0)="^19.392A^^0"
^DIC(19,12941,25)="BEG^ECXADM"
^DIC(19,12941,"U")="ADMISSIONS EXTRACT"
^DIC(19,12943,0)="ECXMOV^Transfer and Discharge Extract^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^513"
^DIC(19,12943,1,0)="^^4^4^2950417^^^^"
^DIC(19,12943,1,1,0)="This option provides the extract manager the ability to extract the"
^DIC(19,12943,1,2,0)="patient movement (transfer and discharge) data for a selected date"
^DIC(19,12943,1,3,0)="range. This data is stored in the PHYSICAL MOVEMENT EXTRACT file"
^DIC(19,12943,1,4,0)="(#727.808) until the data is transmitted to the commercial vendor."
^DIC(19,12943,25)="BEG^ECXMOV"
^DIC(19,12943,"U")="TRANSFER AND DISCHARGE EXTRACT"
^DIC(19,12944,0)="ECXUD^Unit Dose Extract^^R^10000000020^^^^^^^513"
^DIC(19,12944,1,0)="^19.06^4^4^3030115^^^^"
^DIC(19,12944,1,1,0)="This option provides the extract manager the ability to extract the"
^DIC(19,12944,1,2,0)="pharmacy unit dose data for a selected date range. This data is"
^DIC(19,12944,1,3,0)="stored in the UNIT DOSE LOCAL EXTRACT file (#727.809)"
^DIC(19,12944,1,4,0)="until the data is transmitted to the commercial vendor."
^DIC(19,12944,25)="BEG^ECXUD"
^DIC(19,12944,"U")="UNIT DOSE EXTRACT"
^DIC(19,12945,0)="ECXMGR^Extract Manager's Options^^M^10000000020^^^^^^^513"
^DIC(19,12945,1,0)="^19.06^3^3^3060829^^^^"
^DIC(19,12945,1,1,0)="This is the main menu for the DSS extract manager. All setup options,"
^DIC(19,12945,1,2,0)="audit reports, maintenance activities, package extracts, and"
^DIC(19,12945,1,3,0)="transmission management options reside within the menu structure."
^DIC(19,12945,10,0)="^19.01IP^14^6"
^DIC(19,12945,10,4,0)="13559^P^10"
^DIC(19,12945,10,8,0)="13562^E^20"
^DIC(19,12945,10,11,0)="13563^S^15"
^DIC(19,12945,10,12,0)="13566^M^5"
^DIC(19,12945,10,13,0)="13567^T^25"
^DIC(19,12945,10,14,0)="14615^R^8"
