^DIC(19,14069,0)="XUSAP PROXY CONN DETAIL ALL^Proxy (Connector) Detail Report^^R^10000000216^^^^^^^163^y"
^DIC(19,14069,1,0)="^19.06^60^60^3120124^^"
^DIC(19,14069,1,1,0)="This option provides information about Connector Proxy accounts for the "
^DIC(19,14069,1,2,0)="purposes of:"
^DIC(19,14069,1,3,0)="1) Monitoring compliance with the 3-year mandate (per VA Handbook 6500)"
^DIC(19,14069,1,4,0)="   to expire/change verify codes for service accounts;"
^DIC(19,14069,1,5,0)="2) Reporting any mis-configured connector proxy accounts;"
^DIC(19,14069,1,6,0)="3) Listing account activity to help determine whether accounts are "
^DIC(19,14069,1,7,0)="   active, and are being accessed from which remote locations."
^DIC(19,14069,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14069,1,9,0)="When running the report, the following options determine how much "
^DIC(19,14069,1,10,0)="additional content is listed for each account:"
^DIC(19,14069,1,11,0)="- Check/display connector proxy fields? YES/NO (checks for mis-configured"
^DIC(19,14069,1,12,0)="  accounts)"
^DIC(19,14069,1,13,0)="- Scan sign-on log for connector proxy activity? YES/NO (lists account"
^DIC(19,14069,1,14,0)="  activity)"
^DIC(19,14069,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14069,1,16,0)="Possible categorizations for whether accounts are reported as ""Compliant "
^DIC(19,14069,1,17,0)="w/3-year Service Account Mandate?"" are:"
^DIC(19,14069,1,18,0)="- YES (account is complaint) "
^DIC(19,14069,1,19,0)="- *** NO <---- MUST FIX *** "
^DIC(19,14069,1,20,0)="  (date created and date verify code last changed > 3 years in the past)"
^DIC(19,14069,1,21,0)="- No, but user not active. "
^DIC(19,14069,1,22,0)="- UNABLE TO DETERMINE "
^DIC(19,14069,1,23,0)="  (until patch XU*8.0*574, date verify code last changed for Connector"
^DIC(19,14069,1,24,0)="  Proxy accounts was incorrectly recorded as 4/10/2005)"
^DIC(19,14069,1,25,0)="- unable to det. but not active."
^DIC(19,14069,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14069,1,27,0)="If an account's Date Verify Code Last Changed is listed as ""(changed but "
^DIC(19,14069,1,28,0)="date not recorded)"", that means the ""fake"" 4/10/2005"" date is present, "
^DIC(19,14069,1,29,0)="and unless the account was created within the last 3 years, it is "
^DIC(19,14069,1,30,0)="impossible to determine if the account is in compliance with the 3-year "
^DIC(19,14069,1,31,0)="mandate."
^DIC(19,14069,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14069,1,33,0)="Also, if there is a value in the XUS Logon Attempt Count field, that "
^DIC(19,14069,1,34,0)="value is displayed, as it could indicate a remote system attempting to "
^DIC(19,14069,1,35,0)="connect and failing with an invalid verify code."
^DIC(19,14069,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14069,1,37,0)="If the option to ""Check/display connector proxy fields?"" is selected, the "
^DIC(19,14069,1,38,0)="following checks are performed:"
^DIC(19,14069,1,39,0)="- Warnings: (any field listed in the warning section should not be "
^DIC(19,14069,1,40,0)="  populated. However, before changing, consult the National Help Desk or "
^DIC(19,14069,1,41,0)="  Customer Support as some applications may (currently) be depending "
^DIC(19,14069,1,42,0)="  (incorrectly) on a mis-configured connector configuration. "
^DIC(19,14069,1,43,0)="- Values for other fields allowed/expected: (field normally populated for"
^DIC(19,14069,1,44,0)="  connector proxies)"
^DIC(19,14069,1,45,0)="- Other Fields Populated (not expected fields, but not problematic either)"
^DIC(19,14069,1,46,0)="- Other Multiples Populated (not expected, but not problematic either)"
^DIC(19,14069,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14069,1,48,0)="If the option to ""Scan sign-on log for connector proxy activity?"" is "
^DIC(19,14069,1,49,0)="selected, the report will scan the sign-on log for all signon activity "
^DIC(19,14069,1,50,0)="associated with the account. Any activity found is displayed, organized "
^DIC(19,14069,1,51,0)="by client IP address, and within IP address, by date of sign-on. The "
^DIC(19,14069,1,52,0)="purpose of this report section is to help a site determine which accounts "
^DIC(19,14069,1,53,0)="are active, and which external systems (by IP address) are logging onto "
^DIC(19,14069,1,54,0)="the site with the specified account. This may help determine which remote "
^DIC(19,14069,1,55,0)="applications a change to the account (such as verify code change) might "
^DIC(19,14069,1,56,0)="impact, and may also help a site determine whether too many remote "
^DIC(19,14069,1,57,0)="applications/data centers are using the same account (which could result "
^DIC(19,14069,1,58,0)="in a more widespread service disruption if an account must be changed). "
^DIC(19,14069,1,59,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14069,1,60,0)="This option can be scheduled."
^DIC(19,14069,25)="ENALL^XUSAP1"
^DIC(19,14069,200.9)="y"
^DIC(19,14069,"U")="PROXY (CONNECTOR) DETAIL REPOR"
^DIC(19,14070,0)="XUSAP PROXY CONN DETAIL INQ^Proxy (Connector) Inquire^^R^10000000216^^^^^^^163^y"
^DIC(19,14070,1,0)="^^58^58^3120103^"
^DIC(19,14070,1,1,0)="This option provides information about Connector Proxy accounts for the "
^DIC(19,14070,1,2,0)="purposes of:"
^DIC(19,14070,1,3,0)="1) Monitoring compliance with the 3-year mandate (per VA Handbook 6500)"
^DIC(19,14070,1,4,0)="   to expire/change verify codes for service accounts;"
^DIC(19,14070,1,5,0)="2) Reporting any mis-configured connector proxy accounts;"
^DIC(19,14070,1,6,0)="3) Listing account activity to help determine whether accounts are "
^DIC(19,14070,1,7,0)="   active, and are being accessed from which remote locations."
^DIC(19,14070,1,8,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14070,1,9,0)="When running the report, the following options determine how much "
^DIC(19,14070,1,10,0)="additional content is listed for each account:"
^DIC(19,14070,1,11,0)="- Check/display connector proxy fields? YES/NO (checks for mis-configured"
^DIC(19,14070,1,12,0)="  accounts)"
^DIC(19,14070,1,13,0)="- Scan sign-on log for connector proxy activity? YES/NO (lists account"
^DIC(19,14070,1,14,0)="  activity)"
^DIC(19,14070,1,15,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14070,1,16,0)="Possible categorizations for whether accounts are reported as ""Compliant "
^DIC(19,14070,1,17,0)="w/3-year Service Account Mandate?"" are:"
^DIC(19,14070,1,18,0)="- YES (account is complaint) "
^DIC(19,14070,1,19,0)="- *** NO <---- MUST FIX *** "
^DIC(19,14070,1,20,0)="  (date created and date verify code last changed > 3 years in the past)"
^DIC(19,14070,1,21,0)="- No, but user not active. "
^DIC(19,14070,1,22,0)="- UNABLE TO DETERMINE "
^DIC(19,14070,1,23,0)="  (until patch XU*8.0*574, date verify code last changed for Connector"
^DIC(19,14070,1,24,0)="  Proxy accounts was incorrectly recorded as 4/10/2005)"
^DIC(19,14070,1,25,0)="- unable to det. but not active."
^DIC(19,14070,1,26,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14070,1,27,0)="If an account's Date Verify Code Last Changed is listed as ""(changed but "
^DIC(19,14070,1,28,0)="date not recorded)"", that means the ""fake"" 4/10/2005"" date is present, "
^DIC(19,14070,1,29,0)="and unless the account was created within the last 3 years, it is "
^DIC(19,14070,1,30,0)="impossible to determine if the account is in compliance with the 3-year "
^DIC(19,14070,1,31,0)="mandate."
^DIC(19,14070,1,32,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14070,1,33,0)="Also, if there is a value in the XUS Logon Attempt Count field, that "
^DIC(19,14070,1,34,0)="value is displayed, as it could indicate a remote system attempting to "
^DIC(19,14070,1,35,0)="connect and failing with an invalid verify code."
^DIC(19,14070,1,36,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14070,1,37,0)="If the option to ""Check/display connector proxy fields?"" is selected, the "
^DIC(19,14070,1,38,0)="following checks are performed:"
^DIC(19,14070,1,39,0)="- Warnings: (any field listed in the warning section should not be "
^DIC(19,14070,1,40,0)="  populated. However, before changing, consult the National Help Desk or "
^DIC(19,14070,1,41,0)="  Customer Support as some applications may (currently) be depending "
^DIC(19,14070,1,42,0)="  (incorrectly) on a mis-configured connector configuration. "
^DIC(19,14070,1,43,0)="- Values for other fields allowed/expected: (field normally populated for"
^DIC(19,14070,1,44,0)="  connector proxies)"
^DIC(19,14070,1,45,0)="- Other Fields Populated (not expected fields, but not problematic either)"
^DIC(19,14070,1,46,0)="- Other Multiples Populated (not expected, but not problematic either)"
^DIC(19,14070,1,47,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14070,1,48,0)="If the option to ""Scan sign-on log for connector proxy activity?"" is "
^DIC(19,14070,1,49,0)="selected, the report will scan the sign-on log for all signon activity "
^DIC(19,14070,1,50,0)="associated with the account. Any activity found is displayed, organized "
^DIC(19,14070,1,51,0)="by client IP address, and within IP address, by date of sign-on. The "
^DIC(19,14070,1,52,0)="purpose of this report section is to help a site determine which accounts "
^DIC(19,14070,1,53,0)="are active, and which external systems (by IP address) are logging onto "
^DIC(19,14070,1,54,0)="the site with the specified account. This may help determine which remote "
^DIC(19,14070,1,55,0)="applications a change to the account (such as verify code change) might "
^DIC(19,14070,1,56,0)="impact, and may also help a site determine whether too many remote "
^DIC(19,14070,1,57,0)="applications/data centers are using the same account (which could result "
^DIC(19,14070,1,58,0)="in a more widespread service disruption if an account must be changed). "
^DIC(19,14070,25)="EN1^XUSAP1"
^DIC(19,14070,"U")="PROXY (CONNECTOR) INQUIRE"
