^DIC(19,14396,0)="BPS RPT NON-BILLABLE REPORT^Non-Billable Status Report^^R^1^BPS REPORTS^^^^^^553"
^DIC(19,14396,1,0)="^19.06^3^3^3141030^^"
^DIC(19,14396,1,1,0)="This report lists prescriptions that were submitted to ECME but were not"
^DIC(19,14396,1,2,0)="able to be transmitted to the third party because the IB Billable Status"
^DIC(19,14396,1,3,0)="check determined the prescription was not billable."
^DIC(19,14396,25)="EN^BPSRPT0(9)"
^DIC(19,14396,"U")="NON-BILLABLE STATUS REPORT"
^DIC(19,14397,0)="OR CONV INPT QO TO CLIN ORD QO^Create Clinic Order QOs from Inpatient QOs^^R^1^^^^^^^170"
^DIC(19,14397,1,0)="^^50^50^3160602^"
^DIC(19,14397,1,1,0)="This utility provides a means of converting existing Unit Dose "
^DIC(19,14397,1,2,0)="Medications or IV Medication quick orders (QO) into Clinic Medication or "
^DIC(19,14397,1,3,0)="Clinic Infusion quick orders respectively. Upon entering the option, the"
^DIC(19,14397,1,4,0)="user is presented with a list of all Unit Dose and IV Medication quick"
^DIC(19,14397,1,5,0)="orders on the system.  Personal quick orders are excluded from the list."
^DIC(19,14397,1,6,0)="For any item in the list, the utility offers two actions: Move, or Copy."
^DIC(19,14397,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14397,1,8,0)="COPY"
^DIC(19,14397,1,9,0)="---- "
^DIC(19,14397,1,10,0)="Copy will create a copy of the quick order and then, if OR*3.0*350 "
^DIC(19,14397,1,11,0)="(CPRS GUI v30.B) has been installed, will prompt you to delete the"
^DIC(19,14397,1,12,0)="originally selected quick order.  During the copy process, the user is "
^DIC(19,14397,1,13,0)="prompted to enter a new name for the copied order and the Display Group is"
^DIC(19,14397,1,14,0)="set to Clinic Medications or Clinic Infusions. The Copy action can only"
^DIC(19,14397,1,15,0)="work with one quick order at a time and therefore is limited to a single"
^DIC(19,14397,1,16,0)="selection item from the list of available quick orders."
^DIC(19,14397,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14397,1,18,0)="If you choose to delete the original quick order, the utility will check"
^DIC(19,14397,1,19,0)="for any pointers referencing the selected quick order.  If any other items"
^DIC(19,14397,1,20,0)="(menus, orders sets, display group(s), reminder dialog items) are"
^DIC(19,14397,1,21,0)="referencing the selected quick order, the delete action will not be"
^DIC(19,14397,1,22,0)="permitted. If any pointers are found, the utility will display those items"
^DIC(19,14397,1,23,0)="on the screen.  If, at some point in the future, the pointers are removed"
^DIC(19,14397,1,24,0)="(i.e. you find that the selected QO is part of an order menu and then you"
^DIC(19,14397,1,25,0)="remove that QO from the menu) you should then be able to manually delete"
^DIC(19,14397,1,26,0)="the QO via the QO editor [ORCM QUICK ORDERS]."
^DIC(19,14397,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14397,1,28,0)="MOVE"
^DIC(19,14397,1,29,0)="----"
^DIC(19,14397,1,30,0)="Move will modify the selected quick order by changing the Display Group "
^DIC(19,14397,1,31,0)="to Clinic Medications or Clinic Infusions. The Move action allows for"
^DIC(19,14397,1,32,0)="selecting either a single item or a range of items (e.g. 1,3,4-9) to be"
^DIC(19,14397,1,33,0)="converted in succession."
^DIC(19,14397,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14397,1,35,0)="After entering the range of numbers, the user is asked: "
^DIC(19,14397,1,36,0)="""Do you want to MOVE the selected quick order(s)?"" The default answer is"
^DIC(19,14397,1,37,0)="NO. The user must answer YES in order to begin the operation. After"
^DIC(19,14397,1,38,0)="entering ""YES"", the utility will tell the user that the MOVE operation is"
^DIC(19,14397,1,39,0)="in progress and then announce that the operation has completed. ""Moving"
^DIC(19,14397,1,40,0)="selected quick order(s)."" will appear on the screen during the MOVE "
^DIC(19,14397,1,41,0)="operation. When MOVE has completed, "" Done!"" will be tacked onto the end "
^DIC(19,14397,1,42,0)="of the display to let the user know the operation has completed."
^DIC(19,14397,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14397,1,44,0)="During MOVE, if a given order dialog is not found, the following message"
^DIC(19,14397,1,45,0)="will be displayed:"
^DIC(19,14397,1,46,0)="""Abort: Order dialog not found - check file entry and try again."""
^DIC(19,14397,1,47,0)="""Order Dialog: "" (Name of the offending  order dialog will be inserted)"
^DIC(19,14397,1,48,0)="In this scenario, after checking that the selected order dialog is a valid"
^DIC(19,14397,1,49,0)="entry and does not appear corrupted in any way, try the MOVE operation "
^DIC(19,14397,1,50,0)="again. If problems persist, IT assistance may be required."
^DIC(19,14397,25)="UDQO^ORCMEDT9"
^DIC(19,14397,"U")="CREATE CLINIC ORDER QOS FROM I"
^DIC(19,14398,0)="OR DEBUG REPORT^RPC DEBUG REPORT^^A^1^^^^^^^^^1"
^DIC(19,14398,1,0)="^19.06^2^2^3140305^^"
^DIC(19,14398,1,1,0)="This is a report that shows a list of reports generated by CPRS to "
^DIC(19,14398,1,2,0)="capture the sequence of RPCs that were called"
^DIC(19,14398,20)="D DL^ORDEBUG2"
^DIC(19,14398,99)="63251,33087"
^DIC(19,14398,"U")="RPC DEBUG REPORT"
^DIC(19,14399,0)="ORW CLIN IND DATE DFLT^Consults Clinically Indicated Date Default^^A^1^^^^^^^170^^1"
^DIC(19,14399,1,0)="^^4^4^3150217^"
^DIC(19,14399,1,1,0)="This option allows you to set the default value for the ORCDGMRC "
^DIC(19,14399,1,2,0)="CLIN IND DATE DEFAULT parameter at the DIVISION or SYSTEM level.  This "
^DIC(19,14399,1,3,0)="parameter is used to control the default value for the Clinically "
^DIC(19,14399,1,4,0)="Indicated Date used in consult orders."
^DIC(19,14399,20)="D EDITPAR^XPAREDIT(""ORCDGMRC CLIN IND DATE DEFAULT"")"
^DIC(19,14399,"U")="CONSULTS CLINICALLY INDICATED "
^DIC(19,14400,0)="PSS MRR ORDERS DIAGNOSTIC RPT^Orders for MRRs With Removal Properties^^R^1^^^^^^^517"
^DIC(19,14400,1,0)="^^7^7^3151020^"
^DIC(19,14400,1,1,0)="This option enables you to determine which active orders contain "
^DIC(19,14400,1,2,0)="Orderable Items that have the new ""Prompt for Removal in BCMA"" flag value "
^DIC(19,14400,1,3,0)="set to 1, 2 or 3 that need to be discontinued and entered as New (not "
^DIC(19,14400,1,4,0)="copied, edited or renewed) AFTER the installation of Pharmacy Inpatient "
^DIC(19,14400,1,5,0)="Medications PSJ*5.0*315. Failure to re-create these orders could result"
^DIC(19,14400,1,6,0)="in confusing information to display on the BCMA VDL if displayed along"
^DIC(19,14400,1,7,0)="side newer MRR orders that do have the updated removal information."
^DIC(19,14400,25)="EN^PSSMRRDG"
^DIC(19,14400,"U")="ORDERS FOR MRRS WITH REMOVAL P"
^DIC(19,14401,0)="PSS MRR ORDERABLE ITEMS RPT^Orderable Items that Require Removal Report^^R^1^^^^^^^517"
^DIC(19,14401,1,0)="^^11^11^3151022^"
^DIC(19,14401,1,1,0)="This option enables you to determine which Orderable Items have the new "
^DIC(19,14401,1,2,0)="""Prompt for Removal in BCMA"" flag value set to 1, 2 or 3. These OIs are "
^DIC(19,14401,1,3,0)="Medications Requiring Removal. Values 2 and 3 allow medication-free "
^DIC(19,14401,1,4,0)="periods between administrations and Removal Times to be set during order "
^DIC(19,14401,1,5,0)="creation.  Value 2 items will have this as an option.  Value 3 items will "
^DIC(19,14401,1,6,0)="be required to have these medication-free periods defined."
^DIC(19,14401,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,14401,1,8,0)="                       A         ALL"
^DIC(19,14401,1,9,0)="     1        Removal at Next Administration"
^DIC(19,14401,1,10,0)="     2        Removal Period Optional Prior to Next Administration"
^DIC(19,14401,1,11,0)="     3        Removal Period Required Prior to Next Administration"""
^DIC(19,14401,25)="INIT^PSSMRRI"
^DIC(19,14401,"U")="ORDERABLE ITEMS THAT REQUIRE R"
^DIC(19,14402,0)="PSS HR/HA ORDERABLE ITEMS RPT^Orderable Items Report for High Risk\High Alert^^R^1^^^^^^^517"
^DIC(19,14402,1,0)="^^6^6^3151022^"
^DIC(19,14402,1,1,0)="This option enables you to determine which Orderable Items have the ""High "
^DIC(19,14402,1,2,0)="Risk/High Alert"" flag value set to 1, 2 or 3."
^DIC(19,14402,1,3,0)="                       A         ALL"
^DIC(19,14402,1,4,0)="     1        HIGH RISK/ALERT-NO WITNESS REQUIRED IN BCMA"
^DIC(19,14402,1,5,0)="     2        RECOMMEND WITNESS IN BCMA-HIGH RISK/ALERT"
^DIC(19,14402,1,6,0)="     3        WITNESS REQUIRED IN BCMA-HIGH RISK/ALERT"
^DIC(19,14402,25)="INIT^PSSHRHAI"
^DIC(19,14402,"U")="ORDERABLE ITEMS REPORT FOR HIG"
^DIC(19,14403,0)="HMP PATIENT ACTIVITY^Patient Appointments^^B^1^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,14403,1,0)="^^1^1^3150923^"
^DIC(19,14403,1,1,0)="Return appointments for a subscribed patient."
^DIC(19,14403,25)="ACT^HMPACT"
^DIC(19,14403,"RPC",0)="^19.05P^1^1"
^DIC(19,14403,"RPC",1,0)=3513
