^DIC(19,15778,0)="EHM-00599^Review Quick Orders for Inactive ICD9 Codes^^R^1^^^^^^^170^^^^"
^DIC(19,15778,1,0)="^^4^4^3240328^"
^DIC(19,15778,1,1,0)="This option may be run at any time to produce a report of Consult or "
^DIC(19,15778,1,2,0)="Procedure quick orders that have a provisional diagnosis code that "
^DIC(19,15778,1,3,0)="has been inactivated or will be inactivated in the future."
^DIC(19,15778,1,4,0)="Cloned from ""ORCM GMRC CSV CHECK"" option."
^DIC(19,15778,3)=""
^DIC(19,15778,25)="CSVOPT^ORCMGMCK"
^DIC(19,15778,"U")="REVIEW QUICK ORDERS FOR INACTI"
^DIC(19,15779,0)="EHM-00600^Medication Quick Order Report^^A^1^^^^^^^170^^1^^"
^DIC(19,15779,1,0)="^19.06^7^7^3240328^^"
^DIC(19,15779,1,1,0)="This option generates two reports (printed to an e-mail message sent to "
^DIC(19,15779,1,2,0)="the originator of the report) of Quick Orders that should be evaluated "
^DIC(19,15779,1,3,0)="due to the addition of three new fields in CPRS 27:  Route, IV Type and "
^DIC(19,15779,1,4,0)="Schedule.  One report includes QOs that are contained in an order menu, "
^DIC(19,15779,1,5,0)="order set or a reminder dialog.  The other report includes QOs that are "
^DIC(19,15779,1,6,0)="stand alone and not included in another entry. "
^DIC(19,15779,1,7,0)="Cloned from ""OR MEDICATION QO CHECKER"" option."
^DIC(19,15779,3)=""
^DIC(19,15779,20)="D ATWILL^ORWOD"
^DIC(19,15779,"U")="MEDICATION QUICK ORDER REPORT"
^DIC(19,15780,0)="EHM-00601^Convert IV Inpatient QO to Infusion QO^^A^1^^^^^^^170^^1^^"
^DIC(19,15780,1,0)="^^4^4^3240328^"
^DIC(19,15780,1,1,0)="This option will allow the user to ability to convert IV quick orders "
^DIC(19,15780,1,2,0)="that were set-up under the inpatient dialog to the infusion quick orders "
^DIC(19,15780,1,3,0)="format release with CPRS 27."
^DIC(19,15780,1,4,0)="Cloned from ""OR CONVERT INP TO IV"" option."
^DIC(19,15780,3)=""
^DIC(19,15780,20)="D EN^ORINQIV"
^DIC(19,15780,"U")="CONVERT IV INPATIENT QO TO INF"
^DIC(19,15781,0)="EHM-00602^IV Additive Frequency Utility^^A^1^^^^^^^170^^1^^"
^DIC(19,15781,1,0)="^19.06^3^3^3240328^^^"
^DIC(19,15781,1,1,0)="This option allows user the ability to add an additive frequency to "
^DIC(19,15781,1,2,0)="existing Continuous IV Quick Orders."
^DIC(19,15781,1,3,0)="Cloned from ""OR IV ADD FREQ UTILITY"" option."
^DIC(19,15781,3)=""
^DIC(19,15781,20)="D EN^ORADDFQT"
^DIC(19,15781,"U")="IV ADDITIVE FREQUENCY UTILITY"
^DIC(19,15782,0)="EHM-00603^Quick Order Mixed-Case Report^^R^1^^^^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,15782,1,0)="^19.06^9^9^3240328^^"
^DIC(19,15782,1,1,0)="This report identifies quick orders that potentially had the DRUG name"
^DIC(19,15782,1,2,0)="edited such that when the quick order is loaded in CPRS the dosage that is"
^DIC(19,15782,1,3,0)="saved with the quick order does not match any of the dosages available for"
^DIC(19,15782,1,4,0)="selection in the list. This causes the dosage checks not to be able to be"
^DIC(19,15782,1,5,0)="performed correctly.  The edit to the drug that this specifically looks "
^DIC(19,15782,1,6,0)="for is a case change to the DRUG name.  If the name is changed so that it"
^DIC(19,15782,1,7,0)="contains different characters that are not just case changes, this report"
^DIC(19,15782,1,8,0)="will not identify them."
^DIC(19,15782,1,9,0)="Cloned from ""OR QO CASE REPORT"" option."
^DIC(19,15782,3)=""
^DIC(19,15782,25)="CASE^ORQOREP"
^DIC(19,15782,"U")="QUICK ORDER MIXED-CASE REPORT"
^DIC(19,15783,0)="EHM-00604^Quick Order Free-Text Report^^R^1^^^^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,15783,1,0)="^^3^3^3240328^"
^DIC(19,15783,1,1,0)="This report identifies Medication Quick orders that have a free text "
^DIC(19,15783,1,2,0)="dosage that does not match exactly one of the Local Dosages from Pharmacy."
^DIC(19,15783,1,3,0)="Cloned from ""OR QO FREETEXT REPORT"" option."
^DIC(19,15783,3)=""
^DIC(19,15783,25)="DIFF^ORQOREP"
^DIC(19,15783,"U")="QUICK ORDER FREE-TEXT REPORT"
^DIC(19,15784,0)="EHM-00605^Create Clinic Order QOs from Inpatient QOs^^R^1^^^^^^^170^^^^"
^DIC(19,15784,1,0)="^^51^51^3240328^"
^DIC(19,15784,1,1,0)="This utility provides a means of converting existing Unit Dose "
^DIC(19,15784,1,2,0)="Medications or IV Medication quick orders (QO) into Clinic Medication or "
^DIC(19,15784,1,3,0)="Clinic Infusion quick orders respectively. Upon entering the option, the"
^DIC(19,15784,1,4,0)="user is presented with a list of all Unit Dose and IV Medication quick"
^DIC(19,15784,1,5,0)="orders on the system.  Personal quick orders are excluded from the list."
^DIC(19,15784,1,6,0)="For any item in the list, the utility offers two actions: Move, or Copy."
^DIC(19,15784,1,7,0)=" "
^DIC(19,15784,1,8,0)="COPY"
^DIC(19,15784,1,9,0)="---- "
^DIC(19,15784,1,10,0)="Copy will create a copy of the quick order and then, if OR*3.0*350 "
^DIC(19,15784,1,11,0)="(CPRS GUI v30.B) has been installed, will prompt you to delete the"
^DIC(19,15784,1,12,0)="originally selected quick order.  During the copy process, the user is "
^DIC(19,15784,1,13,0)="prompted to enter a new name for the copied order and the Display Group is"
^DIC(19,15784,1,14,0)="set to Clinic Medications or Clinic Infusions. The Copy action can only"
^DIC(19,15784,1,15,0)="work with one quick order at a time and therefore is limited to a single"
^DIC(19,15784,1,16,0)="selection item from the list of available quick orders."
^DIC(19,15784,1,17,0)=" "
^DIC(19,15784,1,18,0)="If you choose to delete the original quick order, the utility will check"
^DIC(19,15784,1,19,0)="for any pointers referencing the selected quick order.  If any other items"
^DIC(19,15784,1,20,0)="(menus, orders sets, display group(s), reminder dialog items) are"
^DIC(19,15784,1,21,0)="referencing the selected quick order, the delete action will not be"
^DIC(19,15784,1,22,0)="permitted. If any pointers are found, the utility will display those items"
^DIC(19,15784,1,23,0)="on the screen.  If, at some point in the future, the pointers are removed"
^DIC(19,15784,1,24,0)="(i.e. you find that the selected QO is part of an order menu and then you"
^DIC(19,15784,1,25,0)="remove that QO from the menu) you should then be able to manually delete"
^DIC(19,15784,1,26,0)="the QO via the QO editor [ORCM QUICK ORDERS]."
^DIC(19,15784,1,27,0)=" "
^DIC(19,15784,1,28,0)="MOVE"
^DIC(19,15784,1,29,0)="----"
^DIC(19,15784,1,30,0)="Move will modify the selected quick order by changing the Display Group "
^DIC(19,15784,1,31,0)="to Clinic Medications or Clinic Infusions. The Move action allows for"
^DIC(19,15784,1,32,0)="selecting either a single item or a range of items (e.g. 1,3,4-9) to be"
^DIC(19,15784,1,33,0)="converted in succession."
^DIC(19,15784,1,34,0)=" "
^DIC(19,15784,1,35,0)="After entering the range of numbers, the user is asked: "
^DIC(19,15784,1,36,0)="""Do you want to MOVE the selected quick order(s)?"" The default answer is"
^DIC(19,15784,1,37,0)="NO. The user must answer YES in order to begin the operation. After"
^DIC(19,15784,1,38,0)="entering ""YES"", the utility will tell the user that the MOVE operation is"
^DIC(19,15784,1,39,0)="in progress and then announce that the operation has completed. ""Moving"
^DIC(19,15784,1,40,0)="selected quick order(s)."" will appear on the screen during the MOVE "
^DIC(19,15784,1,41,0)="operation. When MOVE has completed, "" Done!"" will be tacked onto the end "
^DIC(19,15784,1,42,0)="of the display to let the user know the operation has completed."
^DIC(19,15784,1,43,0)=" "
^DIC(19,15784,1,44,0)="During MOVE, if a given order dialog is not found, the following message"
^DIC(19,15784,1,45,0)="will be displayed:"
^DIC(19,15784,1,46,0)="""Abort: Order dialog not found - check file entry and try again."""
^DIC(19,15784,1,47,0)="""Order Dialog: "" (Name of the offending  order dialog will be inserted)"
^DIC(19,15784,1,48,0)="In this scenario, after checking that the selected order dialog is a valid"
^DIC(19,15784,1,49,0)="entry and does not appear corrupted in any way, try the MOVE operation "
^DIC(19,15784,1,50,0)="again. If problems persist, IT assistance may be required."
^DIC(19,15784,1,51,0)="Cloned from ""OR CONV INPT QO TO CLIN ORD QO"" option."
^DIC(19,15784,3)=""
^DIC(19,15784,25)="UDQO^ORCMEDT9"
^DIC(19,15784,"U")="CREATE CLINIC ORDER QOS FROM I"
^DIC(19,15785,0)="EHM-00606^SUPPLY COVERSION UTILITY MENU^^M^1^^^^^^^^^^^"
^DIC(19,15785,1,0)="^19.06^3^3^3240328^^"
^DIC(19,15785,1,1,0)="This menu provides options to run conversions for Supply Orderable Items "
^DIC(19,15785,1,2,0)="to automatically set the QO-ONLY field to yes."
^DIC(19,15785,1,3,0)="Cloned from ""OR SUPPLY UTIL MENU"" option."
